hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1149","(1150) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed us. And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad al-Nasawī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Yūnus reported from Ibn Shihāb from Ibn al-Sabbāq that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās said: Maymūnah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up one day in a state of grief. Maymūnah said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have noticed a change in your condition since today.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Jibrīl had promised me that he would meet me last night"," but he did not meet me. By Allah"," he never breaks his promise.\"" He said: \""So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) spent his day in that state. Then it occurred to him that a puppy of a dog was under our tent"," so he commanded that it be removed. Then he took water with his hand and sprinkled the place where it had been. When evening came"," Jibrīl (peace be upon him) met him and said to him: 'You had promised me that you would meet me last night.' He said: 'Yes"," but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up that day and commanded the killing of dogs"," to the extent that he commanded the killing of the small garden dog and left the large garden dog.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā thus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 5/21]"""
"1150","(1151) And thus Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us with the hadith of Baḥr ibn Naṣr, combined with the hadith of Ḥarmalah. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us with it in the Fawāʾid of the Shaykh, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī in the Musnad of Ibn Wahb, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr ibn Sābiq al-Khawlānī informed us in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 266 AH; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb ibn Muslim al-Qurashī informed me; Yūnus ibn Yazīd reported from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī from ʿUbayd Allāh from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up one day in a state of grief… and he mentioned the hadith, and in it: \Then he took water with his hand and sprinkled the place where it had been.\"" And in the hadith of Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh.\n\nAnd Shabīb ibn Saʿīd narrated it from Yūnus from Ibn Shihāb from Ibn al-Sabbāq from Maymūnah.\n\nAnd Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah and Sulaymān ibn Kathīr narrated it from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbayd ibn al-Sabbāq from Ibn ʿAbbās from Maymūnah with its meaning.\n\nAnd it was narrated from ʿUqayl from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ibn ʿAbbās from Maymūnah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1151","(1152) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Muslim narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUzayy al-Aylī narrated to us; Salamah narrated from ʿUqayl; Muḥammad ibn Muslim informed me that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed him that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās informed him that Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ… and he mentioned the hadith until he said: \Jibrīl"," upon him peace"," promised me that he would meet me.\"" Maymūnah said: \""There was a puppy in my house"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ removed it and then sprinkled water over its place.\""\n\nAnd in this hadith and in the one preceding it from the narrations concerning a dog licking (a vessel)"," there is an indication of the abrogation of that (earlier ruling). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1152","(1153) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Zayd al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Shabīb ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; my father informed me from Yūnus; Ibn Shihāb said: Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: \I used to spend the night in the mosque during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and I was a young unmarried man. The dogs would urinate and come and go in the mosque"," and they would not sprinkle water over any of that.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: \""And Aḥmad ibn Shabīb said","\"" and he mentioned it in abbreviated form"," and he did not include his words: \""would urinate.\""\n\nThe Muslims have unanimously agreed on the impurity of a dog's urine"," and on the obligation of sprinkling water over the urine of a human being—so how much more so a dog's urine? It is as though that was before the command to kill dogs and to wash vessels from a dog's licking"," or as though the place where they urinated was unknown to them; and whoever knows it is obliged to wash it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (172)]"""
"1153","(1154) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk and Ibn Milḥān said: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," the son of Mary shall soon descend as a just ruler; he shall break the cross"," kill the swine"," abolish the jizyah"," and wealth shall overflow until no one will accept it.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Qutaybah"," and Ibn ʿAbdān did not mention the jizyah in his hadith.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (2109)]"""
"1154","(1155) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad and Aḥmad ibn Salamah said: Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When any one of you wakes up"," let him not put his hand into his vessel\""—or he said"," \""into his wuḍūʾ water\""—\""until he washes it three times"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (278)]"""
"1155","(1156) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us; Abū al-Mughīrah ʿAbd al-Quddūs ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, that he used to say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When any one of you rises at night"," let him not put his hand into the vessel until he pours water over it two or three times"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nAnd Ibn Hurmaz similarly narrated it from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it (24)]"""
"1156","(1157) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Najdah narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from Fāṭimah bint al-Munthir—who was his wife—from Asmāʾ, her grandmother, that a woman asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said: \Scrape it off"," then rub it with water"," then sprinkle water over it"," then pray in it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it (138)]"""
"1157","(1158) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Qudāmah narrated to us; Ayyūb ibn Jābir narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿIṣmah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The prayer was fifty (rakʿahs)"," the ghusl from janābah was seven times"," and washing the garment from urine was seven times. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept asking (for reduction) until the prayer was made five"," the ghusl from janābah was made once"," and washing the garment from urine was made once.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1158","(1159) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; it was read to Ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas informed you.\n\nHe said: And Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us; Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ḥumaydah bint ʿUbayd ibn Rifāʿah, from Kabshah bint Kaʿb ibn Mālik—who was married to Ibn Abī Qatādah—that Abū Qatādah came to her and she poured out wuḍūʾ water for him. A cat came to drink from it, so Abū Qatādah tilted the vessel for her until she drank. Kabshah said: \I saw him and he said: 'Are you surprised"," O daughter of my brother?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""It is not impure; it is among the males and females that go around among you.\""'\""\n\nThis is how Mālik ibn Anas narrated it in the Muwaṭṭaʾ. Some of the narrators shortened its narration and did not establish its isnād.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: \""I asked Muḥammad"," meaning Ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī"," about this hadith"," and he said: 'Mālik ibn Anas rendered this hadith well"," and his narration is more authentic than that of others.'\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: And Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated it in a manner close to the narration of Mālik. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (75)]"""
"1159","(1160) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Umm Yaḥyā, from her paternal aunt, the daughter of Kaʿb, who said: \Abū Qatādah came to us and we brought him wuḍūʾ water. A cat approached and he tilted the vessel toward it and it drank from it"," then he performed wuḍūʾ with the remainder of it. I looked at him and he turned to me and said: 'It seems you are surprised?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \""It is not impure\""—or another word: \""They are among the males and females that go around among you.\""'\""\n\nUmm Yaḥyā is Ḥumaydah"," and the daughter of Kaʿb is Kabshah bint Kaʿb.\n\nAnd Hammām ibn Yaḥyā similarly narrated it from Isḥāq. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"1160","(1161) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us; al-Ḥawḍī narrated to us; Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us.\n\nHe said: And Abū Muslim narrated to us; Ḥajjāj narrated to us; Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah narrated to me. He said: Umm Yaḥyā narrated to me—Ḥajjāj said in his narration: \Meaning his wife\""—from her paternal aunt"," who was married to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah. She said: \""Abū Qatādah came to me and asked for wuḍūʾ water. A cat passed by and he tilted the vessel toward it. I looked at him as though I disapproved of what he was doing"," and he said: 'O daughter of my brother"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \""It is not impure; it is among the males and females that go around among you.\""'\""\n\nIn the hadith of al-Ḥawḍī: \""Her paternal aunt narrated to her that she was married to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah. Abū Qatādah came to her and called for wuḍūʾ water. A cat passed by and he tilted the vessel toward it"," and she looked at him as though she disapproved of what he was doing.\"" The remainder is similar.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Hammām ibn Yaḥyā"," from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr"," from Ibn Abī Qatādah"," from his father. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"1161","(1162) It was narrated to us by ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān, who was informed by Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd, who narrated to us from Tamtām, who narrated to us from ʿAffān, who narrated to us from Hammām, who narrated to us from Yaḥyī ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father, that he was performing wuḍūʾ when a cat passed by, so he inclined the vessel toward it and said: \Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'It (the cat) is not impure (najis).'\""\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī narrated it from al-Thiqah from Yaḥyī ibn Abī Kathīr.\n\nAnd it was narrated through another chain from Ibn Abī Qatādah. [Hasan due to corroborating narrations]"""
"1162","(1163) It was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ, who was informed by al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who narrated to us from Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb, who narrated to us from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Ḥajabī, who narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, who narrated to us from al-Ḥajjāj, from Qatādah ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father, who said: \Abū Qatādah used to incline the vessel for the cat so that it could drink"," and then he would perform wuḍūʾ with it. He was asked about that"," and he said: 'I did not do anything except what I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) doing.'\"" [Hasan due to corroborating narrations]"""
"1163","(1164) It was narrated to us by Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, who narrated to us from Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī, who narrated to us from Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, who informed us from Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd, who narrated to us from Sufyān, from Khālid, from ʿIkrimah, who said: \I saw Abū Qatādah bring his water for purification close to the cat"," so it would drink from it"," and then he would perform wuḍʾ with its leftover water.\""\n\nAll of this serves as evidence supporting the authenticity of the narration of Mālik. Among its corroborating narrations is what follows. [Ṣaḥīḥ due to corroborating narrations. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd"," 2756]"""
"1164","(1165) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who narrated to us from Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Mūsā al-Qāḍī in Bukhārā, who narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb, who informed us from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar al-Rāzī, who narrated to us from Sulaymān ibn Musāfiʿ ibn Shaybah al-Ḥajabī, who said: I heard Manṣūr ibn Ṣafiyyah, the son of Shaybah, narrating from his mother Ṣafiyyah, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said regarding the cat: \Indeed"," it is not impure; it is one of the household members (who go around among you).\"" [Hasan due to corroborating narrations. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 2/1]"""
"1165","(1166) Among them is what was narrated to us by Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Khaṭīb, who informed us from Abū Baḥr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Kawthar, who narrated to us from Bishr ibn Mūsā, who narrated to us from al-Ḥumaydī, who narrated to us from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad, who informed me from Dāwūd ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Tammār, from his mother, that a female slave of hers presented ʿĀʾishah with a dish of harīsah as a gift. She brought it while ʿĀʾishah was standing in prayer, so ʿĀʾishah gestured to her to set it down, and she set it down. There were women with ʿĀʾishah. Then a cat came and ate a morsel from it — or he said, a bite. When ʿĀʾishah finished her prayer, she said to the women: \Eat.\"" They began avoiding the spot where the cat's mouth had been. So ʿĀʾishah took it"," turned it around"," and ate from it"," and she said: \""Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'It is not impure; rather"," it is among the males and females who go round about you.'\"" And I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing wuḍūʾ with its leftover water.\n\nAnd it was narrated through other chains from ʿĀʾishah with the same meaning"," and what we have mentioned is sufficient. [Hasan due to corroborating narrations. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 76]"""
"1166","(1167) And it was narrated to us by Abū Saʿīd al-Khaṭīb, who informed us from Abū Baḥr al-Barbahārī, who narrated to us from Bishr ibn Mūsā, who narrated to us from al-Ḥumaydī, who narrated to us from Sufyān, who informed us from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabīʿ, from his paternal aunt, whose name was Ṣafiyyah bint ʿUmaylah, that al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī was asked about the leftover water of the cat, and he saw no harm in it. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq, 357]"
"1167","(1168) As for what was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — Abū ʿAbdillāh said: \He narrated to me","\"" and Abū Bakr said: \""He informed us\"" — from Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ"," who narrated to us from Abū Bakr ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Faqīh"," who narrated to us from Bakkārs ibn Qutaybah and Ḥammād ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAnbasah"," who both said: \""Narrate to us from Abū ʿĀṣim","\"" who narrated to us from Qurrah ibn Khālid"," who narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn"," from Abū Hurayrah"," who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""The purification of the vessel when a dog licks it is that it be washed seven times"," the first time with earth"," and the cat (requires washing) once or twice.\"" Qurrah expressed uncertainty.\n\nAnd ʿAlī ibn Muslim narrated it with the same meaning from Abū ʿĀṣim.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated it from Bakkārs ibn Qutaybah from Abū ʿĀṣim"," and regarding the cat it is the same.\n\nAbū ʿĀṣim is al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad"," a trustworthy narrator"," except that he erred in incorporating Abū Hurayrah's statement regarding the cat into the marfūʿ hadith about the dog.\n\nAnd ʿAlī ibn Naṣr al-Jahḍamī narrated it from Qurrah"," and he clarified it with a clear explanation. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/64]"""
"1168","(1169) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who narrated to us from Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī, who narrated to us from Abū Maʿshar al-Ḥasan ibn Sulaymān al-Dārimī, who narrated to us from Naṣr ibn ʿAlī, who narrated to us from my father, who narrated to us from Qurrah ibn Khālid, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \The purification of the vessel of any one of you when a dog licks it is that it be washed seven times"," the first of them with earth.\"" Then Abū Hurayrah mentioned the cat — I do not know whether he said \""once\"" or \""twice.\""\n\nNaṣr ibn ʿAlī said: \""I found it in my father's book in another place"," from Qurrah"," from Ibn Sīrīn"," from Abū Hurayrah"," regarding the dog as marfūʿ"," and regarding the cat as mawqūf.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated it from Qurrah as mawqūf regarding the cat. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/365]"""
"1169","(1170) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who informed us from Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh, who narrated to us from Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Birtī, who said: \And Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us"," who narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb"," who said: 'And Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī narrated to us"," who narrated to us from Abū Khalīfah.'\"" They all said: \""Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us"," who narrated to us from Qurrah"," who narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn"," from Abū Hurayrah"," regarding the cat licking the vessel: 'It is to be washed once or twice.'\""\n\nAnd Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī narrated it from Muḥammad in the same way"," as mawqūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/365]"""
"1170","(1171) It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī, who informed us from Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah, who narrated to us from Abū Dāwūd, who narrated to us from Musaddad, who narrated to us from al-Muʿtamir, who said: \And Abū Dāwūd narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd"," who narrated to us from Ḥammād ibn Zayd — both of them from Ayyūb"," from Muḥammad"," from Abū Hurayrah"," who said: 'When the cat licks (the vessel)"," it is washed once.'\""\n\nAnd Maʿmar narrated it in the same manner from Ayyūb.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Qaṣabī erred in it"," for he narrated it from ʿAbd al-Wārith from Ayyūb"," incorporating it into the marfūʿ hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 72]"""
"1171","(1172) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq in Naysābūr and Abū al-Qāsim Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ṣaqr in Baghdād informed us, both saying: Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adhamī narrated to us. They both said: ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Qaṣabī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; Ayyūb narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When a dog licks the vessel of any one of you"," let him wash it seven times"," the first or the last of them with earth (turāb). And the cat [requires washing] once.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by Ḥafṣ ibn Wāqid from Ibn ʿAwn from Muḥammad from Abū Hurayrah"," marfūʿ"," incorporated within the hadith. However"," the narration of the group (al-jamāʿah) is more deserving of precedence. And Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated it from Muḥammad from Abū Hurayrah regarding the cat's leftover (suʾr): it is to be poured out and the vessel washed once or twice. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1172","(1173) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us; Hishām narrated it.\n\nAnd Layth ibn Abī Sulaym narrated from ʬāʾ from Abū Hurayrah: \When the cat licks the vessel"," it is washed seven times.\"" However"," it was only narrated as such by Ibn Jurayj and others from ʬāʾ as his own statement (mawqūf). And it was narrated through another chain from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ṭaḥāwī narrated it (1/20)]"""
"1173","(1174) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿUfayr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah, who said: \The vessel is washed from the cat's licking just as it is washed from the dog.\""\n\nThus did Ibn ʿUfayr narrate it"," as a mawqūf (stopping at the Companion).\n\nAnd it was narrated from Rūḥ ibn al-Faraj from Ibn ʿUfayr as marfūʿ (raised to the Prophet)"," but it is nothing [of significance].\n\nAnd it has been said: from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb"," who said: Khayr ibn Nuʿaym informed me from Abū al-Zubayr from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah"," as a mawqūf. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Ṭaḥāwī in Sharḥ al-Maʿānī (1/20)]"""
"1174","(1175) Abū Bakr al-Ḥārithī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; ʿAllān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb… and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd it is narrated from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ that which constitutes an argument against him in his fatwā regarding the cat, if that is authentic. Otherwise, he is rebutted by what has preceded from the hadith of Abū Qatādah and ʿĀʾishah from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Ṭaḥāwī narrated it (1/20)]"
"1175","(1176) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Abū al-Naḍr Hāshim ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us; ʿĪsā, meaning Ibn al-Musayyab, narrated to me; Abū Zurʿah narrated to me from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet ﷺ used to come to the house of a certain group of the Anṣār, and there was another house near them, i.e., he would not come to it. That distressed them, so they said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you come to the house of so-and-so but you do not come to our house.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""There is a dog in your house.\"" He said: \""But there is a cat in their house.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""The cat is a predatory animal (sabʿ).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Aḥmad narrated it (2/327)]"""
"1176","(1178) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Tarqafī narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; al-Ḥakam, meaning Ibn Abān, narrated to us from ʿIkrimah from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The cat is part of the household's furnishings (matāʿ al-bayt).\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrih. Ibn Mājah narrated it (369)]"""
"1177","(1178) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn from his father from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: It was said: \O Messenger of Allah"," should we perform wuḍūʾ with what the donkeys have left over?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and with what all predatory animals (sibāʿ) have left over.\""\n\nIn other than our narration"," al-Shāfiʿī said: And Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn with its like. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it (10)]"""
"1178","(1179) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣūfī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Mawṣilī narrated to us; Bisṭām ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Mukhtār al-Mawṣilī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn from his father from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \Should we perform wuḍūʾ with what the donkeys have left over?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and with what the predatory animals (sibāʿ) have left over.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated its meaning from Ibrāhīm.\n\nIbrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā al-Aslamī is differed upon regarding his reliability (thiqah); most of the scholars of hadith weakened him and criticized him. Yet al-Shāfiʿī used to distance him from lying.\n\nAbū Saʿd al-Ṣūfī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us"," saying: I heard al-Rabīʿ say: I heard al-Shāfiʿī say: \""Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Yaḥyā was a Qadarī.\"" I said to al-Rabīʿ: \""What then compelled al-Shāfiʿī to narrate from him?\"" He said: \""He used to say: 'That Ibrāhīm should fall from a distance is more beloved to me than that he should lie.' And he was trustworthy in hadith.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī said: \""I have examined his hadiths and there is no munkar hadith among them. Rather"," the munkar only occurs when the responsibility lies with the narrator from him or with the one from whom Ibrāhīm narrates.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Ḥabībah al-Ashalī followed him in narrating this hadith from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn"," and we have mentioned him in the book al-Maʿrifah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1179","(1180) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us from Ibn Abī Ḥabībah from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn from his father from Jābir, who said: It was said: \O Messenger of Allah"," should we perform wuḍūʾ with what the donkeys have left over?\"" He said: \""And with what the predatory animals (sibāʿ) have left over.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1180","(1181) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us, both saying: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb went out in a caravan in which was ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, until they came to a watering pool. ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ said to the owner of the pool: \O owner of the pool"," do predatory animals come to your pool?\"" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said: \""O owner of the pool"," do not tell us"," for we come upon the predatory animals and they come upon us.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Mālik narrated it (43)]"""
"1181","Al-Husayn ibn Bashran informed us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us: Mu'allaa, i.e. ibn Mansur, informed us, and Khalid informed me from Yunus from al-Hasan that he used to see no harm in the leftover water (su') of a donkey or a mule. [Sahih]"
"1182","Al-Husayn — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bashran al-'Adl — informed us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever keeps a dog"," except a dog for herding livestock"," hunting"," or guarding crops"," one qirat will be deducted from his reward every day.\""\n\nAl-Zuhri said: Abu Hurayrah's statement was mentioned to Ibn 'Umar"," and he said: \""May Allah have mercy on Abu Hurayrah; he was a man of farming.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd ibn Humayd from 'Abd al-Razzaq"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah.\n\nSa'id ibn al-Musayyib also narrated it from Abu Hurayrah"," and he said in the hadith: \""Two qirats.\"" [Sahih. Al-Bukhari narrated it"," 2197]"""
"1183","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzzi both informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Yunus informed me from Ibn Shihab who said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever keeps a dog that is not a dog for hunting"," herding livestock"," or guarding land"," two qirats will be deducted from his reward every day.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu al-Tahir and Harmalah ibn Yahya from Ibn Wahb.\n\nSimilarly"," Ibn 'Umar narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""Two qirats.\"" However"," in most narrations from him"," he did not preserve the mention of the dog for guarding land. Abu Hurayrah and Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Shana'i both preserved it from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," except that Sufyan ibn Abi Zuhayr did not preserve the hunting dog and said: \""One qirat.\"" [Sahih]"""
"1184","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Abu al-Muthanna narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya narrated from Shu'bah from Abu al-Tayyah from Mutarrif ibn 'Abdullah from Ibn Mughaffal who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded the killing of dogs, then he said: \What concern do they have with them?\"" Then he granted concession regarding the hunting dog and the sheep dog"," and he said: \""When the dog licks the vessel"," wash it seven times"," and rub it with dirt the eighth time.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Hatim from Yahya ibn Sa'id. [Sahih]"""
"1185","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Isa informed us: Musa ibn Muhammad al-A'yan narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us: I recited to Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf from Malik, and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari narrated it, 732]"
"1186","Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawi informed us orally: 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Sharqi narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us: Sufyan ibn 'Uyyaynah narrated from al-Zuhri from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah from Ibn 'Abbas from Abu Talhah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Ali ibn al-Madini"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya and others"," all of them from Ibn 'Uyyaynah. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari narrated it"," 53/3]"""
"1187","Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-'Abbas al-Duri narrated to us: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: 'Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah narrated to us: Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: 'Isa, i.e. ibn al-Musayyib, narrated to me: Abu Zur'ah narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to visit the houses of a group of the Ansar, and there were houses below them that he would not visit. This distressed them, so they said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you visit the house of so-and-so but do not visit our house.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""There is a dog in your house.\"" He said: \""But in their house there is a cat.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""A cat is a predator (sabu').\""\n\nAbu Sa'id al-Malini informed us: Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz said: 'Isa ibn al-Musayyib is sound in what he narrates.\n\nAnd Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz said: 'Isa ibn al-Musayyib is sound in hadith. [Da'if]"""
"1188","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Asid ibn 'Asim narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us: Mus'ab ibn Sawwar narrated from Mutarrif from Abu al-Jahm from al-Bara' who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no harm in the leftover water (su') of any animal whose meat is eaten.\""\n\n'Abdullah ibn Raja' named him Mus'ab ibn Sawwar"," thus reversing his name"," when in fact he is Sawwar ibn Mus'ab.\n\nSawwar ibn Mus'ab is matruk (abandoned). Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us of this from Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz.\n\nThe Sheikh said: Despite the weakness of Sawwar ibn Mus'ab"," there is disagreement regarding its text. 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated from him as above. Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated from him with his chain: \""There is no harm in the urine (bawl) of any animal whose meat is eaten.\""\n\n'Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated it from Yahya ibn al-'Ala' from Mutarrif from Muharib ibn Dithar from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah"," raised to the Prophet"," regarding urine.\n\n'Amr ibn al-Husayn and Yahya ibn al-'Ala' are both weak"," and none of this is authentic. [Very Da'if. Al-Daraqutni narrated it"," 1/127]"""
"1189","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us: 'Utbah ibn Muslim narrated to me that 'Ubayd ibn Hunayn informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a fly falls into the drink of one of you"," let him submerge it entirely"," then remove it"," for one of its wings carries disease and the other carries a cure.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Khalid ibn Makhlad from Sulayman ibn Bilal. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari narrated it"," 3142]"""
"1190","Abu 'Abdullah — al-Husayn ibn 'Umar ibn Burhan — and Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan both informed us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you"," one of its wings carries disease and the other carries a cure"," and it protects itself with the wing that carries disease"," so let him submerge it entirely"," then remove it.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by 'Umar ibn 'Ali from Ibn 'Ajlan from al-Qa'qa' from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah with a similar meaning. [Sahih]"""
"1191","(1192) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Saʿīd ibn Khālid al-Qāriẓī, who said: I came to Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān at Minā, and he presented to me butter and cheese. A fly fell into the butter, and he began to submerge it with his little finger. I said: \O maternal uncle"," what are you doing?\"" He said: \""Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī informed me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When a fly falls into food"," submerge it"," for one of its wings carries poison and the other carries a cure"," and it delays the cure and advances the poison.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1192","(1193) Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Zubaydī, from Bishr ibn Manṣūr, from ʿAlī ibn Zayd ibn Judʿān, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Salmān, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \O Salmān"," any food or drink into which a creature without blood falls and dies is lawful — its consumption"," its drinking"," and its use for ablution.\""\n\nAbū Saʿd informed us"," Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," Ibn Abī Dāwūd narrated to us"," Yaḥyā ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us"," Baqiyyah… and he mentioned it.\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: The ḥadīths that Saʿīd al-Zubaydī narrates are generally not well-preserved.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us"," ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ said: No one narrated it from Saʿīd al-Zubaydī other than Baqiyyah"," and he is weak. [Very weak. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it (1/37)]"""
"1193","(1194) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Mughīrah, from Ibrāhīm, that he used to say: Ablution is not required from any creature with flowing blood [that falls into a vessel and dies], but concession has been given regarding the beetle, the scorpion, the locust, and the cricket when they fall into vessels — there is no harm in that.\n\nShuʿbah said: I think he also mentioned the gecko.\n\nThe Shaykh said: We narrated the same meaning from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī, ʿAṭāʾ, and ʿIkrimah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it (1/33)]"
"1194","(1195) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād, Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk informed us, Abū Qilābah narrated to me, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me in the year 216, and I said to him: \How old are you"," O Abū ʿAbd Allāh?\"" He said: \""Fifty-four or fifty-five.\""\n\nHe said: Abū al-Qāsim ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to me"," Isḥāq ibn Ḥāzim narrated from Ibn Mismʿī — meaning ʿUbayd Allāh — from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about sea water"," and he said: \""Its water is purifying"," and its dead are lawful.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1195","(1196) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Sabīʿī — among others — informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that he said: \Two dead creatures and two bloods have been made lawful for us: locusts and fish"," and the liver and the spleen.\""\n\nThis is a sound chain of narration"," and it is in the meaning of a marfūʿ narration. Zayd's sons have narrated it from their father in marfūʿ form. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1196","(1197) Abū Jaʿfar Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣighghī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād al-Surrī informed us, Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Usāmah, and ʿAbd Allāh — the sons of Zayd ibn Aslam — narrated from their father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Two dead creatures and two bloods have been made lawful for us. As for the two dead creatures: the locust and the whale. As for the two bloods: the spleen and the liver.\""\n\nThese sons of Zayd are all weak; Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn criticized them. However"," Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī used to consider ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd trustworthy. Nevertheless"," the first ḥadīth is the more correct of the two. [Munkar as marfūʿ; ṣaḥīḥ as mawqūf. Aḥmad narrated it (2/97)]"""
"1197","(1198) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak — may Allah have mercy on him — informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah narrated from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to enter the house of Umm Sulaym and sleep on her bed while she was not… Then he said: One day she was called and told: \This is the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on your bed.\"" She came to him while he had sweated profusely"," and that was in the heat. She took a small bottle and began to collect that sweat and place it in the bottle. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) woke up and said: \""What are you doing?\"" She said: \""Your blessing"," O Messenger of Allah — we will put it in our perfume.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""You have done right.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from Ḥujayn ibn al-Muthannā from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Mājishūn with the same meaning.\n\nThābit al-Bunānī and Anas ibn Sīrīn narrated it from Anas ibn Mālik"," and Abū Qilābah narrated it from Anas from Umm Sulaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (2231)]"""
"1198","(1199) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb, he said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrating from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to perform ablution in the heat and would pass his hands over his armpits, and that did not invalidate his ablution. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1199","(1200) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us, Qabīṣah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir narrated to us, Zakariyyā ibn al-Ḥakam al-Rāsibī narrated to us, al-Firyābī narrated to us. They both said: Sufyān narrated from Ḥumayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) spat in his garment — meaning while he was in prayer.\n\nThe wording is that of al-Firyābī's ḥadīth, and in Qabīṣah's ḥadīth: \That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) spat in his garment.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Firyābī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (398)]"""
"1200","(1201) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw phlegm in the direction of the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it with his hand. The severity of his displeasure was visible on his face, and he said: \When a servant stands in prayer"," he is conversing privately with his Lord"," between himself and the qiblah. When any of you wishes to spit"," let him spit to his left"," or beneath his feet"," or let him do like this.\"" Then he spat in his garment and rubbed one part of it against another. Yazīd said: \""And Ḥumayd showed us [how].\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (397)]"""
"1201","(1202) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, ʿAwf informed us from Abī Rajāʾ from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: We were on a journey with the Prophet ﷺ… Then he mentioned the hadith concerning the water-skin of the polytheist woman. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a vessel and poured into it from the openings of the two water-skins (or the two leather containers). He rinsed his mouth with the water and returned it to the openings of the two water-skins (or the two leather containers), then he tied their openings and released the water-skins. Then he said to the people: \Drink and give water to your animals.\"" Extracted in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of ʿAwf."""
"1202","(1203) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk informed us, Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq informed us, Qabīṣah informed us, Sufyān informed us from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid from Qays from Jarīr, that he used to command his family to perform wuḍūʾ with the remaining water of his siwāk."
"1203","(1204) Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā both said: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā al-Hilālī informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Yaʿqūb al-Iyādī informed us in Baghdad, Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us, Mālik ibn Mighwal informed us from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for the funeral of Abū al-Daḥdāḥ. When he returned, a horse with a lean back was brought to him, and he mounted it while we walked alongside him.\n\nMuslim extracted it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others from Wakīʿ from Mālik."
"1204","(1205) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazyad informed us, my father informed me, Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us from Zayd ibn Aslam and others from Ibn ʿUmar, in a story he mentioned regarding the Ḥajj, he said: I was beneath the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, its saliva touching me, while I could hear him uttering the talbiyah for the Ḥajj."
"1205","(1206) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid informed us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd informed us, al-Haytham ibn Jamīl informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us from Qatādah from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanm from ʿAmr ibn Khārijah, who said: I was holding the reins of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was gulping with its throat, its saliva dripping between my two shoulders. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"1206","(1207) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed me, my father informed me, ʿAbd al-Razzāq and Ibn Bakr both said: Ibn Jurayj informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, and the wording is his: Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us, Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Ziyād informed me that Thābit, the freedman of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd, informed him that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you has been asleep and then awakens and intends to perform wuḍūʾ"," let him not place his hand in the vessel until he pours water over his hand"," for he does not know where his hand spent the night.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim from Muḥammad ibn Bakr"," and he also narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ."""
"1207","(1208) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, he said: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād informed you from Abī al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When a dog drinks from the vessel of one of you"," let him wash it seven times.\""\n\nExtracted in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Mālik as has preceded.\n\nAnd Ibn ʿUyaynah said from Abī al-Zinād: \""lagged\"" (walagha) in place of \""drank\"" (shariba)."""
"1208","(1209) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh and Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbdillāh both said: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr informed us, ʿAlī ibn Mushhir informed us, al-Aʿmash informed us from Abī Razīn and Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When a dog licks the vessel of one of you"," let him pour out its contents"," then wash it seven times.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr."""
"1209","(1210) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us from Abī al-Zinād from Mūsā ibn Abī ʿUthmān from his father from Abū Hurayrah, who attributed it (marfūʿan), saying: \None of you should urinate in standing water and then bathe from it.\"""""
"1210","(1211) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Salmān informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram and Aḥmad ibn Ḥayyān ibn Mulāʿib both said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Bakr al-Sahmī informed us, Hishām ibn Ḥassān informed us from Ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ with the same meaning.\n\nMuslim extracted it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Hishām ibn Ḥassān."
"1211","(1212) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us — dictation — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr ibn Sābiq al-Khawlānī narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed me from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Cover the vessels"," tie the water-skins"," close the doors"," and extinguish the lamps"," for indeed the Shayṭān does not untie a water-skin"," nor uncover a vessel"," nor open a door.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and others from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 2012.]"""
"1212","(1213) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us — Abū Bishr al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us — Khālid ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us from Suhayl from his father from Abī Hurayrah who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded us to cover the water used for wuḍūʾ"," to tie the water-skins"," and to invert the vessels.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Narrated by Ibn Mājah"," 3411.]"""
"1213","(1214) Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-ʿAṭṭār informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us — Abū Usāmah narrated to us — from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb al-Quraẓī from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī who said: \It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," should we perform wuḍūʾ from the well of Buḍāʿah?' — and it is a well into which filth"," carcasses"," menstrual cloths"," and dogs are thrown.\"" He said: \""Water is pure"," and nothing renders it impure.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 66.]"""
"1214","(1215) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Abī Shuʿayb and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥarrānī both said: Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Salīṭ ibn Ayyūb from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ al-Anṣārī, then al-ʿAdawī, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — and it was said to him: 'Water is drawn for you from the well of Buḍāʿah"," and into it are thrown the flesh of dogs"," menstrual cloths"," and the refuse of people.'\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," water is pure"," and nothing renders it impure.\""\n\nThus both narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Salamah from Ibn Isḥāq. And it is said that Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated in this chain from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ al-Anṣārī. And Yaḥyī ibn Wāḍiḥ said from Ibn Isḥāq from Salīṭ from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Rāfiʿ"," as Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb said. And Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd"," Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī"," and Yūnus ibn Bukayr said from Ibn Isḥāq from Salīṭ from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ. And it is said from Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd from Ibn Isḥāq from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Salamah from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Rāfiʿ. And it is said from Salīṭ from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī from his father. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain.]"""
"1215","(1216) Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed him — Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muslim narrated to us from Muṭarrif from Khālid ibn Abī Nawf from Salīṭ from Ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī from his father who said: \I came upon the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was performing wuḍūʾ from Buḍāʿah. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," you perform wuḍūʾ from it"," while into it is thrown that which is thrown of filth?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed"," water is not rendered impure by anything.'\""\n\nAnd thus al-Ḥumaydī narrated it from Bishr ibn al-Sarī and others from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muslim al-Qasmalī. And Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated it from one whom he does not suspect"," from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ al-ʿAdawī from Abī Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain.]"""
"1216","(1217) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn informed him, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed you from one whom he does not suspect, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-ʿAdawī — and Muḥammad said: ʿUbaydullāh — from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī that he said: \It was said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): 'You perform wuḍūʾ from the well of Buḍāʿah"," and into it are thrown that by which people relieve themselves"," the flesh of dogs"," and menstrual cloths.'\""\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," water is not rendered impure by anything.\""\n\nAnd this wording has been narrated through another chain from Abī Saʿīd"," raised (marfūʿ). [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain.]"""
"1217","(1218) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Qays, i.e., Ibn al-Rabīʿ, narrated to us from Ṭarīf from Abī Naḍrah from Abī Saʿīd who said: \We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and we came upon a pool in which there was a carcass. Some of the people performed wuḍūʾ and some of the people held back until the Prophet (ﷺ) came. The Prophet (ﷺ) came among the last of the people and said: 'Perform wuḍūʾ and drink"," for indeed water is not rendered impure by anything.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī"," 1317.]"""
"1218","(1219) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl informed us — Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us — Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Dūlabī narrated to us — Sharīk narrated to us from Ṭarīf from Abī Naḍrah from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, and he mentioned its meaning and said, from the Prophet (ﷺ): \Indeed"," water is not rendered impure by anything.\"" He said: \""So we drew water and gave drink.\""\n\nAbū Jaʿfar al-Dūlabī said: \""Ṭarīf is Abū Sufyān.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""He is not strong (qawī)"," except that I have cited it as a witness for what preceded.\""\n\nAnd it is said that Sharīk narrated with this chain from Jābir"," and it is said from him from Jābir or Abī Saʿīd with doubt"," and Abū Saʿīd is apparently more correct.\n\nAnd another story has been narrated from Abī Saʿīd with the same meaning"," if its narrator preserved it. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain.]"""
"1219","(1220) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣighghī informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us — Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, the freedman of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, narrated to us from his father from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about the pools between Makkah and Madīnah, and they said: \Wild beasts"," dogs"," and donkeys come to them.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""What is in their bellies is theirs"," and what remains is for us"," pure.\""\n\nThus Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Ibn Wahb from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from his father from ʿAṭāʾ from Abī Hurayrah.\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd is weak (ḍaʿīf)"," and the like of him is not used as a proof.\n\nAnd it has been narrated through another chain from Ibn ʿUmar"," raised (marfūʿ)"," but it is not well-known (mashhūr). [Very weak (ḍaʿīf jiddan). Narrated by Ibn Mājah"," 519.]"""
"1220","(1221) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn Baḥr ibn Barrī al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us — Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us from his mother who said: \I entered upon Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī among some women"," and he said: 'If I were to give you to drink from Buḍāʿah"," you would dislike that. And by Allah"," I gave the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to drink from it with my own hand.'\""\n\nAnd this is a good (ḥasan)"," connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā"," 7519.]"""
"1221","(1222) Abū Saʿīd — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Isfarāʾinī — informed us. Abū Baḥr al-Barbahārī narrated to us. Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us. Al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us. Sufyān narrated to us. ʿAmr narrated from ʿIkrimah that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the pond of Majannah. It was said to him: \O Commander of the Faithful"," a dog has just lapped from it.\"" He said: \""The dog drinks with its tongue.\"" Then he drank from it and performed wuḍūʾ.\n\nIt is narrated from Ayyūb from ʿIkrimah in this story that he said: \""That which the dog lapped has gone\"" — meaning the dogs carried it away in their bellies.\n\nThis is a well-known narration from ʿUmar"," even though it is mursal. We have narrated something to its meaning from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥāṭib from ʿUmar. [Weak. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 249]"""
"1222","(1223) Abū Saʿīd al-Isfarāʾinī informed us. Abū Baḥr informed us. Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us. Al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us. Sufyān narrated to us. Manbūdh narrated from his mother, who said: \We used to travel with Maymūnah. She would pass by a pool containing camel dung and beetles"," and she would drink from it or perform wuḍūʾ with it.\"" Sufyān said: \""There is no doubt about this — she intended to drink if she wished"," or to perform wuḍūʾ if she wished.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1510]"""
"1223","(1224) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us. ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us. Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm al-Bazzāz narrated to us. Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah narrated to us. Hushaym narrated from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, who said: I heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib say: \Water is entirely pure; nothing renders it impure.\""\n\nIbn ʿUlayyah added from Dāwūd from Saʿīd: \""We asked him about pools in which dogs lap.\"" He said: \""Water has been sent down as pure; nothing renders it impure.\"" [Sound. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/29]"""
"1224","(1225) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us. Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us. Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us. Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us. Al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us. Abū ʿAmr narrated to us. Al-Zuhrī said regarding a pool into which an animal falls and dies: \The water is pure"," so long as it is not so little that the carcass changes its taste or its smell.\"" [Fair]"""
"1225","(1226) Abū Ṭāhir — Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh — informed us. Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān — informed us. Abū al-Azhar narrated to us. Marwān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us. Rashīd ibn Saʿd narrated to us. Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Rāshid ibn Saʿd from Abī Umāmah al-Bāhilī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Water is not rendered impure by anything"," except that which overcomes its taste or its smell.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Mājah"," 521]"""
"1226","(1227) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us. Jaʿfar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us. Abū al-Azhar narrated to us, mentioning it with its chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When the water amounts to two qullahs"," nothing renders it impure except that which overcomes its smell or its taste.\"" Thus I found it"," and the wording of 'two qullahs' in it is unusual (gharīb). [Weak]"""
"1227","(1228) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us. Abū al-Walīd narrated to us. Al-Shāmātī narrated to us. ʬīyyah ibn Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd narrated to us. My father narrated from Thawr ibn Yazīd from Rāshid ibn Saʿd from Abī Umāmah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Water is pure"," unless its smell"," its taste"," or its colour changes due to an impurity that occurs in it.\"" [Weak]"""
"1228","(1229) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Abū al-Ḥasan — Aḥmad ibn ʿUmayr ibn Yūsuf al-Dimashqī — narrated to us in Damascus. Abū Umayyah — that is, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us. Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us. Thawr ibn Yazīd narrated from Rāshid ibn Saʿd from Abī Umāmah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Water does not become impure unless its smell or its taste changes.\""\n\nʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated it from al-Aḥwaṣ ibn Ḥakīm from Rāshid ibn Saʿd from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) as a mursal narration. And Abū Usāmah narrated it from al-Aḥwaṣ from Abī ʿAwn and Rāshid ibn Saʿd as their own statement. The ḥadīth is not strong.\n\nHowever"," we do not know of any disagreement regarding the impurity of water when it is changed by an impurity. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"1229","(1230) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us. Al-Rabīʿ narrated to us. Al-Shāfiʿī said: \What I have stated — that when the taste"," smell"," or colour of water changes"," it becomes impure — is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) through a chain that the scholars of ḥadīth do not consider established. It is the position of the majority"," and I know of no disagreement among them regarding it.\"""""
"1230","(1231) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū Ṣādiq — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-ʿAṭṭār — informed us. They said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us. Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us. Abū Usāmah narrated to us from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar — that is, ibn al-Zubayr — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about water and what comes upon it from wild beasts and animals. He said: \When the water amounts to two qullahs"," it does not carry impurity (i.e."," it does not become impure).\""\n\nThus narrated Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī and a group from Abū Usāmah. [Sound. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 63]"""
"1231","(1232) Abū Saʿīd — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Isfarāʾinī — informed us that Abū Baḥr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Kawthar — informed us that Bishr ibn Mūsā — narrated to us that al-Ḥumaydī — narrated to us that Abū Usāma — Ḥammād ibn Usāma — narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Kathīr — narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād ibn Jaʿfar al-Makhzūmī — from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar — from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the water reaches the measure of two qullahs"," it does not carry impurity.\""\n\nAnd likewise"," Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Karāma and a group narrated it from Abū Usāma.\n\nAnd Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us"," saying: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Dāraquṭnī"," the Ḥāfiẓ"," said regarding these two narrations: \""Since there was a discrepancy regarding Abū Usāma in its isnād"," we wished to ascertain which version was correct. We examined the matter and found that Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated it from Abū Usāma from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr in both forms. Thus"," both statements from Abū Usāma are confirmed as authentic"," and it is confirmed that al-Walīd ibn Kathīr narrated it from both of them. Abū Usāma would sometimes narrate it from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr"," and at other times he would narrate it from al-Walīd from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād ibn Jaʿfar. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1232","(1233) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿdān al-Ṣaydalānī in Wāsiṭ — narrated to us that Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb — narrated to us that Abū Usāma — from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr — from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr — from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar — from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about water and what frequents it from wild beasts and animals. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the water reaches the measure of two qullahs"," it does not carry impurity.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1233","(1234) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Abū Bakr both said: ʿAlī informed us that Ibn Saʿdān narrated to us that Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that Abū Usāma narrated to us from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād ibn Jaʿfar from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar from his father, from the Prophet (ﷺ), a similar narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1234","(1235) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāʾinī, from the original of his book — and I asked him — narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Mubashshir al-Wāsiṭī — narrated to us that Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb — narrated to us that Abū Usāma — narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Kathīr — narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād ibn Jaʿfar — from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar — from his father, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about water","\"" and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nAnd it has been narrated in one of the two narrations from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shayba from Abū Usāma"," just as al-ʿĀmirī narrated it"," and in the other"," just as al-Ḥumaydī narrated it. And in one of the two narrations from Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī from Abū Usāma"," just as al-ʿĀmirī narrated it"," and in the other"," just as al-Ḥumaydī narrated it. And in all of that there is evidence for the authenticity of both narrations.\n\nAs for the first narration from ʿUthmān: [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1235","(1236) So Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutayba narrated to us that Abū Bakr and ʿUthmān, the two sons of Abī Shayba, narrated to us that Abū Usāma narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Kathīr narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr… and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd as for the other narration from him: [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1236","(1237) So Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsa narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shayba narrated to us that Abū Usāma narrated to us from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād ibn Jaʿfar.\n\nAnd as for the first narration from Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd: [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it, no. 63]"
"1237","(1238) So Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us that Abū Usāma narrated to us from al-Walīd from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr… and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd as for the other narration: [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1238","(1239) So Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us that Abū Usāma narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Kathīr narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād ibn Jaʿfar… and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it, 1/18]"
"1239","(1240) And Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar. Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb narrated to us that Jarīr narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"
"1240","(1241) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) when he was asked about water that is in the open desert and what frequents it from animals and wild beasts. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When the water reaches the measure of two qullahs"," it does not carry impurity.'\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ. And likewise"," Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd al-Zuhrī"," Zāʾida ibn Qudāma"," and a group narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," no. 22411]"""
"1241","(1242) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Rajāʾ al-Adīb informed us from the original of his hearing: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed us by dictation: Abū al-Qāsim ibn al-Ṣaqr narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĀʾishah narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about water that is in the open desert and to which wild beasts and dogs come. He said: \When the water amounts to two qullahs"," it does not carry impurity.\""\n\nHe said: \""Dogs and wild beasts\"" — and it is gharīb (uncommon).\n\nAnd Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl similarly reported it from Ḥammād ibn Salamah. And Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh reported from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq: \""Dogs and beasts of burden.\"" However"," Ibn ʿAyyāsh was differed over regarding his isnād.\n\nAnd Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated this ḥadīth from ʿĀṣim ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from his father from the Prophet ﷺ"," and in it there is strength for the narration of Ibn Isḥāq. [Ṣaḥīgh in other than this chain]"""
"1242","(1243) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed him: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar who said: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the water amounts to two qullahs"," it does not become impure.\""\n\nAnd similarly Bishr ibn al-Sarī"," Yaʿqūb al-Ḥaḍramī"," al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Makkī"," ʿAffān ibn Muslim"," and Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī reported it from Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 65]"""
"1243","(1244) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh and Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh both said: Al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj and Hudbah ibn Khālid both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from ʿĀṣim ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr who said: I entered a garden with ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar in which there was a water trough made from the skin of a dead camel. He performed wuḍūʾ from it, so I said: \Will you perform wuḍūʾ from it when it contains the skin of a dead camel?\"" He narrated to me from his father from the Prophet ﷺ who said: \""When the water reaches the measure of two qullahs or three"," nothing renders it impure.\"" Thus they both said: \""Or three.\""\n\nAnd Yazīd ibn Hārūn and Kāmil ibn Ṭalḥah similarly reported it. The narration of the group who did not express doubt is more preferable. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 1/227]"""
"1244","(1245) Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Jābir narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr al-Miṣṣīṣī narrated from Zāʾidah from Layth from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet ﷺ who said: \When the water amounts to two qullahs"," nothing renders it impure.\""\n\nʿAlī said: This shaykh raised it from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr from Zāʾidah. And Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr reported it from Zāʾidah as mawqūf (stopped at the Companion's statement)"," and that is correct. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"1245","(1246) Aḥmad informed us: ʿAlī said: Al-Qāḍī al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to it to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: Zāʾidah narrated to us from Layth from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿUmar, the same as it, as mawqūf. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"1246","(1247) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Rāzī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAlī Zāhir ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad informed us: Abū Bakr ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to me: Abū Ḥumayd al-Miṣṣīṣī narrated to us: Ḥajjāj narrated: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Lūṭ informed me from Abū Isḥāq from Mujāhid that Ibn ʿAbbās said: \When the water amounts to two qullahs or more"," nothing renders it impure.\""\n\nAnd Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh reported it from Abān from Abī Yaḥyā from Ibn ʿAbbās"," likewise as mawqūf. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1247","(1248) As for the ḥadīth: Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl al-Ṣūfī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Suwayd, meaning Ibn Saʿīd, narrated to us: Al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the water reaches forty qullahs"," it does not carry impurity.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth is one in which al-Qāsim al-ʿUmarī is alone (tafarrada bihi)"," and thus he made an error in it. He was weak in ḥadīth; Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," al-Bukhārī"," and others among the ḥuffāẓ criticized him.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: I heard Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ say: The ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jābir from the Prophet ﷺ — \""When the water reaches forty qullahs\"" — is an error. The correct version is from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr"," as his own statement (qawlihi). Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh said to me"," from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ"," who said: Al-Qāsim was mistaken in it"," and he was weak and prone to many errors. [Bāṭil. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it"," 1/26]"""
"1248","(1249) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Al-Thawrī and Maʿmar informed us from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ who said: \When the water amounts to forty qullahs"," nothing renders it impure.\""\n\nAnd Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim similarly reported it from Ibn al-Munkadir. And Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī reported it from Ibn al-Munkadir as his own statement"," not going beyond that.\n\nAnd Ibn Lahīʿah reported from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from Sulaymān ibn Sinān from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Hurayrah from his father who said: \""When the water amounts to forty qullahs"," it does not carry impurity.\"" More than one narrator opposed him and reported it from Abī Hurayrah"," saying: \""Forty ghurub (large buckets)","\"" and among them were those who said: \""Forty dalw (buckets).\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith said to me"," from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī reported it from ʿAmr ibn Khālid from Ibn Lahīʿah from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth from Abī Hurayrah who said: \""Forty buckets of water — nothing renders it impure"," even if a junub (person in a state of major ritual impurity) bathes in it and another follows.\"" And this is more preferable.\n\nAnd Ibn Lahīʿah is not a valid authority (ghayru muḥtajj bihi).\n\nAnd the statement of the Companion whose statement agrees with the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the two qullahs is more deserving of being followed. And with Allah is the granting of success. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it"," 1/27]"""
"1249","(1250) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: Al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Muslim ibn Khālid informed us from Ibn Jurayj with an isnād the mention of me of which is not present before me, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the water amounts to two qullahs"," it does not carry impurity.\""\n\nAnd he said in the ḥadīth: \""In the qullahs of al-Ḥijr.\""\n\nIbn Jurayj said: \""And I have seen the qullahs of al-Ḥijr"," and one qullah holds two qirbahs or two qirbahs and a bit more.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""Muslim used to hold that that is less than half a qirbah or half a qirbah"," and he would say: 'Five qirbahs is the most that two qullahs can hold"," and the two qullahs may be less than five qirbahs.'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""So the precautionary approach is that one qullah be two and a half qirbahs. When the water amounts to five qirbahs"," it does not carry impurity in a jar or otherwise"," unless there appears in the water from it a smell"," taste"," or color.\"" He said: \""And the qirbahs of the Ḥijāz are large"," so the water that does not carry impurity is only by large qirbahs.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it"," 799]"""
"1250","(1251) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Rāzī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAlī Zāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us: Abū Bakr ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Abū Ḥumayd al-Miṣṣīṣī informed us: Ḥajjāj narrated: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Muḥammad informed me that Yaḥyā ibn ʿUqayl informed him that Yaḥyā ibn Yaʿmar informed him that the Prophet ﷺ said: \When the water amounts to two qullahs"," it does not carry impurity or any harm.\"" He said: \""So I said to Yaḥyā ibn ʿUqayl: 'The qullahs of al-Ḥijr?' He said: 'The qullahs of al-Ḥijr.'\"" He said: \""I think that each qullah holds two faraqs.\"" Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī added in his narration: \""And a faraq is sixteen raṭls.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it"," 1/24]"""
"1251","(1252) Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar al-Sijistānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf, meaning Abū Ḥumah, narrated to us: Abū Qurrrah, meaning Mūsā ibn Ṭāriq, narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Muḥammad informed me, and he mentioned it.\n\nMuḥammad said: I said to Yaḥyā ibn ʿUqayl: \Which qilāl (large jars)?\"" He said: \""The qilāl of Hajar.\"" Muḥammad said: \""I saw the qilāl of Hajar"," and I reckon that each qullah holds approximately two qirbāt (water-skins).\""\n\nThus it is in the book of my shaykh: \""two qirbāt\"" — and this is closer to accuracy than what Muslim ibn Khālid said. The first chain of narration is better preserved"," and Allāh knows best.\n\nAbū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ said: This Muḥammad from whom Ibn Jurayj narrated is Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā"," who narrates from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr and Yaḥyā ibn ʿUqayl. [Weak]"""
"1252","(1253) Abū al-Fatḥ al-Sharīf informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shurayḥī narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us: Sharīk narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī from Mujāhid, who said: \When water amounts to two qullahs"," nothing renders it impure.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""I asked: 'What are the two qullahs?' He said: 'Two large jars (jarratayn).'\"" [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1531]"""
"1253","(1254) Abū Ḥāẓim informed us: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Māsarjisī informed us: Isḥāq, meaning Ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī, informed us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rizmah narrated from Ḥammād ibn Zayd from ʿĀṣim ibn al-Mundhir, who said: \Al-qilāl are the large storage jars (al-khawābī al-ʿiẓām).\"" [Sound]"""
"1254","(1255) Abū Ḥāẓim informed us: Abū Aḥmad informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm, meaning Ibn Sulaymān, said: \We asked Ibn Isḥāq"," meaning Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār"," about the two qullahs"," and he said: 'These are the large jars (al-jirār) in which water is drawn and in which dough is kneaded.'\"" [Sound]"""
"1255","(1256) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Wakīl narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah said: I heard Hushaym say: \Al-qultayn (two qullahs) — meaning two large jars (al-jarratayn al-kibār).\"" [Sound. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/19]"""
"1256","(1257) Abū Ḥāẓim informed us: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ḥasanī said: Wakīʿ said: \By al-qullah is meant al-jarrah (a large jar).\"" [Sound]"""
"1257","(1258) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ said: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam said: \Al-qullah is al-jarrah (a large jar).\"" [Sound]"""
"1258","(1259) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Bakr Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, meaning Ibn ʿAṭāʾ al-Khaffāf, informed us: Saʿīd, meaning Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, narrated from Qatādah from Anas ibn Mālik from Mālik ibn Ṣaʿṣaʿah from the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned the ḥadīth of the Miʿrāj, in which it is stated: \Then I was raised to Sidrat al-Muntahā.\"" The Prophet of Allāh ﷺ related: \""Its leaves are like the ears of elephants"," and its fruits are like the qilāl (large jars) of Hajar.\""\n\nExtracted in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī ʿArūbah. [Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 3674]"""
"1259","(1260) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī said: \As for the ḥadīth of the well of Buḍāʿah"," the well of Buḍāʿah contained abundant water and was wide. Impure things were thrown into it that did not alter its colour"," taste"," or produce any discernible odour in it. It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Do you perform wuḍūʾ from the well of Buḍāʿah while such things are thrown into it?' The Prophet ﷺ replied: 'Water is not rendered impure by anything.' This makes clear that in the case of such water"," his ruling applied to it as he responded concerning it.\"" [Sound]"""
"1260","(1261) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd said: \I asked the caretaker (qayyim) of the well of Buḍāʿah about its depth"," and he said: 'At its fullest"," the water reaches the navel.' I asked: 'And when it is at its lowest?' He said: 'Above the private parts.'\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: \""I measured the well of Buḍāʿah with my cloak — I spread it over it and then measured it — and its width was six cubits. I asked the one who opened the gate of the garden for me and led me to it: 'Has its structure been altered from what it was?' He said: 'No.' And I saw in it water whose colour had changed.\"" [Sound]"""
"1261","(1262) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn that a Zanjī fell into Zamzam — meaning he died therein. Ibn ʿAbbās ordered that he be extracted, and he ordered that the well be emptied. He said: A spring overpowered them, gushing forth from the Rukn. He ordered that it be blocked with pieces of cloth (qaṭāfī) and coarse fabric (maṭārif) until they emptied it. When they had emptied it, it burst forth upon them.\n\nIbn Abī ʿArūbah narrated it from Qatādah: that a Zanjī fell into Zamzam, and Ibn ʿAbbābās ordered them to empty it. This is a balāgh (report) that reached both of them. (C) However, neither of them met Ibn ʿAbbās nor heard from him.\n\nJābir al-Juʿfī narrated it once from Abū al-Ṭufayl from Ibn ʿAbbās, and once from Abū al-Ṭufayl himself: that a slave boy fell into Zamzam and it was emptied. (C) And Jābir al-Juʿfī is not a valid authority (lā yuḥtājj bihi).\n\nIbn Lahīʿah narrated it from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār. (C) And Ibn Lahīʿah is not a valid authority.\n\nAl-Zaʿfarānī said: Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Shāfiʿī said: We do not know this from Ibn ʿAbbās, and Zamzam, in our view — we have not heard of this.\n\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/33]"
"1262","(1263) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Shirawayh narrated to us; he said: I heard Abū Qudāmah say:\n\nI heard Sufyān — meaning Ibn ʿUyaynah — say: I have been in Makkah for seventy years and have not seen anyone, young or old, who knows the hadith of the Zanjī who they say fell into Zamzam. I have not heard anyone say that Zamzam was emptied.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: And likewise it should not be done, because the established reports (āthār) concerning its description state that it is not to be emptied and is not to be disparaged. I do not know whether Abū Qudāmah related this from Abū ʿUbayd or from Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh.\n\nAl-Zaʿfarānī said: Al-Shāfiʿī said to his opponents: You have narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \Water is not rendered impure by anything.\"" Do you think that Ibn ʿAbbās would narrate a report from the Prophet ﷺ and then abandon it"," if this narration of his is authentic? And you narrate from him that he performed wuḍūʾ from a pool in which a corpse had been immersed"," and you narrate from him: \""Water does not become impure.\"" If any of this is authentic"," it indicates that he did not empty Zamzam due to impurity"," but rather for cleansing — if he did so at all. And Zamzam is for drinking"," and blood may have appeared on the surface of the water so that it was visible in it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1263","(1264) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Prophet ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ with water, and it was said to him: \So-and-so bathed in it\"" — meaning one of his wives. He said: \""Indeed"," water is not rendered impure by anything.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 396]"""
"1264","(1265) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī, Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl, and ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar said: Musaddad narrated to us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us; Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ bathed in a vessel, and the Prophet ﷺ came to perform wuḍūʾ or to bathe. She said: \O Messenger of Allāh"," I was in a state of janābah.\"" The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \""Water does not become impure (junub).\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"1265","(1266) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us; Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash from Yaḥyā ibn ʿUbayd, who said: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about the water of the ḥammām (public bath), and he said: \Water does not become impure.\""\n\n[Weak. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1150]"""
"1266","(1267) Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Isfarāʾinī informed us; Abū Baḥr al-Barbarhārī informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Zakariyyā narrated from al-Shaʿbī from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Four things do not become impure: the human being, water, clothing, and the earth.\n\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 1/113]"
"1267","(1268) Abū Yaḥyā al-Ḥimmānī said regarding this hadith: \Four things do not become impure (junub).\"" Abū Ḥāzim narrated it to us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭawābīqī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Abū Yaḥyā al-Ḥimmānī narrated it… and he mentioned it.\n\n[Weak]"""
"1268","(1269) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Yazīd al-Rishk from Muʿādhah from ʿĀʾishah that she said: \Water is not subject to janābah.\""\n\nAl-Zaʿfarānī said: Al-Shāfiʿī said: And we narrate from Zayd ibn Thābit our position"," and we narrate from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad that he ordered a man to bathe in a well from janābah"," and something similar is narrated from ʿUmar.\n\nAs for the report which… [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1269","(1270) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī said, narrating from Khālid al-Wāsiṭī from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Abū al-Bakhtarī from ʿAlī, regarding a rat that falls into a well and dies: \It should be emptied until it overwhelms them.\""\n\nThis is not strong"," because Abū al-Bakhtarī did not hear from ʿAlī; thus it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\nAl-Zaʿfarānī said: Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Shāfiʿī said: Ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālliib"," may Allāh be pleased with him"," said: \""When a rat falls into a well and dies in it"," one or two buckets should be drawn from it; but if it has decomposed"," five or seven buckets should be drawn.\"" This too is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\n[Weak. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1711]"""
"1270","(1271) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī said, in the argumentation of those who cite the report from ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās: \So the report that comes from the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ is to be opposed by the statement of someone else?\"" He said: \""No.\"" I said: \""You have done so"," and despite that you have opposed ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās. You claimed that ʿAlī said: 'When a rat falls into a well"," five or seven buckets should be drawn from it","' and you claimed that it is not purified except by twenty or thirty"," and you claimed that Ibn ʿAbbās emptied Zamzam because of a Zanjī who fell into it"," and you say that forty or sixty buckets suffice for that. And this from ʿAlī and from Ibn ʿAbbās is not established (ghayr thābit).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1271","(1272) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Baghdādī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Khālid narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to us; Abū al-Aswad narrated from ʿUrwah, regarding the incident of Uḥud and what befell the Prophet ﷺ on his face. He said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib went to the well (al-Mihrās) and brought water in a shield. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to drink from it, but he found it to have an odour. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \This is stagnant (ājin) water.\"" He rinsed his mouth with it"," and Fāṭimah washed the blood from her father's face. [Weak]"""
"1272","(1273) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: One whom I do not suspect narrated to me from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the mouth of the ravine, ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib went out and filled his leather shield from the well (al-Mihrās), then brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he might drink from it. He found it to have an odour and so found it unpalatable; he did not drink from it. He washed the blood from his face and poured water over his head, saying: \The wrath of Allah is severe upon the one who has bloodied the face of His Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nThus Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq.\n\nIsḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī narrated it from Wahb ibn Jarīr"," from his father"," from Ibn Isḥāq"," from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Zubayr"," from ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Zubayr"," from his father. And this is a connected (mawṣūl) chain of narration. [Hasan through other routes. Ibn Ḥibbān narrated it (6979)]"""
"1273","(1274) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʤd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us. And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed you, from Abū al-Naḍr, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, from ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar, from Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he performed masḥ (wiping) over the leather socks (khuffayn). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (199)]"
"1274","(1275) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs ibn Salamah al-ʿAnazī informed me; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ and Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf both said that ʿAbdillāh ibn Wahb narrated to them from ʿAmr, and he mentioned it with its chain of narration similar to it, and added: ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar asked ʿUmar about that, and he said: \Yes"," when Saʿd narrates to you anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," do not ask anyone else.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aṣbagh ibn al-Faraj from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1275","(1276) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Asad narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Mukhtār narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah; Abū al-Naḍr informed me, from Abū Salamah, from Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, a hadith he attributed to the Prophet ﷺ regarding wuḍūʾ over the leather socks: that there is no harm in performing wuḍūʾ over the leather socks.\n\nAnd Abū Salamah narrated that ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar was informed of that by Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, and that ʿUmar said to ʿAbdillāh, as if reproaching him: \Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated a hadith to you and you did not act upon it? When Saʿd narrates to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," do not seek any hadith besides his hadith.\"" Al-Bukhārī mentioned its chain of narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it (1/14)]"""
"1276","(1277) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām, who said: Jarīr urinated, then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his leather socks. It was said to him: \Do you do this?\"" He said: \""Yes"," I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate"," then perform wuḍūʾ and wipe over his leather socks.\""\n\nAl-Aʿmash said: Ibrāhīm said: \""This hadith pleased them because Jarīr's Islam came after the revelation of al-Māʾidah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others"," from Abī Muʿāwiyah; and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Ādam"," from Shuʿbah"," from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (380)]"""
"1277","(1278) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us; ʿAbdillāh ibn Dāwūd narrated from Bukayr ibn ʿĀmir, from Abū Zurʿah ibn ʿAmr ibn Jarīr, that Jarīr urinated, then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over the leather socks, and said: \What prevents me from wiping when I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe?\"" They said: \""That was only before the revelation of al-Māʾidah.\"" He said: \""I did not accept Islam except after the revelation of al-Māʾidah.\"" [Hasan through other routes. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (154)]"""
"1278","(1279) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us; ʿAbdillāh ibn Dāwūd narrated from Bukayr ibn ʿĀmir, from Abū Zurʿah ibn ʿAmr ibn Jarīr, that Jarīr urinated, then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over the leather socks, and said: \What prevents me from wiping when I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe?\"" They said: \""That was only before the revelation of al-Māʾidah.\"" He said: \""I did not accept Islam except after the revelation of al-Māʾidah.\"" [Hasan through other routes. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (154)]"""
"1279","(1280) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ibn Milḥān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated. Ibn ʿUbayd said: And Ismāʿīl ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm, from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he went out to relieve himself, and al-Mughīrah followed him with a vessel containing water. He poured it over him when he had finished his need, and he performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his leather socks.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn Khālid, and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah, both from al-Layth ibn Saʿd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (200)]"
"1280","(1281) Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Bishr ibn Bakr narrated from al-Awzāʿī.\n\n(Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf al-Ṭāʾī said: And Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated.)\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm al-Ṣāʾigh in Marw informed me; Abū al-Muwajjih informed us; ʿAbdān informed us; ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us; al-Awzāʿī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Jaʿfar ibn ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī, from his father, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over his turban (ʿimāmah) and his leather socks.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Mubārak. In the hadith of the others: \""That he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over the leather socks and the turban.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān.\n\nLikewise"," Shaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," Ḥarb ibn Shaddād"," and Abān narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr regarding wiping over the leather socks. And Maʿmar narrated it from Yaḥyā"," from Abū Salamah"," from ʿAmr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (202)]"""
"1281","(1282) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī, who said: I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) performing masḥ over his khuffayn (leather socks).\n\nAl-Bukhārī has alluded to these narrations. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1282","(1283) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us; ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, who said: Bilāl narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wuḍūʾ and perform masḥ over the khuffayn and the turban (al-khimār).\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of ʿĪsā. And in the ḥadīth of ibn Numayr, with his isnād from Bilāl: The Prophet (ﷺ) performed wuḍūʾ and performed masḥ over the khuffayn and the ʿimāmah (turban).\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm.\n\nSimilarly, ʿAlī ibn Muṣhir and Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated it from al-Aʿmash, and ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād, Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī, and Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl followed them in that. Al-Thawrī narrated it from al-Aʿmash but did not mention Kaʿb in his isnād. Similarly, Shuʿbah narrated it from al-Ḥakam, among others, in a mursal form. Zāʾidah and ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq narrated it from al-Aʿmash and mentioned al-Barāʾ in it instead of Kaʿb. Those who established its isnād are trustworthy, and Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it as 275]"
"1283","(1284) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Mihrān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Qādim narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad, from ibn Buraydah — and he is Sulaymān ibn Buraydah — from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform wuḍūʾ, washing each part once, and perform masḥ over the khuffayn, and he prayed all the prayers with a single wuḍūʾ. ʿUmar said to him: You did something you did not use to do. He said: \I did it deliberately"," O ʿUmar.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it as 277]"""
"1284","(1285) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated from Sufyān; ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad narrated to us; from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed on the day of the Conquest (of Makkah) five prayers with a single wuḍūʾ and performed masḥ over his khuffayn. ʿUmar said to him: I saw you do something you did not use to do. He said: \I did it deliberately.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1285","(1286) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Bukayr ibn ʿĀmir narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Nuʿm; al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated to me: He travelled with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered a valley, relieved himself, then came out, performed wuḍūʾ, and performed masḥ over his khuffayn. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you forgot — you did not remove the khuffayn.\n\nHe said: \No"," rather you forgot. My Lord"," the Mighty and Majestic"," commanded me with this.\""\n\nWe have narrated the permissibility of performing masḥ over the khuffayn from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās"," Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān"," Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī"," Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī"," ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir"," Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," Anas ibn Mālik"," Sahl ibn Saʿd"," Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī"," al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah"," al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib"," Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," Jābir ibn Samurah"," Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Juzʾ"," and Abū Zayd al-Anṣārī — may Allah be pleased with them all. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it as 156]"""
"1286","(1287) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Jarrāḥī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Shāsawayh narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Sukkari narrated to us; Wahb ibn Zamʿah informed us; ʿAlī al-Bāshānī informed us. He said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak said: There is no disagreement among us regarding masḥ over the khuffayn. A man asks me about masḥ, and I suspect him of being a follower of whims.\n\nIt has reached me from Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir that he said after this account: Everyone from whom it is narrated among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he disliked masḥ over the khuffayn, it has also been narrated from him otherwise.\n\nThe Shaykh said: What has reached us of the dislike of that is from ʿAlī, ʿĀʾishah, and ibn ʿAbbās.\n\nAs for the narration from ʿAlī that he said: \The Book (of Allah) has overtaken masḥ over the khuffayn\"" — this has not from him with a connected isnād that is established.\n\nAs for ʿĀʾishah"," she disliked it"," then it was established from her that she referred the knowledge of that to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and ʿAlī reported the concession (rukhṣah) regarding it from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Nuʿaym narrated it in al-Ḥilyah]"""
"1287","(1288) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and the Qāḍī Abū al-Haytham ʿUtbah ibn Khaythamah — with the authenticity of that — informed us. They said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿUṭāridī narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah al-Ḍarīr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah, from al-Qāsim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Sharīḥ ibn Hānīʾ, who said: I asked ʿĀʾishah about masḥ over the khuffayn. She said: \Go to ʿAlī"," for he is more knowledgeable about that than I am.\"" So I went to ʿAlī and asked him about masḥ. He said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to command us that the resident performs masḥ for one day and one night"," and the traveller for three days and nights.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Abū Muʿāwiyah.\n\nAnd Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah said: al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah narrated to us"," and he mentioned this isnād"," and said: ʿĀʾishah said: \""I have no knowledge of this"," but go to a man and ask him"," for he is more knowledgeable.\"" I said: \""Who is he?\"" She said: \""ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib — go to him and ask him.\""\n\nThen he mentioned something similar to it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it as 276]"""
"1288","(1289) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhab narrated to us in Wāsiṭ; Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated from Sharīk, from al-Miqdām ibn Sharīḥ, from his father, who said: I asked ʿĀʾishah about masḥ over the khuffayn. She said: \Go to ʿAlī"," for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" So I went to him and asked him. He said: \""When we travelled with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," he used to command us to perform masḥ over our khuff (leather socks).\""\n\nAs for ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him)"," he only disliked it when the masḥ of the Prophet (ﷺ) over the khuffayn had not been established for him after the revelation of al-Māʾidah. When it was established for him"," he returned to it. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than that]"""
"1289","(1290) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī in Baghdād — with the authenticity of that — informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Rammādī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; ibn Jurayj informed me; Khuṣayf informed me that Miqsam, the mawlā of ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith, informed him that ibn ʿAbbās informed him, who said: I was with ʿUmar when Saʿd and ibn ʿUmar asked him about masḥ over the khuffayn, and he ruled in favour of Saʿd. I said to Saʿd: \We know that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed masḥ over his khuffayn"," but was it before al-Māʾidah or after it? No one can inform you that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed masḥ after al-Māʾidah.\"" So ʿUmar fell silent. [Ḍaʿīf. Aḥmad narrated it as 1/366]"""
"1290","(1291) Abū Muḥammad informed us; Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Aḥmad narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from ibn ʿAbbās, who said: I was with ʿUmar when Saʿd and ibn ʿUmar disputed before him regarding masḥ over the khuffayn, and he ruled in favour of Saʿd. I said: \If you were to say this regarding a long journey and severe cold…\""\n\nThis is a concession from him for masḥ during a long journey and severe cold"," after he had been disliking it absolutely.\n\nIt has also been narrated from him that he issued a fatwā permitting it for both the resident and the traveller alike."""
"1291","(1292) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī al-Bayhaqī informed us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ghiṭrīf informed us in Jurjān: Abū Khalīfah narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, who said: I heard Mūsá ibn Salamah say: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about wiping over the two khuffs (leather socks). He said: \For the traveller"," three days and their nights"," and for the resident"," one day and one night.\"" And this is a sound (ṣaḥīḥ) chain of narration. [Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1911]"""
"1292","(1293) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Ibn Fuḍayl narrated from Fiṭr ibn Khalīfah, who said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ: \O Abū Muḥammad"," indeed ʿIkrimah used to say: Ibn ʿAbbās used to say: 'The Book (i.e."," the Qurʾān) has superseded wiping over the two khuffs.'\"" He (ʿAṭāʾ) said: \""ʿIkrimah has lied. Ibn ʿAbbās used to say: 'Wipe over the two khuffs"," even if you have just come out of the lavatory.'\""\n\nAnd Wakīʿ and others narrated similarly from Fiṭr.\n\nAnd it is possible that Ibn ʿAbbāh said what ʿIkrimah narrated from him"," and then when it was established to him from the Prophet ﷺ that he wiped after the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah"," he said what ʿAṭāʾ reported. [Sound (ṣaḥīḥ). Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1951]"""
"1293","(1294) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Shaybān narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm from Hammām ibn al-Ḥārith: that Jarīr performed wuḍūʾ from a vessel and wiped over his two khuffs. They said: \Do you wipe over your two khuffs?\"" He said: \""Indeed"," I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the two khuffs.\""\n\nAnd this ḥadīth used to please the companions of ʿAbd Allāh"," meaning Ibn Masʿūd"," and they would say: \""Indeed"," Jarīr's acceptance of Islam was only after the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Sound (ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"1294","(1295) Abū al-Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿĪsá informed us: Baqiyyah narrated to me: Ibrāhīm ibn Adham narrated to me: Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān said: I stayed as a guest with Shahr ibn Ḥawshab. He performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his two khuffs. I said to him: \Do you wipe over your two khuffs?\"" He said: \""Jarīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh came to me as a guest. He performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his two khuffs. I said to him: 'Do you wipe over your two khuffs?' He said: 'Yes"," I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his two khuffs.'\"" He (Muqātil) said: I said: \""After the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah?\"" He said: \""I only accepted Islam after the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah.\""\n\nAbū Yaḥyá said: Ibrāhīm ibn Adham said: \""I have not heard any ḥadīth regarding wiping over the two khuffs better than this.\"" [Good (ḥasan) for its supporting chains]"""
"1295","(1296) And Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Fāmī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Abū Umayyah Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ṭarsūsī narrated to us: Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Adham from Muqātil from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab from Jarīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over his two khuffs.\"" They said: \""After the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah?\"" Jarīr said: \""I only accepted Islam after the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah.\"" [Good (ḥasan) for its supporting chains]"""
"1296","(1297) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us orally: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me: Ibn Shihāb narrated from ʿAbbād ibn Ziyād from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah from al-Mughīrah, who said: \We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. When we were partway along the route"," he fell behind"," and I fell behind with him carrying the water vessel. He went to relieve himself"," then came to me. I poured water over his hands and he performed wuḍūʾ. This was at the time of the Ṣubḥ prayer. When he had washed his face and wished to wash his forearms"," the sleeves of his jubbah became tight upon him — and he was wearing a Syrian jubbah — so he brought his hands out from beneath the jubbah"," washed his forearms"," then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his two khuffs.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥulwānī and Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Sound (ṣaḥīḥ). Narrated by Muslim"," 1274]"""
"1297","(1298) And Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Faqīh informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī narrated to us: Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah narrated from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah from his father, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve his need. I stood pouring water over him from a vessel during the expedition of Tabūk. He washed his face and went to wash his forearms"," but the sleeves of the jubbah became tight upon him"," so he brought them out from below and washed them"," then wiped over his two khuffs.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr from al-Layth from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Saʿd.\n\nAs for the case of the resident"," it is as follows: [Sound (ṣaḥīḥ). Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 2761]"""
"1298","(1299) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá informed us: Abū Khaythamah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Shaqīq from Ḥudhayfah, who said: \I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came to a dunghill of a people and urinated standing. Then he performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his two khuffs.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from al-Aʿmash. [Sound (ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"1299","(1300) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Tamtām narrated to me: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abī Wāʾil from Ḥudhayfah, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ came to a dunghill of a people in al-Madīnah and urinated standing. Then he called for water"," performed wuḍūʾ"," and wiped over his two khuffs.\"" [Sound (ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"1300","(1301) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥām al-Muzakkī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Qays narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Usāmah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the orchards (al-Aswāf) and went to relieve his need"," then he came out.\"" Usāmah said: \""I asked Bilāl: 'What did he do?' Bilāl said: 'The Prophet ﷺ went to relieve his need"," then performed wuḍūʾ. He washed his face and his hands"," wiped over his head"," and wiped over the two khuffs.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Al-Aswāf: a walled garden in al-Madīnah.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""In the ḥadīth of Bilāl there is evidence that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the two khuffs while resident"," because Bilāl understood it to refer to the resident state.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And the ḥadīth of ʿAlī and others regarding the time limit is evidence for the permissibility of wiping over the two khuffs while resident.\"" [Good (ḥasan). Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Awsaṭ"," 8831]"""
"1301","(1302) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Abū Yaʿfūr al-ʿAbdī that he saw Anas ibn Mālik in the house of ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth. He called for water and performed wuḍūʾ, and wiped over his khuffs (leather socks).\n\nAnd it has been narrated on the authority of ʿUmar, Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, and Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1302","(1303) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that al-Thawrī informed us that ʿAmr ibn Qays al-Mulāʾī narrated to us from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah from al-Qāsim ibn Mukhaymirah from Sharīḥ ibn Hānīʾ who said: I came to ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), and asked her about wiping over the khuffs. She said: \Go to Ibn Abī Ṭālib"," for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\"" He said: So I came to ʿAlī and asked him"," and he said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded us to wipe for three days when we were travelling"," and for one day and one night when we were resident.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1303","(1304) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Isḥāq informed us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it with a similar chain, except that he said: He said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) appointed three days and their nights for the traveller"," and one day and one night for the resident.\""\n\nAnd Sufyān"," whenever he mentioned ʿAmr"," would praise him.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1304","(1305) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us that Abū Muʿāwiyah al-Ḍarīr narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah from al-Qāsim ibn Mukhaymirah from Sharīḥ ibn Hānīʾ who said: I asked ʿĀʾishah about wiping over the khuffs. She said: \Ask ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," for he used to go on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\"" So I asked him and he said: \""We used to wipe"," during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," for three days and their nights for the traveller"," and one day and one night for the resident.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Abū Muʿāwiyah"," and he said in the hadith: She said: \""Go to ʿAlī"," for he knows more about that than I do.\"" So I went to ʿAlī and he mentioned it. He also narrated it from the hadith of Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1305","(1306) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār in Baghdād informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Mujashshir narrated to us that Hushaym narrated from Dāwūd ibn ʿAmr from Busr ibn ʿUbaydillāh al-Ḥaḍramī from Abī Idrīs al-Khawlānī who said: ʿAwf ibn Mālik al-Ashjaʿī narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded wiping over the khuffs during the expedition of Tabūk: three days and their nights for the traveller, and one day and one night for the resident. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad 6/27]"
"1306","(1307) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Hushaym ibn Bashīr narrated it with a similar chain.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: I asked Muḥammad, meaning al-Bukhārī, about this hadith and he said: \It is a ḥasan hadith.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1307","(1308) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to me that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked about wiping over the khuffs and he said: \For the traveller: three days and their nights; and for the resident: one day and one night.\"" And my father used to remove his khuffs and wash his feet. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than it. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah 192]"""
"1308","(1309) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbaydillāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdād narrated to us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Qurashī al-Kūfī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated it with the same wording.\n\nThis hadith was narrated by a group from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī from al-Muhājir Abī Makhlad, and Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated it from him from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ. Either the error is from him or from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, or ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated it on both accounts. The narration of the group is more likely to be the preserved one. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"1309","(1310) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Abī al-Najūd from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh who said: I came to Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl al-Murādī and he said: \What has brought you?\"" I said: \""I seek knowledge.\"" He said: \""The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge"," pleased with what he seeks.\"" I said: \""A matter has troubled my chest regarding wiping over the khuffs after relieving oneself and urinating"," and I was a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," so I came to you to ask whether you heard anything from him about that.\"" He said: \""Yes"," the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to command us"," when we were travellers or—he said—travelling"," not to remove our khuffs for three days and their nights"," except due to janābah (major ritual impurity)"," but not due to relieving oneself"," urinating"," or sleeping.\""\n\nMaʿmar narrated it from ʿĀṣim and added in it: \""The wiping of the resident.\"" Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: I asked Muḥammad"," meaning al-Bukhārī: \""Which hadith do you consider most authentic regarding the time limit for wiping over the khuffs?\"" He said: \""The hadith of Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl"," and the hadith of Abī Bakrah is ḥasan.\"" The Sheikh said: The hadith of Sharīḥ ibn Hānīʾ from ʿAlī is the most authentic narration reported in this chapter according to Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj (may Allah have mercy on him). [Ḥasan]"""
"1310","(1311) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Abū Usāmah narrated from Abū Rawq ʿAṭiyyah ibn al-Ḥārith al-Hamdānī who narrated to us that Abū al-Gharīf narrated from Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl al-Murādī who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent us on a military expedition, and he mentioned the hadith, and in it he said: \Let one of you wipe over his khuffs when he is a traveller for three days and their nights"," and when he is resident"," then one day and one night.\"" [Ḥasan in other than it]"""
"1311","(1312) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Saʿīd ibn Masrūq, from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn, from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī, from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: \For the traveller"," three days"," and for the resident"," one day.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 157.]"""
"1312","(1313) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan informed me, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Ādam narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from Nubātah, from ʿUmar, who said: \Wiping for the traveller is three days and their nights.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than his narration. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 794.]"""
"1313","(1314) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr informed us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from ʢĀṣim, from Abū ʿUthmān, from ʿUmar, that he said: \A man may wipe over his leather socks until the time of that day and its night.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1314","(1315) And with his chain of narration, he said: Sufyān narrated to me, Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd said: \Three days for the traveller and one day for the resident.\"" Al-Ḥārith said: \""I would not remove my leather socks until I came to my bed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1926.]"""
"1315","(1316) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Shaqīq, from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith ibn al-Muṣṭaliq, who said: \I went out with ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd to Madīnah"," and he did not remove his leather socks for three days"," wiping over them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1316","(1317) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, Abū Ghassān Mālik ibn Yaḥyā al-Sūsī narrated to us, Abū Badr Shujāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, Ziyād ibn Khaythamah narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Qāsim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Sharīḥ ibn Hāniʾ, who said: \I asked ʿĀʾishah about wiping over the leather socks"," and she said: 'Ask ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib.' So I asked him"," and he said: 'One day for the resident and three days for the traveller.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1317","(1318) Abū Naṣr ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Raffāʾ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Mūsā ibn Khalaf al-ʿAmmī narrated to us, my father narrated from Qatādah, from Mūsā ibn Salamah al-Hudhalī, who said: \I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about wiping over the leather socks"," and he said: 'Three days and their nights for the traveller"," and one day and one night for the resident.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than his narration.]"""
"1318","(1319) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Ghassān Mālik ibn Yaḥyā al-Sūsī narrated to me, Shujāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to me, Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah narrated to me, who said: I heard Manṣūr say: \We were in the chamber of Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī"," and Ibrāhīm al-Taymī was with us. We mentioned wiping over the leather socks"," and Ibrāhīm al-Taymī said: 'ʿAmr ibn Maymūn narrated to us"," from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī"," from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit"," who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed for us three days"," and had we asked him for more"," he would have increased it for us'—meaning the wiping over the leather socks for the traveller.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1319","(1320) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, al-Thawrī narrated from his father, from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn al-Awdī, from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī, from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to wipe over the leather socks one day and one night when we are resident"," and three days when we travel. By Allah"," had the questioner continued in his questioning"," he would have made it five.\"" Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated it from al-Thawrī"," and he said in the hadith: \""Had I asked him for more"," he would have increased it for us.\"" And al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh narrated it from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī without mentioning the wiping of the resident. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1320","(1321) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqrīʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn, from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī, from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit, that a Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wiping over the leather socks, and he said: \Three days and their nights.\"" He said: \""We perceived that had he asked for more"," he would have increased it.\"" ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated it similarly from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh. And Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated it from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī"," inserting al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd between ʿAmr ibn Maymūn and Ibrāhīm al-Taymī"," and omitting Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī between ʿAmr ibn Maymūn and Khuzaymah ibn Thābit"," and he did not mention: \""Had I asked him for more"," he would have increased it for us.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1321","(1322) Abū Naṣr ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl al-Khuzāʿī informed us — Abū Shuʿayb al-Ḥarrānī informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Ibrāhīm al-Taymī narrating from al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd, from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn, from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The traveller may wipe [over his leather socks] for three days.\"" Shuʿbah said: \""I think he added: 'and their nights.'\"" And al-Thawrī narrated it from Salamah"," differing with Shuʿbah in its isnād. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1322","(1323) ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us — ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl al-Khuzāʿī informed us — Abū Shuʿayb informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed us — Sufyān ibn Saʿīd informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \The traveller may wipe for three days.\"" Al-Ḥārith said: \""I do not remove my leather socks until I come to my bed.\"" And Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād narrated it from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī"," differing with all of them. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1323","(1324) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us — ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl informed us — Abū Shuʿayb informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us — Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd informed us, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd, from ʿUmar, who said: \The traveller may wipe over the leather socks for three days.\"" And Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī narrated it from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī"," without the additional wording that Manṣūr and Saʿīd ibn Masrūq narrated from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1324","(1325) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Shuʿbah narrated to us, from al-Ḥakam and Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī, from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said regarding wiping over the leather socks: \For the resident"," one day and one night; and for the traveller"," three days and their nights.\"" And al-Ḥārith ibn Yazīd al-ʿUklī and Abū Maʿshar similarly narrated it from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī. Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: \""I asked Muḥammad — meaning al-Bukhārī — about this hadith"," and he said: 'The hadith of Khuzaymah ibn Thābit regarding wiping over the leather socks is not authentic in my view"," because the hearing [of Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī] from Khuzaymah is not known.'\"" And Shuʿbah used to say: \""Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī did not hear the hadith of wiping from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī.\"" The Sheikh said: \""The story of Zāʾidah from Manṣūr indicates the correctness of what Shuʿbah said"," and it has already passed at the beginning of the chapter.\"" And Dhawwād ibn ʿUlbah al-Ḥārithī — and he is weak — narrated it from Muṭarrif"," from al-Shaʿbī"," from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī"," from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," who said: \""The traveller may wipe for three days\"" — \""and if we were to ask him for more"," he would have given us more.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1325","(1326) Abū Naṣr ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us — ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl al-Khuzāʿī informed us — Abū Shuʿayb informed us — ʿAlī, meaning ibn al-Madīnī, informed us — Shihāb ibn ʿAbbād informed us — Dhawwād ibn ʿUlbah informed us. And Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh informed us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed me — Saʿīd ibn ʿUfayr informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Razīn, from Muḥammad ibn Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from Ayyūb ibn Qaṭan, from ʿUbādah, from Ubayy ibn ʿImārah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in his house, and he said: \O Messenger of Allah"," may I wipe over the leather socks?\"" He ﷺ said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""For one day?\"" He said: \""And two days.\"" He said: \""And two days?\"" He said: \""And three days.\"" He said: \""Three days"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""Yes"," whatever is easy for you.\"" Yaʿqūb said: \""Ubayy ibn ʿImārah al-Anṣārī"," and it is also said: ibn ʿImārah with a kasr on the ʿayn.\"" The Sheikh said: \""And ʿAmr ibn al-Rabīʿ ibn Ṭāriq narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb without mentioning ʿUbādah ibn Nusay in his isnād"," and he said in the hadith: He ﷺ said: 'Yes"," and whatever you wish.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Muḍṭarib. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 158]"""
"1326","(1327) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn informed us — ʿAmr ibn al-Rabīʿ mentioned it and added in it, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb said: \And he had prayed with the Prophet ﷺ facing both qiblahs.\"" And it has been narrated from ʿAmr without mentioning Ayyūb in his isnād. And Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb similarly. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 158]"""
"1327","(1328) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Aḥmasī in Kūfah informed us — al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥumayd ibn al-Rabīʿ informed me — Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Salām, mawlā of Khuzāʿah, informed us — Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb, who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Razīn informed me, from Muḥammad ibn Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from ʿUbādah ibn Nusay, from Ubayy ibn ʿImārith — thus said Abū ʿUbayd with a kasr [on the ʿayn] — who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in the house of ʿImārah facing both qiblahs"," and he said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," may I wipe over the leather socks?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'One day?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'And two days?' He said: 'And two days.' He said: 'And three days"," O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Yes' — until he counted seven. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes"," whatever is easy for you.'\"" Thus is our narration. And it has been said regarding Ibn Abī Maryam in this isnād"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd"," and other than this has been said in this isnād. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us"," saying: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: \""There is disagreement regarding its isnād"," and it is not strong.\"" And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," saying: \""This isnād is not established"," and there is much disagreement regarding it concerning Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb.\"" And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," Muḥammad ibn Yazīd"," and Ayyūb ibn Qaṭan are all unknown (majhūlūn). And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1328","(1329) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us — Miqdām ibn Dāwūd informed us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Jaʿfar al-Baghdādī informed us — al-Miqdām ibn Dāwūd ibn Talīd al-Ruʿaynī informed us — ʿAbd al-Ghaffār ibn Dāwūd al-Ḥarrānī informed us — Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr and Thābit, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you performs wuḍūʾ and puts on his leather socks"," let him pray in them and wipe over them"," and then let him not remove them if he wishes"," except from janābah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 1/290]"""
"1329","(1330) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — Asad ibn Mūsā informed us — Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us, from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād, from Zayd ibn al-Ṣalt, who said: I heard ʿUmar saying: \When one of you performs wuḍūʾ and puts on his leather socks"," let him wipe over them and pray in them"," and let him not remove them if he wishes"," except from janābah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it"," 1/203]"""
"1330","(1331) He said, and Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr and Thābit, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it. Ibn Ṣāʿid said: \I do not know of anyone who brought it except Asad ibn Mūsā.\"" The Sheikh said: \""And ʿAbd al-Ghaffār ibn Dāwūd al-Ḥarrānī followed him in the musnad hadith"," but it is not found among the people of Baṣra from Ḥammād"," and it is not well-known. And Allah knows best.\"" As for ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," the narration from him regarding that is well-known"," and that is in what [has preceded]. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1331","(1332) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr ibn Sābiq al-Khawlānī narrated to us: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us: Mūsā ibn ʿAlī ibn Rabāḥ narrated from his father, from ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir al-Juhānī, who said: I set out from Shām for Madīnah on Friday, and I entered upon ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. He said to me: \When did you put your leather socks on your feet?\"" I said: \""On Friday.\"" He said: \""Did you remove them?\"" I said: \""No.\"" He said: \""You have followed the Sunnah.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 1/289.]"""
"1332","(1333) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us. And Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Ibn Lahīʿah, ʤmr ibn al-Ḥārith, and al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed you from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥakam al-Balawī, that he heard ʿAlī ibn Rabāḥ al-Lakhmī report that ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir al-Juhānī said: I came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb with the news of a conquest from Shām, and I was wearing two thick Jurmūqānī leather socks. ʿUmar looked at them and said: \How long have you had them on without removing them?\"" He said: \""I said: 'I put them on on Friday"," and today is Friday—eight days.'\"" He said: \""You have attained [the Sunnah].\""\n\nAnd Mufaḍḍal ibn Faḍālah narrated it from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb"," and he said in it: \""You have attained the Sunnah.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it. Ibn Mājah narrated it"," 558.]"""
"1333","(1334) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mufaḍḍal ibn Faḍālah narrated to us from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥakam al-Balawī, from ʿAlī ibn Rabāḥ, from ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir, from ʿUmar, a similar narration, and he said: \You have attained the Sunnah.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," the specification of a time limit. It may be that he retracted to it when the established narration from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the time limit came to him"," or it may be that his statement which accords with the well-known Sunnah is more appropriate. And it has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar that he used to not specify any time limit for it. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1334","(1335) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿAbādah narrated to us: Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: that he used to not specify any time limit for wiping over the leather socks.\n\nAnd ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ narrated it with the same meaning from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar.\n\nAnd we have narrated the specification of a time limit from ʿUmar, ʿAlī, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, and their statement accords with the Sunnah which is more well-known and more frequently narrated.\n\nAnd the original ruling is the obligation of washing the feet, and recourse to that is more appropriate. And with Allah lies success.\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Zaʿfarānī said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī returned to the specification of a time limit for wiping in our presence in Baghdad before he departed from it. [Ṣaḥīgh. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it, 1/196.]"
"1335","(1336) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn ʤwn narrated to us: Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us by dictation: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā al-Hilālī narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Zakariyyā narrated from ʀmir, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, from his father, who said: I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. He said: \Do you have water?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" So he dismounted from his mount and walked until he disappeared from me in the darkness of the night. Then he came"," and I poured water over him from the vessel. He washed his hands and his face. He was wearing a woollen jubbah"," and he was unable to extract his arms from it until he brought them out from beneath the jubbah. He washed his arms and wiped over his head. Then I bent down to remove his leather socks"," and he said: 'Leave them"," for I put them on while they were pure.' So he wiped over them.\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū Nuʿaym. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr from his father"," from Zakariyyā.\n\nAnd ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī al-Safar narrated it with the same meaning from ʀmir al-Shaʿbī in an abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 203.]"""
"1336","(1337) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Maḥmawyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn Ghaylān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Aʿyan narrated to us from Ismāʿīl—he is Ibn Abī Khālid—from ʀmir, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah, from his father, and he mentioned its meaning, up to his saying: \I said: 'Shall I not remove your leather socks"," O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'I put them on while they were pure; I have not become junub since then.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1337","(1338) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr al-Mukharramī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad, from Ḥamzah ibn al-Mughīrah, from his father, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he said: \Stay behind"," O Mughīrah"," and go forth"," O people.\"" So I stayed behind"," and I had water with me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ relieved himself"," then returned"," and I poured water over him. He washed his face"," then went to wash his hands"," and he was wearing a Roman jubbah whose sleeves were tight. So he inserted his hand from beneath it and washed his hands"," and he wiped over his head and wiped over his leather socks.\n\nSufyān said: Ḥuṣayn added in it"," from al-Shaʿbī"," from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah"," from his father"," who said: \""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," may Allah bless you"," do you wipe over your leather socks?' He said: 'I put them on while they were pure.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Nasāʾī narrated it"," 125.]"""
"1338","(1339) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Isfarāyinī narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb—meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Thaqafī—narrated to us: al-Muhājir narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ: that he granted permission for a traveller for three days and their nights, and for a resident for one day and one night, that when he performed ablution and put on his leather socks, he could wipe over them. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"
"1339","(1340) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Bundār—meaning Muḥammad ibn Bashshār—and Bishr ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAqadī, and Muḥammad ibn Abān said: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us: al-Muhājir ibn Makhlad Abū Makhlad narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ: that he granted permission for a traveller for three days and their nights, and for a resident for one day and one night, that when he performed ablution and put on his leather socks, he could wipe over them.\n\nAnd Musaddad, ʤmr ibn ʿAlī, Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā, and al-ʿAbbās ibn Yazīd narrated it from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb. And al-Shāfiʿī narrated it from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, except that al-Rabīʿ expressed doubt regarding his words: \when he performed ablution and put on his leather socks","\"" attributing it to al-Shāfiʿī"," whereas it is in the ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1340","(1341) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad and al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Rabīʿ—and the wording is his—said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us from ʀṣim ibn Abī al-Najūd, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, who said: I came to Ṣafwān ibn ʀṣāl al-Murādī, and he said: \What brought you?\"" I said: \""I have come seeking knowledge.\"" He said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no one who leaves his house seeking knowledge except that the angels lower their wings for him"," pleased with what he does.'\"" He said: \""I have come to ask you about wiping over the leather socks.\"" He said: \""Yes"," I was in the army that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out"," and he commanded us to wipe over the leather socks when we had put them on in a state of purity—three days when we travelled"," and one night when we resided—and not to remove them for urine"," defecation"," or sleep"," and not to remove them except for janābah.\"" And he said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'In the west there is a gate of repentance"," the distance of which is seventy years; it will not be closed until the sun rises from its direction.'\"" Ḥasan."""
"1341","(1342) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us that al-Shāmātī — meaning Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad — informed us that Yūsuf ibn Mūsā and Ḥawtharah ibn Muḥammad both said that Abū Usāmah informed us that Abū Rawq informed us that Abū al-Gharīf informed us, from Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl al-Murādī, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent us on a military expedition and said: 'Let one of you"," when he is a traveller"," wipe over his khuffayn if he put them on in a state of purity"," for three days and their nights; and let the resident wipe for one day and one night.'\"" [Ḥasan for other than its own chain]"""
"1342","(1343) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhab al-Muqriʾ in Wāsiṭ informed us that Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb informed us that Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī informed us, from Zāʾidah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Ḥakam, from al-Qāsim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Sharīḥ ibn Hānīʾ, who said: \I came to ʿĀʾishah to ask her about wiping over the khuffayn. She said: 'Go to ʿAlī"," for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).' So I came to him and said: 'We are in a cold land with much snow — what do you think about the khuffayn?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""For the traveller"," three days and their nights; and for the resident"," one day and one night — he shall wipe over his khuffayn when he puts them on in a state of purity.\""'\"" The addition in this wording is unique to Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1343","(1344) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us. (Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us. Both said that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Sufyān informed us, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, who said: \I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: 'I asked ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb: \""Should one of us perform wuḍūʾ while his feet are in the khuffayn?\"" He said: \""Yes"," provided he put them on while they were in a state of purity.\""'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1344","(1345) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us that Dalham ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us. And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Bakr al-Marwazī informed us that Abū Nuʿaym informed us that Dalham ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us, from Ḥujayr ibn ʿAbdillāh, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: \Al-Najāshī gifted the Prophet (ﷺ) two plain black khuffayn. He wore them and wiped over them.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Nuʿaym. In the ḥadīth of ʿUbaydullāh it states: \""Al-Najāshī gifted the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) two plain black khuffayn. He performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over them.\"" [Ḥasan for other than its own chain. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (155)]"""
"1345","(1346) Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-ʿAbbās informed us that ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth informed us that his father informed us, from al-Shaybānī, from al-Shaʿbī, from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his khuffayn. A man present with al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah said: \O Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah"," where did the Prophet (ﷺ) get khuffayn?\"" Al-Mughīrah replied: \""Al-Najāshī gifted them to him.\"" The Shaykh said: \""Al-Shaʿbī only narrated the ḥadīth of wiping from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah from his father. This is a witness for the ḥadīth of Dalham ibn Ṣāliḥ"," and Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1346","(1347) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn informed us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: \I asked Maʿmar about a tear in the khuff. He said: 'If anything from the places of wuḍūʾ becomes exposed"," do not wipe over it; rather"," remove it.'\"" He said: \""And ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us"," saying: 'I heard al-Thawrī say: \""Wipe over them as long as they remain attached to the foot"," even if they are torn.\"" He said: 'And such were the khuff of the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār — torn and split.'\"" The statement of Maʿmar ibn Rāshid on this matter is more preferable to us. [Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it (754)]"""
"1347","(1348) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father, from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding the muḥrim: \He shall not wear khuffayn"," except for one who cannot find sandals; in that case"," he should cut them so that they fall below the ankles.\"" [Narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs.] Abū ʿAbdillāh said that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh said: \""In this is an indication that if the khuff does not cover the entire foot"," it is not a khuff over which wiping is permissible.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1348","(1349) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf both said that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā al-Dārabjirdī informed us that Abū ʿĀṣim informed us that Sufyān informed us, from Abū Qays, from Huzayl ibn Sharḥbīl, from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) wiped over his jawrabayn and his naʿlayn. [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (159)]"
"1349","(1350) Abū Saʿīd ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbdūs ibn Maḥfūẓ al-Faqīh al-Janzarūdhī informed us that Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr informed us that Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Anas informed us that Abū ʿĀṣim narrated it in a similar manner. Abū Muḥammad said: \I saw Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj weaken this report and say: 'Abū Qays al-Awdī and Huzayl ibn Sharḥbīl cannot be relied upon for this"," given their disagreement with the most eminent narrators who narrated this report from al-Mughīrah"," for they said: \""He wiped over the khuffayn.\""' And he said: 'We do not abandon the explicit text of the Qurʾān on the basis of narrations from the likes of Abū Qays and Huzayl.'\"" I mentioned this account from Muslim to Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Daghūlī"," and I heard him say: \""I heard ʿAlī ibn Makhlad ibn Shaybān say: 'I heard Abū Qudāmah al-Sarakhsī say: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī said: \""I said to Sufyān al-Thawrī: 'If you were to narrate to me the ḥadīth of Abū Qays from Huzayl"," I would not accept it from you.' So Sufyān said: 'The ḥadīth is weak' — or 'feeble' — or a word to that effect.\""'\"" Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us"," saying: \""I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal say: 'I mentioned this ḥadīth to my father"," and my father said: \""This is only narrated through the ḥadīth of Abū Qays.\"" My father said: \""My father [Aḥmad] disliked ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrating it"," saying: 'It is munkar.'\""'\"" Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Isfarāyinī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Barāʾ informed us"," saying: \""ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: 'The ḥadīth of al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah regarding wiping was narrated from al-Mughīrah by the people of Madīnah"," the people of Kūfah"," and the people of Baṣrah. Huzayl ibn Sharḥbīl narrated it from al-Mughīrah"," except that he added: \""And he wiped over the jawrabayn","\"" contradicting the people [i.e."," the other narrators].'\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār in Baghdād informed us that Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar informed us that al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Ghassān said: \""I asked Abū Zakariyyā — meaning Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn — about this ḥadīth"," and he said: 'All the people narrate it as referring to the khuffayn"," except Abū Qays.'\"" Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd said: \""ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī used not to narrate this ḥadīth"," because the well-known narration from al-Mughīrah is that the Prophet (ﷺ) wiped over the khuffayn.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: \""This was also narrated from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," but it is not connected nor strong.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1350","(1351) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us that Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad al-Shāmātī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ informed us that al-Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr informed us that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus informed us, from Abū Sinān ʿĪsā ibn Sinān, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Mūsā, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wiping over the jawrabayn and the naʿlayn.\"" Al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān's direct hearing from Abū Mūsā is not established"," and ʿĪsā ibn Sinān is weak and cannot be used as a proof. Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad said: \""I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: 'ʿĪsā ibn Sinān is weak.'\"" [Ḥasan for other than its own chain. Ibn Mājah narrated it (560)]"""
"1351","(1352) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed me; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shuʿbah, from Abū Warqāʾ, who heard a man from his people, called ʿAbd Allāh ibn Kaʿb, say: \I saw ʿAlī urinate"," then he wiped over his socks and sandals.\"" [Hasan due to supporting narrations. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 773.]"""
"1352","(1353) Isrāʾīl narrated from al-Zibriqān ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Kaʿb ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \I saw ʿAlī urinate"," then he performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his sandals and his socks.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it; Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Isrāʾīl narrated it.\n\nAnd likewise"," al-Thawrī narrated it from al-Zibriqān. [Hasan due to supporting narrations.]"""
"1353","(1354) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Ādam narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Manṣūr, who said: \I heard Khālid ibn Saʿd say: 'I saw Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī wiping over the socks and sandals.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 774.]"""
"1354","(1355) ʿAlī ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ismāʿīl ibn Rajāʾ, from his father, who said: \I saw al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib urinate"," then he performed wuḍūʾ"," wiped over the socks and sandals"," and then prayed.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 1984.]"""
"1355","(1356) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shuʿayrī narrated to us; Maḥmish ibn ʿIṣām narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī, from al-Aʿmash — I think — from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that he said: \I saw Anas ibn Mālik come to the privy and perform wuḍūʾ"," and he wiped over a white"," fastened turban and over two black"," fine-cloth socks.\""\n\nSome weak narrators raised it to the Prophet ﷺ"," but it has no basis.\n\nIt has also been narrated regarding wiping over the socks from Abī Umāmah"," Sahl ibn Saʿd"," and ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth. Abū Dāwūd said: \""That has also been narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and Ibn ʿAbbās.\""\n\nThe master Abū al-Walīd — may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy on him — used to interpret the hadith of wiping over the socks and sandals to mean that he wiped over socks that had leather soles"," not that he wiped over socks alone or sandals alone.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of that from him. And I found a narration from Anas ibn Mālik that supports this.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 779.]"""
"1356","(1357) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadbādhī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Munādī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; ʢāṣim al-Aḥwal narrated from Rāshid ibn Najīḥ, who said: \I saw Anas ibn Mālik enter the privy while wearing two socks — the lower part of which was leather and the upper part was fine wool — and he wiped over them.\""\n\n[Hasan. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 36357.]"""
"1357","(1358) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Khalīl informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bishr al-Qazzāz narrated to us; Abū ʿUmayr narrated to us; Riwād narrated from Sufyān, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʢāṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ, washing each part once, and wiped over his sandals.\n\nThis is how Riwād ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated it. He is alone in narrating these anomalies from al-Thawrī, and this is one of them. The trustworthy narrators narrated it from al-Thawrī without this wording. It was also narrated from Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb from al-Thawrī in this manner, but it is not preserved.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ due to supporting narrations. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq, 783.]"
"1358","(1359) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Wākīʿī narrated to me; my father narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us; Sufyān narrated it with his chain of narration, that the Prophet ﷺ wiped over the sandals.\n\nThe authentic narration is that of the group.\n\nʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Dārawardī and Hishām ibn Saʿd narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, and they mentioned in the hadith a sprinkling of water over the foot while the sandal was on it. This may indicate that he washed the foot while it was in the sandal. Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, Warqāʾ ibn ʿUmar, and Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Abī Kathīr narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, and they mentioned in the hadith that he washed his feet. The hadith is one single hadith. The larger number of narrators is more deserving of being preserved than the smaller number, along with the excellence of the memory of those who preserved the washing after the sprinkling over those who did not preserve it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ due to supporting narrations.]"
"1359","(1360) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad and ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā both said: Hushaym narrated to us from Yaʿlā ibn ʢāṭāʾ, from his father. ʿAbbād said: \Aws ibn Abī Aws al-Thaqafī informed me.\"" He said: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wuḍūʾ and wipe over his sandals and his feet.\""\n\nAnd Musaddad said: \""That he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 160.]"""
"1360","(1361) Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Yaʿlā ibn ʢāṭāʾ, from Aws al-Thaqafī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his sandals. This narration is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous).\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us of it; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it.\n\nThis chain of narration is not strong, and it carries the same possibility as the first hadith. What indicates that the intended meaning is the washing of the feet while in the sandals is what follows. [Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī, 113.]"
"1361","(1362) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us. He said: I read to Mālik, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from ʿUbayd ibn Jurayj, that he said to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar: \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," I have seen you practise four things which I have not seen any of your companions practise.\"" He said: \""What are they?\"" He mentioned them and said regarding them: \""I have seen you wear the sandals of Sibt (i.e."," made of tanned leather free of hair).\"" He said: \""As for the sandals of Sibt"," I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wearing sandals that had no hair on them and performing wuḍūʾ in them"," so I love to wear them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\nA group also narrated it from Saʿīd al-Maqburī. And Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from Ibn ʿAjlān from al-Maqburī"," adding in it: \""And he would wipe over them.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 477.]"""
"1362","(1363) Abū Bakr ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn al-ʿAlāʾ informed us; Sufyān informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated to us, from Saʿīd, from ʿUbayd ibn Jurayj, who said: It was said to Ibn ʿUmar: \We have seen you do something which we have not seen anyone else do besides you.\"" He said: \""What is it?\"" They said: \""We have seen you wear these sandals of Sibt.\"" He said: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wear them and perform wuḍūʾ in them"," and wipe over them.\""\n\nThis addition"," if it is preserved"," does not contradict washing them"," for he may have washed them while they were on his feet and then wiped over them"," just as he wiped over his forelock and his turban. And Allah knows best. [Jayyid. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 199.]"""
"1363","(1364) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Sufyān narrated to us, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: ʿAlī urinated while standing, then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over the two sandals. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 1995.]"
"1364","(1365) And with his chain of narration, he said: Sufyān narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abū Ẓabyān, who said: ʿAlī urinated while standing, then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over the two sandals, then he went out and prayed Ẓuhr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 1998.]"
"1365","(1366) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us; Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ẓabyān, who said: I saw ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib at al-Raḥbah. He urinated while standing until the foam appeared. Then a vessel of water was brought to him. He washed his hands, sniffed water into his nostrils and rinsed his mouth, washed his face and his forearms, and wiped over his head. Then he took a handful of water and placed it upon his head until I saw the water trickling down upon his beard. Then he wiped over his two sandals. Then the prayer was established, so he removed his sandals, then stepped forward and led the people in prayer.\n\nIbn Numayr said: al-Aʿmash said: \I narrated this to Ibrāhīm"," and he said: 'When you see Abū Ẓabyān"," inform me.' So I saw Abū Ẓabyān standing in the Kunāsah and said: 'This is Abū Ẓabyān.' So he went to him and asked him about the hadith.\""\n\nThe well-known narration from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) is that he washed his feet when he described the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and he did not contradict the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). As for his wiping over the two sandals"," it is interpreted as washing the feet while the sandals were on"," and wiping over the sandals"," because wiping is a concession for one whose feet are covered by the two khuffs"," and it does not extend beyond its proper place. The original obligation is the washing of the two feet"," except in cases specified by an established Sunnah or an undisputed consensus. There is no basis for wiping over sandals or over socks. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 2000.]"""
"1366","(1367) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Asadī informed me; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us; Shuʿbah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-ʿAdl informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my father informed us; Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Abū Bakr ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar ibn Saʿd, who heard Abū ʿAbdillāh, the freedman of Banī Taym ibn Murrah, narrate from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that he witnessed ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf asking Bilāl about the wuḍūʾ of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: \He would go out to relieve himself"," and I would bring him water"," and he would perform wuḍūʾ and wipe over his turban and his two sandals.\"" Another narrator said: \""Taym ibn Murrah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 153.]"""
"1367","(1368) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū Muḥammad Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Nuṣayr al-Ṣūfī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ informed us; Abū Shihāb al-Ḥannāṭ narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wipe over the two mūqīyn (sandals) and the turban (khimār). [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains.]"
"1368","(1369) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us; Abū al-Naḍr informed us; Abū Khaythamah informed us; ʿĀṣim ibn Abī al-Najūd narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, who said: I came to Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl and said to him: \Something has been troubling my heart regarding wiping over the two khuffs. Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) concerning it?\"" He said: \""Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us"," when we were on a journey or were travellers"," not to remove our khuffs for three days and their nights"," on account of relieving oneself"," urinating"," or sleeping"," except in the case of janābah (major ritual impurity).\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"1369","(1370) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us; al-Shāmātī, that is Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad, informed us; al-Ashajj, that is Abū Saʿīd, informed us; ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb informed us; Yazīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who is al-Dālānī, narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Isḥāq, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), regarding a man who wipes over his two khuffs and then decides to remove them: \He should wash his feet.\"" [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"1370","(1371) Abū Bakr ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī informed us; Abū Nuʿaym informed us; ʿAbd al-Salām narrated it with the same meaning.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: \We do not know whether Yaḥyā heard from Saʿīd or not"," nor whether Saʿīd heard from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\"" [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"1371","(1372) Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq in Baghdād informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Qurashī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to me, from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, in the story of wiping (al-masḥ), he said: \And my father used to remove his leather socks and wash his feet.\""\n\nIt is also narrated from ʿAṭāʾ something similar. [Ṣaḥīḥ by virtue of other narrations]"""
"1372","(1373) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us: Isḥāq ibn Khaldūn informed us: al-Haytham ibn Jamīl informed us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr, from Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah and al-Aswad, regarding a man who performs wuḍūʾ and wipes over his leather socks, then removes them: they both said, \He should wash his feet.\""\n\nAbū Ḥanīfah narrated it from Ḥammād"," from Ibrāhīm himself. And it is narrated from al-Ḥakam and others"," from Ibrāhīm: \""He may pray and need not wash his feet","\"" and this is the view of al-Ḥasan. A third view is also narrated from Ibrāhīm. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/205]"""
"1373","(1374) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Yūnus informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Mustamlī informed us: Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ, from Marwān, from al-Aʿmash, from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, from Abī Maʿshar, from Ibrāhīm, who said: \When one wipes over his leather socks and then removes them"," it is as though he has removed his wuḍūʾ (i.e."," his wuḍūʾ is broken).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn ʿAdī in al-Kāmil"," 3/396]"""
"1374","(1375) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed us: my father said: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: \I asked al-Zuhrī about a man who performed wuḍūʾ and inserted his feet into the leather socks while they were still pure"," then he had a minor occurrence (aḥdath) and wiped over them"," then removed them — should he wash them or renew his wuḍūʾ?\"" He said: \""Rather"," he should renew his wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Something similar is narrated from Makhūl. We have narrated from al-Shāfiʿī in the book of Abī Ḥanīfah and Ibn Abī Laylā regarding the invalidation of wuḍūʾ (tafrīq al-wuḍūʾ). The narrations on this have already passed in its chapter. It is narrated from al-Shaʿbī regarding a man in whose leather sock a pebble entered: he said"," \""He should perform wuḍūʾ.\"" He meant — and Allah knows best — that he should remove his leather sock to take out the pebble and then perform wuḍūʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1375","(1376) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: ʿUmard ibn Ruḍayḥ informed us: ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Maymūnah, from Abī Burdah, from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, who said: \We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he commanded us to wipe over the leather socks for three days and their nights for the traveller"," and one day and one night for the resident"," so long as he does not remove them or they are not removed.\""\n\nʿUmard ibn Ruḍayḥ is the sole narrator of this"," and he is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī). [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"," 1005]"""
"1376","(1377) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Isfarāʾinī therein informed us: Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā informed us: al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā informed us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim, from Thawr ibn Yazīd, from Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah, from the scribe of al-Mughīrah, from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he used to wipe over the upper part of the leather sock and its lower part. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 165]"
"1377","(1378) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī both informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd informed us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim, from Thawr ibn Yazīd, and Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah narrated to us, from the scribe of al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, who said: \I performed wuḍūʾ for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabūk"," and he wiped over the upper part of the leather sock and its lower part.\""\n\nThus he said in this isnād: \""Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah narrated to us.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/190]"""
"1378","(1379) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥulwānī informed us: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd, and he mentioned it with its meaning, and he said: \From Rajāʾ.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1379","(1380) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Mūsā ibn Marwān al-Raqqī and Maḥmūd ibn Khālid al-Dimashqī both said: al-Walīd informed us, and he mentioned it with its meaning, and he said: \From Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: \""It is narrated that Thawr did not hear this ḥadīth from Rajāʾ.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: he said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Ibn al-Mubārak narrated it from Thawr"," and he said: \""I was told"," from Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah"," from the scribe of al-Mughīrah"," from the Prophet ﷺ","\"" as a mursal narration"," in which al-Mughīrah is not mentioned.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And thus Abū ʿĪsā mentioned it"," from al-Bukhārī and Abī Zurʿah al-Rāzī. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 165]"""
"1380","(1381) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: Makkī ibn ʿAbdān informed us: ʿAmmār ibn Rajāʾ informed us: Zayd ibn Ḥubāb informed us: Sufyān al-Thawrī, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to wipe over the outer surface of the leather sock and its inner surface. [Ḥasan by virtue of other narrations]"
"1381","He said: And ʿAmmār narrated to us, Zayd narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿUmarī narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, a similar narration. [Hasan in virtue of other narrations supporting it]"
"1382","Abū ʿAbd al-Rahmān al-Sulamī and Abū Nasr ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us — they both said: Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us — Muhammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb that he used to say: \The one who performs masḥ over the khuffayn places one hand on top of the khuff and one hand beneath the khuff"," then he wipes.\""\n\nMālik said: \""And that is the most preferable of what I have heard regarding the masḥ over the khuffayn.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq 854]"""
"1383","Abū Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from ʿUrwah ibn al-Mughīrah from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah that the Prophet ﷺ wiped the outer surface of his khuffayn.\n\nThus narrated Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād, and similarly narrated Ismāʿīl ibn Mūsā from Ibn Abī al-Zinād. And Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Hāshimī, Muhammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ, and ʿAli ibn Ḥujr narrated from Ibn Abī al-Zinād from his father from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr from al-Mughīrah. And Allāh knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of other narrations. Al-Ṭayālisī 692]"
"1384","Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Abū Usāmah narrated from Ashʿath from al-Ḥasan from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate"," then he came and performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his khuffayn. He placed his right hand upon his right khuff and his left hand upon his left khuff"," then he wiped the upper part of both with a single wiping"," until it was as though I were looking at the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon the khuffayn.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Abī Shaybah 1957]"""
"1385","Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us — Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abū Isḥāq from ʿAbd Khayr from ʿAlī, who said: \If the religion were based on personal opinion"," the lower part of the khuff would be more deserving of masḥ than its upper part. And I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the outer surface of his khuffayn.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 162]"""
"1386","Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir al-Saqaṭī narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Ziyād informed us — Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated it with its isnād. He said: ʿAlī said: \If the religion of Allah were based on personal opinion"," the inner surface of the khuff would be more entitled to masḥ than its upper part. And indeed I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping thus with his fingers.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1387","Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us — Yazīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from al-Aʿmash this hadith, saying: \I did not consider the inner surface of the two feet to be more deserving of masḥ until I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the back of his khuffayn.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1388","Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ṭayyib Muhammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaʿīrī narrated to us — Maḥmish ibn ʿIṣām narrated to us — Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me — Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Abū Isḥāq from ʿAbd Khayr al-Khaywānī from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, who said: \I used to consider the inner surface of the two feet more deserving of masḥ than their outer surface"," until I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform wuḍūʾ and wipe over the back of his two feet upon his khuffayn.\""\n\nAnd in all these narrations restricted to the khuffayn there is an indication of an abbreviation that occurred therein. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1389","Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us — Abū Muhammad ibn Shawdhab al-Muqriʾ in Wāsiṭ narrated to us — Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us — Abū Nuʿaym narrated from Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq from Abū Isḥāq from ʿAbd Khayr, who said: \I saw ʿAlī perform wuḍūʾ and then wipe"," and then he said: 'Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the back of the two feet"," I would have considered their lower part — or their inner part — more entitled to that.'\""\n\nAnd similarly narrated Abū al-Sawdāʾ from Ibn ʿAbd Khayr from his father. (c) ʿAbd Khayr was not used as a proof by the two authors of the Ṣaḥīḥ.\n\nAnd this and what has been narrated to the same effect is intended thereby to refer to the two feet of the khuff"," by virtue of what has preceded and by virtue of what we have narrated from Khālid ibn ʿAlqamah from ʿAbd Khayr from ʿAlī regarding the description of the Prophet's ﷺ wuḍūʾ"," in which he mentioned that he washed his three times each. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1390","Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to me — Khālid ibn Abī Bakr narrated to me — Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from his father that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābl Allāh be pleased with him asked Saʿd ibn Abī Wāqqāṣ about masḥ over the khuffayn. So ʿUmar said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding us to wipe over the back of the khuffayn when one puts them on"," provided they are in a state of purity.\""\n\nKhālid ibn Abī Bakr is not strong (in narration)"," and in what has preceded there is sufficiency. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Yaʿlā 171]"""
"1391","(1392) And Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī — informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated to us: Ḥumayd ibn Mikhraq al-Anṣārī narrated to me that he saw Anas ibn Mālik at Qubāʾ wipe the outer surface of his leather socks with a single pass of his hand."
"1392","(1393) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed me: Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Rūḥ narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abū ʿAwn, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿIrār, from Qays ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, that he urinated, then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his leather socks on the upper surfaces of the two feet."
"1393","(1394) And al-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Isḥāq, from al-ʿAlāʾ, who said: \I saw Qays ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah urinate"," then he came to the Tigris"," performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over the upper surface of his leather socks in this manner"," and I saw the traces of his fingers on his leather socks.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed it to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Hāshimī narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī al-Qabbānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār both said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated it."""
"1394","(1395) And likewise Shuʿbah and others narrated it from Abū Isḥāq. And the meaning of this was narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed it to us in the Aḥādīth of Shuʿbah: Abū Bakr ibn Bālawayh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Rūḥ narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿIrār, from Qays ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, that he urinated, then performed wuḍūʾ and wiped over his leather socks on the upper surfaces of the two feet."
"1395","(1396) Abū Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā — informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us: Hushaym narrated from Manṣūr. And Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Manṣūr ibn Zādhān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Aflaḥ, the freedman of Abū Ayyūb, from Abū Ayyūb, that he used to command wiping over the leather socks, and he himself would wash his feet. He was asked about that: \How do you command wiping while you wash?\"" He said: \""Evil is what I have brought upon myself! If it is a hardship for you"," then the sin is upon me. I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do it and command it. However"," I am a man for whom wuḍūʾ has been made beloved.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Zahrānī."""
"1396","(1397) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥām al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: Mālik informed you that Nāfiʿ narrated to them from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you comes to the Friday prayer"," let him perform ghusl (ritual bath).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik."""
"1397","(1398) Abū al-Fatḥ — Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār in Baghdad — informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān — narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Ibn Shihāb informed me from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever among you comes to the Friday prayer"," let him perform ghusl.\"""""
"1398","(1399) He said: And Ibn Shihāb narrated to me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said while standing upon the pulpit: \Whoever among you comes to the Friday prayer"," let him perform ghusl.\"""""
"1399","(1400) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it, mentioning it from both of them together, incorporated into the first wording.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ."
"1400","(1401) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas and others informed you that Ṣafwān ibn Sulaym narrated to them."
"1401","(1402) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik from Ṣafwān ibn Sulaym from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Ghusl on Friday is obligatory upon every person who has reached puberty.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Qaʿnabī. And in the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb it reads: \""Ghusl on Friday…\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 839.]"""
"1402","(1403) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Zuhrī narrated to us in Makkah; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us; Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us; Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from his father that a man from among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) entered the mosque on Friday while ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb was delivering the sermon. ʿUmar said: \What time is this?\"" He said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," I returned from the market and heard the call to prayer"," so I did no more than perform wuḍūʾ and came.\"" ʿUmar said: \""Wuḍūʾ as well? Yet you know that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to command ghusl.\""\n\n[Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 842.]"""
"1403","(1404) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed us; Abū al-Muthannā al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to us; Juwayriyah ibn Asmāʾ narrated from Mālik ibn Anas from al-Zuhrī from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Ibn ʿUmar that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, while he was standing to deliver the Friday sermon, a man from among the early Muhājirūn came. ʿUmar called out to him: \What time is this?\"" He said: \""I was occupied today and did not return to my family until I heard the adhān"," so I did no more than perform wuḍūʾ.\"" ʿUmar said: \""Wuḍūʾ as well? Yet you know that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to command ghusl.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ. This is a ḥadīth that Mālik ibn Anas transmitted as mursal in the Muwaṭṭaʾ"," not mentioning ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar in its isnād. It was narrated as mawṣūl outside the Muwaṭṭaʾ"," and the mawṣūl version is ṣaḥīḥ"," for Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī and Maʿmir ibn Rāshid narrated it from al-Zuhrī as mawṣūl. This is also established from the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1404","(1405) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed me; my father narrated to me; al-Awzāʿī narrated to me; Yaḥyā narrated to me; Abū Salamah narrated to me; Abū Hurayrah said: While ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) was addressing the people on Friday, ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān entered the mosque. ʿUmar drew his attention and said: \What is the matter with men who come late after the call?\"" ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," when I heard the call to prayer I did no more than perform wuḍūʾ and came.\"" ʿUmar said: \""Wuḍūʾ as well? Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'When one of you comes to Friday"," let him perform ghusl.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from al-Walīd ibn Muslim from al-Awzāʿī. al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr.\n\nal-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: Since ʿUthmān did not leave the prayer for ghusl and ʿUmar did not command him to go out for ghusl"," this indicates that both of them knew that the command of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding ghusl was a matter of choice (i.e."," recommended"," not obligatory).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1405","(1406) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to me from the original of his book; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd said: I asked ʿAmrah about ghusl on Friday. She said: I asked ʿĀʾishah about ghusl on Friday, and she said: \The people were workers who provided for themselves"," and they would return in their [working] condition. It was said to them: 'If only you would perform ghusl.'\""\n\nExtracted in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 861.]"""
"1406","(1407) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muslimah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, i.e. ibn Muḥammad, narrated from ʿAmr, i.e. ibn Abī ʿAmr, from ʿIkrimah that a group of people from Iraq came and said: \O Ibn ʿAbbās"," do you consider ghusl on Friday to be obligatory?\"" He said: \""No"," but it is purer and better for whoever performs it. And whoever does not perform it"," there is no obligation upon him. I shall inform you how ghusl began. The people were laborers who wore wool and worked on their backs"," and their mosque was narrow with a low ceiling—it was merely a shelter of palm branches. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out on a hot day"," and the people sweated in that wool until odors arose from them"," causing some of them discomfort. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) noticed that smell"," he said: 'O people"," when this day comes"," perform ghusl"," and let one of you apply the best of his oil and perfume that he finds.'\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""Then Allah brought prosperity"," and they wore other than wool"," ceased their labor"," their mosque was expanded"," and some of the discomfort from sweat that had been harming them was removed.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 1/68.]"""
"1407","(1408) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to me; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd said: I asked ʿAmrah about ghusl on Friday. She said: I asked ʿĀʾishah about ghusl on Friday, and she said: \The people were workers who provided for themselves"," and they would return in their [working] condition. It was said to them: 'If only you would perform ghusl.'\""\n\nThis ḥadīth with this wording is gharīb from this chain; it is only known from the ḥadīth of al-Ḥasan and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 1/268.]"""
"1408","(1409) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdad; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us; ʿAffān narrated to us; Hammām narrated to us; Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan from Samurah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ on Friday"," then for him is [sufficient reward] and an excellent [deed]"," and whoever performs ghusl"," then it is more excellent.\""\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated from Shuʿbah from Qatādah.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf — Abū Dāwūd.]"""
"1409","(1410) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rajāʾ narrated to us; ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us; Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan from Samurah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever performs wuḍūʾ on Friday"," then for him is [sufficient reward] and an excellent [deed]"," and whoever performs ghusl"," then ghusl is more excellent.\"" And similarly it was narrated by Saʿīd ibn Sufyān al-Jaḥdarī from Shuʿbah. However"," Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah contradicted them both and narrated it as mursal.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"1410","(1411) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan from the Prophet (ﷺ) as mursal.\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated by Abān ibn Yazīd al-ʿAṭṭār from Qatādah. And Abū Ḥurrah al-Raqāshī narrated it from al-Ḥasan as well.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"
"1411","(1412) Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak — informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far — informed us; Yunus ibn Habib — narrated to us; Abu Dawud — narrated to us; Abu Hurrah — narrated from al-Hasan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, who said: \And I do not know it except from the Prophet (ﷺ) — that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever performs wudu"," then he has done well and it is a blessing"," and whoever performs ghusl"," then ghusl is more excellent.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"1412","(1413) Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated it from Abu Hurrah with his chain of narration, saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — and he did not doubt that he informed us of it — Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhawayh narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Mandah al-Isfahani narrated to us; Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us; Abu Hurrah narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nIt has also been narrated from another chain from the Prophet (ﷺ), though its chain of narration is subject to scrutiny. [Da'if]"
"1413","(1414) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; al-Rabi' —\n\n(And) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Hamid al-Bilali informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Baghdadi narrated to us in Makkah; Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever performs wudu on Friday"," then he has done well and it is a blessing"," and whoever performs ghusl"," then ghusl is more excellent"," and ghusl is from the Sunnah.\"" Abu Dawud did not mention: \""and ghusl is from the Sunnah.\"" [Da'if. Narrated by Ibn Majah"," 1091]"""
"1414","(1415) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Awfa al-Ta'i narrated to us; Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us; Hibban ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Subayh, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever comes to the Friday prayer"," let him perform ghusl.\"" When winter came and it became severe upon us"," we complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he said: \""Whoever performs wudu"," then he has done well and it is a blessing"," and whoever performs ghusl"," then ghusl is more excellent.\""\n\nIt has also been narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Da'if]"""
"1415","(1416) Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Khazzaz narrated to us; Asid ibn Zayd al-Jammal — Abu Muhammad — narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us; 'Awf narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever performs wudu on Friday"," then he has done well and it is a blessing"," and whoever performs ghusl"," then ghusl is more excellent.\""\n\nAl-Thawri narrated it from one who narrated to him"," from Abu Nadrah"," from Jabir"," from the Prophet (ﷺ). And Ishaq narrated it from Abu Dawud al-Hafri"," from Sufyan. [Da'if]"""
"1416","(1417) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Ali ibn Hamshadh al-'Adl narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Shayban ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, while he was addressing the people, a man came and said: \Why do you delay until this hour?\"" The man said: \""It is only that I heard the call and so I performed wudu.\"" 'Umar said: \""And wudu? Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'When one of you goes to the mosque"," let him perform ghusl'?\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Nu'aym.\n\nSimilarly"," Harb ibn Shaddad narrated it from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: \""When one of you goes to the Friday prayer"," let him perform ghusl.\"" And al-Awza'i said"," from Yahya: \""When one of you comes…\"" And Mu'awiyah ibn Salam said"," from Yahya: \""When one of you comes…\"" [Sahih]"""
"1417","(1418) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us —\n\n(And) Abu Sa'id informed us; Abu Muhammad al-Muzani informed us; 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa informed us — both saying: Abu al-Yaman informed us; Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Tawus said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas: \They have mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Perform ghusl on Friday"," and wash your heads"," even if you are not in a state of janabah"," and apply perfume.'\"" Ibn 'Abbas said: \""As for the ghusl"," yes"," but as for the perfume"," I do not know.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Yaman.\n\nAnd it has been narrated in the hadith of Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""Ghusl on Friday is obligatory upon every one who has reached puberty.\"" And Abu Hurayrah said"," from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""Whoever performs ghusl on Friday — the ghusl of janabah — and then goes out…\"" He then mentioned his going out after the ghusl in the first"," second"," third"," fourth"," and fifth hour. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 844]"""
"1418","(1419) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhawayh al-'Adl narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya informed us; al-Layth narrated from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \When one of you intends to come to the Friday prayer"," let him perform ghusl.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya.\n\nIt is mentioned that Ibn 'Umar said: \""Ghusl is only incumbent upon one for whom the Friday prayer is obligatory.\""\n\nAnd from him: He would not perform ghusl while traveling on Friday.\n\nAnd others among the scholars have recommended performing ghusl once every week for the purpose of cleanliness"," and they cited as evidence what… [Sahih]"""
"1419","(1420) Abu 'Abdullah — Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Dabbi — informed us; Abu Ahmad — Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdan — in Marw narrated to us; Abu al-Ahwas — Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qadi — narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid — Abu al-Hajjaj — from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \It is a right upon every Muslim that he perform ghusl in every seven days"," one day.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari said: And Aban ibn Salih narrated it"," and he mentioned it.\n\nThis appears to indicate that what is intended by it is also the ghusl of Friday. [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Hibban"," 1232]"""
"1420","(1421) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us; Tamtam — meaning Muhammad ibn Ghalib — narrated to us; Musa narrated to us; Wuhaib narrated to us; Ibn Tawus narrated from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \We are the last"," but the foremost on the Day of Resurrection. Though every nation was given the Book before us"," and we were given it after them. This is the day concerning which they differed"," and Allah guided us to it. Tomorrow is for the Jews"," and the day after tomorrow is for the Christians.\"" Then he fell silent and said: \""It is a right upon every Muslim"," in every seven days"," one day"," that he wash his head and his body.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il"," in abridged form. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 2298]"""
"1421","(1422) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, that he heard ʿAlqama ibn Waqqāṣ say: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Actions are judged only by intentions"," and a person shall have only that which he intended. So"," whoever migrates for the sake of Allah and His Messenger"," his migration is for the sake of Allah and His Messenger; and whoever migrates to attain some worldly gain or to marry a woman"," his migration is for that to which he migrated.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Numayr"," from Yazīd ibn Hārūn"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through other chains from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1422","(1423) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan, meaning Ibn Sufyān, narrated to us, Abū Bakr, meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah, narrated to us, Jarīr narrated from Layth, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to perform a single ghusl for both janābah and Jumuʿah. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (317)]"
"1423","(1424) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād informed us; and Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿd al-Shuʿaybī both said: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zakariyyā informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Qabbānī narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Hārūn ibn Muslim al-ʿIjlī narrated to us, Abān ibn Yazīd al-Aṭṭār narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Qatādah, who said: My father came to me while I was performing ghusl on the day of Jumuʿah, and he said: \Is your ghusl for janābah or for Jumuʿah?\"" I said: \""For janābah.\"" He said: \""Then perform another ghusl"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Whoever performs ghusl on the day of Jumuʿah shall remain in a state of purity until the next Jumuʿah.'\"" This is the wording of Abū Ḥāzim's hadith. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (1222)]"""
"1424","(1425) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Thaqafī narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Manṣūr, from Mujāhid, who said: \If a man performs ghusl for janābah on the day of Jumuʿah after the rising of dawn"," it shall suffice him for the ghusl of Jumuʿah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shaybānī in his Muwaṭṭaʾ (3/67)]"""
"1425","(1426) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us, Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Zādān, who said: \Two men among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) exchanged insults"," and one of them said: 'Then I am like the one who does not perform ghusl on the day of Jumuʿah.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by the author in al-Shuʿab (3023)]"""
"1426","(1427) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us from his original copy, Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us, Abū Khālid Yazīd ibn Saʿīd al-Iskandarānī narrated in Alexandria, saying: It was read to Mālik ibn Anas: \Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrated to you from his father"," from Abū Hurayrah"," who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said on one of the Jumuʿahs: 'O assembly of Muslims"," indeed this is a day that Allah"," the Most High"," has made an Eid for you"," so perform ghusl and use the siwāk.'\"" This is how this shaykh narrated it from Mālik.\n\nAnd the group narrated it from Mālik"," from al-Zuhrī"," from Ibn al-Sabbāq"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," as a mursal hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik (144)]"""
"1427","(1428) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Ibn Fuḍayl narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to perform ghusl on the two Eids as he would perform ghusl for janābh. It has also been narrated from others as well, and that shall be mentioned, if Allah the Most High wills, in the book of the Two Eids. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1348)]"
"1428","(1040) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated, saying: I heard ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh say: I said to Sufyān: \Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"," from Abū Hurayrah regarding a man who is away tending his camels.\""\n\nSufyān said: \""This was brought by al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb"," whereas ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said: 'I heard Jābir ibn Zayd say it.'\"" ʿAlī said: I said to Sufyān: \""Shuʿbah narrated it in this manner from Jābir.\"" He said: \""Shuʿbah was among the people of ḥifẓ (retention) and truthfulness"," and he was not among those who intended falsehood.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: It has also been narrated from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah"," from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," from Ibn al-Musayyab"," from Abū Hurayrah. And Ibn Abī ʿArūbah only heard it from Abū al-Rabīʿ"," from ʿAmr. Likewise"," Saʿd ibn al-Ṣalt narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah. It has also been narrated through another weak chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn ʿAdī in al-Kāmil (1/378)]"""
"1429","(1430) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyyā narrated to us, Muṣʿab ibn Shaybah narrated it with its chain, similar to it, except that he said: \He used to perform ghusl for four things.\""\n\nAnd likewise Misʿar narrated it from Muṣʿab ibn Shaybah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1430","(1431) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim al-Zāhid narrated to us, Abū Saʿīd al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn Ḥassān al-Marwazī narrated in Naysābūr, Sufyān narrated from ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī al-Safar, from Muṣʿab ibn Shaybah, from Ṭalq ibn Ḥabīb, who said: I heard ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Zubayr say: I heard ʿĀʾishah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Ghusl is prescribed for five things: janābah"," cupping"," the ghusl of Jumuʿah"," washing the deceased"," and ghusl after the water of the ḥammām (public bath).\""\n\nMuslim narrated in his Ṣaḥīḥ the hadith of Muṣʿab ibn Shaybah from Ṭalq ibn Ḥabīb"," from Ibn al-Zubayr"," from ʿĀʾishah"," from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""Ten things are part of the fiṭrah","\"" but he omitted this hadith and did not include it. I do not think he omitted it except due to the criticism of some ḥuffāẓ regarding it.\n\nIt has a corroborating witness (shāhid) in the hadith of ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," except that he did not mention the ghusl after washing the deceased. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1431","(1432) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, who said: We used to bathe for five things: cupping (hijamah), the public bath (hammam), plucking the underarm hair (natf al-ibt), sexual impurity (janabah), and the day of Jumu'ah.\n\nAl-A'mash said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he said: They did not consider any bath obligatory except that for janabah, although they considered it desirable (mustahabb) to bathe on the day of Jumu'ah. [Da'if]"
"1432","(1433) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to me, 'Umar ibn Hafs narrated to me, my father narrated to me, al-A'mash narrated to me, Mujahid narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, who said: He would bathe after the hammam, on the day of Jumu'ah, after janabah, after cupping (hijamah), and after shaving with a razor (musy). [Sahih]"
"1433","(1434) Abu Zakariyya: Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us: Abu Sahl: Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir informed us, from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever washes a dead person"," let him bathe; and whoever carries him"," let him perform wudu'.\""\n\n[Sahih. Ibn Majah narrated it"," 1463]"""
"1434","(1435) Abu Nasr ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khumayrawah informed us, al-Husayn ibn Idris informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib informed us, 'Abd al-'Aziz — I think he was ibn al-Mukhtar — informed us, Suhayl narrated from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \From his washing"," bathing is required; and from his carrying"," wudu' is required\"" — meaning the deceased.\n\nAnd Ibn Jurayj and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it similarly from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih"," from his father"," from Abu Hurayrah. [Sahih]"""
"1435","(1436) Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Ishaq, mawla of Zaidah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, with the same meaning. Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us, Abu Dawud informed us, Hamid ibn Yahya informed us, from Sufyan, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated it from Suhayl on one occasion as marfu' and on another as mawquf.\n\nAnd Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated it from Suhayl similarly. [Sahih]"
"1436","(1437) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu Bakr: Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi in Baghdad informed us, 'Abd Allah ibn Mihran al-Darir, the trustworthy and reliable — and he was among the most retentive of people — informed us, 'Affan ibn Muslim informed us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid informed us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih informed us, from his father, from al-Harith ibn Makhlad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \From his washing"," bathing is required; and from his carrying"," wudu' is required\"" — meaning regarding the deceased and the funeral. Thus he narrated it"," and I do not think he preserved it accurately. [Da'if]"""
"1437","(1438) And it was reported from Wuhayb: Abu Waqid narrated, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Thawban, and Ishaq, mawla of Zaidah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \From his washing"," bathing is required; and from his carrying"," wudu' is required.\""\n\n'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdana informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us"," Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed us"," Musa — meaning Ibn Isma'il — informed us"," Wuhayb"," and he mentioned it. And he added: I mentioned that to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib"," and he said: \""Had I known that he was impure"," I would never have touched him.\"" And it was said from Ishaq"," from Abu Sa'id"," and it was said otherwise. [Da'if]"""
"1438","(1439) Abu Bakr: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisi informed us: Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah informed us, Abu Ahmad ibn Fars informed us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari informed me: Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from Ibn Wahb, from Usamah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, mawla of al-Mahri, from Ishaq, mawla of Zaidah, from Abu Sa'id, the like of it and the like of it: \Whoever washes a dead person"," let him bathe; and whoever carries him"," let him perform wudu'.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari said: And Ma'mar narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir"," from Ishaq"," from Abu Hurayrah"," from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: And Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us"," from Aban"," from Yahya"," from a man from Banu Layth"," from Ishaq"," from Abu Hurayrah"," from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: And Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us"," from Hammad"," from Muhammad ibn 'Amr"," from Abu Salamah"," from Abu Hurayrah"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," the like of it. He said: And al-Awza'i narrated to us"," from al-Darawardi"," from Muhammad ibn 'Amr"," from Abu Salamah"," from Abu Hurayrah"," his statement. Al-Bukhari said: And this is more likely correct. He said: And Ibn Hanbal and 'Ali said: Nothing is sound in this chapter. [Da'if]"""
"1439","(1440) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani informed us, he said: I heard Ahmad ibn Hanbal being asked about bathing after washing a deceased person, and he said: \Wudu' suffices for it.\""\n\nAbu Salih inserted between him and Abu Hurayrah in this — meaning Ishaq"," mawla of Zaidah. He said: And the hadith of Mus'ab is da'if; it contains characteristics upon which no action is performed.\n\nThe sheikh said: And Abu 'Isa said: I asked Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari about this hadith"," and he said: \""Indeed"," Ahmad ibn Hanbal and 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah said: Nothing is sound in this chapter.\"" Muhammad said: And the hadith of 'A'ishah in this chapter is not of that calibre. [Sahih. Abu Dawud narrated it"," 3162]"""
"1440","(1441) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asam informed us: al-Rabi' said: Al-Shafi'i said: \What prevented me from making bathing obligatory after washing a deceased person is that in its isnad there is a man of whose knowledge I have not been able to obtain"," to this day"," what would satisfy me. But if I find someone who satisfies me"," I shall make it obligatory"," and I shall make wudu' obligatory for touching the deceased when one has come into contact with him"," for they are both in a single hadith.\""\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah"," the hafiz"," informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Abu Bakr al-Mutarriz informed us"," he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Yahya saying: \""I do not know of any hadith regarding 'Whoever washes a dead person"," let him bathe' that is thabit (established). Even if it were established"," we would be obligated to act upon it.\""\n\nImam Ahmad said: And it has been narrated from another weak chain from Abu Salamah as marfu'. [Sahih. Al-Mu'allimi narrated it in al-Ma'rifah"," 1/357]"""
"1441","(1442) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyá narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Maḥbūb al-Ramlī narrated to us in Makkah; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Tamīmī narrated to us in Miṣr, both saying: Yaḥyá ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to me from Ḥunayn ibn Abī Ḥakīm from Ṣafwān ibn Sulaym from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ: **\Whoever gives a bath to the deceased"," let him take a bath.\""**\n\nThis is the wording of al-Qāḍī. In the narration of al-Ḥāfiẓ"," he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\""From washing the deceased"," (there is incumbent) a bath; and from carrying him"," (there is incumbent) wuḍūʾ.\""**\n\nIbn Lahīʿah and Ḥunayn ibn Abī Ḥakīm are not used as proof. The preserved narration from the ḥadīth of Abū Salamah is what al-Bukhārī alluded to — it is mawqūf"," from the statement of Abū Hurayrah. [Weak]\n\n---"""
"1442","(1443) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyá ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah that he said: **\Whoever gives a bath to the deceased"," let him take a bath; and whoever carries the deceased"," let him perform wuḍūʾ; and whoever walks with the funeral"," let him not sit until the burial is completed.\""**\n\nAl-Shaykh said: This is the authentic narration as mawqūf upon Abū Hurayrah"," as al-Bukhārī alluded to. It has also been narrated through another chain from Abū Hurayrah as marfūʿ. [Weak]\n\n---"""
"1443","(1444) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath narrated to us in Baghdād by dictation; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm, i.e., al-Barqī, and Jaʿfar ibn Musāfir both said: ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us from al-ʿAlāʾ from his father from Abū Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\Whoever gives a bath to the deceased"," let him take a bath; and whoever carries him"," let him perform wuḍūʾ.\""**\n\nZuhayr ibn Muḥammad — al-Bukhārī said: The people of Shām narrated from him ḥadīths containing munkar (objectionable narrations). Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nasāʾī said: Zuhayr is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī). It has also been narrated through another chain from Abū Hurayrah as marfūʿ. [Weak]\n\n---"""
"1444","(1445) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to me; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to me from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbbās from ʿAmr ibn ʿUmayr from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\Whoever washes the deceased"," let him take a bath; and whoever carries him"," let him perform wuḍūʾ.\""**\n\nThis ʿAmr ibn ʿUmayr is only known through this ḥadīth and is not well-known (laysa bi-l-mashhūr). [Weak]\n\n---"""
"1445","(1446) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us from Ṣāliḥ, the freed slave of al-Tawʾamah, from Abū Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\Whoever gives a bath to the deceased"," let him take a bath; and whoever carries a janāzah"," let him perform wuḍūʾ.\""**\n\nThis is the well-known narration from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Dhiʾb. And Ṣāliḥ"," the freed slave of al-Tawʾamah"," is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī). [Authentic. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī"," 2314]\n\n---"""
"1446","(1447) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad, i.e., ibn ʿĀṣim al-Dimashqī, narrated to us; Maḥmūd ibn Khālid narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us. He said: I said to al-Layth ibn Saʿd: \Indeed"," Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed me from Ṣāliḥ"," the freed slave of al-Tawʾamah"," from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — meaning: **'And whoever carries him"," let him perform wuḍūʾ.'**\"" Al-Layth said: \""It has reached us that this is from the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah.\"" It was mentioned to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," and ʿAbd Allāh said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended that no one should attend the funeral except one who has performed wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: This has also been narrated through another chain from Abū Hurayrah explicitly"," but its chain is weak. [Authentic]\n\n---"""
"1447","(1448) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿĀṣim al-Dimashqī narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us; al-Walīd narrated to us; Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to me from Mūsā ibn Wardān from Abū Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\Whoever intends to carry the deceased"," let him perform wuḍūʾ.\""**\n\nAl-Shaykh said: The marfūʿ narrations in this chapter from Abū Hurayrah are not strong due to the ignorance of some of their narrators and the weakness of some of them. The authentic narration from Abū Hurayrah is from his own statement"," mawqūf"," not marfūʿ. [Weak]\n\n---"""
"1448","(1449) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me; Yaḥyá ibn Ayyūb narrated to me from ʿUqayl ibn Khālid from Ibn Shihāb from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah who said: **\Whoever washes the deceased"," let him take a bath; and whoever places him in his grave"," let him perform wuḍūʾ.\""** And it has been said that it is from Ibn al-Musayyab's own statement. [Good]\n\n---"""
"1449","(1450) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsá narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed me; Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated to me from al-Zuhrī. He said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me: **\It is from the Sunnah that whoever gives a bath to the deceased should take a bath"," and whoever descends into his grave at the time of burial should perform wuḍūʾ. And there is no wuḍūʾ incumbent upon anyone else — neither upon one who prays over the deceased"," nor upon one who carries his janāzah"," nor upon one who walks with it.\""** And it has passed from Ibn al-Musayyab that he said: \""Had I known it to be impure"," I would never have touched it.\""\n\nAnd something to this effect has been narrated from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān as marfūʿ. [Authentic]\n\n---"""
"1450","(1451) The faqīh Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Urmwī informed us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Nasawī narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān al-Nasawī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Minhāl narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Maʿmarr ibn Rāshid narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq from his father from Ḥudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\Whoever gives a bath to the deceased"," let him take a bath.\""**\n\nOthers narrated from Maʿmarr from Yaḥyá ibn Abī Kathīr from Abū Isḥāq from Abū Hurayrah. And Abān narrated from Yaḥyá from Abū Isḥāq that he heard Abā Hurayrah.\n\nAl-Shaykh Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh said: The report of Abū Isḥāq from his father from Ḥudhayfah is discarded (sāqiṭ). He said: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: \""No ḥadīth is established in this matter.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh — may Allah have mercy on him — said: The well-known narration from Abū Isḥāq is from Nājiyah ibn Kaʿb al-Asadī from ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Weak]"""
"1451","(1452) As it was narrated to us by Abū ʿAlī: al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh — narrated to us ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Shawdhāb al-Muqriʾ in Wāsiṭ — narrated to us Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb — narrated to us ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā, from Isrāʾīl, from Abū Isḥāq, from Nājiyah ibn Kaʿb al-Asadī, from ʿAlī, who said: \When Abū Ṭālib died"," I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," your misguided uncle has perished.' He said: 'Go and bury him.' I said: 'I will not bury him.' He said: 'Who then will bury him? Go and bury him"," and do not do anything until you come to me.' So I went and buried him"," and he commanded me to perform ghusl"," then he supplicated for me with supplications"," and nothing on the face of the earth would have pleased me more than that.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by al-Thawriyy"," Shuʿbah"," and Sharīk"," from Abū Isḥāq; and al-Aʿmash narrated it from him from a man from ʿAlī.\n\nNājiyah ibn Kaʿb al-Asadī — his uprightness (ʿadālah) is not established according to the two Ṣaḥīḥ compilers"," and it is not in the narration that he washed him.\n\nNarrated to us Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Barāʾ"," who said: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: The ḥadīth of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to bury Abū Ṭālib — we only found it among the people of Kūfah"," and there is some weakness in its chain. Abū Isḥāq narrated it from Nājiyah"," and we do not know of anyone other than Abū Isḥāq who narrated from Nājiyah.\n\nImām Aḥmad said: And it has been narrated through another weak chain from ʿAlī in this manner. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3214]"""
"1452","(1453) It was narrated to us by Abū Muḥammad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf, by dictation — narrated to us Abū Isḥāq: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dubaylī in Makkah — narrated to us Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Zayd al-Ṣāʾigh — narrated to us Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us al-Ḥasan ibn Yazīd al-Aṣamm, who said: I heard al-Suddī narrating from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When Abū Ṭālib died"," I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'Your elderly uncle has died.' He said to me: 'Go and bury him"," and do not do anything until you come to me.' So I performed ghusl"," then came to him"," and he supplicated for me with supplications that the red camels would not please me more than.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1453","(1454) And narrated to us ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — narrated to us al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍr al-Harawī therein — narrated to me Aḥmad ibn Najdah — narrated to us Saʿīd, and he mentioned it with its chain similarly, adding: \the red camels and their black ones.\"" And ʿAlī used to perform ghusl whenever he washed a dead person. Al-Ḥasan ibn Yazīd al-Aṣamm is alone in narrating this with this chain. [Ḥasan]"""
"1454","(1455) And narrated to us Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī — narrated to us Abū Aḥmad: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ, who said: Al-Ḥasan ibn Yazīd al-Kūfī is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī), and his ḥadīth from al-Suddī is not well-preserved (laysa bi-l-maḥfūẓ). The locus of this famous ḥadīth is upon Abū Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī from Nājiyah ibn Kaʿb from ʿAlī.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad al-Farwī narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī ʿAlī al-Lahbī, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn, from ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān, from Usāmah ibn Zayd, who said: \ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of the death of Abū Ṭālib. He said: 'Go and wash him"," and do not do anything until you come to me.' So I washed him and buried him"," then came to him and he said: 'Go and perform ghusl.'\""\n\nNarrated to us by Abū Bakr: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Nawqānī therein — narrated to us Abū ʿAbdillāh: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Iṣfahānī al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Ṭayālisī — narrated to us Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad al-Farwī — narrated to us ʿAlī ibn Abī ʿAlī"," and he mentioned it. This is munkar (rejected)"," having no basis with this chain.\n\nAnd ʿAlī ibn Abī ʿAlī al-Lahbī is weak (ḍaʿīf); Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn declared him weak"," and al-Bukhārī and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nasāʾī declared him weak. And it is narrated from ʿAlī through another chain in this manner"," and its chain is weak. And it is narrated from ʿAlī as his own statement"," and it is not strong. [Very weak]"""
"1455","(1456) Narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us Abū Bakr: Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh — narrated to us Ṣāliḥ ibn Muqātil ibn Ṣāliḥ — narrated to us my father — narrated to us Muḥammad ibn al-Zibriqān, from Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, who said: \When Abū Ṭālib died"," I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," the misguided elder has died.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Go and wash him and shroud him.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I?' He said: 'Who has more right to that than you? Go and wash him"," shroud him"," and bury him"," and do not do anything until you come to me.' So I went and did so — he said — and when I came to him"," he said: 'Go and perform the ghusl of janābah.'\"" This is an error"," and the well-known narration from Abū Isḥāq is from Nājiyah from ʿAlī"," as mentioned above.\n\nAnd Ṣāliḥ ibn Muqātil ibn Ṣāliḥ narrates rejected narrations (al-manākīr).\n\nAnd it has been narrated in this regard from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī as his own statement. [Munkar (Rejected)]"""
"1456","(1457) Narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, who both said: Narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us ʿAlī ibn Maʿbad — narrated to us ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr, from Zayd, from Jābir, from al-Shaʿbī, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī, that he said: \Whoever washes a dead person"," let him perform ghusl.\"" And it has been narrated in this regard from Ibn ʿAbbās as his own statement. [Weak]"""
"1457","(1458) Narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, who both said: Narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir — narrated to us Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from Maṭar, from ʿAmmār ibn Abī ʿAmmār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Whoever washes a dead person"," let him perform ghusl.\""\n\nIt was narrated from him with this chain"," but the authentic narration from Ibn ʿAbbās is contrary to that. [Weak]"""
"1458","(1459) Narrated to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, who both said: Narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar — narrated to us Ibn Jurayj, from ʬAṭāʾ, who said: \Ibn ʿAbbās was asked: 'Is there a ghusl upon one who washes a dead person?' He said: 'Did your companion make you impure? Wudūʾ from him is sufficient.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1459","(1460) And narrated to us Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, who both said: Narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim — narrated to us al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ, from Sufyān, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he was asked about the ghusl for washing the dead, and he said: \Are they impure that you should perform ghusl from them?\"" — meaning the ghusl for washing the dead. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1460","(1461) And narrated to us Abū ʿAbdillāh — narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās — narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī — narrated to us Muʿallā and Manṣūr ibn Salamah, who both said: Narrated to us Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \There is no ghusl upon you for washing your dead when you have washed them. Your dead person is a believer"," pure"," and not impure. It is sufficient for you to wash your hands.\""\n\nThis has been narrated as marfūʿ (elevated to the Prophet)"," but its elevation is not correct. [Ḥasan]"""
"1461","(1462) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Hamdānī informed us; Abū Shaybah Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us; Khālid ibn Makhlad informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no obligation upon you to perform ghusl after washing your deceased"," when you have washed him. Indeed"," he is a Muslim"," a believer"," and pure. And the Muslim is not impure; it is sufficient for you that you wash your hands.\""\n\nThis chain is weak. The weakness therein"," as I surmise"," lies with Abū Shaybah. Part of it has been narrated through another route from Ibn ʿAbbās as a marfūʿ hadith.\n\n[Rejected (Munkar). Reported by al-Ḥākim (1/543).]"""
"1462","(1463) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿIṣmah ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAdl informed us; Abū Muslim al-Musayyab ibn Zuhayr al-Baghdādī informed us; Abū Bakr and ʿUthmān, the two sons of Abū Shaybah, both said: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not declare your dead to be impure"," for indeed the Muslim is not impure"," neither alive nor dead.\""\n\nAnd thus it has been narrated through another"," strange (gharīb) route from Ibn ʿUyaynah"," though the well-known version is mawqūf (stopped at the Companion).\n\n[Rejected (Munkar). Reported by al-Ḥākim (1/542).]"""
"1463","(1464) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ushnānī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us; Maḥbūb ibn Mūsā informed us; Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī informed us from ʬāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: I said to Ibn ʿUmar: \Should one perform ghusl after washing the deceased?\"" He said: \""What is the deceased?\"" I said: \""I hope that he is a believer.\"" He said: \""Then touch the believer as much as you are able.\""\n\n[Ḥasan (good).]"""
"1464","(1465) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬāʾ informed us; al-ʿUmarī informed us from Nāfiʿ, who said: Ibn ʿUmar used to say: \Whoever washes a deceased and something from the body touches him"," let him perform ghusl; otherwise"," let him perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\n[Weak (Ḍaʿīf).]"""
"1465","(1466) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibn Ṣāʿid informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Mukharramī informed us; Abū Hishām al-Mughīrah ibn Salamah al-Makhzūmī informed us; Wuhayb informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar informed us from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \We used to wash the deceased; among us were those who would perform ghusl and among us were those who would not perform ghusl.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ (authentic). Reported by al-Dāraquṭnī (2/72).]"""
"1466","(1467) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham informed us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah informed us. He said: Nāfiʿ said: \We used to wash the deceased; some of us would perform wuḍūʾ and some would perform ghusl. Then we would return and shroud him"," then apply perfume to him"," and pray over him"," and we would not repeat the wuḍūʾ.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ (authentic).]"""
"1467","(1468) And through his chain, he said: Shuʿayb informed me; he said: Nāfiʿ said: \I saw ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar apply perfume to Saʿīd ibn Zayd and carry him among those who carried him. Then he entered the mosque and prayed"," and he did not perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ (authentic). Reported by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (6115).]"""
"1468","(1469) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Karāmah informed us; Abū Usāmah informed us from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar from Abī ʿAbd al-Ghaffār from ʿĀʾishah bint Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, who said: \Saʿd washed Saʿīd ibn Zayd and applied perfume to him. Then he came to the house and performed ghusl. Then he said to us: 'I did not perform ghusl because of washing him; rather"," I performed ghusl because of the heat.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ (authentic). Reported by al-Ḥākim (3/497).]"""
"1469","(1470) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqrīʾ informed us from an old book; Abū Farwah Yazīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Yazīd ibn Sinān informed me; my father informed me; my father Yazīd ibn Sinān informed us; Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah informed us from Jābir from al-Shaʿbī from ʿAlqamah from Ibn Masʿūd, who said: \If your companion is impure"," then perform ghusl. But if he is a believer"," why should we perform ghusl because of the believer?\""\n\nIts chain is not strong.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ through other routes. Reported by Ibn Abī Shaybah (11138).]"""
"1470","(1471) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū al-Yamān al-Ḥakam ibn Nāfiʿ informed us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us from Makḥūl, who said: \I stood beside Anas in this mosque and asked him about wuḍūʾ after (handling) the janāʾiz (deceased). He said: 'We were in prayer and we are returning to prayer"," so there is no wuḍūʾ (required).'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ (authentic).]"""
"1471","(1472) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar narrated from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm that ʿĀʾishah said: \Glory be to Allah! Are the bodies of believing men impure? He is nothing but a man who picked up a stick and carried it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1472","(1473) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to me that Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān narrated from Abī ʿImrān al-Jawnī from Yazīd ibn Bābānūs, who said: I said to ʿĀʾishah, \What do you say about al-ʿirāk?\"" She said"," \""Do you mean al-ḥayḍ (menstruation)?\"" We said"," \""Yes.\"" She said"," \""Call it by the name that Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has given it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad 6/219]"""
"1473","(1474) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Faqīh in Bukhārā informed us that Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ Jazarah narrated to me that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Barqī and Muḥammad ibn Idrīs Abū Ḥātim and Aḥmad ibn Ḥammūyah Abū Sinān al-Balkhī al-Thaqafī all said: Saʿīd ibn al-Ḥakam ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Abī Kathīr informed us that Zayd ibn Aslam narrated from ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿd from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out on the day of al-Aḍḥā or al-Fiṭr to the muṣallā and prayed. Then he turned back and admonished the people, commanding them to give charity. He said, \O people"," give charity.\"" Then he turned and passed by the women and said"," \""O assembly of women"," give charity"," for I have seen that you are the majority of the inhabitants of the Fire.\"" They said"," \""Why is that"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said"," \""You frequently curse and are ungrateful to your husbands. I have not seen anyone more deficient in intellect and religion who overwhelms the mind of a prudent man more than you"," O assembly of women.\"" They said to him"," \""What is the deficiency in our intellect and our religion?\"" He said"," \""Is not the testimony of a woman equal to half the testimony of a man?\"" They said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""That is the deficiency in her intellect. Is it not so that when a woman menstruates"," she neither prays nor fasts?\"" They said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""That is the deficiency in her religion.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam"," and Muslim narrated it from al-Ḥulwānī and others from Ibn Abī Maryam. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 1393]"""
"1474","(1475) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh and Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīh al-Muzakkī informed us — and the wording is that of Abū al-Faḍl — both saying that Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us that Maʿmar narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal from Muʿādhah al-ʿAdawiyyah that a woman asked ʿĀʾishah: \Why does the menstruating woman make up the fasts but not make up the prayers?\"" She said to her"," \""Are you a Ḥarūriyyah?\"" She said"," \""I am not a Ḥarūriyyah"," but I am asking.\"" She said"," \""That used to happen to us during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and we were commanded to make up the fasts but were not commanded to make up the prayers.\""\n\nMaʿmar said: And Ayyūb informed us from Abī Qilābah from Muʿādhah from ʿĀʾishah a similar narration.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq from Maʿmar from ʿĀṣim"," and he also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ḥammād from Ayyūb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 351]"""
"1475","(1476) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us that Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim from his father from ʿĀʾishah, who said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) until we reached Sarf or somewhere near it, and I began menstruating. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me while I was weeping and said, \What is the matter with you? Have you entered the state of nifās (postpartum bleeding)?\"" I said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""This is a matter that Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has decreed for the daughters of Ādam. Perform what the pilgrim performs"," except for the ṭawāf (circumambulation) of the House (the Kaʿbah).\""\n\nShe said: And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered — or she said"," offered a sacrifice — of a cow.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī from Sufyān"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 290]"""
"1476","(1477) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb dictated to us that Ḥusayn ibn Ḥasan ibn Muhājir narrated to us that Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed me that ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Abī al-Aswad from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to extend his head to me from the mosque while he was in iʿtikāf (spiritual retreat), and I would wash his head while I was menstruating.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī, and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from ʿUrwah.\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of Umm ʿAṭiyyah from the Prophet (ﷺ): He commanded the menstruating women to withdraw from the muṣallā of the Muslims. This will be mentioned, Allah willing, in the Book of the Two ʿĪds. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1477","(1478) ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Ṣūfī narrated to us that al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated from Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd who narrated to me that al-Zuhrī narrated from Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wrote a letter to the people of Yemen containing the obligatory acts, the sunnah practices, and the blood-money rulings, and he sent it with ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm. He mentioned the ḥadīth, and in it he said: \And no one should touch the Qurʾān except one who is in a state of purity.\"" Others narrated it as a mursal narration"," and Allah knows best.\n\nAnd it is narrated from Ibn ʿUmar that he disliked the menstruating woman touching the muṣḥaf. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"1478","(1479) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī both informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \The menstruating woman and the one in a state of janābah (major ritual impurity) should not recite anything from the Qurʾān.\"" This narration is not strong. [Munkar]"""
"1479","(1480) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us that Abū ʿAmr, who is al-Awzāʿī, said: Al-Zuhrī was asked about the one in a state of janābah, the woman in nifās (postpartum bleeding), and the menstruating woman. He said: They have not been given permission to recite anything from the Qurʾān.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, and also from ʿAṭāʾ, Abī al-ʿĀliyah, al-Nakhaʿī, and Saʿīd ibn Jubayr regarding the menstruating woman: \She should not recite the Qurʾān.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1480","(1481) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ informed that Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to him from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of Allah, the Most High: {Keep away from women during menstruation} — he said: Keep away from sexual intercourse with their private parts. {And do not approach them until they are pure} — he said: When they become free from the blood and purify themselves with water. {Then come to them from where Allah has commanded you} — he said: In the private part, and do not go beyond that to anything else. Whoever does any of that has indeed transgressed. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ṭabarī 2/392]"
"1481","(1482) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Abū Usāmah narrated from Sufyān from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: **\And do not approach them until they are pure\""** — he said: \""Until the blood ceases.\"" **\""And when they have purified themselves\""** — he said: \""When they have performed ghusl (ritual bath).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1482","(1483) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us that Hushaym narrated from Yūnus from al-Ḥasan regarding the woman in menstruation: when she becomes pure from the blood, he said: \Her husband should not approach her until she performs ghusl.\"" [Ḥasan for other than itself. It was narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah (1029)]"""
"1483","(1484) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that Abū ʿĀmir Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us that al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us that Sālim informed that he heard al-Ḥasan say: \There is no harm for a man to be intimate with his wife when water is not present"," if she has become pure from her menstruation during a journey"," provided she has performed tayammum (dry ablution).\"" [Ḥasan for other than itself. It was narrated by al-Dārimī (1176)]"""
"1484","(1485) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated that it reached him from Sālim and Sulaymān ibn Yasār: that they were asked about the menstruating woman — may her husband approach her if she sees purity before performing ghusl? They both said: \No"," until she performs ghusl.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was narrated by Mālik (127)]"""
"1485","(1486) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us that Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar al-Raqqī narrated to us that Qabīṣah narrated, and Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us that Muḥammad — meaning Ibn Kathīr — narrated; they both said: Sufyān narrated from al-Muthannī ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," we are in the desert for four or five months"," and among us are women in postpartum bleeding"," menstruating women"," and those in janābah (major ritual impurity). What do you advise?\"" He said: **\""Upon you is the earth (i.e."," perform tayammum).\""** [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1486","(1487) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad from ʿĀʾishah who said: \When one of us was menstruating"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would command her to wrap herself with an izār (lower garment)"," and then he would be intimate with her (above it).\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Thawrī from Manṣūr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was narrated by al-Bukhārī (297)]"""
"1487","(1488) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Jurjānī narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Mushhir narrated from al-Shaybānī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad from his father from ʿĀʾishah who said: \When one of us was menstruating"," the Prophet ﷺ would command her to wrap herself at the onset of her menstruation"," then he would be intimate with her (above it). And which of you can control his desires as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ controlled his desires?\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn al-Khalīl from ʿAlī ibn Mushhir"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was narrated by al-Bukhārī (296)]"""
"1488","(1489) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥām al-Muzakkī, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Sabīʿī, Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad al-Sūsī, Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāriq al-ʿAṭṭār, and others said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī informed us that Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad al-Qurashī narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us that Hārūn ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Khālid ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated from al-Shaybānī from ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād from Maymūnah bint al-Ḥārith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would be intimate with his wives above the izār while they were menstruating.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was narrated by Muslim (294)]"""
"1489","(1490) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqrīʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us that al-Shaybānī narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād from Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wished to be intimate with one of his wives while she was menstruating"," he would command her to wrap herself (with an izār).\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Nuʿmān from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was narrated by al-Bukhārī (297)]"""
"1490","(1491) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ḥusayn ibn Ḥasan — meaning ibn Muhājir — narrated to us that Hārūn ibn Saʿīd al-Aylī narrated to us that Ibn Wahb narrated to me that Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated from his father from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \I heard Maymūnah say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would lie down with me while I was menstruating"," with a cloth between me and him.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn al-Aylī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was narrated by Muslim (295)]"""
"1491","(1492) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Ḥāmid ibn Sahl informed us, Muʿādh ibn Faḍālah informed us, Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh informed us.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us verbally, Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī informed us, Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī informed us, Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Zaynab, from Umm Salamah, who said: \I was lying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a blanket when I experienced menstruation. I slipped away quietly and put on the clothes of my menses. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: 'Have you entered the state of menstruation (nufisti)?' I said: 'Yes.' He then called me"," and I lay down with him in the blanket.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it from the ḥadīth of Hishām. [Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 294]"""
"1492","(1493) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqrīʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us, Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us, Khālid narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Umm Salamah, that she was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a blanket when she experienced menstruation. He said to her: \Get up"," wrap yourself with a waist cloth"," then return.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of other narrations. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 6/323]"""
"1493","(1494) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original, Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī informed us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Khālid ibn Makhlad informed us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Sharīk ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Nimr narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a single blanket when I slipped away.\"" He said: \""What is the matter with you?\"" I said: \""I have experienced menstruation.\"" He said: \""Tie your waist cloth firmly"," then come back.\""\n\nMālik narrated it from Rabīʿah from ʿĀʾishah as a mursal narration.\n\nAnd it is possible that this occurred with both ʿĀʾishah and Umm Salamah together.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in virtue of other narrations. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 6/184]"""
"1494","(1495) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadbādhī informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us, ʿUbayd Allāh, meaning Ibn Mūsā, informed us, Isrāʾīl narrated from Miqdām ibn Shurayḥ, from his father, who said: \I asked ʿĀʾishah: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) touch you intimately while you were menstruating?' She said: 'When I was menstruating"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: \""Tie your waist cloth"," O daughter of Abī Bakr","\"" and then he would touch me intimately for a long part of the night.' I asked: 'Did he eat with you while you were menstruating?' She said: 'He would give me a bone"," and I would bite from it. Then he would take it and bite from the same place where I had bitten.' I asked: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) drink from your drink?' She said: 'He would hand me the vessel"," and I would drink. Then he would take it and place his mouth where I had placed mine and drink.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 279]"""
"1495","(1496) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Tamtām informed us, Abū Ḥudhayfah informed us, Sufyān narrated from al-Miqdām ibn Shurayḥ ibn Hāniʾ, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \I would drink from the cup while I was menstruating"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would place his mouth on the place from which I had drunk. And I would take a bone and gnaw from it"," and he would place his mouth on the place from which I had gnawed.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Sufyān al-Thawrī and Misʿar from al-Miqdām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 300]"""
"1496","(1497) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Dāwūd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Makkī narrated from Manṣūr ibn Ṣafiyyah, from his mother, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would recline in my lap while I was menstruating and recite the Qurʾān.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Zuhayr from Manṣūr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 293]"""
"1497","(1498) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Abī ʿImrān al-Jawnī, from Yazīd ibn Bābānūs, who said: \We entered upon ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and he mentioned the hadith"," in which she said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would cover me with a garment and touch my head while I was menstruating and I was wearing a waist cloth.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1498","(1499) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Hārūn ibn Muḥammad ibn Bakkār informed me, Marwān, meaning Ibn Muḥammad, informed us, al-Haythum ibn Ḥumayd informed us, al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Ḥarām ibn Ḥakīm, from his paternal uncle, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): \What is permissible for me from my wife when she is menstruating?\"" He said: \""For you is what is above the waist cloth.\"" He said: \""And he also mentioned eating with the menstruating woman.\"" He (Ḥarām) narrated the hadith. His paternal uncle was ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿd al-Anṣārī. It was also said: Ḥarām ibn Muʿāwiyah from his paternal uncle ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿd.\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 1212]"""
"1499","(1500) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn al-Faḍl informed us, ʿAmr ibn Qusayṭ al-Raqqī informed us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAmr narrated from Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah, from Abī Isḥāq, from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAmr, from ʿUmayr, the freed slave of ʿUmar, who said: \A group of people from Iraq came to ʿUmar. ʿUmar said to them: 'Did you come with permission?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What has brought you?' They said: 'We have come to ask about three things.' He said: 'What are they?' They said: 'A man's voluntary prayer in his house — what is it? And what is permissible for a man from his wife when she is menstruating? And about the ritual bath from janābah.' ʿUmar said: 'Are you sorcerers?' They said: 'No"," O Commander of the Faithful"," we are not sorcerers.' He said: 'You have asked me about three things that no one has asked me about since I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about them before you. As for a man's prayer in his house"," it is light — so illuminate your house as much as you can. As for the menstruating woman"," what is above the waist cloth is permissible"," and what is beneath it is not for him. As for the ritual bath from janābah: pour water with your right hand over your left"," then insert your hand into the vessel and wash your private parts and whatever has afflicted you. Then perform your ablution for prayer. Then pour water over your head three times"," rubbing your head each time. Then wash the rest of your body.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 987]"""
"1500","(1501) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Ḥammād informed us, Thābit al-Bunānī narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The Jews"," when a woman among them menstruated"," would expel her from the house. They would not eat with her"," nor drink with her"," nor cohabit with her in the house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about that"," so Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: 'They ask you about menstruation. Say: It is a harm (adhan)"," so keep away from women during menstruation' [al-Baqarah: 222] to the end of the verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Cohabit with them in the houses"," and do everything except intercourse.' The Jews said: 'This man does not want to leave anything of our practice without opposing us in it.' Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr and ʿAbbād ibn Bishr came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," the Jews say such and such. Shall we not have intercourse with them during menstruation?' The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) changed color"," so we thought he had become angry with them"," and they left. Then a gift of milk was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and he sent someone after them"," who gave them to drink. So we believed that he had not been angry with them.\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl. In the ḥadīth of Abī Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded that they eat with them"," drink with them"," cohabit with them in the houses"," and do whatever they wished except intercourse.\"" He narrated the rest with the same meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī from Ḥammād.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 302]"""
"1501","(1502) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Ṣāliḥ, Ibn Bukayr, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus, and Ibn Rumḥ narrated to us from al-Layth ibn Saʿd, who said: Ibn Shihāb narrated to me from Ḥabīb, the freedman of ʿUrwah, from Nadbah, the freedwoman of Maymūnah, from Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would be intimate with one of her co-wives while she was menstruating, provided she had wrapped a garment reaching the middle of her thighs or her knees, and she would hold it around herself. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 267]"
"1502","(1503) Abū ʿAbdullāl-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī narrated to us: Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated to us from his father, from al-Zuhrī, who said: Ḥabīb, the freedman of ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, informed me that Nadbah, the freedwoman of Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him: Maymūnah sent me to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās with a letter, so I went to him. I found that his bed was separated from the bed of his wife. I returned to Maymūnah and delivered her message to her, then I mentioned that to her. Maymūnah said to me: Go back to his wife and ask her about that. So I went back to her and asked her, and she informed me: When she menstruates, ʿAbdullāh separates his bed from hers. So Maymūnah sent word to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās and rebuked him, saying: Do you turn away from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? By Allah, when one of his wives was menstruating, she would wrap herself with a garment reaching the middle of her thighs, and then he would be intimate with the rest of her body. [Weak. Narrated by Aḥmad 6/332]"
"1503","(1504) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us from Jābir ibn Ṣubayḥ, who said: I heard Khilās al-Hajarī say: I heard ʿĀʾishah say: I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sleep under a single garment while I was menstruating with heavy bleeding. If anything from me reached him, he would wash only that spot and go no further. And if something reached his garment, he would wash only that spot and go no further, and he would pray in it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 269]"
"1504","(1505) Abū ʿAlī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muslimah narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh, meaning Ibn ʿUmar ibn Ghānim, narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning Ibn Ziyād, from ʿUmārah ibn Ghurāb, that his paternal aunt narrated to him: She asked ʿĀʾishah: One of us menstruates, and she and her husband have only one bed. She said: I will tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do. He entered and went to his prayer place — Abū Dāwūd said, meaning the prayer place of his house — and did not turn back until sleep overcame me and the cold distressed him. He said: \Come close to me.\"" I said: \""I am menstruating.\"" He said: \""Even so"," uncover your thighs.\"" So I uncovered my thighs"," and he placed his cheek and his chest upon my thighs. I leaned over him until he became warm and fell asleep. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 270]"""
"1505","(1506) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū Muslim narrated to us: Abū ʿUmar narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated to us from Ayyūb from ʿIkrimah, from one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ, when he wished something from a menstruating woman, would instruct her to place a garment over her private part, and then he would do as he wished. Abū Bakr said: All the wives of the Prophet ﷺ are trustworthy (thiqāt). [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 272]"
"1506","(1507) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abū Isḥāq narrated to us from Abū Mayṣarah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would be intimate with me under a single garment while I was menstruating, but he was the most restrained of you regarding his desire, or he had the greatest control over his desire. Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated it thus, and Isrāʾīl corroborated it. Shuʿbah narrated it, clarifying that this occurred after wrapping the lower garment (iẓtizār). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 272]"
"1507","(1508) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū Mayṣarah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: I would wrap myself with a lower garment while I was menstruating, and I would enter the blanket with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The aḥādīth that have preceded in this chapter are more authentic and more explicit. It is possible that what is intended by those of these narrations that may be authentic is what is clarified in those earlier aḥādīth. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dārimī 1048]"
"1508","(1509) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us: It was read to Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth: Your father informed you from Bukayr, from Abū Murrah, the freedman of ʿAqīl ibn Abī Ṭālib, from Ḥakīm ibn ʿIqāl, who said: I asked ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers: What is forbidden to me from my wife while I am fasting? She said: Her private part. I said: What is forbidden to me from my wife when she is menstruating? She said: Her private part. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains. Narrated by al-Ṭaḥāwī 2/95]"
"1509","(1510) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us: Abū al-Naḍr Hāshim ibn al-Qāsim informed us: al-Ḥakam ibn Fuḍayl informed us: Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ informed us from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Guard against the menstruating woman in the area of the sandal-strap. [Weak]"
"1510","(1511) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī informed us: al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us: al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from al-Ḥakam, from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Miqsam, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ, regarding the one who approaches his wife while she is menstruating, he said: He should give charity of a dīnār or half a dīnār. Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān and ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ al-Khaffāf also narrated it from Shuʿbah. ʿAffān ibn Muslim and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated it from Shuʿbah, stopping it at Ibn ʿAbbās (as a mawqūf narration). Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir informed us: ʿAffān informed us: Shuʿbah narrated to us — and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us: Shuʿbah narrated to us — and he mentioned it with his chain, stopping it at Ibn ʿAbbās. Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm, Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī, Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl, and a group also narrated it from Shuʿbah, stopping it at Ibn ʿAbbās. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī clarified from Shuʿbah that he retracted from raising it (to the Prophet) after he had been raising it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 264]"
"1511","(1512) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh informed us — from his original book — 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to me; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to me; Shu'bah narrated to me from al-Hakam; from 'Abd al-Hamid, i.e., 'Abd al-Rahman; from Miqsam; from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding the one who approaches his wife while she is menstruating — and he (Ibn 'Abbas) mentioned it as a mawquf (stopping at the Companion's level).\n\nIbn Mahdi said: It was said to Shu'bah, \You used to raise it (to the Prophet ﷺ).\"" He replied"," \""I was mad"," and then I recovered.\"" So Shu'bah retracted the raising of the hadith and attributed it to the statement of Ibn 'Abbas. [Sahih Mawquf]"""
"1512","(1513) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid al-'Adani informed us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me; Matar al-Warraq narrated to me from al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah; from Miqsam; from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: \Let him give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.\"" Thus did a group narrate from al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah from Miqsam.\n\nIn the narration of Shu'bah from al-Hakam there is an indication that al-Hakam did not hear it from Miqsam; rather"," he heard it from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab from Miqsam. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""
"1513","(1514) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata' informed us; Sa'id narrated to us from Qatadah; from Miqsam; from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to give a dinar or half a dinar in charity. Qatadah explained it, saying: \If he can afford it"," then a dinar; and if he cannot"," then half a dinar.\""\n\nQatadah did not hear it from Miqsam. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"""
"1514","(1515) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Musa ibn al-Hasan ibn 'Abbad informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Bakr informed us; Sa'id narrated to us from Qatadah; from 'Abd al-Hamid; from Miqsam; from Ibn 'Abbas: that a man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, and he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to give a dinar or half a dinar in charity. And he (Sa'id) did not hear it from 'Abd al-Hamid either. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"
"1515","(1516) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; Isma'il al-Qadi informed us; Hudbah ibn Khalid informed us; Hammad ibn al-Ja'd informed us; Qatadah narrated to me; al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah narrated to me that 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to him that Miqsam narrated to him from Ibn 'Abbas: that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and claimed that he had approached his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet of Allah ﷺ commanded him to give a dinar in charity, and if he could not find one, then half a dinar.\n\nThus did Hammad ibn al-Ja'd narrate it from Qatadah from al-Hakam as a marfu' (raised) hadith. And in the narration of Shu'bah from al-Hakam there is an indication that it is mawquf. And similarly Abu 'Abd Allah al-Shaqari narrated it as mawquf, except that he omitted 'Abd al-Hamid from his chain of narration. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"
"1516","(1517) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us; 'Arim informed us; Sa'id ibn Zayd informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah al-Shaqari — I think — narrated to me from al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah; from Miqsam; from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding the hadith about the menstruating woman when her husband approaches her. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"
"1517","(1518) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us; he said: Abu Dawud al-Sijistani said — and al-Awza'i narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Malik from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, I think, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \I command him to give two-fifths of a dinar in charity.\""\n\nAnd this is a third difference in its chain and text.\n\nIshaq al-Hanzali narrated from Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid from al-Awza'i with this chain from 'Umar ibn al-Khatrab"," may Allah be pleased with him: that he had a wife who disliked men"," so whenever she wanted him"," she would claim menstruation as an excuse"," and he thought she was lying"," so he approached her and found her truthful. He then came to the Prophet ﷺ"," and he commanded him to give two-fifths of a dinar in charity.\n\nAnd similarly Ishaq narrated from 'Isa ibn Yunus from Zayd ibn 'Abd al-Hamid from his father: that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," had a wife — and he mentioned it. And it is munqati' (disconnected) between 'Abd al-Hamid and 'Umar. [Munkar]"""
"1518","(1519) Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah informed us; Sharik narrated to us from Khusayf; from Miqsam; from Ibn 'Abbas; from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When a man has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating"," let him give half a dinar in charity.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Sharik narrated it once and doubted whether to raise it. And al-Thawri narrated it from 'Ali ibn Badhimah and Khusayf"," but he sent it as a mursal (disconnected) hadith. [Sahih li-ghayrihi. Abu Dawud narrated it (no. 1266)]"""
"1519","(1520) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Abu al-Muthanna informed us; Musaddad informed us; Yahya narrated to us from Sufyan; 'Ali ibn Badhimah and Khusayf narrated to me; from Miqsam; from the Prophet ﷺ, regarding the one who approaches his wife while she is menstruating — the hadith. Khusayf al-Jazari is not used as a proof. [Sahih li-ghayrihi]"
"1520","(1521) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us; Abu al-Aswad informed us; Nafi' ibn Yazid narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj; from Umayyah 'Abd al-Karim al-Basri; from Miqsam; from Ibn 'Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you approaches her (his wife) while she is in her blood (menstruating)"," let him give a dinar in charity; and if he has intercourse with her after she has seen purity but has not yet bathed"," let him give half a dinar in charity.\""\n\nThus in the narration of Ibn Jurayj.\n\nAnd Ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated from 'Abd al-Karim"," but he made the explanation (tafsir) as the statement of Miqsam. [Munkar]"""
"1521","(1522) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to give charity of one dīnār or half a dīnār. Miqsam explained that, saying: If he had intercourse with her while the blood was flowing, then one dīnār; and if he had intercourse with her after the cessation of blood before she performed ghusl, then half a dīnār.\n\nIt was also narrated from Saʿīd from ʿAbd al-Karīm from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Munkar]"
"1522","(1523) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us: Abū Qilābah informed us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm Abī Umayyah from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the one who has intercourse with her while she is menstruating: \He should give charity of one dīnār; if he does not find one"," then half a dīnār.\"" Miqsam explained it"," saying: \""If it was during the flow of blood"," then one dīnār; if it was during the cessation of blood"," then half a dīnār; and if she had not performed ghusl"," then half a dīnār.\"" [Munkar]"""
"1523","(1524) Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī narrated it from ʿAbd al-Karīm from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: \If the blood is fresh (ʿabīṭ)"," let him give charity of one dīnār; and if it is yellowish (ṣufrah)"," then half a dīnār.\"" Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Bāghandī and al-Narsī both said: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā al-ʿAbsī narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\nHishām al-Dastawāʾī also narrated it from ʿAbd al-Karīm"," but he stopped it (as a mawqūf narration). [Munkar]"""
"1524","(1525) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Karīm Abī Umayyah narrated from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: \He should give charity of one dīnār or half a dīnār.\"" This is more likely to be correct. And ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn Abī al-Mukhāriq Abī Umayyah is not used as a proof (lāyuḥtāju bihi).\n\nIt was also narrated from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Jazarī from Miqsam"," stopped (mawqūf) at Ibn ʿAbbās"," which corresponds with the explanation of Miqsam. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it]"""
"1525","(1526) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Muṭahhar narrated to us: Jaʿfar, meaning Ibn Sulaymān, narrated from ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥakam al-Bunānī from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Jazarī from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \If he has intercourse with her during the blood"," then one dīnār; and if he has intercourse with her after the cessation of blood"," then half a dīnār.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it]"""
"1526","(1527) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Mufassir, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Ibn ʿAṭāʾ from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: \He should give charity of one dīnār or half a dīnār.\"" And Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAṭāʾ is not used as a proof by his ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it]"""
"1527","(1528) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us: ʿAṭāʾ al-ʿAṭṭār narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: \He should give charity of one dīnār; if he does not find one"," then half a dīnār.\""\n\nʿAṭāʾ is Ibn ʿAjlan"," weak (ḍaʿīf) and abandoned (matrūk). It was also narrated from him from ʿAṭāʾ and ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās"," but it is nothing (laysa bi-shayʾ).\n\nIt was narrated from ʿAṭāʾ and ʿIkrimah that they both said: \""There is nothing upon him; he should seek forgiveness from Allah.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh said: The totality of these reports"," both marfūʿ and mawqūf"," trace back to ʿAṭāʾ al-ʿAṭṭār"," ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd"," and ʿAbd al-Karīm Abī Umayyah"," and there is question regarding them.\n\nThe Shaykh said: It was also narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās as a mawqūf narration. If it is preserved"," then it is a valid statement of Ibn ʿAbbās. [Bāṭil]"""
"1528","(1529) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Abū al-Jawāb narrated to us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the man who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating. He said: \If he has intercourse with her during the blood"," he should give charity of one dīnār; and if he has intercourse with her not during the blood"," he should give charity of half a dīnār.\"" Imām Aḥmad"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ"," who said: \""There is nothing upon him except that he should seek forgiveness from Allah"," the Most High.\""\n\nThe well-known narration from Ibn Jurayj is from ʿAbd al-Karīm Abī Umayyah from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās"," as has been mentioned previously. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīgh]"""
"1529","(1530) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ said:\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy upon him, said — meaning in the book Aḥkām al-Qurʾān — regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating or after the cessation of blood before she has performed ghusl: \He should seek forgiveness from Allah"," the Most High"," and not repeat it until she becomes pure"," and ṣalāh becomes permissible for her. Something has been narrated regarding this"," and if it were established"," we would take it"," but the like of it is not established.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh]"""
"1530","(1531) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — read to him — Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Shaʿbī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Arzunānī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ṭāhir ibn Ḥarmalah narrated to us: My grandfather narrated to me: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to me, saying: \I saw in Ṣanʿāʾ a grandmother at the age of twenty-one. She began menstruating at the age of nine and gave birth at the age of ten. And her daughter began menstruating at the age of nine and gave birth at the age of ten.\""\n\nIt is mentioned from al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ that he said: \""I came across a female neighbor of ours who became a grandmother at the age of twenty-one.\""\n\nAnd from Mughīrah al-Ḍabbī that he said: \""I experienced wet dreams (iḥtilām) at the age of twelve.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," that she said: \""When a girl reaches nine years of age"," she is a woman\"" — meaning"," and Allah knows best"," that when she menstruates"," she is a woman. [Mawḍūʿ]"""
"1531","(1532) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us; 'Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Junayd informed us; al-Nufayli said: I read to Ma'ql, from 'Ata', who said: The minimum duration of menstruation is one day.\n\n[Authenticated by others. Narrated by al-Darimi, 845.]"
"1532","(1533) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Asamm informed us; al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri informed us; Muhammad ibn Mus'ab said: I heard al-Awza'i saying: Here among us is a woman who menstruates in the morning and becomes pure by the evening.\n\n[Hasan. Narrated by al-Daraqutni, 1/309.]"
"1533","(1534) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; he said: Ishaq said:\n\n'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi said: There was a woman called Umm al-'Ala' who said: My menstruation has been two days since time immemorial.\n\nHe said: And Ishaq said: It has been authentically established for us in our time from more than one woman that she said, \My menstruation is two days.\""\n\nAnd Yazid ibn Harun said: I have a woman who menstruates for two days.\n\nAnd in what Abu 'Abdillah permitted me to narrate from him"," from Abu al-'Abbas"," from al-Rabi'"," from al-Shafi'i"," that he said: I saw a woman whose menstruation was established to me as never exceeding one day"," and it was established to me from women that they never menstruated less than three days"," and from women that they never menstruated less than fifteen days"," and from one woman or more that they never menstruated less than thirteen days. How can you claim that what we have known to occur does not occur?\n\nThe Sheikh said: And it has been narrated from 'Ali and Shurayh that they both permitted three menstrual cycles in a month and five nights. This will be addressed in the Book of 'Iddah"," Allah the Most High willing.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: And we hold the view narrated from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)"," because it is in accordance with what has been narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he did not assign a fixed time for menstruation.\n\nHe cited as evidence the hadith of the Prophet (peace be upon him): \""When menstruation begins"," abandon the prayer. When its duration has passed"," wash the blood from yourself and pray.\""\n\n[Authenticated.]"""
"1534","(1535) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Malik informed us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that she said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh said to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): \O Messenger of Allah"," I never become pure; should I abandon the prayer?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""That is from a vein and is not menstruation. When menstruation begins"," abandon the prayer. When its duration has passed"," wash the blood from yourself and pray.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abdillah ibn Yusuf"," from Malik.\n\n[Authenticated. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 300.]"""
"1535","(1536) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; Abu Muhammad 'Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Hayyan, Abu al-Shaykh al-Isbahani, informed us; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah narrated to me; Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us; Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhal, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', who said: The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days.\n\n[Authenticated. Narrated by al-Darimi, 833.]"
"1536","(1537) Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated it from Yahya ibn Adam, from Mufaddal, and Ibn al-Mubarak, from Sufyan, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', who said: The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days. And this was the view to which Ahmad ibn Hanbal inclined.\n\nAbu Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us of that; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us; al-Husayn ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Sa'd al-Zuhri narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\n[Authenticated. Narrated by al-Daraqutni, 1/208.]"
"1537","(1538) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid al-Faqih informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us; Waki' narrated, from al-Rabi', from al-Hasan, who said: She sits for fifteen days.\n\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Darimi, 833.]"
"1538","(1539) And by his chain, from al-Rabi', from 'Ata', who said: Menstruation is fifteen days.\n\n[Authenticated by others.]"
"1539","(1540) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us; Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Marwazi informed us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Subayh narrated to us, from 'Ata', who said: Menstruation is fifteen days. If it exceeds that, then she is a mustahadah (one experiencing irregular bleeding). He said: And I saw Ibn Mahdi incline toward the view of 'Ata' regarding menstruation.\n\nIbn Mahdi said: There was among us a woman whose menstruation was fifteen days.\n\n[Authenticated by others.]"
"1540","(1541) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl informed us; Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Mutarrif narrated to us; 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from his brother, and Yahya ibn Sa'id, and Rabi'ah, that they said regarding the menstruating woman: The maximum period for which she refrains from prayer is fifteen days; then she performs ghusl and prays.\n\n'Abdillah said: And I found the people saying that.\n\n[Authenticated.]"
"1541","(1542) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥannāṭ narrated to us; Abū Hishām al-Rifāʿī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us.\n\nʿAlī said: And Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Mukharramī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us; Sharīk narrated to us, saying: \We have among us a woman who menstruates fifteen days of the month with a regular"," consistent menstrual period.\""\n\nʿAlī said: And Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥannāṭ narrated to us; Abū Hishām narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated from Sharīk and Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ"," both of whom said: \""The maximum duration of menstruation is fifteen days.\"" And as for the hadith which… [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/209]"""
"1542","(1543) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from al-Jald ibn Ayyūb from Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah from Anas, who said: \The woman experiencing istihādah (irregular bleeding) waits three"," five"," seven"," nine"," ten — she does not exceed that.\"" [Very weak (Ḍaʿīf jiddan). Narrated by al-Dārimī"," 839]"""
"1543","(1544) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; al-Jald ibn Ayyūb narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah, who said: Anas ibn Mālik said: \The menstrual period of a woman is five"," six"," seven"," eight"," ten; then she performs ghusl (ritual bath)"," fasts"," and prays.\""\n\nThis hadith is known through al-Jald ibn Ayyūb"," and he has been criticized for it. [Very weak (Ḍaʿīf jiddan)]"""
"1544","(1545) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī said regarding the hadith of al-Jald ibn Ayyūb: \Ibn ʿUlayyah informed me from al-Jald ibn Ayyūb from Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah from Anas ibn Mālik that he said: 'The menstrual period (qurʾ) of a woman' — or he said"," 'the menstruation (ḥayḍ) of a woman' — 'is three"," four"," up to ten.'\""\n\nIbn ʿUlayyah said to me: \""Al-Jald ibn Ayyūb is a Bedouin who does not know hadith.\""\n\nHe also said to me: \""A woman from the family of Anas experienced istihādah"," and Ibn ʿAbbās was asked about her"," and he issued a fatwā concerning her while Anas was still alive. How could Anas ibn Mālik possess the knowledge of menstruation that you describe"," yet his own family would need to ask someone else about a matter in which he had knowledge?\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""We and you do not establish the hadith of one like al-Jald"," and the error of one who is more reliable than him is indicated by even less than this.\""\n\nAbū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us"," saying: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb said: \""Ḥammād\"" — meaning ibn Zayd — \""used to weaken al-Jald and say: 'He did not understand hadith.'\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us"," saying: As for the report of Anas"," Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us"," saying: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us"," saying: \""I and Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim went to al-Jald ibn Ayyūb"," and he narrated to us the hadith of Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah from Anas concerning the menstruating woman. We went to confront him"," and lo"," he did not distinguish between the menstruating woman (ḥāʾiḍ) and the woman with istihādah (mustaḥāḍah).\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Dārimī informed us"," saying: I heard Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq say: I heard Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī say: \""I asked Abū ʿĀṣim about al-Jald ibn Ayyūb"," and he severely weakened him and said: 'He was a shaykh from among the Arab shaykhs; our colleagues were lax in narrating from him.'\""\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us in Baghdad; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us"," saying: ʿAbd Allāh — meaning ibn al-Mubārak — said: \""The people of Basra reject the hadith of al-Jald ibn Ayyūb and say: 'He is a shaykh from among the Arab shaykhs; he is not a hadith scholar.'\""\n\nIbn al-Mubārak said: \""And the people of Egypt know him better than others.\"" Yaʿqūb said: \""And I heard Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," Ṣadaqah ibn al-Faḍl"," and Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm"," and it has reached me from Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," that they all weaken al-Jald ibn Ayyūb and do not consider him as a source of authoritative evidence (ḥujjah).\""\n\nAbū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Junaydī — meaning Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Junayd — narrated to us; al-Bukhārī narrated to us; ʿAbdān narrated from Ibn al-Mubārak"," who said: \""The people of Basra weaken the hadith of al-Jald ibn al-Baṣrī.\"" He said: \""And Ṣadaqah narrated to me"," saying: 'Ibn ʿUyaynah used to say: \""And who is al-Jald? And who was al-Jald?\""'\""\n\nAnd Abū Saʿd al-Ṣūfī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; Ibn Ḥammād — meaning Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥammād — narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad — meaning Ibn Ḥanbal — narrated to us"," saying: I heard my father mention al-Jald ibn Ayyūb and say: \""His hadith is not worth anything; he is weak in hadith.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And hadiths have been narrated concerning the minimum and maximum duration of menstruation that are weak"," the weakness of which I have explained in the Khilāfiyāt.\"" [Very weak (Ḍaʿīf jiddan)]"""
"1545","(1546) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā both informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Hishām narrated from his father from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \Fāṭimah ibn Abī Ḥubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'I am a woman who experiences istihādah (irregular bleeding) and never become pure; should I abandon the prayer?' He said: 'No"," that is only a vein (ʿirq) and is not menstruation (ḥayḍ). When menstruation comes"," leave the prayer"," and when it departs"," wash the blood from yourself and pray.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1546","(1547) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Muʾaddib narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Zuḥayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. He mentioned it with its chain, similar to it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus, and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\nAnd thus Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, Ḥammād ibn Zayd, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad, Abū Muʿāwiyah al-Ḍarīr, Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr, and a large group narrated it from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah — except that Ḥammād added wuḍūʾ (ablution) in it, and Ibn ʿUyaynah added ghusl (ritual bath) with uncertainty (shakk).\n\nAnd Mālik ibn Anas, the Imam, narrated it from Hishām and said in the hadith: \When her usual duration has passed"," wash the blood from yourself and pray.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1547","(1548) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to me; Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I never become pure; should I abandon the prayer?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'That is only a vein and is not menstruation. When menstruation comes"," leave the prayer"," and when its duration has passed"," wash the blood from yourself and pray.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik.\n\nAnd al-Bukhārī narrated it from Aḥmad ibn Abī Rajāʾ from Abū Usāmah from Hishām"," but he differed from them in its text (matn)"," saying in the hadith: \""He said: 'No"," that is a vein. But leave the prayer for the number of days in which you used to menstruate"," then perform ghusl and pray.'\""\n\nAnd something has been narrated from Abū Usāmah indicating that he was uncertain about it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1548","(1549) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Yāsīn narrated to me; Muḥammad ibn Karāmah al-Kūfī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr and Abū Usāmah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) Abū Bakr said: And ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me; Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Abū Usāmah, Muḥammad ibn Kanāsah, and Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated from Hishām from his father from ʿĀʾishah: \That Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'I experience istihādah and never become pure; should I abandon the prayer?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'That is only a vein. But leave the prayer for the days in which you used to menstruate"," then perform ghusl and pray.'\"" Or as he said. \""And I believe the hadith is according to the wording of Abū Usāmah"," for we have narrated from others the wording that the group narrated from Hishām.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abū Usāmah with the wording that the group narrated regarding the onset and departure of menstruation. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1549","(1550) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ibn Karāmah narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. He mentioned it and said in the hadith: \Should I abandon the prayer?\"" He said: \""That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. When menstruation comes"," leave the prayer"," and when it departs"," perform ghusl and pray.\""\n\nThis is more likely to be the preserved version due to its agreement with the narration of the group"," except that he said: \""Then perform ghusl (fa-ghtasli).\""\n\nAnd Ibn ʿUyaynah also said it with uncertainty (shakk). And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1550","(1551) Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr — meaning Ibn ʿAlqamah — narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah: \That Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh used to experience istihādah"," and the Prophet ﷺ said to her: 'The blood of menstruation (dam al-ḥayḍah) is black and recognizable. When that occurs"," refrain from the prayer. When it is the other (blood)"," perform wuḍūʾ and pray"," for it is only a vein (ʿirq).'\""\n\nʿAbd Allāh said: I heard my father say: \""Ibn Abī ʿAdī used to narrate it to us from ʿĀʾishah"," then he abandoned it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain (Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrih). Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 286]"""
"1551","(1552) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us that Ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated from Muḥammad, meaning Ibn ʿAmr, that Ibn Shihāb narrated to me from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr from Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh: that she was experiencing istihāḍah (irregular bleeding), so the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \The blood of menstruation (ḥayḍ) is a black blood that is recognizable. When that occurs"," then abstain from prayer. When it is the other (i.e."," non-menstrual bleeding)"," then perform wuḍūʾ and pray"," for it is only a vein (ʿirq).\""\n\nIbn al-Muthannā said: Ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated it to us from his book thus"," and then he narrated it to us from memory"," saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from ʀāʾishah: that Fāṭimah was experiencing istihāḍah. And he mentioned its meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"1552","(1553) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, saying that Abū Dāwūd said that Makhūl said: \Women are not unaware of menstruation; its blood is black and thick. When that departs and it becomes thin and yellowish"," then she is a mustahāḍah (one experiencing irregular bleeding). Let her perform ghusl and pray.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: The meaning of what Makhūl said has been narrated in a marfūʿ (elevated) narration from Abī Umāmah through a weak chain. [Weak]"""
"1553","(1554) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that al-Bāghandī — Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān — narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us that Ḥassān ibn Ibrāhīm al-Kirmānī informed us that ʿAbd al-Malik informed us from al-ʿAlāʾ, who said: I heard Makhūl say, from Abī Umāmah al-Bāhilī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — and he mentioned the hadith, saying: \The blood of menstruation is black and thick"," with redness over it"," and the blood of the mustahāḍah is yellow and thin. If it overcomes her"," let her use a cotton pad (kursuf). If it overcomes her again"," let her add another one. If it overcomes her during prayer"," let her not break the prayer even if it drips. And her husband may come to her"," and she fasts and prays.\""\n\nThis ʿAbd al-Malik is unknown (majhūl)"," and al-ʿAlāʾ is Ibn Kathīr"," who is weak in hadith. Makhūl did not hear anything from Abī Umāmah"," and Allah knows best.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us of that from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī"," the ḥāfiẓ. [Bāṭil (False). Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/218]"""
"1554","(1555) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Hārūn ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʀāʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh was experiencing istihāḍah, so she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that. He said: \That is only a vein and not menstruation. When menstruation comes"," leave the prayer"," and when it departs"," perform ghusl and pray.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad from Sufyān"," thus. And Ibn ʿUyaynah used to have doubts about the mention of ghusl in it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1555","(1556) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us that al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us that Sufyān narrated to us that Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated — and he mentioned it with its chain and its meaning, saying: \And when it departs"," perform ghusl and pray.\"" Or he said: \""Wash the blood from yourself and pray.\""\n\nIt has also been narrated with the addition of wuḍūʾ for every prayer"," but it is not preserved (maḥfūẓah). Abū Usāmah narrated it from Hishām and mentioned ghusl in it; however"," he contradicted the majority (al-jamāʿah) in its context (siyāq). In the report there is an indication that he used to have doubts about it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1556","(1557) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed us that my father informed me, saying: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: Ibn Shihāb narrated to me that ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr and ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd ibn Zurārah informed me that ʀāʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh, who was married to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, experienced istihāḍah for seven years. She complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. When menstruation comes"," leave the prayer"," and when it departs"," perform ghusl and then pray.\"" ʀāʾishah said: Umm Ḥabībah used to sit in a vessel (mirkan) belonging to her sister Zaynab bint Jaḥsh"," to the extent that the redness of the blood would rise to the surface of the water.\n\nThe mention of ghusl in this hadith is authentic"," and his statement: \""When menstruation comes and when it departs\"" — al-Awzāʿī is alone in narrating it from among the trustworthy companions of al-Zuhrī. The authentic position is that Umm Ḥabībah had a regular habit (muʿtādah)"," and this wording was mentioned by Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʀāʾishah in the story of Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh. Bishr ibn Bakr narrated it from al-Awzāʿī just as others among the trustworthy narrators did. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 2004]"""
"1557","(1558) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī narrated to us that Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us that al-Awzāʿī narrated to me that al-Zuhrī narrated to me that ʿUrwah and ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd ibn Zurārah informed me that ʀāʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh, who was married to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, experienced istihāḍah for seven years. She complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \This is not menstruation; rather"," it is a vein. Perform ghusl and then pray.\"" ʀāʾishah said: She used to perform ghusl for every prayer and then pray"," and she would sit in a vessel belonging to her sister Zaynab bint Jaḥsh"," to the extent that the redness of the blood would rise to the surface of the water. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1558","(1559) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us that ʿAffān narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us that Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated from ʿIkrimah from ʀāʾishah, who said: A wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed iʿtikāf with him while she was a mustahāḍah, and she would see redness and yellowness. Sometimes we would place a basin (ṭast) beneath her while she was praying.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 3004]"
"1559","(1560) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān and ʿImrān ibn Mūsā both said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah informed us that Khālid narrated — Abū Bakr said: and Ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm narrated to me that Isḥāq ibn Shāhīn narrated to us that Khālid, meaning Ibn ʿAbd Allāh, narrated from Khālid, meaning al-Ḥadhāʾ, from ʿIkrimah from ʀāʾishah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed iʿtikāf, and some of his wives performed iʿtikāf with him while she was a mustahāḍah, seeing blood. Sometimes she would place a basin beneath her because of the blood.\n\nHe (the narrator) claimed that ʀāʾishah saw saffron-colored water and said: \This is as though it is something that so-and-so used to experience.\"" The wording is that of Wahb"," and the hadith of Isḥāq is the same. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Shāhīn. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1560","(1561) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Khālid narrated to us that Muʿallā, meaning Ibn Manṣūr, narrated from ʿAlī ibn Mushhir from al-Shaybānī from ʿIkrimah, who said: Umm Ḥabībah was experiencing istihāḍah, and her husband would have intercourse with her. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 309]"
"1561","(1562) Abū ʿAlīyy informed us that Abū Bakr informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Aḥmad ibn Abī Surayj al-Rāzī informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Jahm informed us that ʿAmr ibn Abī Qays informed us from ʿĀṣim from ʿIkrimah from Ḥamnah bint Jaḥsh: that she was experiencing istiḥāḍah (irregular vaginal bleeding), and her husband would have intercourse with her.\n\nIt is narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that he permitted intercourse with her, and this is the view of Ibn al-Musayyab, al-Ḥasan, ʿAṭāʾ, Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh in other than this chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd, 310]"
"1562","(1563) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: I asked my father about intercourse with a woman experiencing istiḥāḍah, and he said: Wakīʿ informed us from Sufyān from Ghaylān from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Maysarah from al-Shaʿbī from Qamīr from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The woman experiencing istiḥāḍah is not to be approached by her husband.\"" My father said: \""And I saw in the book of al-Ashjaʿī the same as what Wakīʿ narrated.\""\n\nGhandar narrated it from Shuʿbah from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Maysarah from al-Shaʿbī that he said: \""The woman experiencing istiḥāḍah is not to be approached by her husband.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated it from Shuʿbah"," and he distinguished the statement of al-Shaʿbī from the statement of ʿĀʾishah.\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Dārimī"," 830]"""
"1563","(1564) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him that Makhlad ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Jaʿfar al-Firyābī informed us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh informed us that my father informed us that Shuʿbah informed us from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Maysarah from al-Shaʿbī from Qamīr, the wife of Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The woman experiencing istiḥāḍah should abstain from ṣalāh during the days of her ḥayḍ (menstruation)"," then she should perform ghusl (ritual bath) and make wuḍūʾ (ablution) for every ṣalāh.\""\n\nHe said: And al-Shaʿbī said: \""She does not fast"," and her husband does not approach her.\""\n\nThe matter of intercourse with her reverts to the statement of al-Shaʿbī"," as Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal stated.\n\nWe have left it based on what has preceded regarding the evidence permitting intercourse with her when her ḥayḍ has passed and she has performed ghusl.\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 16960]"""
"1564","(1565) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-āfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī and Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan both said: al-Qaʿnabī informed us that Mālik informed us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah that Fāṭimah ibn Abī Ḥubaysh said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I do not become pure; should I abandon the ṣalāh?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""That is only a vein and not ḥayḍ. So when it (the ḥayḍ) comes"," abandon the ṣalāh"," and when its duration has passed"," wash the blood from yourself and pray.\"" The wording is from Ismāʿīl.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1565","(1566) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Farrāʾ informed us that Muḥāḍir ibn al-Muwarrʿ informed us that Hishām informed us.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad informed us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah: that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am experiencing istiḥāḍah and do not become pure; should I abandon the ṣalāh?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""That is only a vein and is not ḥayḍ. So when the ḥayḍ comes"," abandon the ṣalāh"," and when it has gone"," wash the blood from yourself and then pray.\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," and the ḥadīth of Muḥāḍir carries the same meaning. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1566","(1567) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us that al-Layth informed us from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from Jaʿfar from ʿIrāk from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah that she said: \Umm Ḥabībah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the blood.\"" ʿĀʾishah said: \""I saw her vessel full of blood.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \""Remain (in abstention) for the duration that your ḥayḍ used to hold you back"," then perform ghusl.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿd"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ considered her in both cases: when her ḥayḍ had departed"," or the duration that her ḥayḍ used to hold her had passed"," she was to be considered among the pure women"," and he did not command istitḥārah (seeking purification). It has also been narrated in a weak ḥadīth something that might suggest that there is [a command for istitḥārah in it]. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 65]"""
"1567","(1568) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq informed us that Ibn ʿAbd al-Malik, meaning Muḥammad, informed us that al-Firyābī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh informed us from Ḥarām ibn ʿUthmān from Ibn Jābir from his father: that the daughter of Mardath al-Anṣāriyyah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \My ḥayḍ has become unrecognizable.\"" He said: \""How?\"" She said: \""It takes me"," and when I become pure from it"," it returns to me.\"" He said: \""When you see that"," remain (in abstention) for three (days).\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," Abū Bakr"," meaning Ibn Isḥāq"," said: \""The report is weak.\""\n\nAnd it is possible that he said that because purity often occurs in the middle of ḥayḍ"," and then there is ḥayḍ after that.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Ḥarām ibn ʿUthmān is weak; a ḥujjah (proof) cannot be established by someone like him. [Very weak]"""
"1568","(1569) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us that Ibrāhīm, meaning Ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Saʿdī, informed us that Yazīd, meaning Ibn Hārūn, informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us that al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm informed him: that he asked Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab about the woman experiencing istiḥāḍah, and he said: \O my nephew"," no one knows more about this than I do. When the ḥayḍ comes"," let her abandon the ṣalāh"," and when it departs"," let her perform ghusl and then pray.\""\n\nLikewise"," Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it from Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dārimī"," 787]"""
"1569","(1570) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Isḥāq, meaning Ibn Bakr ibn Muḍar, informed us from his father from Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah from ʿIrāk ibn Mālik from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh"," who was married to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf"," complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the blood"," and he said to her: 'Remain (in abstention) for the duration that your ḥayḍ used to hold you back"," then perform ghusl.'\"" And she used to perform ghusl at every ṣalāh.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Quraysh al-Tamīmī from Isḥāq ibn Bakr. Likewise"," Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated it from Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 334]"""
"1570","(1571) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him that Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us that Qutaybah informed us that al-Layth informed us.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that Ibn Milḥān informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us from al-Layth from Yazīd from Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah from ʿIrāk ibn Mālik from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah: that Umm Ḥabībah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the blood. ʿĀʾishah said: \I saw her vessel filled with blood.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \""Remain (in abstention) for the duration that your ḥayḍ used to hold you back"," then perform ghusl.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth. And al-Zuhrī narrated it from ʿUrwah in an abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1571","(1572) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to me — Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us — al-Layth, and (separately) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Salama narrated to us — Qutayba ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — al-Layth, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwa ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾisha, that she said: Umm Ḥabība bint Jaḥsh asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \I suffer from istiḥāḍa (irregular bleeding).\"" He ﷺ said: \""That is merely a vein. Then perform ghusl (ritual bath) and pray.\"" So she would perform ghusl for every prayer.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutayba"," and thus did a group narrate it from al-Zuhri. And Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ narrated it from al-Zuhri from ʿUrwa"," differing from them in both the isnād and the text. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1572","(1573) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — al-Asfāṭī, and Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsa narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd — both saying: Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us — Jarīr narrated, from Suhayl, meaning Ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from al-Zuhri, from ʿUrwa ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Fāṭima bint Abī Ḥubaysh narrated to me that she directed Asmāʾ — or Asmāʾ herself narrated to me — that Fāṭima bint Abī Ḥubaysh directed her to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ﷺ instructed her to remain (i.e., abstain from prayer) for the days she used to remain (during her period), then perform ghusl. Thus did Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrate it from Suhayl.\n\nAnd Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated it from Suhayl, from al-Zuhri, from ʿUrwa, from Asmāʾ, regarding the affair of Fāṭima bint Abī Ḥubaysh, mentioning the description of her ghusl when she saw yellowish water above the water.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAlqama narrated it from al-Zuhri, from ʿUrwa, from Fāṭima, mentioning her istiḥāḍa and the Prophet's ﷺ instruction to her to abstain from prayer when she saw black blood.\n\nIn this, and in the narration of Hishām ibn ʿUrwa from his father from ʿĀʾisha, there is evidence that Fāṭima bint Abī Ḥubaysh used to distinguish between the two types of blood. The narration of Suhayl is subject to scrutiny, and in his isnād and in the second narration from him there is evidence that he did not preserve it as it should have been preserved. [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd narrated it, no. 281]"
"1573","(1574) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ibn Milḥān narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us — al-Layth, from Ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from al-Mundhir ibn al-Mughīra, from ʿUrwa ibn al-Zubayr, that Fāṭima bint Abī Ḥubaysh narrated to him: She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and complained to him about the bleeding. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \That is merely a vein. Look — when your period (qurʾ) comes"," do not pray. And when the period has passed"," then purify yourself (taṭahharī) and pray between one period and the next.\""\n\nIn this there is evidence that he did not preserve it"," even though it was a hearing of ʿUrwa from Fāṭima bint Abī Ḥubaysh. For Hishām ibn ʿUrwa has clarified that his father only heard the account of Fāṭima bint Abī Ḥubaysh from ʿĀʾisha"," and his narration in both the isnād and the text is more authentic than the narration of al-Mundhir ibn al-Mughīra.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: And Qatāda narrated it from ʿUrwa ibn al-Zubayr"," from Zaynab bint Umm Salama: that Umm Ḥabība bint Jaḥsh suffered from istiḥāḍa"," and the Prophet ﷺ instructed her to leave the prayer during the days of her period"," then perform ghusl and pray.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: Qatāda did not hear anything from ʿUrwa.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And the narration of ʿIrak ibn Mālik from ʿUrwa from ʿĀʾisha regarding the affair of Umm Ḥabība is more authentic than this narration.\n\nAs for the narration of Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit from ʿUrwa from ʿĀʾisha regarding the affair of Fāṭima"," then it is weak (ḍaʿīfa)"," and the explanation of its weakness will come"," if Allah the Most High wills. Likewise"," the ḥadīth of ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd al-Kātib from Ibn Abī Mulayka from Fāṭima is weak. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 3482]"""
"1574","(1575) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Qutayba narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar informed us — Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā — Yaḥyā ibn al-Mutawakkil, Abū ʿAqīl, from Buhayya, who said: I heard a woman asking ʿĀʾisha — meaning about the cause of her ḥayḍ — not knowing how to pray. ʿľisha said to her: \I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman whose ḥayḍ had become disrupted and who was shedding blood"," not knowing how to pray.\"" She said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed me to tell her to consider the number of days and nights she used to menstruate in each month before the affliction befell her — and her regular period — and to count those days and nights"," then to abstain from prayer for that duration"," then to perform ghusl and perfect her purification"," then to use a cloth as a sanitary pad (istithfār)"," then for her to pray. I hope that this is from Satan"," and that Allah the Most High will remove it from her"," if Allah the Most High wills.\"" She said: \""So I instructed her and she did so"," and Allah removed it from her. So instruct your companion to do likewise.\"" These are the words of the ḥadīth of Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī. [Munkar. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 284]"""
"1575","(1576) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed us from Mālik. (Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf, by dictation, narrated: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik, from Nāfīʿ, mawlā of Ibn ʿUmar, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: that a woman used to shed blood during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Umm Salama asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on her behalf. He ﷺ said: \Let her consider the number of nights and days she used to menstruate in the month before the affliction befell her"," then let her leave the prayer for that amount of the month. And when that has passed"," let her perform ghusl"," use a cloth as a sanitary pad (istithfār)"," and then let her pray.\"" These are the words of the ḥadīth of al-Shāfiʿī. This is a well-known ḥadīth which Mālik ibn Anas included in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ"," and Abū Dāwūd narrated it in Kitāb al-Sunan — except that Sulaymān ibn Yasār did not hear it directly from Umm Salama. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 275]"""
"1576","(1577) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān al-Ahwāzī informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ibn Milḥān narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us — al-Layth, from Nāfīʿ, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that a man informed him from Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: that a woman used to shed blood during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Umm Salama asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on her behalf. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let her consider the number of days and nights she used to menstruate before the affliction befell her"," and their extent in the month"," and let her leave the prayer for that. And when that has passed and the time of prayer arrives"," let her perform ghusl"," use a cloth as a sanitary pad"," and pray.\"" ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqba"," Ṣakhr ibn Juwayriyya"," and Juwayriyya bint Asmāʾ followed him (in narrating) from Nāfīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1577","(1578) As for the ḥadīth of ʿUbayd Allāh: Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsa narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslama narrated to us — Anas, meaning Ibn ʿIyāḍ, narrated — from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfīʿ, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from a man among the Anṣār: that a woman used to shed blood. He mentioned the meaning of the ḥadīth of al-Layth and said: \And when that has passed and the time of prayer arrives"," let her perform ghusl.\"" And he narrated its meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1578","(1579) As for the ḥadīth of Ismāʿīl: Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yazīd narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Abī ʿAbbād narrated — Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUqba, from Nāfīʿ, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that a man informed him from Umm Salama: that a woman used to shed blood during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Umm Salama said to her: \Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Let her consider the number of days and nights she used to menstruate before the affliction befell her"," and their extent in the month"," then let her leave the prayer for that amount"," then perform ghusl"," then use a cloth as a sanitary pad in her garment"," then let her pray.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1579","(1580) As for the ḥadīth of Ṣakhr: al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad informed us — Ibn Dāsa narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Mahdī narrated to us — Ṣakhr ibn Juwayriyya, from Nāfīʿ, with the isnād of al-Layth and its meaning, and he said: \Let her leave the prayer for that amount"," then when the time of prayer arrives"," let her perform ghusl"," use a cloth as a sanitary pad"," and pray.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1580","(1581) As for the ḥadīth of Juwayriyya bint Asmāʾ: Abū Naṣr ibn Qatāda informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Hāshim al-Baghawī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to me — Juwayriyya bint Asmāʾ, from Nāfīʿ, that Sulaymān ibn Yasār informed him, that a man informed him from Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: that a woman used to shed blood during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Umm Salama asked the Prophet ﷺ on her behalf. He ﷺ said: \Let her consider the number of nights and days she used to menstruate before the affliction befell her"," and their extent in the months"," then let her leave the prayer for that amount. And when that has passed and the time of prayer arrives"," let her perform ghusl"," use a cloth as a sanitary pad"," and pray.\""\n\nAnd it was narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqba"," from Nāfīʿ"," from Sulaymān ibn Yasār"," from Marjāna"," from Umm Salama. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1581","(1582) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Isfahani informed us; Muhammad ibn Hamzah narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Imran narrated to us; Khalid ibn Nizar al-Ayli, who was trustworthy, narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Tahman, who was reliable in hadith, narrated to us; Musa ibn 'Uqbah, who was among the trustworthy narrators and from whom Malik used to dictate, narrated to us; Nafi' narrated from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Marjanah from Umm Salamah: that a woman used to suffer from excessive bleeding (istihadah) during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that Umm Salamah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \Let her count the number of days and nights during which she used to menstruate before the condition befell her"," and their extent within the month. Let her abstain from prayer for that duration. When that period has passed"," let her perform ghusl"," fasten a cloth upon herself"," and pray.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Umm Salamah"," except that he named the woman suffering from istihadah in the hadith"," saying: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh. [Sahih]"""
"1582","(1583) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umari al-Muqri' in Baghdad informed us; Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir narrated to us; 'Affan narrated to us; Wuhaib narrated to us; Ayyub narrated from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Umm Salamah: that Fatimah suffered from istihadah and used to perform ghusl from a vessel of hers, and she would come out while traces of yellowness remained upon her. So Umm Salamah sought the fatwa of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on her behalf, and he said: \Let her look at the days of her purity and the days of her menstruation; let her abstain from prayer during those days"," and let her perform ghusl during the rest"," and let her fasten a cloth upon herself and pray.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by Hammad ibn Zayd from Ayyub"," and he said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh. And the hadith of Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father from 'A'ishah concerning the matter of Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh is more authentic than this.\n\nIn this hadith there is evidence that the woman for whom Umm Salamah sought the fatwa was someone other than her. And it may be said — if her naming is authentic in the hadith of Umm Salamah — that she had two conditions during the period of her istihadah: a condition in which she could distinguish between the two types of blood"," and he (the Prophet ﷺ) instructed her to abstain from prayer when the menstrual blood approached and to pray when it receded; and a condition in which she could not distinguish between the two types of blood"," and he instructed her to return to her customary cycle. And other possibilities also exist"," and Allah knows best. It was narrated from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah without naming the woman. [Sahih]"""
"1583","(1584) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated from Abu al-Nadr from Abu Salamah from Umm Salamah from the Prophet ﷺ that he said regarding the woman suffering from istihadah: \She should count the number of nights and days during which she used to menstruate"," then perform ghusl and pray.\"" [Sahih in other chains]"""
"1584","(1585) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Wahban ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir from Fatimah bint Qays, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the woman suffering from istihadah, and he said: \She should sit for the number of days of her menstrual period"," then perform ghusl at every period of purity"," then use padding"," and then pray.\""\n\nAnd thus it was narrated by Qatn ibn Nusayr from Ja'far ibn Sulayman"," and he said in the hadith: \""Indeed"," Fatimah bint Qays asked.\"" And this is not known except from the narration of Ja'far ibn Sulayman. And Allah knows best. [Da'if. Al-Tabarani narrated it in al-Awsat"," 2960]"""
"1585","(1586) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud said: Al-'Ala' ibn al-Musayyab narrated from al-Hakam from Abu Ja'far: that Sawdah suffered from istihadah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her that when her days had passed, she should perform ghusl and pray. Imam Ahmad, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: And in what Ibn Khuzaymah narrated from al-'Atari from Hafs ibn Ghiyath from al-'Ala', it is more complete than that.\n\nAbu Dawud said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated from 'Ali and Ibn 'Abbas: \The woman suffering from istihadah sits for the days of her menstrual period.\"" And likewise al-Sha'bi narrated from Qamirah"," the wife of Masruq"," from 'A'ishah.\n\nAnd it is the statement of al-Hasan"," Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab"," 'Ata'"," Makhul"," Ibrahim"," Salim"," and al-Qasim: that the woman suffering from istihadah abstains from prayer during the days of her menstrual period. [Very Da'if]"""
"1586","(1587) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us; al-'Abbas ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr and Abu al-Nadr both narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Mayssarah, Mujalid, and Bayan. Ibn Abi Bukayr said in his hadith that they heard al-Sha'bi narrating from Qamirah, the wife of Masruq, from 'A'ishah, who said: \The woman suffering from istihadah abstains from prayer during the days of her menstruation"," then performs ghusl"," then makes wudu' for every prayer.\"" [Hasan]"""
"1587","(1588) 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Bashran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us; Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, narrated to us; Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, narrated from Talq, meaning Ibn Habib, who said: A woman wrote to Ibn 'Abbas concerning bleeding that had been continuous for two years. She wrote to him, considering it a grave matter, that if he had any knowledge, he should inform her of it. He replied: \She should sit for the time of her menstrual days"," then perform ghusl and pray.\"" And two months had not passed before she was cured. [Hasan]"""
"1588","(1589) Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-'Adl informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanj narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from 'Alqamah ibn Abi 'Alqamah from his mother, the freed slave of 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said: \The women used to send to 'A'ishah a small box containing cotton with traces of yellow from menstrual blood"," and she would say: 'Do not hasten until you see the white discharge.'\"" By that she meant purity from menstruation. Ibn Bukayr said: \""Al-kursuf is cotton.\"" [Hasan in other chains. Malik narrated it"," 129]"""
"1589","(1590) And with his chain, Malik narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr from his aunt, who narrated to him from the daughter of Zayd ibn Thabit: that it reached her that women used to call for lamps in the depths of the night to examine their purity by it. And she used to disapprove of that for them and say: \The women did not used to do this.\"" And this has been narrated in another way as well. [Sahih. Malik narrated it"," 129]"""
"1590","(1591) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Khalaf narrated to us; 'Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us; Isma'il narrated from 'Abbad ibn Ishaq from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr from 'Amrah from 'A'ishah: that she used to forbid women from examining themselves at night during menstruation, and she would say: \It may be yellowish or darkish.\"" And this has been narrated in a third way as well. [Hasan]"""
"1591","(1592) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Isḥāq, narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr, from his wife Fāṭimah bint Muḥammad, who was in the care of ʿAmrah, that she said: A woman from Quraysh sent to ʿAmrah a cotton cloth containing something yellow — I believe she intended to refer to yellowness — asking her: \If a woman sees nothing from menstruation except this"," is she considered pure?\"" She said: \""No"," until she sees pure whiteness.\""\n\nIt is also narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"," from Fāṭimah bint al-Mundhir"," from Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr.\n\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Dārimī 1860]"""
"1592","(1593) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq the Faqīh informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us.\n\nAnd Ibrāhīm informed us; Abū Bakr, meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah, narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Fāṭimah, from Asmāʾ, who said: \We were in her care"," together with her brother's daughters. One of us would become pure"," then pray"," then experience a slight yellowish discharge"," so she would ask her about it"," and she would say: 'Abstain from prayer as long as you see that"," until you see pure whiteness.'\""\n\n[Sound. Narrated by al-Dārimī 861]"""
"1593","(1594) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq informed us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād informed us; Ashʿath narrated from al-Ḥasan, who said: \When a woman sees a faint trace (al-tarīʾah)"," she should abstain from prayer"," for it is menstruation.\""\n\nAnd Ibrāhīm informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Salām"," from Yaḥyā"," from Abū Salamah"," who said: \""When a woman sees a faint trace (al-tarīʾah)"," let her consider the days during which she used to menstruate"," and let her not pray during them.\"" The correct term is al-tarīyah"," which refers to something faint and slight. [Sound]"""
"1594","(1595) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; Musaddad informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Ayyūb, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Umm ʿAṭiyyah, who said: \We did not consider the turbid (al-kudrah) or the yellowish (al-ṣufrah) discharge to be anything.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," from Ibn ʿUlayyah. [Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 320]"""
"1595","(1596) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī informed us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Abān narrated from Qatādah, from Ḥafṣah, from Umm ʿAṭiyyah, who said: \We did not consider the yellowish (al-ṣufrah) or the turbid (al-kudrah) discharge after purification (al-ṭuhr) to be anything.\"" [Sound]"""
"1596","(1597) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated from Qatādah, from Umm al-Hudhayl, from Umm ʿAṭiyyah, who had given bayʿah to the Prophet ﷺ, and she said: \We did not consider the turbid (al-kudrah) or the yellowish (al-ṣufrah) discharge after purification to be anything.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: \""Umm al-Hudhayl is Ḥafṣah.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Likewise"," Ḥajjāj ibn Minḥāl and others narrated it from Ḥammād ibn Salamah"," and it was also narrated by Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah from Qatādah. It was also narrated from ʿĀʾishah through a weak chain of narration not worth mentioning.\"" [Sound]"""
"1597","(1598) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed me; Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Mubārrak al-Ḥannāṭ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ashras al-Sulamī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Sulaymān al-Zayyāt al-ʿAbadī narrated from Baḥr al-Siqāʾ from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, that she said: \We did not consider the turbid (al-kudrah) or the yellowish (al-ṣufrah) discharge to be anything while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\nIts meaning has also been narrated from ʿĀʾishah through a better chain of narration than that. [Baseless (Bāṭil)]"""
"1598","(1599) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us; Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Rāshid, narrated from Sulaymān, meaning Ibn Mūsā, from ʿAṭāʾ, from ʿĀʾishah, that she said: \When a woman sees blood"," let her abstain from prayer until she sees it white like chalk. When she sees that"," let her perform ghusl and pray. If after that she sees a yellowish or turbid discharge"," let her perform wuḍūʾ and pray. If she sees red blood"," let her perform ghusl and pray.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1599","(1600) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Muʿāwiyah ibn Salām narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us; Abū Salamah narrated that Umm Abī Bakr informed him that ʿĀʾishah informed her that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding a woman who sees something doubtful after purification: \It is only a vein"," or it is only veins.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Aḥmad 2/71]"""
"1600","(1601) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us; Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Sābiq, narrated to us; Shaybān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Umm Abī Bakr, that she informed him that ʿĀʾishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A woman sees something of blood after purification — what should she do?\"" He said: \""It is only a vein"," or veins.\"" This may mean that the intended reference is to the yellowish discharge"," or it may mean when the bleeding exceeds fifteen days. And Allah knows best."""
"1601","(1602) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated to us; Miṣʿar narrated from Abū Bakr ibn ʿUmārah ibn Ruwaybah, from the sister of Abū Bakr ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿUtbah, from Umm Salamah, who said: \One of us would remain with her yellowness (i.e."," traces of menstrual blood) at the time she performed ghusl.\"" [Weak. Al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Kabīr 1009]"""
"1602","(1603) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAmr al-ʿAqadī narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qāḍī informed us; al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us; Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr al-Raqqī narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl, from Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah, from his uncle ʿImrān ibn Ṭalḥah, from his mother Ḥamnah bint Jaḥsh, who said: \I used to experience excessive and severe istihāḍah (irregular bleeding)"," so I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to seek his ruling and to inform him. I found him in the house of my sister Zaynab bint Jaḥsh. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I am a woman who experiences excessive and severe istihāḍah — what do you rule concerning it? It has prevented me from Ṣalāh and fasting.' He said: 'I would suggest to you the use of cotton (kursuf)"," for it absorbs the blood.' She said: 'It is more than that.' He said: 'Then use a cloth.' She said: 'It is even more than that — I gush forth profusely.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'I shall command you with two matters; whichever of them you do"," it will suffice you regarding the other"," and if you have the strength for both"," then you know best.' Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'This is but a kick from the kicks of Shayṭān. So consider yourself menstruating for six or seven days according to the knowledge of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.' Then perform ghusl when you see that you have become pure and cleansed. Then pray for twenty-three or twenty-four nights and their days"," for that will suffice you. And do likewise every month"," just as women menstruate and just as they become pure at the times of their menstruation and their purity. And if you have the strength to delay Ẓuhr and hasten ʿAṣr"," then perform ghusl and combine the two prayers — Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr — and delay Maghrib and hasten ʿIshāʾ"," then perform ghusl and combine the two prayers"," so do that. And fast"," if you are able.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'And this of the two matters is more pleasing to me.'\"" [Weak. Abū Dāwūd narrated it 287]"""
"1603","(1604) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAmr narrated it with its isnād similarly, except that he added at his words: \or twenty-four nights and its days"," and fast.\""\n\nHe also added: \""And perform ghusl with Fajr"," so do that"," and fast if you are able.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: ʿAmr ibn Thābit narrated it from Ibn ʿAqīl"," who said: Ḥamnah said"," and I said: \""This of the two matters is more pleasing to me.\"" He did not attribute it to the words of the Prophet (ﷺ) and made it the words of Ḥamnah.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And this ʿAmr ibn Thābit is not one whose narration is used as proof (muḥtāj bih). And it has reached me from Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī that he heard Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī say: \""The ḥadīth of Ḥamnah bint Jaḥsh concerning the mustaḥāḍah is a ḥasan ḥadīth"," except that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah is old (qadīm)"," and I do not know whether ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl heard from him or not.\"" And Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal used to say: \""It is a ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: As for Ḥamnah bint Jaḥsh"," ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: \""She is Umm Ḥabībah"," who was known by the kunya Umm Ḥabībah"," and she is Ḥamnah bint Jaḥsh.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of that; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed me; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; he said: I heard ʿAlī say it.\n\nYaḥyā ibn Maʿīn contradicted him"," claiming that the mustaḥāḍah was Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh"," who was under ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf"," and that she was not Ḥamnah.\n\nAbū Muḥammad al-Sukkārī in Baghdād informed us of that; Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us; al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Ghassān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," and he mentioned it.\n\nThe Shaykh said: The ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAqīl indicates that she is other than Umm Ḥabībah. And Ibn ʿUyaynah would sometimes say in the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah: \""Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh","\"" and that is an error — she is Umm Ḥabībah. That is what the companions of al-Zuhrī said unanimously.\n\nThe ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAqīl may pertain to the woman with an established menstrual habit (al-muʿtādah)"," except that she expressed uncertainty"," so he instructed her: if it is six"," she should leave it for six"," and if it is seven"," she should leave it for seven.\n\nThe woman experiencing her first instance (al-mubtadiʾah) should refer to the minimum of menstruation. And it may also pertain to the mubtadiʾah"," in which case she should refer to the most common menstrual period among women. And Allah knows best.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy upon him) said: And it is narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ that he said regarding the virgin (al-bikr) from whom blood continues: \""She should sit as the women of her family sit.\"" [Weak. Abū Dāwūd narrated it 287]"""
"1604","(1605) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; he said: Abū Dāwūd said: Anas ibn Sīrīn narrated, who said: \A woman from the family of Anas ibn Mālik experienced istihāḍah"," so they asked me"," and I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about it. He said: 'When she sees the flowing blood (al-dam al-baḥrānī)"," she should not pray. And when she sees purity (al-ṭuhr)"," even if it be only an hour of the day"," she should perform ghusl and pray.'\""\n\nAnd I read it in the book of Ibn Khuzaymah"," from Ziyād ibn Ayyūb"," from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah"," from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ"," from Anas ibn Sīrīn"," except that he said: \""As for when she sees the flowing blood"," she should not pray.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1605","(1606) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Narsī narrated to us; Abū Ghassān narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated from Abū Sahl from the people of Baṣrah, from Musṣah al-Azdīyah, from Umm Salamah, who said: \The women experiencing nifās (postpartum bleeding) in the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would sit for forty nights or forty days after their nifās"," and we would anoint our faces with wars (a plant dye) to treat the dark discoloration (kalaf).\""\n\nThus a group narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah"," from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā"," and he is Abū al-Ḥasan al-Aḥwal al-Kūfī. And Abū al-Walīd said"," from Zuhayr"," from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā — and it is not preserved (laysa bi-maḥfūẓ).\n\nAnd it was narrated by Abū Badr Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā. [Ḥasan for other than its chain. Abū Dāwūd narrated it 311]"""
"1606","(1607) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī in Baghdād narrated it to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Abū Badr al-Kindī Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd al-Kūfī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated from Abū Sahl, from Musṣah al-Azdīyah, from Umm Salamah, who said: \The women experiencing nifās would sit in the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for forty days"," and we would anoint our faces with wars and saffron.\""\n\nIt has reached me from Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī that he said: \""I asked Muḥammad"," meaning al-Bukhārī"," about this ḥadīth"," and he said: 'ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā is trustworthy (thiqah)"," and Shuʿbah narrated from him. And Abū Sahl — Kathīr ibn Ziyād — is trustworthy"," and I do not know of any other ḥadīth from Musṣah besides this one.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Yūnus ibn Nāfiʿ narrated it from Abū Sahl Kathīr ibn Ziyād similarly. [Ḥasan for other than its chain]"""
"1607","(1608) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥalīm al-Marwazī informed us; Abū al-Muwajjah informed us; ʿAbdān narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Yūnus ibn Nāfiʿ, from Kathīr ibn Ziyād Abū Sahl, who said: Musṣah al-Azdīyah narrated to me, who said: \I performed Ḥajj and visited Umm Salamah. I said: 'O Umm al-Muʾminīn"," Samurah ibn Jundub commands the women to make up the prayers of their menstruation (ḥayḍ).' She said: 'They shall not make them up. A woman from among the wives of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would sit in nifās for forty nights"," and the Prophet (ﷺ) would not command her to make up the prayers of her nifās.'\"" [Ḥasan for other than its chain]"""
"1608","(1609) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to me; Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Abū Bishr, from Yūsuf ibn Māḥak, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The woman experiencing nifās waits for forty days or thereabouts.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Dārimī narrated it 957]"""
"1609","(1610) And with his isnād, he said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Bishr ibn Manṣūr, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \She waits — meaning the woman experiencing nifās — seven days. If she becomes pure"," (well and good); if not"," then fourteen. If she becomes pure"," (well and good); if not"," then twenty-one. If she becomes pure"," (well and good); if not"," then forty"," and then she prays.\""\n\nAnd narrations have been transmitted regarding this from ʿUmar and Anas ibn Mālik. [Weak]"""
"1610","(1611) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us; Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated from Abū Ḥurrah, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿUthmān ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ al-Thaqafī, who said: \The woman experiencing nifās waits for forty days"," then performs ghusl.\""\n\nAnd marfūʿ (elevated) aḥādīth have been narrated concerning it"," all of which are weak besides what we have mentioned. And some of the scholars of ḥadīth held the view of what we have narrated. [Weak. Ibn ʿAdī narrated it 7/87]"""
"1611","Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hanbal was asked — and I was listening — about the woman experiencing postpartum bleeding (nifas), how long should she remain (abstaining from prayer) when she sees the blood? He said: Forty days, then she should perform ghusl. Some of them held the view that what we have narrated regarding this should be understood according to their (the women's) customary habit, and that other women, if they see bleeding beyond that, should remain (abstaining) so long as it does not exceed sixty days, based on what is actually observed. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Daraqutni, 1/222]"
"1612","Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Layth, from Ata and al-Sha'bi, who both used to say: When the prolonged bleeding persists for her, she should wait up to sixty days, then perform ghusl and pray. [Da'if]"
"1613","And Abu Abdullah informed us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; al-Shamatī, that is Ja'far ibn Ahmad, narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from al-Layth, from al-Sha'bi, who said: The woman experiencing postpartum bleeding (nifas) should remain (abstaining) for sixty days. [Da'if. Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah, 17452]"
"1614","And Abu Abdullah informed us; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Abu al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Hammad narrated from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, who said: When the woman experiencing postpartum bleeding (nifas) sees (the blood), she should remain (abstaining) for fifty nights. And similarly it was narrated by Yunus ibn Ubayd from al-Hasan. In this there is evidence that he (al-Hasan) interpreted what was narrated from Uthman ibn Abi al-As regarding the forty days to mean that Uthman ibn Abi al-As held the view that if she becomes pure before forty days, her husband should not approach her until she reaches forty. And we have narrated from Ibn Abbas that which indicates he held a contrary view regarding the period before forty. [Sahih]"
"1615","And Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; Ali ibn Umar al-Hafith informed us; Muhammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Hassani narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us; Isra'il narrated from Amr ibn Ya'la al-Thaqafi, from Arfajah al-Sulami, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: It is not permissible for the woman experiencing postpartum bleeding (nifas) when she sees purity except that she prays. [Da'if. Narrated by al-Daraqutni, 1/223]"
"1616","Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ziyad al-Nahwi in Baghdad narrated to us; Abu Ismail Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Sulami narrated to us; Abd al-Salam ibn Muhammad al-Himsi — his nickname was Sulaym — narrated to us; Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us; al-Aswad ibn Tha'labah narrated from Ubaydah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: \When seven days have passed for the woman experiencing postpartum bleeding (nifas) and she then sees purity"," let her perform ghusl and pray.\"" Thus Abu Abdullah narrated it to us from Abu Sahl. [Munkar. Narrated by al-Hakim"," 1/284]"""
"1617","And Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated to us, and he mentioned it, except that he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ali narrated to us from al-Aswad. And at the end of it he said: Sulaym said: I met Ali ibn Ali, and he narrated to me from al-Aswad, from Ubaydah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace be upon him). This is more authentic, and its chain of narration is not strong. [Munkar. Narrated by al-Daraqutni, 1/221]"
"1618","And Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu Iyas, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The time (of abstention) for the woman experiencing postpartum bleeding (nifas) is forty nights"," unless she sees purity before that.\"" Similarly it was narrated by Salam al-Tawil from Humayd"," from Anas. And it was narrated by al-Arzami Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah through his chains from Musnah"," from Umm Salamah. And it was narrated by al-Ala' ibn Kathir from Makhul"," from Abu Hurayrah and Abu al-Darda'"," from the Prophet (peace be upon him). Zayd al-Ammi"," Salam ibn Salm al-Madani"," al-Arzami"," and al-Ala' ibn Kathir al-Dimashqi — all of them are weak (in narration). And Allah knows best. [Da'if. Narrated by Ibn Majah"," 649]"""
"1619","Abu Bakr al-Farisi narrated to us; Abu Ishaq al-Isfahani narrated to us; Abu Ahmad ibn Faris narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us; Sahm, the freedman of Banu Sulaym, said: His freedwoman Umm Yusuf gave birth in Makkah and did not see any blood. She met A'ishah, who said: \You are a woman whom Allah has purified.\"" When she departed (from Mina)"," she saw (blood). Muhammad said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated it to us. [Da'if. Narrated by al-Bukhari in al-Tarikh al-Kabir"," 4/194]"""
"1620","Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Faqih informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us; Abu Aqil narrated from Buhayyah, who said: I heard a woman asking A'ishah — I think he said — about her menstruation. A'ishah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) about a woman whose menstruation had become disrupted and who was flowing with blood. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded me to tell her: \Let her consider the amount of days she used to menstruate each month while her menstruation was regular. Let her sit (abstain from prayer) for that number of days"," and let her leave the prayer during those days and for that duration. Then let her perform ghusl"," then let her use a cloth (as a sanitary covering)"," then let her pray.\"" [Munkar. Narrated by Abu Dawud"," 1284]"""
"1621","(1622) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Aḥmad ibn Bishr ibn Saʿd al-Marthadī narrated to us that Khalaf ibn Hishām narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbdillāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed me that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us that Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father from ʿĀʾishah that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \I experience istiḥāḍah (irregular bleeding) and do not become pure; should I abandon the prayer?\"" He ﷺ said: \""That is a vein (ʿirq)"," and it is not menstruation (ḥayḍ). When the menstrual period begins"," leave the prayer"," and when it passes"," wash the trace of blood from yourself"," perform wuḍūʾ"," and pray"," for that is only a vein and not menstruation.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū al-Rabīʿ. And in the ḥadīth of Khalaf it is stated that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: \""Wash the blood from yourself"," perform wuḍūʾ"," and pray.\"" The remainder carries the same meaning. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Khalaf ibn Hishām"," without the words \""and perform wuḍūʾ.\"" It is as though he considered it weak due to its contradiction of the other narrators from Hishām. Abū Ḥamzah al-Sukkārī narrated it from Hishām"," except that he sent the ḥadīth as mursal and did not mention ʿĀʾishah. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1622","(1623) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Marwazī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us that Abū Ḥamzah narrated to us, saying: I heard Hishām narrate from his father that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I experience istiḥāḍah and do not become pure.\"" — the ḥadīth"," and in it he said: \""Perform ghusl at the time of your purity and perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer.\""\n\nAbū Bakr said: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Shāfiʿī narrated from Dāwūd al-ʿAṭṭār from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah; and al-Ḥasan ibn Ziyād narrated from Abū Ḥanīfah from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah the ḥadīth"," and in it he said: \""And perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: The correct view is that this statement is the saying of ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/280]"""
"1623","(1624) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah, who said: Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am a woman who experiences istiḥāḍah and does not become pure; should I abandon the prayer?\"" He ﷺ said: \""No"," that is only a vein and not menstruation. When your menstrual period begins"," leave the prayer"," and when it departs"," wash the blood from yourself"," then pray.\"" He said: My father said: \""Then perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer until that time comes.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," without the statement of ʿUrwah"," and the statement of ʿUrwah in it is authentic.\n\nThis was also narrated in the Ḥadīth of Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 226]"""
"1624","(1625) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that Wakīʿ narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ḥasanī narrated to us that Wakīʿ narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah, who said: Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am a woman who experiences istiḥāḍah and does not become pure; should I abandon the prayer?\"" He ﷺ said: \""No"," that is only a vein and not menstruation. Avoid the prayer during the days of your menstruation"," then perform ghusl and perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer"," even if blood drips onto the mat.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith.\n\nAnd thus narrated ʿAlī ibn Hāshim"," Qurrah ibn ʿĪsā"," Muḥammad ibn Rabīʿah"," and a group from al-Aʿmash. There was disagreement regarding it from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dāwūd al-Khuraybī. Ḥafṣ ibn Ghayyāth"," Abū Usāmah"," and Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad narrated it from al-Aʿmash and stopped it at ʿĀʾishah"," abbreviating it.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us"," saying: We came from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dāwūd al-Khuraybī to Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān"," and he said: \""Where have you come from?\"" We said: \""From Ibn Dāwūd.\"" He said: \""What did he narrate to you?\"" We said: \""He narrated to us from al-Aʿmash from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah the ḥadīth.\""\n\nYaḥyā said: \""Sufyān al-Thawrī was the most knowledgeable of people regarding this. He claimed that Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit did not hear anything from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Yaḥyā al-Samarqandī narrated to us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us"," saying: I heard ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Madīnī say: \""Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit did not hear anything from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr.\"" Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd said: \""The ḥadīth of Ḥabīb from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr is nothing.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us"," saying: I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī say: I said to Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn: \""Is Ḥabīb reliable?\"" He said: \""Yes"," he only narrated two ḥadīths.\"" I think Yaḥyā meant two munkar ḥadīths: the ḥadīth 'the menstruating woman prays even if blood drips onto the mat' and the ḥadīth of qiblah.\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us"," saying: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: \""The ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash from Ḥabīb is weak.\""\n\nThe weakness of the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash from Ḥabīb is indicated by the fact that Ḥafṣ ibn Ghayyāth stopped it at ʿĀʾishah"," and he denied that the ḥadīth of Ḥabīb was marfūʿ. Asbāṭ also stopped it from al-Aʿmash. Ibn Dāwūd narrated it from al-Aʿmash as marfūʿ in its beginning and denied that it contained wuḍūʾ for every prayer. The weakness of the ḥadīth of Ḥabīb is also indicated by the narration of al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah"," who said: \""She used to perform ghusl for every prayer\"" in the ḥadīth of the mustaḥāḍah. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"1625","(1626) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Abū al-ʿAlāʾ — meaning Ayyūb ibn Abī Miskīn — narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh from Umm Kulthūm from ʿĀʾishah from the Prophet ﷺ, who said regarding the mustaḥāḍah: \She should abandon the prayer during the days of her menstrual period"," then perform ghusl once"," then perform wuḍūʾ for a period equivalent to the days of her menstrual period. If she sees yellowish discharge"," she should sprinkle water and perform wuḍūʾ and pray.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"1626","(1627) He said: And al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Abū al-ʿAlāʾ narrated from Ibn Shubrumah from the wife of Masrūq from ʿĀʾishah from the Prophet ﷺ a similar ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"
"1627","(1628) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Sinān al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Yazīd narrated — and he mentioned both with their two chains of narration, except that he made the first one a statement of ʿĀʾishah. Abū Dāwūd said: \And the ḥadīth of Ayyūb Abī al-ʿAlāʾ is weak and not authentic.\""\n\nThe Shaykh — may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy on him — said: It was narrated from Abū Yūsuf as marfūʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 299]"""
"1628","(1629) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn Abī Khidāsh narrated to us that ʿAmmār ibn Maṭar narrated to us that Abū Yūsuf Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid from al-Shaʿbī from Qamīrah, the wife of Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah that Fāṭimah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I am a woman who experiences istiḥāḍah.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""That is only a vein. Look at the days of your menstrual period. When they have passed"," perform ghusl and use a cloth (istidhfār)"," then perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/210]"""
"1629","(1630) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Muḥammad al-Bāhilī narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn Abī Khidāsh narrated to us, and he mentioned it with a similar wording.\n\nʿAlī said: ʿAmmār ibn Maṭar was alone in narrating it, and he is weak, from Abū Yūsuf. What is in the hands of the people from Ismāʿīl with this chain is mawqūf: \The mustaḥāḍah should abandon the prayer during the days of her menstrual period"," perform ghusl"," and perform wuḍūʾ for every prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/210]"""
"1630","(1631) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Mukram ibn Aḥmad narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥarbī narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Bayān, who said: I heard al-Shaʿbī narrate from Qamīrah from ʿĀʾishah that she said regarding the mustaḥāḍah: \She should abandon the prayer during the days of her menstruation"," perform ghusl"," use a cloth (istidhfār)"," and perform wuḍūʾ at every prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dārimī"," 790]"""
"1631","(1632) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us: Zā'idah narrated to us: Bayān from 'Āmir, and he mentioned it and said: Then she performs wuḍū' for every ṣalāh.\n\nSuch is the narration of 'Abd al-Malik ibn Maisarah, and of Bayān, and Mughīrah, and Firās, and Mujālid, from al-Sha'bī, from Qumayr, from 'Ā'ishah: She performs wuḍū' for every ṣalāh.\n\nAnd the narration of Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind and 'Āṣim, from al-Sha'bī, from Qumayr, from 'Ā'ishah: She takes a ghusl every day once. And likewise in the narration of 'Uthmān ibn Sa'd al-Kātib, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, in the story of Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh, from the Prophet ﷺ. (j) And 'Uthmān ibn Sa'd is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī).\n\nAnd it was narrated from al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, and he is not strong. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1632","(1633) Abu Naṣr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Azīz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatādah informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn Maṭar narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn 'Alī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: I read upon Sharīk, from Abī al-Yaqẓān, from 'Adī ibn Thābit, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The mustaḥāḍah leaves the ṣalāh during the days of her ḥayḍ"," then she takes a ghusl"," and performs wuḍū' for every ṣalāh"," and she fasts and she prays.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihī. Abū Dāwūd referenced it (297)]"""
"1633","(1634) And Abu Naṣr informed us: Abu 'Amr narrated to us: Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Yaḥyā said: I read upon Sharīk, from Abī al-Yaqẓān, from 'Adī ibn Thābit, from his father, from 'Alī, the like of it.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbās Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb said: I heard al-'Abbās ibn Muhammad al-Dūrī saying: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Ma'īn saying: \'Adī ibn Thābit"," from his father"," from his grandfather\"" — Yaḥyā said: \""I found his name to be Dīnār.\""\n\nAbu al-Faḍl said: I referred it back to Yaḥyā"," and he said: \""It is thus — his name is Dīnār.\""\n\nAbu 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: The ḥadīth of 'Adī ibn Thābit is weak (ḍa'īf) and is not authentic. And Abū al-Yaqẓān narrated it from 'Adī ibn Thābit"," from his father"," from 'Alī. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihī]"""
"1634","(1635) Abu Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abu Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī said: Abū Ya'lā — it was read upon Bishr ibn al-Walīd: Abū Yūsuf informed you from Abī Ayyūb al-Afrīqī, from 'Abd Allah ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Aqīl, from Jābir: that the Prophet ﷺ commanded the mustaḥāḍah to perform wuḍū' for every ṣalāh.\n\nAbū Yūsuf is unique in narrating this from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Alī — Abī Ayyūb al-Afrīqī.\n\nAnd Abū Yūsuf is thiqah when he narrates from a thiqah.\n\nAnd in what Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz authorized to me, his narration from him, from Abī al-'Abbās, from al-Rabī', from al-Shāfi'ī, that it was said to him: \Have we not narrated that the Prophet ﷺ commanded the mustaḥāḍah to perform wuḍū' for every ṣalāh?\"" Al-Shāfi'ī said: \""I said: Yes"," you have narrated that"," and upon that we act"," by analogy (qiyās) with the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding wuḍū' from what exits from the posterior or the vulva or the genitals.\"" He said: \""And had this been preserved with us"," it would have been more beloved to us than qiyās.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihī. Al-Ṭabarānī referenced it in al-Awsaṭ (1597)]"""
"1635","(1636) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: 'Alī ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us: from Ayyūb, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn 'Abbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out of the privy, and food was brought near to him. They offered him the wuḍū', and he said: \I was only commanded to perform wuḍū' when I stand for ṣalāh.\""\n\nAbu Bakr said: The Prophet ﷺ was informed that Allah"," the Most High"," commanded him to perform wuḍū' when he stands for ṣalāh — not at the entrance of its time or at its exit. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd referenced it (3760)]"""
"1636","(1637) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbās Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us: al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us.\n\n(h) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: And Ismā'īl ibn Aḥmad al-Jurjānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: 'Amr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Raḥmān, from 'Ā'ishah: that Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh was under 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn 'Awf, and she experienced istiḥāḍah for seven years. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \This is not ḥayḍ; rather"," it is a vein (irq). So take a ghusl.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Rabī'. And in the ḥadīth of Ḥarmalah: that she consulted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""This is not ḥayḍ; rather"," it is a vein. So take a ghusl and pray.\"" 'Ā'ishah said: And she used to take a ghusl at every ṣalāh in a vessel in the room of her sister Zaynab bint Jaḥsh"," until the redness of the blood would rise above the water. Ibn Shihāb said: So Abū Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām narrated it to us"," and he said: \""May Allah have mercy on Hind! Had she heard this fatwā — and by Allah"," she would have wept — for she used to not pray.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Salamah from Ibn Wahb at length"," and al-Bukhārī referenced it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Dhi'b from al-Zuhri without the story of Hind.\n\nAnd likewise al-Awzā'ī said"," from al-Zuhri"," from both of them together. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1637","(1638) And Ibrāhīm ibn Sa'd narrated it from al-Zuhri, from 'Amrah, from 'Ā'ishah. Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me: Abū Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥasan informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Muḥammad al-Baghawī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkānī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Sa'd narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its meaning, without the story of Hind.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkānī.\n\nAnd likewise Ma'mar, Yūnus, and Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated it from al-Zuhri, from 'Amrah, from 'Ā'ishah. And sometimes Ma'mar and Yūnus said: from al-Zuhri, from 'Amrah, from Umm Ḥabībah. And Layth ibn Sa'd narrated it from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'Ā'ishah. And the ḥadīth is ṣaḥīḥ from all of them. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1638","(1639) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayyid al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us: Yaḥyā, meaning Ibn Bukayr, narrated to me: al-Layth narrated to me, from Ibn Shihāb, from 'Urwah, from 'Ā'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said: Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh consulted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she said: \I experience istiḥāḍah.\"" He said: \""That is only a vein. So take a ghusl"," then pray.\"" And she used to take a ghusl at every ṣalāh. Al-Layth said: And Ibn Shihāb did not mention that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh to take a ghusl at every ṣalāh; rather"," it was something she did on her own.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ from al-Layth"," and he mentioned the statement of Layth ibn Sa'd. (t) And Ibn 'Uyaynah also said something similar to its meaning.\n\nAnd in what Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz authorized to me"," his narration from him"," from Abī al-'Abbās"," from al-Rabī'"," from al-Shāfi'ī"," that he said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only commanded her to take a ghusl and pray. There is no indication in it that he commanded her to take a ghusl for every ṣalāh.\"" And I do not doubt"," by Allah"," that her ghusl was a voluntary act (tatawwu'an) beyond what she was commanded with"," and that was permissible for her.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed him by reading to him: Abu al-'Abbās informed us: al-Rabī' informed us: al-Shāfi'ī said: \""Other than al-Zuhri has narrated this ḥadīth"," that the Prophet ﷺ commanded her to take a ghusl for every ṣalāh.\"" But those who narrated it from 'Amrah with this isnād and this context — al-Zuhri is more precise (aḥfaẓ) than them. And he narrated in it something indicating that the ḥadīth is erroneous: \""She leaves the ṣalāh for the duration of her aqrā' (periods).\"" And 'Ā'ishah says: \""Al-aqrā' means al-aṭhār (the periods of purity).\""\n\nAnd he only intended — and Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It is with this wording in Muslim (334)]"""
"1639","(1640) Abū al-Ḥusayn 'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn 'Uthmān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Bakr ibn Muḍar narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibn al-Hād narrated to me: Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us.\n\n(h) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, and the wording is his: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqīh informed us: al-'Abbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: Ibn Kāsib narrated to us: Ibn Abī Ḥāzim narrated to us: Yazīd ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Hād narrated to us: from Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad, from 'Amrah, from 'Ā'ishah: that Umm Ḥabībah experienced istiḥāḍah, and she mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \It is not ḥayḍ; rather"," it is a stirring (rakḍah) from the womb. So look at the duration of her aqrā' in which she used to have ḥayḍ"," and leave the ṣalāh"," then take a ghusl at every ṣalāh and pray.\""\n\nAbu Bakr said: Some of our shaykhs said: The report of Ibn al-Hād is not preserved (ghayr maḥfūẓ).\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār narrated it from al-Zuhri"," from 'Urwah"," from 'Ā'ishah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Nasā'ī referenced it (209)]"""
"1640","(1641) Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed him: Abu Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Hannād narrated to us: 'Abdah narrated to us, from Ibn Isḥāq, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'Ā'ishah: that Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh experienced istiḥāḍah during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he commanded her to take a ghusl for every ṣalāh. And he narrated the ḥadīth.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: And Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated it — and I did not hear it from him — from Sulaymān ibn Kathīr, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'Ā'ishah: \Zaynab bint Jaḥsh experienced istiḥāḍah"," and the Prophet ﷺ said to her: 'Take a ghusl for every ṣalāh.'\"" And he narrated the ḥadīth.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: And 'Abd al-Ṣamad"," meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Wārith"," narrated it from Sulaymān ibn Kathīr"," and he said: \""Perform wuḍū' for every ṣalāh.\"" And this is a wahm (error) from 'Abd al-Ṣamad"," and the correct statement is that of Abū al-Walīd.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And the narration of Abū al-Walīd is also not preserved. For Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated it from Sulaymān ibn Kathīr"," just as the rest of the people narrated it from al-Zuhri. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihī]"""
"1641","(1642) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muslim narrated to us; Sulaymān, meaning Ibn Kathīr, narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The sister of Zaynab bint Jaḥsh experienced istihāḍah (irregular bleeding) for seven years. She would fill a vessel with water for herself"," then enter it until the redness of the blood rose above the water. She then sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said to her: 'This is not menstruation (hayd); rather"," it is a vein (ʿirq). Perform ghusl and pray.'\""\n\nThis narration does not contain the command to perform ghusl for every prayer"," and this is more appropriate as it is consistent with all other narrations from al-Zuhrī. The narration of Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from al-Zuhrī is erroneous due to its contradiction of all other narrations from al-Zuhrī and its contradiction of the authentic narration from ʿIrbāk ibn Mālik from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah. [Authenticated by other chains]"""
"1642","(1643) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Miṣrī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿUthmān ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; my father, Isḥāq ibn Bakr ibn Muḍar, and al-Naḍr ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; they said: Bakr ibn Muḍar narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah, from ʿIrbāk ibn Mālik, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh"," who was married to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf"," complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the bleeding. He said to her: 'Remain (in a state of non-prayer) for the duration that your menstruation used to prevent you"," then perform ghusl.'\"" He said: \""So she used to perform ghusl at the time of every prayer on her own initiative.\""\n\nIn these two authentic narrations there is evidence that the Prophet ﷺ did not command her to perform ghusl at the time of every prayer; rather"," she used to do that on her own initiative. So how can the command to perform ghusl at every prayer be established from the hadith of ʿUrwah? [Authentic]"""
"1643","(1644) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, that he said: \The woman experiencing istihāḍah is not obligated to do more than perform a single ghusl"," then perform wuḍūʾ after that for prayer.\"" [Authentic. Mālik narrated it"," no. 139]"""
"1644","(1645) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik narrated, and he mentioned it with the same meaning, except that he said: \Then she performs wuḍūʾ after that for every prayer.\""\n\nAbū Muʿāwiyah narrated it from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father with the same meaning. [Authentic]"""
"1645","(1646) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Khālid narrated to us, from Ibn Lahīʿah, from Abī al-Aswad, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah, that she did not consider the woman experiencing istihāḍah to be obligated to do more than a single ghusl.\n\nWe have also narrated previously from Qamīr, the wife of Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah, that which indicates this. [Authenticated by other chains. Al-Dārimī narrated it, no. 814]"
"1646","(1647) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Abū Maʿmar ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn Abī al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Sahl Muḥammad ibn Naṣawayh al-Marwazī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Abū Maʿmar narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; Ḥusayn narrated — and in the narration of Abū Dāwūd: from al-Ḥusayn, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: Zaynab bint Abī Salamah informed me that there was a woman who was experiencing continuous bleeding and who was married to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to perform ghusl at the time of every prayer and to pray.\n\nThus did Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrate it. However, Hishām al-Dastawāʾī contradicted him and sent it as a mursal narration. [Authentic. Abū Dāwūd narrated it, no. 275]"
"1647","(1648) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hishām narrated, from Yaḥyā, from Abū Salamah, that Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh asked the Prophet ﷺ. She said: \I am experiencing continuous bleeding.\"" So he commanded her to perform ghusl at the time of every prayer and to pray.\n\nAl-Awzāʿī narrated it from Yaḥyā"," but he made the woman experiencing istihāḍah Zaynab bint Umm Salamah. [Weak]"""
"1648","(1649) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sūsī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us; Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us. He said: Abū Salamah and ʿIkrimah, the mawlā of Ibn ʿAbbās, informed me that Zaynab bint Umm Salamah used to perform iʿtikāf with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was experiencing continuous bleeding. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to perform ghusl for every prayer.\n\nIt has also been narrated from another chain from ʿIkrimah with a different (contradictory) version. [Authentic]"
"1649","(1650) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Hushaym narrated, from Abī Bishr, from ʿIkrimah, that Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh experienced istihāḍah and asked the Prophet ﷺ. He commanded her to wait for the days of her menstrual period, then perform ghusl and pray. If she saw anything after that, she should perform wuḍūʾ, use a cloth for protection (istithfār), pad herself, and pray.\n\nThis narration is also munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). It is closer to the hadith of ʿĀʾishah in the chapter on ghusl, and the hadith of ʿĀʾishah, being established from her through a sound chain, is more deserving of being considered authentic. We have also narrated from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that she would perform a single ghusl and then perform wuḍūʾ, and this does not contradict the Prophet ﷺ in what he narrated from him. [Authenticated by other chains]"
"1650","(1651) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us; Abū ʿAwwānah narrated, from ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah, from his father, who said: \She performs a single ghusl"," then performs wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nIt has also been narrated in this regard from another chain. [Ḥasan]"""
"1651","(1652) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, al-Mujawwiz — meaning al-Ḥasan ibn Sahl — informed us, ʿĀṣim informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah: that a woman experienced istihāḍah (irregular bleeding) during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded her to delay the Ẓuhr prayer and hasten the ʿAṣr prayer, performing a single ghusl for both; and to delay the Maghrib prayer and hasten the ʿIshāʾ prayer, performing a single ghusl for both.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh similarly narrated it from al-Ḥasan ibn Sahl ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, and this is an error on the part of al-Ḥasan.\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh for other than it. Al-Nasāʾī narrated it (213).]"
"1652","(1653) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ informed us, ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah: that a woman experienced istihāḍah during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she was commanded to delay the Ẓuhr prayer, hasten the ʿAṣr prayer, and perform a single ghusl for both; and to delay the Maghrib prayer, hasten the ʿIshāʾ prayer, and perform a single ghusl for both; and to perform a ghusl for the Fajr prayer.\n\nA group narrated it similarly from Shuʿbah, and a group among them mentioned that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim refused to raise the hadith (to the Prophet ﷺ).\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"
"1653","(1654) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: A woman experienced istihāḍah during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she was commanded. I asked: \Who commanded her — the Prophet ﷺ?\"" She said: \""I will not narrate to you anything from the Prophet ﷺ.\"" She said: \""She was commanded to delay the Ẓuhr prayer and hasten the ʿAṣr prayer"," performing a single ghusl for both; and to delay the Maghrib prayer and hasten the ʿIshāʾ prayer"," performing a single ghusl for both; and to perform a ghusl for the Fajr prayer.\""\n\nMuʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated it from Shuʿbah"," and in it he said: \""So I asked ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: 'From the Prophet ﷺ?' He said: 'I will not narrate to you anything from the Prophet ﷺ.'\""\n\nAl-Naḍr ibn Shumayl also narrated it from Shuʿbah in the same manner.\n\nMuḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yāsar narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," but he contradicted Shuʿbah in raising it (to the Prophet ﷺ) and named the woman experiencing istihāḍah. [Ṣaḥīgh]"""
"1654","(1655) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl informed us, Hannād ibn al-Sarī informed us, ʿAbdah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq; and Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Yaḥyā informed me, Muḥammad — meaning Ibn Salamah — narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah: that Sahlah bint Suhayl experienced istihāḍah and came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he commanded her to perform ghusl at the time of every prayer. When that became difficult for her, he commanded her to combine Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr with a single ghusl, and Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ with a single ghusl, and to perform a ghusl for Fajr. This is the wording of the hadith of Abū ʿAlī.\n\nIn the hadith of Abū ʿAbd Allāh, from ʿĀʾishah, she said: \It is only Sahlah bint Suhayl: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command her to perform ghusl at the time of every prayer. When it became difficult for her"," he commanded her…\"" — and he mentioned the hadith.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Isḥāq said: Some of our shaykhs said: No one narrated this report with a chain (musnad) other than Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"," and Shuʿbah did not mention the Prophet ﷺ and denied that the hadith was marfūʿ (raised to the Prophet ﷺ)"," and he also considered him to be in error regarding the naming of the woman experiencing istihāḍah.\n\nAbū Bakr said: The narrators have differed regarding the isnād of this report.\n\nThe Shaykh — may Allah have mercy on him — said: Shuʿbah and Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated it as has been mentioned above.\n\nIbn ʿUyaynah narrated it but sent it as a mursal narration"," except that he agreed with Muḥammad in raising it (to the Prophet ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (290).]"""
"1655","(1656) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn Muḥammad — informed us, Isḥāq informed us, Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father: that a woman from among the Muslims experienced istihāḍah and asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — and he mentioned the hadith. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"
"1656","(1657) It was narrated from al-Thawrī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from Zaynab bint Jaḥsh.\n\nʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn ʿUthmān ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us, Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād informed us, Ibn al-Mubārak informed me, Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from Zaynab bint Jaḥsh, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Ḥamnah, saying: \She is experiencing istihāḍah.\"" He said: \""Let her sit for the number of days of her menstrual period"," then perform ghusl"," and delay the Ẓuhr prayer and hasten the ʿAṣr prayer"," performing ghusl and praying; and delay the Maghrib prayer and hasten the ʿIshāʾ prayer"," performing ghusl and praying both; and perform ghusl for Fajr.\""\n\nIt was also narrated from Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays through another route. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it. Al-Ṭabarānī narrated it (145).]"""
"1657","(1658) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah informed us, Khālid narrated — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad informed us, ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Bayān informed us, Khālid narrated — from Suhayl, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah; and in the hadith of Abū ʿAlī, from Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays; and in the hadith of Abū ʿAbd Allāh, from Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr.\n\nThe narration of Abū ʿAlī is more authentic. She said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh has been experiencing istihāḍah for such and such a time and has not prayed.\"" He said: \""Subḥān Allāh! This is from Shayṭān. Let her sit in a basin.\"" So she sat in it until we saw yellowness (ṣafrāʾ) above the water. He said: \""She should perform ghusl for Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr as a single ghusl"," then perform ghusl for Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ as a single ghusl"," then perform ghusl for Fajr as a single ghusl"," then perform wuḍūʾ between that.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Abū ʿAbd Allāh.\n\nIn the hadith of Abū ʿAlī: \""Let her sit in a basin"," and when she sees yellowness above the water"," let her perform ghusl.\"" And he mentioned it.\n\nSuhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUrwah"," and there was disagreement regarding it from him. The well-known narration is that of the majority from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUrwah"," from ʿĀʾishah"," concerning the matter of Umm Ḥabībah bint Jaḥsh"," as has been mentioned above. It was also narrated in this regard from Ibn Abī Mulaykah. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (296).]"""
"1658","(1659) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Tamīm al-Qanṭarī in Baghdād informed us, Abū Qilābah al-Raqāshī informed us, Abū ʿĀṣim al-Nabīl informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd al-Qurashī informed us, Ibn Abī Mulaykah said: My maternal aunt Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh came to ʿĀʾishah and said: \I fear that I may enter the Fire — I have been abandoning prayer for a year"," two years"," and I do not pray.\"" She said: \""Wait until the Prophet ﷺ comes.\"" So he came"," and ʿĀʾishah said: \""This is Fāṭimah"," saying such and such.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \""Tell her to abandon prayer every month for the number of days of her menstrual period"," then to perform a single ghusl each day"," then to perform purification (ṭahūr) at the time of every prayer"," and to clean herself and pad herself. It is only a disease that has occurred"," or a kick from Shayṭān"," or a ruptured vein.\""\n\nʿUmar ibn Shabbah narrated it from Abū ʿĀṣim in the same manner and said: \""Then purification thereafter for every prayer.\"" Others contradicted him regarding ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it. Al-Ḥākim narrated it (1/283).]"""
"1659","(1660) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad informed us, ʿAmr ibn Zurārah informed us, Abū ʿUbaydah al-Ḥaddād narrated from ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from his maternal aunt Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh: that she experienced istihāḍah and came to ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers, and mentioned that to her. The Prophet ﷺ entered, and she said: \O Messenger of Allah"," Fāṭimah has mentioned that she is experiencing istihāḍah.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Tell Fāṭimah to abstain from prayer every month for the number of days of her menstrual period before this condition occurs"," then to perform a single ghusl"," then to perform purification at the time of every prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1660","(1661) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Abū al-Ashʿath Aḥmad ibn al-Miqdām informed us. ʿAlī said, and Abū Dharr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us, Ḥammād ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAnbasah informed us — both of them said: Muḥammad ibn Bakr al-Bursānī informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd al-Kātib informed me, Ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated: that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh —\n\nAnd in the hadith of Abū al-Ashʿath: that his maternal aunt Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh experienced istihāḍah and remained for a period of time without praying. She came to the Mother of the Believers, ʿĀʾishah, and mentioned that to her. The Prophet ﷺ entered, and she said: \O Messenger of Allah"," Fāṭimah has mentioned that she is experiencing istihāḍah.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Tell Fāṭimah to abstain every month for the number of days of her menstrual period before this condition occurs"," then to perform a single ghusl"," then to perform purification at the time of every prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1661","(1662) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Abū al-Ashʿath — Aḥmad ibn al-Miqdām — narrated. ʿAlī said: and Abū Dharr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr — narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAnbasah narrated to us. Both said: Muḥammad ibn Bakr al-Bursānī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd al-Kātib narrated to me; Ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated to me: that Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh — and in the ḥadīth of Abū al-Ashʿath, that her aunt Fāṭimah bint Abī Ḥubaysh — experienced istiḥāḍah (irregular bleeding), so she remained for a long time without performing ṣalāh. She came to Umm al-Muʾminīn ʿĀʾishah and mentioned that to her and related the story. She said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Tell Fāṭimah to abstain from ṣalāh for the number of days of her menstrual period each month. When those days have passed"," let her perform a single ghusl"," inserting [a cloth] and cleaning herself and using a binding [for protection]"," then performing wuḍūʾ for each ṣalāh and praying. For what has afflicted her is a stroke from Shayṭān"," or a severed vein"," or a disease that has befallen her.\""\n\nʿUthmān ibn Saʿd said: I asked Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," and he narrated to me something similar from his father from ʿĀʾishah.\n\nThe Shaykh — may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy on him — said: it was narrated from al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah the meaning of the second narration from ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd. And al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh is not used as a proof"," and ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd al-Kātib is not strong; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd and Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn both weakened him. And something concerning this was narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ lighayrihi]"""
"1662","(1663) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Quṭan ibn Nusayr al-Ghubarī narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī: that Fāṭimah bint Qays asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the woman experiencing istiḥāḍah — how should she proceed? He said: \She should sit for the days of her menstrual period"," then perform ghusl every day at every time of purification and pray.\""\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Muṭahḥar narrated it similarly from Jaʿfar. And Wahbān ibn Baqiyyah said: \""She performs ghusl at every purification.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ lighayrihi. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/219]"""
"1663","(1664) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Mūsā ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Wahbān ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān narrated it with its isnād from Fāṭimah bint Qays. She said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the woman experiencing istiḥāḍah, and he said: \She should sit for the days of her menstrual period"," then perform ghusl at every purification"," then use padding"," then pray.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Isḥāq said: Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān is a matter of consideration"," and this ḥadīth is not known from Ibn Jurayj or from Abū al-Zubayr from any other source"," and with such a narration no proof is established"," and there is disagreement regarding him.\n\nThe Shaykh said: and it was narrated to us from ʿAlī that she should perform ghusl every day"," and in a narration: for every ṣalāh.\n\nAnd from Ibn ʿAbbās: at every ṣalāh.\n\nAnd in a narration: when the ghusl became too difficult for her"," he commanded her to combine the two prayers.\n\nAnd from Ibn ʿUmar and Anas ibn Mālik: she performs ghusl from one purification to the next. And in one of the narrations from ʿĀʾishah it is likewise"," and in the second narration: a ghusl every day.\n\nAnd in another narration from ʿAlī"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," and ʿĀʾishah: wuḍūʾ for every ṣalāh.\n\nAnd in what Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him"," from Abū al-ʿAbbās"," from al-Rabīʿ"," from al-Shāfiʿī"," who said: in the Ḥadīth of Ḥamnah"," the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \""If you are able"," then combine Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr with one ghusl"," and combine Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ with one ghusl"," and pray Fajr with a ghusl.\"" He informed her that this was the more beloved of the two options to him for her"," and that the first option suffices her — that she perform ghusl at the time of purification from ḥayḍ"," after which he did not command her with any further ghusl. He said: and if any ḥadīth is narrated concerning the mustaḥāḍah in absolute terms"," the Ḥadīth of Ḥamnah clarifies that it is a matter of choice and that other than it suffices in its place.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ lighayrihi]"""
"1664","(1665) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Faqīh — informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī informed us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Zāʾidah narrated from Abū Ḥuṣayn from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī from ʿAlī, who said: \I was a man who experienced much madhī (pre-seminal fluid)"," and the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with me"," so I was too shy to ask him. I instructed a man"," and he asked him. He said: 'When you find that"," wash your private part and perform wuḍūʾ.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1665","(1666) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib was a man who experienced much madhī, so he would take a small wick and insert it into his urethra. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1666","(1667) Abū Aḥmad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from his father from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, who said: \I find it descending from me like small beads. When any one of you finds that"," let him wash his private part and perform wuḍūʾ — his wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh — meaning the madhī.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 85]"""
"1667","(1668) And with his isnād, he said: Mālik narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from Jundub, the freedman of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah al-Makhzūmī, who said: \I asked ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar about madhī"," and he said: 'When you find it"," wash your private part and perform your wuḍūʾ for ṣalāh.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Mālik"," 86]"""
"1668","(1669) ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī al-Muʾadhdhin informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Khanb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Tirmidhī narrated to us; Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways narrated to me; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Yūnus ibn Yazīd from al-Zuhrī from Khārijah ibn Zayd, who said: \Zayd ibn Thābit experienced incontinence of urine"," so he treated it as much as he could. When it overcame him"," he abandoned [treatment].\"" The narrator said: \""And he would perform ṣalāh while it was coming out of him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 582]"""
"1669","(1670) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad informed us; Isḥāq — meaning al-Ḥanẓalī — informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: \Zayd grew old until he experienced incontinence of urine"," so he treated it as much as he was able. When it overcame him"," he performed wuḍūʾ and prayed.\"" And a ḥadīth with its meaning has been narrated with an isnād containing weakness. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 582]"""
"1670","(1671) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī — in Baghdād narrated to us; Hishām — meaning Ibn ʿAmmār — narrated to us; Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Mihrān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās: that a man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have hemorrhoids"," and whenever I perform wuḍūʾ"," it flows.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""When you perform wuḍūʾ and it flows from your private part to your foot"," then there is no [obligation of] wuḍūʾ upon you.\"" [Munkar. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"," 582]"""
"1671","(1672) Abū Saʿd — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣūfī — informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī — informed us; Abū Yaʿlā — informed us; Suwayd — informed us; Baqiyyah — narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik, and he mentioned it with his chain of narration: that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \I suffer from hemorrhoids"," and when I perform wuḍūʾ"," it flows.\"" Then he mentioned the remainder in a similar manner.\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: This is munkar (rejected); I do not know of anyone other than ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Mahrān who narrated it from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār.\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: And he is majhūl (unknown)"," not well-known. [Munkar. Narrated by Ibn ʿAdī in al-Kāmil 5/307]"""
"1672","(1673) Abū Aḥmad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl — informed us; Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī — informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — informed us; Ibn Bukayr — informed us; Mālik — narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him: that he entered upon ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) after he had performed the Fajr prayer on the night in which ʿUmar was stabbed. ʿUmar was woken, and it was said to him: \The prayer! The prayer! The Fajr prayer!\"" ʿUmar said: \""Yes"," and there is no share in Islam for the one who abandons the prayer.\"" So ʿUmar prayed while his wound was gushing blood. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 82]"""
"1673","(1674) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān — informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan — informed us; Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir — informed us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim — informed us; Shaybān — narrated from Yaḥyya ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿIkrimah, regarding the nosebleed that does not stop: He should block his nose, perform wuḍūʾ, and pray.\n\nAl-Walīd said: And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Namir informed me that he heard Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī say the same. End of the Book of Purification and Menstruation. [Ḥasan]"
"1674","(1675) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Mahrān — informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā — informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad — Junāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Junāḥ al-Muḥāribī in Kūfah — informed us; Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharzah — informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā — informed us; Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān — informed us. He said: I heard ʿIkrimah ibn Khālid narrating to Ṭāwūs, saying: A man came to Ibn ʿUmar and said: \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," do you not go out for jihād?\"" He said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Islam is built upon five (pillars): the testimony that there is no god but Allah"," the establishment of prayer"," the giving of zakāh"," the pilgrimage (Ḥajj)"," and the fasting of Ramadhān.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā"," and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Numayr"," from his father"," from Ḥanẓalah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 8]"""
"1675","(1676) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq — by way of recitation — and Abū al-Qāsim — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad al-Sarrāj — informed us by dictation, both saying: Abū al-Ḥasan — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī — informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī — informed us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār — informed us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah — informed us; ʿImrān ibn Ḥudayr — narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUbayd al-Sadūsī, from Ḥumrān ibn Abān, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Whoever knows that prayer is a right and obligatory"," or divinely decreed"," will enter Paradise.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/60]"""
"1676","(1677) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān — informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bishr al-ʿAbdī — informed us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah — informed us; Qatādah — narrated from Zurārah ibn Awfā, from Saʿid ibn Hishām: that he entered upon ʿĀʾishah and said: \O Umm al-Muʾminīn"," tell me about the night prayer (qiyām) of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" She said: \""Do you not recite {O you who are wrapped [in garments]} [al-Muzzammil]?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" She said: \""Allah"," the Most High"," initially made qiyām obligatory at the beginning of this sūrah. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions stood (in prayer) for a year"," until their feet swelled. Then Allah held back its concluding portion for twelve months in the heavens. Then Allah"," the Most High"," revealed the alleviation at the end of this sūrah"," and so the night prayer became voluntary after having been obligatory.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from Muḥammad ibn Bishr"," within a longer ḥadīth.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy upon him) alluded to the meaning of this without the narration"," and added: \""And it is said that what is described in al-Muzzammil was abrogated by the statement of Allah"," the Most High: {Establish prayer at the decline of the sun} — the decline of the sun being its inclination {until the darkness of the night} — i.e."," the first part of the night {and the Qurʾān of dawn} — the Qurʾān of dawn being the Fajr prayer. {Indeed"," the Qurʾān of dawn is ever witnessed.} {And from [part of] the night"," pray with it as additional [worship] for you.} Thus He made it known that the night prayer is supererogatory"," not obligatory"," and that the obligatory prayers are those mentioned"," whether by night or by day.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim 746]"""
"1677","(1678) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī — informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — informed us; Ibn Bukayr — informed us; Mālik — narrated from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: \The decline of the sun (dulūk al-shams) means its inclination.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 19]"""
"1678","(1679) And with his chain of narration, he said: Mālik narrated from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, that he said: An informant informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās used to say: \The decline of the sun (dulūk al-shams) is when the shadow returns"," and the darkness of the night (ghasaq al-layl) is the gathering of the night and its darkness.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Mālik 20]"""
"1679","(1680) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; Yaḥyya ibn Abī Ṭālib — informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ — informed us; Saʿīd — narrated from Qatādah, regarding the statement of Allah, the Most High: {At the decline of the sun} — he said: \When the sun inclines from the meridian of the sky for the Ẓuhr prayer until the darkness of the night.\"" He said: \""The beginning of the night is the Maghrib prayer.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1680","(1681) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān in Baghdād — informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — informed us; ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham al-Dayrāqūlī — informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me; Abū Muḥammad — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī — informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā — informed us; both saying: Abū al-Yamān — informed us; Shuʿayb — narrated from al-Zuhrī. He said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me that Abū Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \The prayer in congregation surpasses the prayer of any one of you alone by twenty-five degrees. The angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the Fajr prayer.\"" Then Abū Hurayrah said: \""Recite"," if you wish: {And the Qurʾān of dawn — indeed"," the Qurʾān of dawn is ever witnessed.}\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī Bakr ibn Isḥāq"," from Abī al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 621]"""
"1681","(1682) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; ʿAmr ibn Zurārah ibn Wāqid al-Kilābī informed us; Marwān al-Fazārī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us; Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim informed us, saying: I heard Jarīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh saying: We were sitting in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said: \You will see your Lord just as you see this moon; you will not be crowded in seeing Him. If you are able"," then do not be overcome regarding a prayer\"" — meaning"," let it not escape you — \""before the rising of the sun and before its setting\"" — meaning ʿAṣr and Fajr. Then Jarīr recited: \""So glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"," and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"," both from Marwān"," except that al-Ḥumaydī incorporated the recitation into the hadith. A group of trustworthy narrators other than Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah also incorporated the recitation into the hadith. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 529.]"""
"1682","(1683) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Shaykh Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed me; my father informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed us; Sufyān informed us, from ʢĀṣim, from Abū Razīn, saying: Nāfiʾ ibn al-Azraq came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said: \Are the five prayers mentioned in the Qurʾān?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" Then he recited: \""So glorify Allah when you enter the evening\"" — he said: this is the prayer of Maghrib — \""and when you enter the morning\"" — the prayer of Fajr — \""and in the afternoon\"" — the prayer of ʿAṣr — \""and when you enter the noontide\"" — the prayer of Ẓuhr. And he recited: \""And after the prayer of ʿIshāʾ"," three times of undress for you.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 2/445.]"""
"1683","(1684) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us; ʿAmr ibn ʿUbayd informed us, from al-Ḥasan, regarding the words of the Most High: \So glorify Allah when you enter the evening\"" — he said: the prayer of Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ — \""and when you enter the morning\"" — the prayer of al-Ghadāh (Fajr) — \""and to Him is the praise in the heavens and the earth"," and in the afternoon\"" — he said: ʿAṣr — \""and when you enter the noontide\"" — he said: Ẓuḥr. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"1684","(1685) He said: And ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, something similar to it. [Ḥasan.]"
"1685","(1686) He said: And ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; ʿAmr informed us, from al-Ḥasan, regarding the words of the Most High: \Establish prayer at the two ends of the day\"" — he said: the prayer of Fajr"," and the other end is Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr — \""and in the hours of the night\"" — Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"1686","(1687) He said: And ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Saʿīd informed us, from Qatādah, regarding the words of the Most High: \Establish prayer at the two ends of the day\"" — he said: the prayer of Ṣubḥ (Fajr) and the prayer of ʿAṣr — \""and in the hours of the night\"" — he said: Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ. [Ḥasan.]"""
"1687","(1688) He said: And ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Saʿīd informed us, from Qatādah, who said: The prayer was originally two rakʿahs in the morning and two rakʿahs in the evening. [Ḥasan.]"
"1688","(1689) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū Bakr Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, meaning Ibn ʿAṭāʾ al-Khaffāf, informed us; Saʿīd, meaning Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, informed us, from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, from Mālik ibn Ṣaʿṣaʿah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who mentioned the story of the Miʿrāj, and in it he said: \Fifty prayers were enjoined upon me every day\"" — or he said: \""I was commanded with fifty prayers every day\"" — the doubt being from Saʿīd. \""I came until I reached Mūsā"," and he said to me: 'With what have you been commanded?' I said: 'I have been commanded with fifty prayers every day.' He said: 'I have tested the people before you"," and I dealt with the Children of Israel with the most severe treatment. Your ummah will not be able to bear that. Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten it for your ummah.' So I returned"," and He removed five prayers from me. I continued to go back and forth between my Lord and Mūsā. Every time I came to him"," he said to me the same as he had said"," until I returned with five prayers every day. When I came to Mūsā"," he said to me: 'With what have you been commanded?' I said: 'I have been commanded with five prayers every day.' He said: 'I have tested the people before you"," and I dealt with the Children of Israel with the most severe treatment. Your ummah will not be able to bear that"," so return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten it for your ummah.' I said: 'I have returned to my Lord until I felt shy"," but I am pleased and I submit.' Then I was called — or a caller called me\"" — the doubt being from Saʿīd — \""'I have enacted My obligation and have lightened for My servants"," and I have made every good deed worth ten times its like.'\""\n\nIt is narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 3674.]"""
"1689","(1690) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-Umawī informed us from the original of his book; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān al-Murādī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb al-Qurashī informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us; Sharīk ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Nimr informed us, saying: I heard Anas ibn Mālik narrating to us about the night on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey from the Mosque of the Kaʿbah. He mentioned the hadith, and in it: \He was revealed to what He willed of that which He revealed: fifty prayers upon his ummah every day and night. Then he descended until he reached Mūsā"," and Mūsā detained him and said: 'O Muḥammad"," what has your Lord entrusted to you?' He said: 'He has entrusted to me fifty prayers upon my ummah every day and night.' He said: 'Your ummah will not be able to bear that. Return"," and let Him lighten it for you and for them.'\n\nI turned to Jibrīl"," peace be upon him"," as though consulting him regarding that"," and he gestured to me: 'Yes"," if you wish.' So Jibrīl ascended with him and said: 'O Lord"," lighten it for us"," for my ummah will not be able to bear this.' So He removed ten prayers from him. Then he returned to Mūsā"," and Mūsā detained him. Mūsā kept sending him back to his Lord until it was reduced to five prayers. Then he detained him at the fifth and said: 'O Muḥammad"," by God"," I urged the Children of Israel to something less than these five"," and they neglected it and abandoned it. And your ummah is weaker in bodies"," hearts"," eyes"," and ears. Return"," and let your Lord lighten it for you.' I turned to Jibrīl to gesture to him"," and Jibrīl did not dislike that. So he raised the matter at the fifth and said: 'O Lord"," my ummah is weak — their bodies"," their hearts"," their ears"," and their eyes — so lighten it for us.' He said: 'The word is not changed with Me. It is as it was written upon you in the Mother of the Book"," and for you is every good deed worth ten times its like. It is fifty in the Mother of the Book"," and it is five upon you.'\"" And he mentioned the hadith.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Sulaymān ibn Bilāl"," and Muslim narrated it from Hārūn al-Aylī from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 7079.]"""
"1690","(1691) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us from the original of his book; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ and Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Shāfiʿī both said: Mālik informed us, from his paternal uncle Abū Suhayl ibn Mālik, from his father, that he heard Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbayd Allāh saying: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the people of Najd, his head disheveled. We could hear the buzzing of his voice but could not understand what he was saying until he drew near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and lo, he was asking about Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Five prayers in the day and night.\"" He said: \""Is there anything else upon me besides them?\"" He said: \""No"," unless you perform voluntary prayers.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""And fasting the month of Ramaḍān.\"" He said: \""Is there anything else upon me besides it?\"" He said: \""No"," unless you fast voluntarily.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Zakāh to him. He said: \""Is there anything else upon me besides it?\"" He said: \""No"," unless you give voluntary charity.\"" The man turned away"," saying: \""By Allah"," I will not add to this nor subtract from it.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""He has succeeded"," if he was truthful.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said in his hadith: And he mentioned charity"," and he said: \""Is there anything else upon me besides it?\""\n\nIt is narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 46.]"""
"1691","(1692) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū ʿAmr al-Ḍarīr informed us, Ḥammād from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān from ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn Muḥayrīz — from a man from Kinānah who said: I heard ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Five prayers have been prescribed by Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," upon His servants. Whoever fulfils them and does not neglect them shall have a covenant with Allah that He will forgive him and admit him into Paradise. And whoever does not fulfil them"," belittling their obligation"," shall have no covenant with Allah; if He wills"," He will punish him"," and if He wills"," He will forgive him.\""\n\nAnd Mālik said from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd in this chain of narration: \""A man from Banī Kinānah known as al-Mukhdajī.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh for other than it. Mālik narrated it (268).]"""
"1692","(1693) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibn Milḥān informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, al-Layth from Ibn al-Hād from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \What do you think if there were a river at the door of one of you in which he bathed five times every day — what would you say remains of his filth?\"" They said: \""Nothing of his filth would remain.\"" He said: \""That is the likeness of the five prayers; by them Allah erases sins.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another route from Ibn al-Hād.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (505).]"""
"1693","(1694) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, al-Asfāṭī — meaning al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl — informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways informed us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad from Abū Masʿūd said: Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \Stand and pray.\"" That was at the declining of the sun when the sun had tilted. So he stood and prayed four rakʿahs of Ẓuhr. Then he came when his shadow was equal to his height and said: \""Stand and pray.\"" So he prayed four rakʿahs of ʿAṣr. Then he came when the sun had set and said: \""Stand and pray.\"" So he prayed three rakʿahs of Maghrib. Then he came when the twilight had disappeared and said: \""Stand and pray.\"" So he prayed four rakʿahs of the latter ʿIshāʾ. Then he came when the dawn had broken and said: \""Stand and pray.\"" So he prayed two rakʿahs of Ṣubḥ. Then he came the following day at midday when the shadow of everything was equal to its height and said: \""Stand and pray.\"" So he prayed four rakʿahs of Ẓuhr. Then he came when his shadow was twice his height and said: \""Stand and pray.\"" So he prayed four rakʿahs of ʿAṣr. Then he came at the same time as the previous day when the sun had set and said: \""Stand and pray.\"" So he prayed three rakʿahs of Maghrib. Then he came after the twilight had disappeared and it had darkened and said: \""Stand and pray.\"" So he prayed four rakʿahs of the latter ʿIshāʾ. Then he came when the dawn had brightened and said: \""Stand and pray.\"" So he prayed two rakʿahs of Ṣubḥ. Then he said: \""Between these two [extremes] is the time for prayer.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm did not hear it from Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī; rather"," it is a report that reached him. And something similar has been narrated in another mursal hadith.\n\n[Munkar]"""
"1694","(1695) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh — meaning Ibn al-Munādī — informed us, Yūnus ibn Muḥammad al-Muʾaddib informed us, Shaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Naḥwī from Qatādah, who said: Anas ibn Mālik informed us that Mākh ibn Ṣaʿṣaʿah narrated to them, and he mentioned the hadith of the Miʿrāj in its entirety, and in it is the obligation of the five prayers.\n\nQatādah said: And al-Ḥasan — meaning al-Baṣrī — narrated to us that when the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) brought them [the prayers] to his people, he withdrew from them until the sun had declined from the centre of the sky. Then it was called out among them: \Prayer is being assembled.\"" The people were alarmed by that and gathered. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed with them four rakʿahs without reciting aloud in them. The people followed the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ)"," and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) followed Jibrīl (peace be upon him)"," until the sun tilted from the centre of the sky"," while it was white and pure. Then it was called out among them: \""Prayer is being assembled.\"" The people were alarmed by that and gathered. The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) prayed ʿAṣr with them — four rakʿahs without reciting aloud in them. The people followed the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ)"," and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) followed Jibrīl (peace be upon him)"," until the sun had set. Then it was called out among them: \""Prayer is being assembled.\"" They gathered"," and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) prayed with them three rakʿahs"," reciting aloud in the first two but not in the single one — meaning aloud. The people followed the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ)"," and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) followed Jibrīl (peace be upon him)"," until the twilight had disappeared. Then it was called out among them: \""Prayer is being assembled.\"" They gathered"," and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) prayed with them four rakʿahs"," reciting aloud in two rakʿahs and not reciting aloud in the other two. The people followed the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ)"," and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) followed Jibrīl (peace be upon him). The people spent the night not knowing whether more would be added to that or not"," until the dawn broke. Then it was called out among them: \""Prayer is being assembled.\"" They gathered"," and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) prayed with them two rakʿahs"," lengthening the recitation in them. The people followed the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ)"," and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) followed Jibrīl (peace be upon him).\n\nIn this hadith and what has been narrated to its meaning is evidence that this occurred in Makkah after the Miʿrāj"," and that the five prayers were prescribed at that time with their specified numbers. It has been established from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) something contrary to that.\n\n[Munkar]"""
"1695","(1696) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, Fayyāḍ ibn Zuhayr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah who said: The prayer was prescribed upon the Prophet (ﷺ) in Makkah as two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs. When he departed for Madīnah, it was prescribed as four, and the prayer of travel was confirmed as two rakʿahs.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad from Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ from Maʿmar. He said: And ʿAbd al-Razzāq followed him from Maʿmar.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This restriction [specifying two rakʿahs] was narrated uniquely by Maʿr ibn Rāshid from al-Zuhrī, while the rest of the trustworthy narrators narrated it without restriction.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1696","(1697) Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Sūsī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf informed us, Abū al-Mughīrah informed us, al-Awzāʿī said: Al-Zuhrī was asked: How was the prayer of the Prophet (ﷺ) in Makkah before he emigrated to Madīnah? He said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me from ʿĀʾishah who said: Allah prescribed the prayer — the first time He prescribed it — as two rakʿahs. Then He completed it in residence, and the prayer of travel was confirmed upon the first obligation.\n\nIt has been narrated from ʿĀmir al-Shaʿbī from Masrūq from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (1040).]"
"1697","(1698) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqrīʾ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Sinān informed us, Bikkār ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn informed us, Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind from ʿĀmir from Masrūq from ʿĀʾishah who said: The first prayer that was prescribed was two rakʿahs. When the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) arrived in Madīnah and felt secure, he added two rakʿahs — except Maghrib, because it is witr (odd) — and the recitation in the morning prayer was made long. She said: When he travelled, he would pray his first prayer — meaning he would shorten it.\n\n[Ḥasan for other than it. Ibn Ḥibbān narrated it (12738).]"
"1698","(1699) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah from Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, and Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ṣaffār informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, saying: I read to Mālik from Ibn Shihāb that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz delayed the prayer one day. ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr came to him and informed him that al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah had delayed the prayer one day while he was in Kūfah. Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī came to him and said: \What is this"," O Mughīrah? Do you not know that Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came down and prayed"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed; then he prayed"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed; then he prayed"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed; then he prayed"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed; then he prayed"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed; then he said: 'With this I have been commanded.'\"" ʿUmar said to ʿUrwah: \""Be careful what you narrate"," O ʿUrwah! Did Jibrīl establish the time of prayer for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" ʿUrwah said: Thus would Bashīr ibn Abī Masʿūd narrate from his father. ʿUrwah said: And ʿĀʾishah"," the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray ʿAṣr while the sun was still in its chamber before it appeared [over the horizon].\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (499).]"""
"1699","(1700) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation, Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from al-Zuhrī that ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr said in the presence of ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came down and led me in prayer"," and I prayed with him. Then he came down and led me in prayer"," and I prayed with him. Then he came down and led me in prayer"," and I prayed with him","\"" until he counted five prayers. ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said: \""Fear Allah and consider what you are saying"," O ʿUrwah!\"" ʿUrwah said: Bashīr ibn Abī Masʿūd informed me from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Jibrīl came down and led me in prayer"," and I prayed with him. Then he came down and led me in prayer"," and I prayed with him","\"" until he counted five prayers.\n\nAnd thus did the majority of the companions of al-Zuhrī narrate it — such as Maʿmar"," Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah"," al-Layth ibn Saʿd"," and others — without mentioning the time in which he prayed and without explaining it. And thus did Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī narrate it from al-Zuhrī"," except that he added what Abū Masʿūd reported regarding what he observed him doing after that.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (3049).]"""
"1700","(1701) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me, Usāmah informed me that Ibn Shihāb informed him that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz was sitting on the pulpit and delayed ʿAṣr somewhat. ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr said to him: \Indeed"," Jibrīl (peace be upon him) informed Muḥammad (ﷺ) of the time of prayer.\"" ʿUmar said to him: \""Know what you are saying.\"" ʿUrwah said: \""I heard Bashīr ibn Abī Masʿūd al-Anṣārī narrating from his father"," who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came down and informed me of the time of prayer"," and I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him. Then I prayed with him.'\"" He counted with his fingers five prayers. \""And I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) praying Ẓuhr when the sun declined"," and sometimes he would delay it when the heat became intense. And I saw him praying ʿAṣr while the sun was still elevated and white before the yellowness entered it"," and a man would leave the prayer and reach Dhū al-Ḥulayfah before the sun set. And he would pray Maghrib when the sun fell. And he would pray ʿIshāʾ when the horizon darkened"," and sometimes he would delay it until the people gathered. And he prayed Ṣubḥ in the darkness of dawn (ghalas)"," then he prayed another time and brightened with it (asfara). Then his prayer after that was in the darkness of dawn until he passed away"," and he did not return to brightening [with it].\""\n\nAnd the explanation of how Jibrīl (peace be upon him) prayed with the Prophet (ﷺ) is in the hadith of Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm"," and it is in the narration of Ibn ʿAbbās and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (1394).]"""
"1701","(1702) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Maryam informed us: al-Firyābī informed us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith, from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥakīm ibn ʿAbbād, from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Jibrīl ʿalayhi al-salām led me in prayer twice at the House. He led me in the Ẓuhr prayer when the sun had declined"," and it was the length of a sandal strap. Then he led me in the ʿAṣr prayer when the shadow of every thing was equal to it. Then he led me in the Maghrib prayer when the fasting person broke his fast. Then he led me in the ʿIshāʾ prayer when the twilight had vanished. Then he led me in the Fajr prayer when food and drink became forbidden for the fasting person. Then the following day he led me in the Ẓuhr prayer when the shadow of every thing was equal to its own shadow. Then he led me in the ʿAṣr prayer when the shadow of every thing was twice its length. Then he led me in the Maghrib prayer when the fasting person broke his fast. Then he led me in the ʿIshāʾ prayer in the first third of the night. Then he led me in the Fajr prayer when the sky had brightened. He then turned to me and said: 'O Muḥammad"," this is the time of the prophets before you"," and the time is between these two times.'\"" [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (393).]"""
"1702","(1703) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah al-Zubayrī informed us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dāwar narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who is Ibn al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah al-Makhzūmī, from Ḥakīm, who mentioned it with the same meaning.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, Abū Hurayrah, and Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī regarding the story of Jibrīl's ʿalayhi al-salām leading the Prophet ﷺ in prayer in Makkah. And it is confirmed from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the prayer times without this story. We shall narrate its chains of transmission, if Allah the Most High wills. [Ḥasan.]"
"1703","(1704) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us: Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \Dulūk al-shams refers to its inclination after the midday.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it (6273).]"""
"1704","(1705) And ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Ḍabbī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Abū ʿAwanah and Khālid narrated from Mughīrah, from al-Shaʿbī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Dulūk al-shams refers to its passing the meridian (zawāl).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1705","(1706) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh informed us from the original of his book: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us: ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Razīn informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj, from Qatādah, from Abū Ayyūb, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the times of prayer, and he said: \The time for the Fajr prayer is as long as the first horn of the sun has not risen. The time for the Ẓuhr prayer is when the sun passes the meridian of the sky"," as long as the ʿAṣr has not arrived. The time for the ʿAṣr prayer is as long as the sun has not turned yellow and its first horn has not set. The time for the Maghrib prayer is when the sun has set"," as long as the twilight has not disappeared. The time for the ʿIshāʾ prayer is until the middle of the night.\""\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (612).]"""
"1706","(1707) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Tamtām, meaning Muḥammad ibn Ghālib, informed us: Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī informed us: Hammām ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Qatādah narrated from Abū Ayyūb al-ʿAtakī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The time for the Ẓuhr prayer is when the sun has declined and a man's shadow is equal to his height"," as long as the ʿAṣr has not arrived.\"" And he mentioned the remainder of the hadith with the same meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it from al-Dāwarqī from ʿAbd al-Ṣamad from Hammām. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1707","(1708) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharazah al-Ghifārī informed us: ʿUthmān — (ḥ) — And Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: ʿAbīdah ibn Ḥumayd narrated from Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī, Saʿd ibn Ṭāriq, from Kathīr ibn Muddarik, from al-Aswad, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd said: \The length of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in summer was three cubits to five cubits"," and in winter five cubits to seven cubits.\"" This is the wording of Abū Dāwūd's hadith.\n\nThis matter varies according to countries and regions"," so it is estimated in each region according to what is known regarding the time of the sun's decline. [Jayyid. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (400).]"""
"1708","(1709) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us through dictation: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī informed us: Ayyūb ibn Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed me: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Uways informed me: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl said: Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān said: I heard Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm convey that Abū Masʿūd said: \Jibrīl ʿalayhi al-salām came down to the Prophet ﷺ regarding the prayer times. He commanded him"," and he led the Ẓuhr prayer when the sun had declined. Then he led the ʿAṣr prayer when the shadow of every thing was equal to it once. Then he led the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set. Then he led the ʿAtamah"," which is the ʿIshāʾ"," when the twilight had vanished. Then he led the Ṣubḥ prayer when the dawn had risen. Then he came to him the following day and delayed the Ẓuhr until it was equal to his shadow"," and delayed the ʿAṣr until it was equal to his shadow twice. Then he led the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set. Then he darkened the ʿIshāʾ"," then brightened for the Ṣubḥ. Then he said: 'Between these two is the prayer.'\""\n\nṢāliḥ ibn Kaysān said: And ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ used to narrate from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh regarding the time of prayer similarly to what Abū Masʿūd used to narrate. Ṣāliḥ said: And ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and Abū al-Zubayr al-Makkī used to narrate the same from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Sulamī. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi.]"""
"1709","(1710) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ informed us: Sufyān informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah said: Ḥakīm ibn Ḥakīm ibn ʿAbbād ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf informed me, from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Jibrīl ʿalayhi al-salām led me in prayer at the House twice. He led me in the Ẓuhr prayer when the sun had declined and it was the length of a sandal strap. Then he led me in the ʿAṣr prayer when the shadow of every thing was equal to it.\""\n\nAnd he mentioned the hadith"," and in it he said: \""Then the following day he led me in the Ẓuhr prayer when the shadow of every thing was equal to it. Then he led me in the ʿAṣr prayer when the shadow of every thing was twice its length.\""\n\nAnd he mentioned the hadith"," and at its end: \""Then he turned to me and said: 'O Muḥammad"," verily this is the time of the prophets before you"," and the time is between these two times.'\""\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was of the view that the beginning of the time for the ʿAṣr is distinct from the end of the time for the Ẓuhr"," and that the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet ﷺ — 'He led me in the ʿAṣr prayer when the shadow of every thing was equal to it' — means when the shadow of every thing was completed as equal to it"," exceeding that by the least amount by which it would exceed. He said: And it has reached me from some of the companions of Ibn ʿAbbās the meaning that I have described"," and I think he mentioned it from Ibn ʿAbbās.\n\nThe Shaykh said"," and it is as if he intended that. [Ḥasan.]"""
"1710","(1711) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr informed us: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us: Sufyān narrated from Layth, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The time of the Ẓuhr extends to the ʿAṣr"," the ʿAṣr to the Maghrib"," the Maghrib to the ʿIshāʾ"," and the ʿIshāʾ to the Fajr.\""\n\nḤabīb ibn Abī Ḥabīb"," the companion of al-Anmāṭ"," followed him up from ʿAmr ibn Ḥarim"," from Jābir ibn Zayd"," from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the time of the Ẓuhr"," and he said: \""And the time of the Ẓuhr prayer is when the sun declines until the ʿAṣr prayer — whatever time you pray"," you have caught it.\""\n\nAnd the meaning that al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah the Most High have mercy on him"," described is found in the established Sunnah. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"1711","(1712) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrāk informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us: Shuʿbah and Hammām informed us, from Qatādah, from Abū Ayyūb al-Azdī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The time for Ẓuhr is when the sun has passed its zenith and a man's shadow is equal to his height"," so long as ʿAṣr has not arrived. The time for ʿAṣr is so long as the sun has not turned yellow. The time for Maghrib is so long as the twilight has not disappeared.\"" Shuʿbah said: \""So long as the light of the twilight has not set.\"" He said: \""The time for ʿIshāʾ is between you and the middle of the night"," and the time for Ṣubḥ is when Fajr has risen"," so long as the sun has not risen.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: Shuʿbah said: \""Sometimes he would raise it (to the Prophet ﷺ) and sometimes he would not raise it.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah and Hammām"," and in it is the clarification that the time for Ṣalāt al-Ẓuhr extends until the time for ʿAṣr"," and when the time for ʿAṣr arrives"," the time for Ẓuhr has passed. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 612.]"""
"1712","(1713) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū Muḥammad Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim informed us: Wakīʿ informed us: Badr ibn ʿUthmān informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Mūsā al-Ashʿarī informed us, from his father.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Wakīʿ informed us, from Badr ibn ʿUthmān, from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Mūsā — I heard it from him — from his father: that a questioner came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him about the times of Ṣalāh, and he did not reply to him with anything. Then he commanded Bilāl, and he called the Iqāmah when Fajr had split open, and he (the Prophet ﷺ) prayed. Then he commanded him, and he called the Iqāmah for Ẓuhr while the one who said it said, \The sun has passed its zenith","\"" or \""It has not yet passed","\"" and he (the Prophet ﷺ) knew better than them. Then he commanded him"," and he called the Iqāmah for ʿAṣr while the sun was still high. Then he commanded him"," and he called the Iqāmah for Maghrib when the sun had set. Then he commanded him"," and he called the Iqāmah for ʿIshāʾ when the twilight had disappeared. He said: Then he prayed Fajr the next day while the one who said it said"," \""The sun has risen","\"" or \""It has not yet risen","\"" and he (the Prophet ﷺ) knew better than them. And he prayed Ẓuhr close to the time of ʿAṣr of the previous day. And he prayed ʿAṣr while the one who said it said"," \""The sun has turned red.\"" And he prayed Maghrib before the twilight had disappeared. And he prayed ʿIshāʾ in the first third of the night. Then he said: \""Where is the questioner about the time? Between these two times is (the valid) time.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. And ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated it from Badr ibn ʿUthmān"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""Then he delayed Ẓuhr until it was close to the time of ʿAṣr of the previous day.\""\n\nAnd in that is evidence for the soundness of the interpretation of al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy on him). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 1613.]"""
"1713","(1714) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah al-Zubayrī informed us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī informed us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ḥakīm, from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Jibrīl came to me at the door of the Kaʿbah twice.\"" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it"," meaning in the second occasion: \""Then he prayed ʿAṣr when the shadow of everything was twice its (original) length.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1714","(1715) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and ʿImrān ibn Mūsā both said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh informed us: My father informed us: Shuʿbah informed us, from Qatādah, from Abū Ayyūb, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The time for Ẓuhr is so long as ʿAṣr has not arrived. The time for ʿAṣr is so long as the sun has not turned yellow. The time for Maghrib is so long as the glow of the twilight has not fallen. The time for ʿIshāʾ is up to the middle of the night. The time for Ṣalāt al-Fajr is so long as the sun has not risen.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAnbarī.\n\nAnd al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it from Qatādah"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""And the time for Ṣalāt al-ʿAṣr is so long as the sun has not turned yellow and its first ray has not fallen.\"" And its chain has been mentioned previously. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1715","(1716) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us. It was read to Ibn Wahb: \Mālik ibn Anas informed you.\""\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us"," saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us"," from Zayd ibn Aslam"," from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār"," from Busr ibn Saʿīd"," and from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj"," from Abū Hurayrah"," that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Whoever catches one rakʿah of Ṣubḥ before the sun rises has indeed caught Ṣubḥ"," and whoever catches one rakʿah of ʿAṣr before the sun sets has indeed caught ʿAṣr.\"" The wording is from the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb. It is narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 1554.]"""
"1716","(1717) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī informed us: Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī — and he was among the best of Allah's creation — informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us, and Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us by dictation: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever catches one rakʿah of ʿAṣr before the sun sets has indeed caught it"," and whoever catches one rakʿah of Fajr before the sun rises has indeed caught it.\"" The wording is from the ḥadīth of Abū al-ʿAbbās.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 610.]"""
"1717","(1718) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ informed us, from Sufyān. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAyyāsh informed us: Ḥakīm ibn Ḥakīm informed me: Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr informed me, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Jibrīl (peace be upon him) led me in prayer at the House (the Kaʿbah) twice.\"" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it he said: \""Then he led me in Maghrib when the fasting person breaks his fast.\"" And he said in the second occasion: \""Then he led me in Maghrib when the fasting person breaks his fast.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1718","(1719) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī and Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥakīm al-Marwazī — both in Marw — informed us, saying: Abū al-Muwajjah Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Fazārī informed us: ʿAbdān ibn ʿUthmān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn informed me: Wahb ibn Kaysān informed us: Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī informed us, saying: Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) when the sun had passed its zenith and said: \Stand"," O Muḥammad"," and pray Ẓuhr.\"" So he stood and prayed Ẓuhr when the sun had passed its zenith. Then he remained until a man's shadow was equal to his (own height)"," and he came to him and said: \""Stand"," O Muḥammad"," and pray ʿAṣr.\"" So he stood and prayed ʿAṣr. Then he remained until the sun had set"," and he said: \""Stand and pray Maghrib.\"" So he stood and prayed it when the sun had set completely. Then he remained until the twilight had disappeared"," and he came to him and said: \""Stand and pray ʿIshāʾ.\"" So he stood and prayed it. Then he came to him when Fajr had dawned for Ṣubḥ and said: \""Stand"," O Muḥammad"," and pray.\"" So he stood and prayed Ṣubḥ. Then he came to him the next day when a man's shadow was equal to his (own height) and said: \""Stand"," O Muḥammad"," and pray Ẓuhr.\"" So he stood and prayed Ẓuhr. Then he came to him when a man's shadow was twice its (original) length and said: \""Stand"," O Muḥammad"," and pray.\"" So he stood and prayed ʿAṣr. Then he came for Maghrib when the sun had set at a single time"," without departing from it"," and said: \""Stand and pray Maghrib.\"" Then he came for ʿIshāʾ when the first third of the night had passed and said: \""Stand and pray ʿIshāʾ.\"" Then he came for Ṣubḥ when it had become very bright and said: \""Stand and pray Ṣubḥ.\"" Then he said: \""Between these two (times) is all (the valid) time.\""\n\nAnd Burd ibn Sinān narrated its meaning from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ"," from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 526.]"""
"1719","(1720) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ṣawwāf in Baṣrah informed us: ʿAmr ibn Bishr al-Ḥārithī informed us: Burd ibn Sinān informed us, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh: that Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) to teach him Ṣalāh. He came to him when the sun had passed its zenith, and Jibrīl went forward and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was behind him, and the people were behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he prayed Ẓuhr. Then he came to him when the shadow was equal to the stature of a person, and Jibrīl went forward and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was behind him, and the people were behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he prayed ʿAṣr. Then he came to him when the sun had set, and Jibrīl (peace be upon him) went forward and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was behind him, and the people were behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he prayed Maghrib. Then he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth and said in it: Then he came to him on the second day at a single time when the sun had set, and Jibrīl (peace be upon him) went forward and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was behind him, and the people were behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he prayed Maghrib. He said, and at the end of it he said: \Between the two (prayers) is (the valid) time.\"" He said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about Ṣalāh"," and he prayed with them just as Jibrīl (peace be upon him) had prayed with him. Then he said: \""Where is the questioner about Ṣalāh? Between the two (prayers) is (the valid) time.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains]"""
"1720","(1721) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣfahānī informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥātim informed me: Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah ibn ʿAlqamah informed me in what he wrote to me: My father informed me: al-Awzāʿī informed us: Ḥassān ibn ʿAṭiyyah informed me.\n\nʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, saying: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the times of the Ṣalawāt. So he prayed Ẓuhr when the shadow returned, and he prayed ʿAṣr when the shadow of everything was equal to it (its original length), and he prayed Maghrib when the sun had set, and he prayed ʿIshāʾ when the twilight had disappeared, and he prayed Ṣubḥ when the first Fajr appeared. Then he prayed Ẓuhr on the second day when the shadow of everything was equal to it (its original length), and he prayed ʿAṣr when the shadow of everything was twice its (original) length, and he prayed Maghrib when the sun had set, and he prayed ʿIshāʾ in the third of the night, and he prayed Ṣubḥ after it had become bright. Then he said: \Indeed"," Jibrīl led me in prayer to teach you that between these two is (the valid) time.\"" [Ḥasan through other chains]"""
"1721","(1722) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī in Marw informed us; Abū al-Muwajjah Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \This is Jibrīl"," upon him be peace"," teaching you your religion.\"" Then he mentioned the times of the prayer. Then he mentioned that he prayed al-Maghrib when the sun had set. Then when he came to him the following day"," he prayed al-Maghrib when the sun had set"," at the same time. [Hasan. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 502]"""
"1722","(1723) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Usayd narrated from Muḥammad that he heard Abū Hurayrah relate that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told them that Jibrīl, upon him be peace, came to him and he prayed the prayers with him in two times, except for al-Maghrib. He said: \He came to me for al-Maghrib and he prayed with me at the hour when the sun set. Then he came to me the following day for al-Maghrib and he prayed with me at the hour when the sun set; he did not change it.\""\n\nMuḥammad is Ibn ʿAmmār ibn Saʿd al-Muʾadhdhin.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm from Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī"," and from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," and from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," regarding this story about the prayer of al-Maghrib"," in a similar manner. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/307]"""
"1723","(1724) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī informed me; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl al-Balkhī narrated to us; Makkī narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd, from Salamah—meaning Ibn al-Akwʿ—who said: We used to pray al-Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the sun disappeared behind the veil.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm, and Muslim narrated it from another route from Yazīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 536]"
"1724","(1725) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed me; my father narrated to me; al-Awzāʿī narrated to us.\n\nAbū al-Najāshī narrated to me; Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj al-Anṣārī narrated to me, saying: We used to pray al-Maghrib in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and one of us would depart and he would still be able to see the places where his arrows had fallen.\n\nIt is recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of al-Awzāʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 534]"
"1725","(1726) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: We used to pray al-Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would come to Banī Salamah, and had we shot arrows, we would have seen the places where they fell.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī, 954]"
"1726","(1727) And with his chain of narration, he said: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Ṣāliḥ, the freed slave of al-Tawʾamah, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, who said: We used to pray al-Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would come to the market, and had we shot arrows, we would have seen where they fell. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1727","(1728) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qāḍī in Marw narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us, and the wording is his: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; Ismāʿīl—meaning Ibn ʿUlayyah—narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who said: Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated to me from Mirdās ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Yazanī, who said: Abū Ayyūb came to us as a warrior, and ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir was at that time in charge of Egypt. He delayed al-Maghrib, so Abū Ayyūb stood up to him and said: \What is this prayer"," O ʿUqbah?\"" He said: \""We were occupied.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I do not grieve except that the people will think that you saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing this and then you do likewise. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'My ummah will continue to be upon goodness—or upon the fiṭrah—so long as they do not delay al-Maghrib until the stars intermingle.'\"" [Hasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 1418]"""
"1728","(1729) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; my grandfather Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from his uncle Abū Suhayl ibn Mālik, from his father, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī: \Pray al-Ẓuhr when the sun has declined"," and al-ʿAṣr when the sun is white and pure before yellowness enters it"," and al-Maghrib when the sun has set"," and al-ʿIshāʾ so long as you have not fallen asleep"," and pray al-Ṣubh when the stars are visible"," and recite in it two long sūrahs from al-Mufaṣṣal.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 2/395]"""
"1729","(1730) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Zakariyyā al-ʿAnbarī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām informed us; Isḥāq informed us; Jarīr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm and ʿUmārah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, who said: ʿAbd Allāh—meaning Ibn Masʿūd—used to pray al-Maghrib while we would see that the sun was still rising. He said: One day we looked at that, and he said: \What are you looking at?\"" They said: \""At the sun.\"" ʿAbd Allāh said: \""By the One besides whom there is no deity"," this is the appointed time of this prayer.\"" Then he said: {Establish prayer at the decline of the sun until the darkness of the night} [al-Isrāʾ 78]. \""This is the decline of the sun.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 2/395]"""
"1730","(1731) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him; Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us, saying: It was read to ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣfahānī informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Ikhmīmī in Makkah narrated to us; Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us; Badr ibn ʿUthmān narrated to me; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, that a questioner came to him and asked him about the times of the prayer, and he did not reply to him with anything. He commanded Bilāl, who called the iqāmah for al-Fajr when the dawn had split open, and the people could scarcely recognize one another. Then he commanded him and he called the iqāmah for al-Ẓuhr when the sun had declined, and the one who said would say: \The day has reached its midpoint","\"" though he knew better than them. Then he commanded him and he called the iqāmah for al-ʿAṣr while the sun was still high. Then he commanded him and he called the iqāmah for al-Maghrib when the sun had set. Then he commanded him and he called the iqāmah for al-ʿIshāʾ when the twilight had disappeared. Then on the following day he delayed al-Fajr until he had departed from it and the one who said would say: \""The sun has risen"," or nearly so.\"" Then al-Ẓuhr when it was close to al-ʿAṣr. Then he delayed al-ʿAṣr until he had departed from it and the one who said would say: \""The sun has turned red.\"" Then he delayed al-Maghrib until it was near the disappearance of the twilight. Then he delayed al-ʿIshāʾ until the first third of the night had passed. Then in the morning he called the questioner and said: \""The time is between these two.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Ibn Yūsuf.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr"," from his father"," from Badr ibn ʿUthmān"," with this wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 614]"""
"1731","(1732) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us from the original of his hearing: my grandfather, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Abū Qudāmah, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿīd al-Yashkurī, and Abū Ayyūb al-Nahrāwānī, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad al-Anṣārī, informed us: Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah from his father, who said:\n\nA man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the times of prayer. He said: \Pray with us these two [days].\"" When the sun passed its zenith"," he commanded Bilāl"," and he gave the adhān. Then he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah — meaning for Zuhr. Then he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah for ʿAṣr while the sun was still high"," white"," and clear. Then he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah for Maghrib when the upper edge of the sun had disappeared. Then he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah for ʿIshāʾ when the twilight (shafaq) had vanished. Then he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah for Fajr when the dawn had risen.\n\nThe next day"," he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah for Zuhr"," and he cooled it (performed it in the cooler part of the time)"," and he did well in cooling it. Then he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah for ʿAṣr while the sun was still white"," and he delayed it beyond what he had done the previous day. Then he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah for Maghrib before the twilight had disappeared. Then he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah for ʿIshāʾ when a third of the night had passed. Then he commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah for Fajr and he brightened it (performed it in full light). Then he said: \""The time of your prayer is as you have seen.\""\n\nAbū Ayyūb added in his hadith: Then he said: \""Where is the one who asked about the time of prayer?\"" The man said: \""Here I am"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""The time of your prayer is between what you have seen.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Abū Ṣāliḥ.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Qudāmah"," ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿīd. In the ʿIlal of Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī"," from al-Bukhārī"," who said: The hadith of Abū Mūsā is ḥasan"," and the hadith of al-Thawrī from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad from Ibn Buraydah from his father regarding the times (mawāqīt) is a ḥasan hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 613.]"""
"1732","(1733) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Isfarāyīnī narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah from Abū Ayyūb from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr — Shuʿbah said: \Sometimes he would raise it [to the Prophet] and sometimes he would not raise it\"" — who said:\n\nThe time of Zuhr is as long as ʿAṣr has not arrived; the time of ʿAṣr is as long as Maghrib has not arrived; the time of Maghrib is as long as the glow of the twilight (thawr al-shafaq) has not set; the time of ʿIshāʾ is as long as the night has not reached its midpoint; and the time of Ṣubḥ is as long as the sun has not risen.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through various routes from Shuʿbah"," and in some of them he did not raise it twice and raised it once.\n\nHishām al-Dastawāʾī"," Hammām ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj raised it from Qatādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1733","(1734) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us: my father narrated to me from Qatādah from Abū Ayyūb from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\When you have prayed Fajr"," its time [extends] until the first edge of the sun rises. Then when you have prayed Zuhr"," its time [extends] until ʿAṣr arrives. Then when you have prayed ʿAṣr"," its time [extends] until the sun turns yellow. Then when you have prayed Maghrib"," its time [extends] until the twilight (shafaq) disappears. Then when you have prayed ʿIshāʾ"," its time [extends] until the middle of the night.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 612.]"""
"1734","(1735) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: my father narrated to me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith al-Makhzūmī narrated to me: Thawr ibn Zayd narrated from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said:\n\nA man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the time of prayer. He said: \Pray with us.\"" … And he mentioned the hadith"," and in it: \""Then he prayed Maghrib when the sun had set.\"" And he said on the second day: \""Then he prayed Maghrib before the disappearance of the twilight (shafaq).\""\n\nIt was narrated by Burd ibn Sinān from ʿAṭāʾ"," and he mentioned the story of Jibrīl's leading the Prophet ﷺ in prayer"," and he mentioned the time of Maghrib as one [time]. That is one story"," and the question of the questioner about the times of the prayers is another story"," as we think — and Allah knows best.\n\nIt has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿAbbās from his own statement: \""The time of Maghrib extends to ʿIshāʾ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1735","(1736) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: my father narrated to me: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to me: my father narrated to me: Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah, who said: ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\Let not the Bedouins overcome you regarding the name of your Maghrib prayer.\"" Then he said: \""The Bedouins call it ʿIshāʾ.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Maʿmar from ʿAbd al-Wārith.\n\nHārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated something similar from ʿAbd al-Ṣamad. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 538.]"""
"1736","(1737) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Firyābī informed us: Abū Masʿūd informed us: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad informed us: my father narrated to me from Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim from Ibn Buraydah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mughaffal, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\Let not the Bedouins overcome you regarding the name of your prayer"," for the Bedouins call it ʿAtamah.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī"," said: The hadith of Abū Masʿūd indicates that it refers to the last ʿIshāʾ prayer"," and similarly it has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar regarding the last ʿIshāʾ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Except that those who narrated it from ʿAbd al-Ṣamad with the first wording are more numerous. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1737","(1738) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said, and the last [group] said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Ibn Abī Labīd from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Ibn ʿUmar that the Prophet ﷺ said:\n\n\Let not the Bedouins overcome you regarding the name of your prayer — it is ʿIshāʾ — except that they milk their camels at nightfall (yuʿtimūn bi-l-ibil).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 644.]"""
"1738","(1739) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rāwād from a man from the people of Ṭāʾif from Ghaylān ibn Shuraḥbīl from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n\Let not the Bedouins overcome you regarding the name of your prayer"," for it is in the Book of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic"," ʿIshāʾ. The Bedouins only named it ʿAtamah on account of their camels — for milking them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by al-Bazzār.]"""
"1739","(1740) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah al-Zuraqī from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥakīm ibn ʿAbbād ibn Ḥunayf from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\Jibrīl"," peace be upon him"," led me in prayer at the House twice.\"" … And he mentioned the hadith"," and said in it: \""And he led me in the ʿIshāʾ prayer when the twilight (shafaq) had disappeared.\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"1740","(1741) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Abū Muṣʿab narrated to us: al-Dāwardī narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The shafaq is the redness (al-ḥumrah).\"" Abū Muṣʿab said: Mālik said: \""The shafaq is the redness.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 2122.]"""
"1741","(1742) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār reported to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī reported to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq reported to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar reported from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The shafaq (evening twilight) is the redness.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1742","(1743) And ʿAbdullāh ibn Nāfiʿ narrated it similarly from his father from Ibn ʿUmar, as a mawqūf (stopped) narration.\nAnd it was narrated from ʿAtīq ibn Yaʿqūb from Mālik from Nāfiʿ as a marfūʿ (raised) narration, but the correct version is mawqūf.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other than that form. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq, 2122]"
"1743","(1744) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad informed us: Hārūn ibn Sufyān reported from ʿAtīq ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Ṣiddīq from Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The shafaq is the redness. When the shafaq sets"," the prayer becomes obligatory.\""\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 261]"""
"1744","(1745) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk reported: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq reported: I heard Abū ʿAbdillāh, i.e. Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, report: Hushaym reported from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaḥyā — Abū ʿAbdillāh said: he is the brother of Muʿāwiyah ibn Yaḥyā al-Ṣadafī — from Ḥibbān ibn Abī Jabalah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The shafaq is the redness.\"" (T) And it has been narrated from ʿUmar"," ʿAlī"," and Abū Hurayrah that they said: \""The shafaq is the redness.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1745","(1746) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī reported: Muḥammad ibn Shādhān reported: Muʿallā reported: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah reported from Thawr ibn Yazīd from Makḥūl from ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit and Shaddād ibn Aws, who both said: \The shafaq is two: the redness and the whiteness. When the redness disappears"," the prayer becomes permissible. And the dawn (fajr) is two: the extended (mustaṭīl) and the spreading (muʿtariḍ). When the spreading (muʿtariḍ) breaks open"," the prayer becomes permissible.\""\nAnd it has been narrated from Sufyān from Thawr from Makḥūl that he said: \""When the redness departs"," then pray.\"" Sufyān said: \""And that is more beloved to us"," and that is the shafaq according to us"," because the whiteness does not depart until the night has passed.\""\nThe Shaykh said: And that which Sulaymān ibn Mūsā narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Jābir from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the times of prayer — that he prayed ʿIshāʾ before the setting of the shafaq — contradicts all other narrations.\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/269]"""
"1746","(1747) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed him: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār reported: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal reported to me: my father reported to me: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith al-Makhzūmī reported to me: Thawr ibn Yazīd reported from Sulaymān, and he mentioned it.\nAnd Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nasāʾī narrated it from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Saʿīd from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith al-Makhzūmī, and he said in the first narration: \And ʿIshāʾ when the shafaq sets.\"" And he said in the second: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith said regarding ʿIshāʾ: \""I think up to one-third of the night.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 504]"""
"1747","(1748) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us: Abū al-Nuʿmān Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl reported: Abū ʿAwanah reported from Abū Bishr from Bashīr ibn Thābit from Ḥabīb ibn Sālim from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, who said: \I am the most knowledgeable of people regarding the time of this prayer — the ʿIshāʾ al-Ākhirah (last ʿIshāʾ). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray it at the time of the setting of the moon on the third (of the month).\"" (T) And Shuʿbah narrated it similarly from Abū Bishr. And Hushaym ibn Bashīr and Raqabah ibn Maṣqalah narrated it from Abū Bishr from Ḥabīb ibn Sālim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 165]"""
"1748","(1749) Through what Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī reported: ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim reported: Wakīʿ reported: Sufyān reported from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥakīm from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Jibrīl led me in prayer at the House twice.\"" He mentioned the hadith"," and in it: \""He led me in the ʿIshāʾ prayer at the first third of the night\"" — meaning on the second occasion. [Ḥasan]"""
"1749","(1750) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah reported: Abū Dāwūd reported: Musaddad reported: ʿAbdullāh ibn Dāwūd reported from Badr ibn ʿUthmān: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Mūsā reported from Abū Mūsā that a questioner came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not answer him anything until he commanded Bilāl, who then gave the iqāmah. He mentioned the hadith, and in it: \He commanded Bilāl"," and he established the ʿIshāʾ when the shafaq had set. Then when the next day came\"" — he mentioned the hadith — \""and in it: he prayed ʿIshāʾ up to one-third of the night. Then he said: 'Where is the one who asked about the time of prayer? The time is between these two.'\""\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through various routes from Badr ibn ʿUthmān. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1750","(1751) Abū al-Qāsim ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh informed us in the Mosque of al-Ruṣāfah in Baghdād: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Najjād reported: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq reported: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh reported: Ḥaramī ibn ʿUmarah ibn Abī Ḥafṣah reported: Shuʿbah reported from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah from his father: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the times of prayer, so he said: \Attend the prayer with us.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilāl"," and he called the adhān at dusk"," and he prayed Fajr. Then he commanded him for Ẓuhr when the sun passed the meridian. Then he commanded him for ʿAṣr while the sun was still high. Then he commanded him for Maghrib when the sun had set. Then he commanded him for ʿIshāʾ when the shafaq had set. Then he commanded him the next day"," and he illuminated Fajr brightly. Then he commanded him for Ẓuhr and made it cool. Then he commanded him for ʿAṣr while the sun was white and pure"," with no yellowness mixed in. Then he commanded him for Maghrib before the shafaq set. Then he commanded him for ʿIshāʾ at the passing of one-third of the night or some of it — Abū Rūh was uncertain. When morning came"," he said: \""Where is the questioner? Between what you have seen is the time.\""\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿArʿarah from Ḥaramī ibn ʿUmarah"," Abū Rūh.\nAnd we have narrated it from the hadith of al-Thawrī from ʿAlqamah ibn Murthad"," who said: \""He established the ʿIshāʾ when one-third of the night had passed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1751","(1752) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī informed me; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb informed me from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that ʿĀʾishah said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the ʿIshāʾ prayer at ʿAtamah (late night)"," until ʿUmar called out: 'The prayer! The women and children have fallen asleep.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out and said: 'No one among the people of the earth is waiting for it except you.' And on that day"," it was not performed except in Madīnah. They used to perform the ʿIshāʾ prayer between the disappearance of the twilight of the night and the first third of the night.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from Abū al-Yamān"," and he also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān from al-Zuhrī."""
"1752","(1753) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Tamtām narrated to us; Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī narrated to us; Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Qatādah narrated to us from Abū Ayyūb al-ʿAtakī from ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — and he mentioned the ḥadīth, and in it he said: \The time of the ʿIshāʾ prayer extends until the middle of the night.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Hammām and others from Qatādah"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""Until the middle of the night\"" (al-layl al-awsaṭ).\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of Hishām from Qatādah: \""When you perform the ʿIshāʾ prayer"," its time extends until the middle of the night.\"""""
"1753","(1754) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadhābādhī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Saʿdī informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl informed us from Anas ibn Mālik, who was asked: \Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) have a ring made?\"" He said: \""Yes. He delayed the ʿIshāʾ prayer one night until half the night had passed. When he had prayed"," he turned his face toward us and said: 'The people have prayed and fallen asleep"," and you have been in prayer ever since you waited for the prayer.'\"" It is as though I were looking at the glitter of his ring.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdillāh ibn Munīr from Yazīd ibn Hārūn."""
"1754","(1755) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdillāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Qurrah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to us; Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn Naṣr and ʿAbdillāh ibn Muḥammad both said: ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Aṭṭār narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Ḥanafī narrated to us; Qurrah narrated to us from Qatādah from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \We watched the Prophet (ﷺ) one night until it was close to the middle of the night. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) came and prayed.\"" He said: \""It is as though I were looking at the glitter of his ring"," a silver band.\"" In the narration of Abū Dāwūd: \""Until half the night had passed","\"" and the rest is similar in meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ."""
"1755","(1756) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated to us from Thābit from Anas, who was asked: \Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) have a ring?\"" He said: \""Yes. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed the ʿIshāʾ prayer one night"," and half the night had nearly passed or was at half the night. Then he came and said: 'The people have prayed and fallen asleep"," and you have been in prayer as long as you waited for the prayer.'\""\n\nAnas said: \""It is as though I were looking at the glitter of his ring made of silver.\"" And he gestured with his left hand and described it."""
"1756","(1757) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us; Bahz al-ʿAmmī narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Thābit, that they asked Anas ibn Mālik about the ring of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he mentioned it with similar meaning, except that he said: \And he raised his left little finger.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Nāfiʿ."""
"1757","(1758) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdillāh ibn Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Khurāsānī al-ʿAdl narrated to us; Yaḥyā, meaning Ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zibriqān, informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us; Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind informed us from Abū Naḍrah from Abū Saʿīd, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed the ʿIshāʾ prayer until close to half the night. Then he came out and prayed and said: 'You have been in prayer as long as you waited for it"," were it not for the frailty of the feeble and the old age of the elderly.'\"" I think he said: \""And the need of the one in need — I would have delayed this prayer until half the night.\"""""
"1758","(1759) And thus narrated it Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal and others from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind. But Abū Muʿāwiyah al-Ḍarīr contradicted them from Dāwūd, and he said it was from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh.\n\nAbū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind from Abū Naḍrah from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to his Companions while they were waiting for the ʿIshāʾ prayer"," and he said: 'The people have prayed and fallen asleep"," and you are waiting for it. Indeed"," you have been in prayer as long as you waited for it. Were it not for the frailty of the feeble and the old age of the elderly"," I would have delayed this prayer until half the night.'\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Umm Kulthūm bint Abī Bakr from ʿĀʾishah regarding this story: \""Until the greater part of the night had passed and the people of the mosque had fallen asleep.\"" And in the ḥadīth of Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī: \""Until the night became intensely dark.\"" And in the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbbās: \""Until the people fell asleep and woke up"," and fell asleep and woke up.\"" And in the narration of al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah from Nāʿim from Ibn ʿUmar: \""He came out to us when a third of the night had passed or after that.\"" And in the ḥadīth of Abū al-Minhāl from Abū Barzah al-Aslamī: \""He used not to mind delaying the ʿIshāʾ prayer until a third of the night","\"" then he said: \""Until half the night.\"" And Muʿādh said: Shuʿbah said: \""Then I met him another time and he said: 'Or a third of the night.'\"" And Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith said from Shuʿbah: \""Until half the night.\"" And Ḥammād ibn Salamah said from Abū al-Minhāl: \""Until a third of the night.\"""""
"1759","(1760) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Isfarāyīnī narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Abū Mūsā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl ibn Ghazwān narrated to us from al-Aʿmash from Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," the prayer has a beginning and an end. The beginning of the time of the Ẓuhr prayer is when the sun declines"," and the end of its time is when the time of the ʿAṣr enters. The beginning of the time of the ʿAṣr is when its time enters"," and the end of its time is when the sun turns yellow. The beginning of the time of the Maghrib is when the sun sets"," and the end of its time is when the horizon disappears. The beginning of the time of the ʿIshāʾ is when the horizon disappears"," and the end of its time is when the night reaches its midpoint. The beginning of the time of the Fajr is when the dawn breaks"," and the end of its time is when the sun rises.\""\n\n(Jīm) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn weaken the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl from al-Aʿmash from Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah — I think Yaḥyā meant the ḥadīth: \""Indeed"," the prayer has a beginning and an end\"" — and he said: \""It is only narrated from al-Aʿmash from Mujāhid.\"" And he said in another place in the Tārīkh: \""The ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash from Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah"," who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed"," the prayer has a beginning and an end.'\"" All the people narrated it from al-Aʿmash from Mujāhid"," as a mursal ḥadīth.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Al-Bukhārī (may Allah have mercy on him) mentioned something to that effect."""
"1760","(1761) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr informed us; Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; Zāʾidah narrated to us from al-Aʿmash from Mujāhid, who said: \It was said that the prayer has a beginning and an end","\"" and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd thus narrated it Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Fazarī and Abū Zubayd ʿAbthar ibn al-Qāsim from al-Aʿmash from Mujāhid."""
"1761","(1762) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār informed us in Baghdad: al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Abū al-Ashʿath informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṭufāwī informed us: Ayyūb narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Mujāhid, who used to say: \See whether my ḥadīth corresponds to what you have heard from the Book.\"" Indeed"," ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿārī: \""Pray Dhuhr when the sun rises high — meaning when it passes the meridian — and pray ʿAṣr while the sun is white and clear"," and pray Maghrib when the sun sets"," and pray ʿIshāʾ until the first half of the night"," and pray Fajr in the darkness of dawn or in the blackness"," and lengthen the recitation.\"" [Ṣaḥīh in its own right. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 2035.]"""
"1762","(1763) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr informed us: Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah informed me: Thābit al-Bunānī narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rabāḥ from Abū Qatādah from the Prophet (ﷺ) in a long ḥadīth, in which he said: \There is no negligence in sleep; negligence is only upon one who does not pray the ṣalāh until the time of the next one comes.\"" Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīh from Shaybān from Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah. [Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by Muslim"," 681.]"""
"1763","There is no ḥadīth under this chapter."
"1764","(1764) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim informed us: Wakīʿ informed us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥakīm from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Jibrīl (peace be upon him) led me in prayer at the House twice.\"" He then mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it regarding the first time he said: \""He led me in Fajr prayer when food and drink became forbidden upon the fasting person.\"" And regarding the second time he said: \""He led me in Fajr prayer and it became bright (asfar).\""\n\nAnd we have narrated in the ḥadīth of Wahb ibn Kaysān from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh regarding this incident"," in which he said: \""Then Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when the dawn rose for Fajr and said: 'Stand"," O Muḥammad"," and pray.' So he stood and prayed Fajr. And in the second time"," he prayed when it had become very bright (asfar jiddan).\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"1765","(1765) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥātim al-Dārabardī informed us in Marw: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rūḥ al-Madāʾinī informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Fajr is two fajrs: as for the fajr that appears like the tail of a wolf"," it does not permit prayer nor does it prohibit food. And as for the fajr that spreads horizontally across the horizon"," it permits prayer and prohibits food.\"" This is how it was narrated with this isnād as a connected (mawṣūl) narration. It has also also been narrated as a mursal narration"," and the mursal is more correct. [Ṣaḥīh in its own right. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/304.]"""
"1766","(1766) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ informed us: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī informed us. And Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn Sahl informed us: Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us — both said: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Fajr is two fajrs.\"" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth similarly in full. It has also been narrated through another chain as a marfūʿ (raised) and mawqūf (stopped) narration. [Ṣaḥīh in its own right. Narrated as mursal by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/268.]"""
"1767","(1767) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adamī informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Marzūq al-Ṭabarī informed us: ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad, meaning al-Nāqid, informed us: Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī informed us: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Fajr is two fajrs: a fajr in which food is permitted and prayer is prohibited"," and a fajr in which prayer is permitted and food is prohibited.\"" This is how Abū Aḥmad narrated it as a musnad (connected) narration. Others narrated it as a mawqūf (stopped) narration"," and the mawqūf is more correct. [Ṣaḥīh in its own right. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 356.]"""
"1768","(1768) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated it to us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ informed us, from Sufyān, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Fajr is two fajrs: a fajr that rises during the night"," in which food and drink are permitted and prayer is not permitted; and a fajr in which prayer is permitted and food and drink are prohibited — and it is the one that spreads over the summits of the mountains.\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"1769","(1769) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated from Anas ibn Mālik that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the time of the Fajr prayer. He commanded Bilāl, so he called the adhān when Fajr rose. Then he called the iqāmah and he (the Prophet ﷺ) prayed. The following day, he delayed it until it became bright (asfar). Then he commanded him to call the iqāmah, so he called the iqāmah and he prayed. Then he called the man and said: \Did you witness the prayer yesterday and today?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Between these two is the (valid) time (for prayer).\""\n\nAnd we have narrated its meaning in the ḥadīth of Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and it is a ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 642.]"""
"1770","(1770) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Tamtām Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us: Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī informed us: Hammām ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Qatādah narrated from Abū Ayyūb from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said — and he mentioned the ḥadīth — in which he said: \And the time of the Ṣubḥ prayer is from the rising of Fajr so long as the sun has not risen. When the sun rises"," then refrain from prayer"," for it rises between the two horns of Shayṭān.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī from ʿAbd al-Ṣamad from Hammām"," except that he said: \""When the sun rises"," then refrain from prayer"," for it rises between the two horns of Shayṭān.\"" [Ṣaḥīh.]"""
"1771","(1771) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad, meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith, narrated to us; Hammām narrated it with its chain of narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1772","(1772) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: it was read to Ibn Wahb, \Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you.\"" And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb"," meaning al-Shaybānī al-Ḥāfiẓ"," narrated to us; Tamīm ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Yūnus informed me"," from Ibn Shihāb"," that ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Whoever catches one rakʿah of ʿAṣr before the sun sets"," or one rakʿah of Fajr before the sun rises"," has indeed caught it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah"," and he added in the hadith: \""And the sajdah (prostration) here means the rakʿah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 609]"""
"1773","(1773) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh narrated, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever catches one rakʿah of the prayer has caught all of it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 607]"""
"1774","(1774) Abū Muḥammad Junāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Junāḥ al-Qāḍī al-Muḥāribī in al-Kūfah narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn narrated to us; al-Faḍl, meaning ibn Dukayn, narrated to us; Shaybān narrated, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you catches the first prostration of ʿAṣr prayer before the sun sets"," let him complete his prayer. And when he catches the first prostration of Fajr prayer before the sun rises"," let him complete his prayer.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 531]"""
"1775","(1775) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir, the grandson of Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, narrated to us; my grandfather Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said —\n\n(Aḥmad ibn Salamah said:) And Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to me; Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, and Busr ibn Saʿīd, and from al-Aʿraj, who narrated to him from Abū Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Whoever catches one rakʿah of Fajr before the sun rises"," and one rakʿah after it has risen"," has indeed caught Fajr. And whoever catches one rakʿah of ʿAṣr before the sun sets"," and three rakʿahs after it has set"," has indeed caught ʿAṣr.\""\n\nMuslim ibn Khālid al-Zanjī narrated something similar from Zayd ibn Aslam"," from al-Aʿraj and ʿAṭāʾ"," regarding the Fajr prayer. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 554]"""
"1776","(1776) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us; ʿAffān narrated to us; Hammām narrated, saying: Qatādah was asked about a man who prayed one rakʿah and then the edge of the sun rose. He said: Khilās narrated to me from Abū Rāfiʿ, that Abū Hurayrah narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Let him complete his prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it"," 2/490]"""
"1777","(1777) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bazzāz in al-Ṭabarān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭūsī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us; Rūḥ narrated to us; Saʿīd, meaning ibn Abī ʿArūbah, narrated, from Qatādah, from Khilās, from Abū Rāfiʿ, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever prays one rakʿah of Fajr before the sun rises and then the sun rises"," let him pray another rakʿah to it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than it. Aḥmad narrated it"," 347]"""
"1778","(1778) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miqrīʾ al-Mihrajānī therein informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us; my father narrated, from Qatādah, from ʿAzrah ibn Tamīm, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \When one of you prays one rakʿah of Fajr and then the sun rises"," let him pray another rakʿah to it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than it]"""
"1779","(1779) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Saʿīd ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Rāzī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hishām narrated to us; Qatādah narrated, from Anas, who said: Abū Bakr led us in Fajr prayer and recited Āl ʿImrān. They said: The sun is about to rise. He said: Had it risen, it would not have found us heedless. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it, 3545]"
"1780","(1780) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated, from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī, who said: I prayed behind ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) the Fajr prayer, and he did not give the salām until the men of sound judgment thought that the sun had risen. When he gave the salām, they said: O Commander of the Faithful, the sun was about to rise. He said something that I did not understand, so I asked: What did he say? They said: He said: \Had it risen"," it would not have found us heedless.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ṭaḥāwī narrated it in Sharḥ al-Maʿānī"," 1/180]"""
"1781","(1781) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq and ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us in Makkah: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from Misʿar, from Ibrāhīm al-Saksakī, from Ibn Abī Awfā, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," the best of Allah's servants are those who observe the sun"," the moon"," the stars"," and the shadows for the remembrance of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn al-ʿAlāʾ is alone in narrating it with this isnād as such. And he is trustworthy. [Munkar. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/115]"""
"1782","(1782) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated to us: Misʿar informed us from Ibrāhīm al-Saksakī, who said: Our companions narrated to us from Abū al-Dardāʾ that he said: Indeed, the most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah are those who love Allah and who make Allah beloved to the people, and those who observe the sun, the moon, the stars, and the shadows for the remembrance of Allah.\n\nIt has also been narrated as a mawqūf report from Abū Hurayrah with the same meaning. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 34603]"
"1783","(1783) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us: Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad Abū Yūsuf narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Wāṣil, from Abū Ayyūb al-Aswārī, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: Beware, indeed the best of the Ummah of Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him) are those who observe the sun, the moon, and the stars for the times of prayer."
"1784","(1784) The jurist Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us in Ṭabarān: Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from what he read to Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night"," so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call to prayer.\""\n\nIbn Shihāb said: And Ibn Umm Maktūm was a blind man who would not give the call to prayer until it was said to him"," \""You have reached morning"," you have reached morning.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"," and al-Shāfiʿī and a group of narrators narrated it from Mālik as mursal. The hadith in the original is mawṣūl"," and a group connected it from Mālik"," among them Ibn Wahb"," Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah"," ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and Kāmil ibn Ṭalḥah. A group also connected it from al-Zuhrī. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1785","(1785) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus and al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed me from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Indeed"," Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night"," so eat and drink until you hear the call to prayer of Ibn Umm Maktūm.\""\n\nYūnus said in the hadith: And Ibn Umm Maktūm was the blind one concerning whom Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: \""He frowned and turned away"," because the blind man came to him\"" [ʿAbasa: 1–2]. He used to give the call to prayer along with Bilāl. Sālim said: He was a man with impaired vision"," and he would not give the call to prayer until the people"," upon seeing the emergence of the dawn"," would say to him"," \""Give the call to prayer.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from al-Layth"," and from Ḥarmalah from Ibn Wahb"," without the story. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1786","(1786) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Sulmān al-Najjād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night"," so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call to prayer.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1787","(1787) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sawādah al-Qushayrī narrated to us from his father, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Let not Bilāl's call to prayer nor the whiteness of the elongated horizon deceive you regarding your pre-dawn meal"," until it spreads thus.\"" And Ḥammād gestured with his hand"," meaning horizontally.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 1094]"""
"1788","(1788) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ, narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlūshā informed us in Asadābād, Hamadhān: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us: Abū ʿAlī Bishr ibn Mūsā al-Asadī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Ziyād ibn Nuʿaym al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to me, saying: I heard Ziyād ibn al-Ḥārith al-Ṣudāʾī narrating, saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam. And he mentioned a long hadith, saying: When the time for the call to prayer of the morning prayer came, he commanded me, so I gave the call to prayer. I began to say, \Shall I pronounce the iqāmah"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) kept looking toward the direction of the east"," toward the dawn"," and saying"," \""No.\"" When the dawn rose"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went down and relieved himself"," then turned to me"," and his companions had gathered. He said"," \""Is there any water"," O brother of Ṣudāʾ?\"" I said"," \""No"," except a little that will not suffice you.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said"," \""Put it in a vessel"," then bring it to me.\"" I did so"," and he placed his palm in the water. The Ṣudāʾī said: I saw between two of his fingers a spring gushing forth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: \""Were it not that I feel modesty before my Lord"," we would have drunk and given others to drink. Call out to my companions: whoever has a need for water.\"" So I called out to them"," and whoever among them wished took some. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood for the prayer. Bilāl intended to pronounce the iqāmah"," so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \""The brother of Ṣudāʾ has given the call to prayer"," and whoever gives the call to prayer is the one to pronounce the iqāmah.\"" The Ṣudāʾī said: So I pronounced the iqāmah.\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Ghānim from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād in an abbreviated form"," and he said in the hadith: When the first call to prayer of the morning came"," the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded me"," so I gave the call to prayer. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 514]"""
"1789","(1789) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Aṣamm informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us: Azhar ibn Saʿd al-Sammān narrated to us: Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated to us.\n\nHe said: And Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, and the wording is his: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me: My father narrated to me: Ismāʿīl narrated to us from Sulaymān, from Abū ʿUthmān, from Ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Let not Bilāl's call to prayer—or he said"," Bilāl's announcement—prevent any of you from his pre-dawn meal"," for he gives the call to prayer—or he says"," he makes the announcement—so that those among you who are praying may return"," or that those who are sleeping may awaken.\"" Then he said: \""It is not that he says thus—or he said"," thus—until he says thus.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it through various routes from Sulaymān"," and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 4992]"""
"1790","(1790) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Fāriyābī informed us: Isḥāq ibn Mūsā narrated to us: ʿAbadah ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah.\n\nAnd from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, both saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had two mu'adhdhins: Bilāl and Ibn Umm Maktūm. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night"," so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call to prayer.\""\n\nal-Qāsim said: There was not between their two calls to prayer except that this one would descend and this one would ascend.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from ʿAbadah"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through other routes from ʿUbayd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 380]"""
"1791","(1791) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Ḥabīb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: My aunt Unaysah narrated to me, saying: Bilāl and Ibn Umm Maktūm used to give the adhān for the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Bilāl gives the adhān at night"," so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the adhān.\"" We used to delay Ibn Umm Maktūm from giving the adhān"," saying: \""You have had your suḥūr"," you have had your suḥūr.\"" There was no interval between their two adhāns except that one would descend and the other would ascend.\n\nʿAmr ibn Marzūq and a group likewise narrated it from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī"," 1661]"""
"1792","(1792) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Abū al-Walīd and Abū ʿUmar both said: Shuʿbah narrated from Khubayb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: I heard my aunt Unaysah say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Ibn Umm Maktūm calls out at night"," so eat and drink until Bilāl calls out.\"" Thus narrated Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb al-Rāzī from both of them.\n\nMuḥammad ibn Yūnus al-Kudaymī narrated it from Abū al-Walīd as narrated by al-Ṭayālisī and ʿAmr ibn Marzūq. Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb and a group narrated it with doubt (shakk)."""
"1793","(1793) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated:\n\nKhubayb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me, saying: I heard my aunt, who had performed Ḥajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Bilāl gives the adhān at night"," so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the adhān\"" — or he said: \""Indeed"," Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the adhān at night"," so eat and drink until Bilāl gives the adhān.\"" She said: This one would ascend and this one would descend"," so we would cling to him and say: \""You have had your suḥūr.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us"," saying: If the narration of Abū ʿUmar and others is authentic"," then it is possible that there was a rotation (nawbah) between Ibn Umm Maktūm and Bilāl. When it was Bilāl's turn"," he would give the adhān at night"," and when it was Ibn Umm Maktūm's turn"," he would give the adhān at night.\n\nThis is permissible and sound"," even if it is not authentic. The narration of Ibn ʿUmar"," Ibn Masʿūd"," Samurah"," and ʿĀʾishah is authentic: that Bilāl used to give the adhān at night. The Shaykh said: It has also been narrated in the ḥadīth of ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah that the adhān of Ibn Umm Maktūm was given first. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1794","(1794) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Madanī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Ibn Umm Maktūm is a blind man. When he gives the adhān"," eat and drink until Bilāl gives the adhān.\"" ʿĀʾishah said: And Bilāl used to see the dawn (i.e."," he could perceive the true dawn).\n\nHishām said: ʿĀʾishah used to say: \""Ibn ʿUmar was mistaken.\""\n\nIt was thus narrated with its isnād. However"," the ḥadīth of ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from ʿĀʾishah is more authentic.\n\nAl-Wāqidī narrated it"," but it is not a proof"," with his isnād from Zayd ibn Thābit. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 406]"""
"1795","(1795) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Fawāris both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Wāqidī narrated to us, Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd, the mawlā of al-Aswad, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, from Zayd ibn Thābit, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the adhān at night"," so eat and drink until Bilāl gives the adhān.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ by virtue of other narrations]"""
"1796","(1796) Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥākim narrated to us, Abū Baḥr al-Barbarhārī narrated to us, Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Ḥumaydī informed us, Sufyān narrated to us, Shabīb ibn Gharrādah narrated:\n\nThat he heard Ḥibbān ibn al-Ḥārith say: I came to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib while he was encamped at the well of Abū Mūsā. I found him eating, so he said: \Come close and eat.\"" I said: \""I intend to fast.\"" He said: \""And I also intended to fast.\"" When he finished his food"," he said to Ibn al-Nabbāḥ: \""Announce the prayer (iqāmah).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 7609]"""
"1797","(1797) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Abū Muslim narrated to us, Abū ʿUmar al-Ḍarīr narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Mūsā informed us, Ḥammād narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: That Bilāl gave the adhān before the rising of the dawn, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to return and call out: \Beware! The servant has slept! Beware! The servant has slept!\"" — three times.\n\nMūsā ibn Ismāʿīl added in his ḥadīth: He returned and called out: \""Beware! The servant has slept.\""\n\nThis is a ḥadīth whose connected chain (waṣl) is uniquely narrated by Ḥammād ibn Salamah from Ayyūb.\n\nIt was also narrated from Saʿīd ibn Zarbī from Ayyūb"," except that Saʿīd is weak. The narration of Ḥammād is singular (munfaridah). The ḥadīth of ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar is more authentic than it"," along with the narration of al-Zuhrī from Sālim from his father. [Munkar. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 532]"""
"1798","(1798) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh, informed us, ʿAbdān narrated to us, Hudbah and Ṭālūt both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, and he mentioned the ḥadīth similar to the ḥadīth of Abū ʿUmar al-Ḍarīr.\n\nThen he said: ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: Ḥammād erred in this ḥadīth. The authentic ḥadīth is that of ʿUbaydullāh, i.e., from Nāfiʿ, and the ḥadīth of al-Zuhrī from Sālim. [Munkar]"
"1799","(1799) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, saying: I heard Abū Bakr al-Muṭayyiz say: I heard Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā say: The ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Salamah from Ayyūb from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar — that Bilāl gave the adhān before the rising of the dawn — is shāddh (irregular), not settled upon the heart, and it contradicts what the people have narrated from Ibn ʿUmar.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Maʿmir ibn Rāshid narrated it from Ayyūb, saying: \Bilāl gave the adhān once at night","\"" and he narrated it mursal. It was also narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rawwād from Nāfiʿ as a connected (mawṣūl) narration"," but it is weak and not authentic. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1800","(1800) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Kharrāz informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr ibn Khālid al-Naysābūrī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rawwād, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: That Bilāl gave the adhān at night, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \What prompted you to do that?\"" He said: \""I awoke while I was drowsy (wasnān)"," so I thought that the dawn had risen"," so I gave the adhān.\"" The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to call out in Madīnah three times: \""Indeed"," the servant has slept.\"" Then he seated him by his side until the dawn rose"," then he said: \""Stand up now.\"" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the two rakʿahs of the dawn (fajr).\n\nʿĀmir ibn Mudrik also narrated it from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz as a connected"," abbreviated narration"," but it is a mistake (wahm). The correct narration is that of Shuʿayb ibn Ḥarb. [Munkar]"""
"1801","(1801) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī narrated to us; Ayyūb ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Shuʿayb ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rawwād; Nāfiʿ narrated to us, from a muʾadhdhin of ʿUmar who was called Masrūḥ, that he gave the adhān before dawn, so ʿUmar commanded him. He mentioned something similar to it, i.e., similar to the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Salamah. Abū Dāwūd said: And Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ or another, that a muʾadhdhin of ʿUmar, called Masrūḥ or another, [did likewise]. And al-Dāwardī narrated it from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: ʿUmar had a muʾadhdhin called Masʿūd, and he mentioned something similar. Abū Dāwūd said: And this is more authentic than that, i.e., the ḥadīth of ʿUmar is more authentic. The Shaykh said: And it has been narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb that he said: \Hasten the adhān of Fajr"," so that the one who is sleeping may wake up and the one in the house may rise.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 533]"""
"1802","(1802) Abū Ṭāhir al-Imām informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us; Abū al-Azhar narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Burqān; Shaddād, the freed slave of ʿIyāḍ, said: Bilāl came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was eating suḥūr, and he said: \Do not give the adhān until you see the dawn.\"" Then he came the next day and he said: \""Do not give the adhān until the dawn rises.\"" Then he came the next day and he said: \""Do not give the adhān until you see the dawn"," like this.\"" And he gathered his two hands together and then separated them. This is a mursal ḥadīth. Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: Shaddād"," the freed slave of ʿIyāḍ"," did not meet Bilāl. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us of that; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us"," from Abū Dāwūd. The Shaykh said: And it has been narrated through other chains"," all of which are weak; we have explained their weakness in the book al-Khilāf. It is only known as mursal from the ḥadīth of Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl and others. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 534]"""
"1803","(1803) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us, from Ḥumayd, who said: Bilāl gave the adhān at night, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Return to your place and call out three times: Indeed"," the servant has overslept.\"" And he was saying: \""Would that Bilāl's mother had never given birth to him!\"" And he was drenched with the splatter of the blood of his forehead. So he called out three times: \""Indeed"," the servant has overslept.\"" Thus a group narrated it from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl as mursal. The authentic aḥādīth that have been previously mentioned"," along with the practice of the people of the Two Sacred Sanctuaries"," are more deserving of acceptance. And with Allah is the success. [Munkar. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī 1/244]"""
"1804","(1804) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us; Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh, i.e., Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, narrated to us; Shuʿayb ibn Ḥarb narrated to us. He said: I said to Mālik ibn Anas: \Did the Prophet ﷺ not command Bilāl to repeat the adhān?\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed"," Bilāl gives the adhān at night"," so eat and drink.'\"" I said: \""Did he not command him to repeat the adhān?\"" He said: \""No"," the adhān has always been given at night according to us.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1805","(1805) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us; Abū Khaythamah narrated to us; Abū Isḥāq narrated to us; Simāk narrated to us; Jābir ibn Samurah narrated and said: Bilāl used to give the adhān when the sun had set (i.e., at Maghrib), and then he would not give the iqāmah until he saw the Prophet ﷺ. When he saw him, he would give the iqāmah at the moment he saw him. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Abū Khaythamah. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Muslim 606]"
"1806","(1806) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān al-Hamdānī informed me; Hilāl ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Raqqī narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Asad narrated to us; Wuhaib ibn Khālid narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith, who said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a group from my people, and we stayed with him for twenty nights. He was merciful and compassionate. When he saw our longing for our families, he said: \Return and be among them"," and teach them and pray. When the time of prayer arrives"," let one of you give the adhān"," and let the eldest of you lead you in prayer.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muʿallā ibn Asad. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 602]"""
"1807","(1807) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us. He said: Mālik said: \Fajr has always been called for (with the adhān) before dawn. As for the other prayers"," we did not see them called for except after their time had entered.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1808","(1808) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us. He said: al-Shāfiʿī said: \No prayer other than Fajr is given the adhān except after its time has entered"," because I do not know of anyone who reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he gave the adhān for any prayer before its time other than Fajr. And we did not see the muʾadhdhins among us give the adhān except after the entry of its time"," except for Fajr.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1809","(1809) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī al-Faqīh in Naysābūr and Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us; Ibn ʿAwn narrated to us, from Ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The people of Yemen have come to you; the people of Yemen have come to you. They are the most tender of hearts. Faith is Yemeni"," understanding (fiqh) is Yemeni"," and wisdom is Yemeni.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr al-Nāqid"," from Isḥāq al-Azraq"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Abū Ṣāliḥ"," from Abū Hurayrah. al-Shāfiʿī said: \""And Makkah and Madīnah are Yemeni"," along with what this indicates of their virtue in their knowledge.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 4127]"""
"1810","(1810) And he mentioned the ḥadīth which Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī narrated to us by dictation and recitation; Abū Ḥāmad ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is near that you will strike the livers of camels and not find a scholar more knowledgeable than the scholar of Madīnah.\"" al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in al-Qadīm from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī 2680]"""
"1811","(1811) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakim al-Miṣrī narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī Fudayk informed me, saying: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdād, saying: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us, saying: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAwf, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Azhar, from Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \For the Qurayshi"," there is the strength of two men who are not from Quraysh.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Fudayk. Zayd added in his narration: It was said to al-Zuhrī"," \""What do you mean by that?\"" He said: \""Sharpness of judgment.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 4/81]"""
"1812","(1812) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Busr ibn Saʿīd, and from al-Aʿraj — all of them narrating from Abū Hurayrah — that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever catches one rakʿah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises has indeed caught the Fajr"," and whoever catches one rakʿah of the ʿAṣr prayer before the sun sets has indeed caught the ʿAṣr.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," both from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1813","(1813) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read before Mālik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever catches one rakʿah of the prayer has indeed caught the prayer.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it from Ibn Yūsuf"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 555]"""
"1814","(1814) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us, saying: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in the year twenty-five and three hundred, saying: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and ʿAlī ibn Saʿīd both narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated — ʿAlī said, meaning al-Thawrī — from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Abū al-Ṭufayl, from Muʿādh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) combined Ẓuhr with ʿAṣr, and Maghrib with ʿIshāʾ, in the year of Tabūk. And ʿAlī ibn Saʿīd said: \In the expedition of Tabūk.\""\n\nIt is narrated in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Abū al-Zubayr from Abū al-Ṭufayl"," and from the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn Dīnār it is gharīb; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar is the sole narrator of it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1815","(1815) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us, saying: Sharīḥ ibn Yūnus narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿīd ibn Yarbuʿ, from his grandfather ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from a mawlā of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, who said: \If the menstruating woman becomes pure before the sun sets"," she should pray Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr together"," and if she becomes pure before Fajr"," she should pray Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ together.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 7025]"""
"1816","(1816) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr informed us, saying: Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Zāʾidah narrated to us, saying: Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād narrated from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \If a woman becomes pure during the time of the ʿAṣr prayer"," let her begin with Ẓuhr and pray it"," then let her pray ʿAṣr. And if she becomes pure during the time of the ʿIshāʾ"," let her begin and pray Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ.\""\n\nAnd Layth ibn Abī Sulaym narrated it from Ṭāwūs and ʿAṭāʾ"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: \""And if she becomes pure before Fajr"," she should pray Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dārimī 889]"""
"1817","(1817) And it is in what Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him: Abū al-Walīd informed us, saying: al-Shāmātī narrated to us, saying: Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj narrated to us, saying: Ḥafṣ narrated from Layth… and he mentioned it. And it was narrated from both of them as their own statement, and we have narrated it from a group of the Tābiʿīn other than them, and from the seven jurists of the people of Madīnah. [Ḥasan for other than itself]"
"1818","(1818) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, saying: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar lost consciousness and his mind was affected, so he did not make up the prayers.\n\nHe said: And Mālik said: \That is because the time had passed. As for the one who regains consciousness while still within a time"," then he should pray.\""\n\nThis is how it is in the narration of a group from Nāfiʿ. And in the narration of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ: \""A day and a night.\"" And in the narration of Ayyūb from Nāfiʿ: \""Three days.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 24]"""
"1819","(1819) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Baghdādī al-Raffāʾ informed us, saying: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād informed us that his father said: \The jurists whom I met — those whose opinion was followed"," meaning the Tābiʿīn of the people of Madīnah — used to say…\"" and he mentioned rulings"," among them: \""The one who loses consciousness does not make up the prayers unless he regains consciousness during the time of a prayer"," in which case he should pray it. And he does make up fasting. The one who loses consciousness and regains consciousness before the sun sets should pray Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr"," and if he regains consciousness before the rise of Fajr"," he should pray Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ.\"" They said: \""And likewise does the menstruating woman if she becomes pure before the sun sets or before the rise of Fajr.\""\n\nAnd a musnad ḥadīth has been narrated concerning it"," but its chain contains weakness. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan]"""
"1820","(1820) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, saying: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Daghūlī narrated to us, saying: Khārijah ibn Muṣʿab narrated to us, saying: Mughīth ibn Badīl narrated to us, saying: Khārijah narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAṭāʾ — he is Ibn Yasār — from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Aylī, from al-Qāsim, that he asked ʿĀʾishah about a man who loses consciousness and misses the prayer for a day, two days, or more than that. She said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no making up for any of that"," except that if he loses consciousness during his prayer and regains consciousness while still within its time"," then he should pray it.\"" [Bāṭil. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī 2/82]"""
"1821","(1821) And Abū Sa'd informed us — Abū Aḥmad informed us — Muḥammad narrated to us — Khārijah narrated to us — Mughīth narrated to us — Khārijah narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAṭāʾ from al-Ḥakam from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — the same as that.\n\nAnd likewise did Aḥmad ibn Khālid narrate it from al-Khārijah al-Akbar, and likewise it was narrated from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from Abū Ḥusayn, who was ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥusayn ibn ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār — al-Bukhārī mentioned it in al-Tārīkh and said: \There is room for scrutiny regarding it.\""\n\nAnd al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aylī — they abandoned him; Ibn al-Mubārak used to disparage him"," and Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal prohibited narrating his ḥadīth. [Bāṭil (False)]"""
"1822","(1822) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Mubashshir narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Sinān narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Sufyān from al-Suddī from Yazīd, the freed slave of ʿAmmār: that ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir lost consciousness during Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, and ʿIshāʾ, and he regained consciousness at half the night, so he prayed Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, and ʿIshāʾ. [Ḍaʿīf (Weak) — al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it (2/81)]"
"1823","(1823) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: \This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us from Muḥammad ﷺ\"" — and he mentioned aḥādīth"," and he said: \""And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Leave me as long as I leave you"," for those who came before you were destroyed by their questions and their disagreement with their prophets. And when I forbid you from something"," avoid it; and when I command you with a matter"," do of it what you are able.'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ (Authentic) — Muslim narrated it (1337)]"""
"1824","(1824) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated from ʿUqbah, who was Abū Thubayt al-Rāsibī, and he was thiqah (trustworthy) — from Abū al-Jawzāʾ: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb forbade women from spending the night away from ʿIshāʾ, fearing that they would menstruate — meaning the ʿIshāʾ prayer. [Ḍaʿīf (Weak)]"
"1825","(1825) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Abū al-Jawāb narrated to us — Ibn Shubrumah narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \If a woman is negligent in her prayer until she menstruates"," she must make up that prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ (Authentic) — al-Dārimī narrated it (885)]"""
"1826","(1826) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr al-Salūlī, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Kūfī, narrated to us — Isrāʾīl narrated from Abū Isḥāq from ʿAmr ibn Sharḥīl, who said: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I heard the caller of the Prophet ﷺ calling out: 'When the prayer is established"," let not the intoxicated approach the prayer.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf (Weak)]"""
"1827","(1827) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā al-Khuttalī narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from Isrāʾīl from Abū Isḥāq from ʿAmr from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, in the story of the prohibition of wine. He mentioned the ḥadīth, and in it: the verse in al-Nisāʾ was revealed: {O you who have believed, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying} [al-Nisāʾ: 43]. And the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call out: \Let not the intoxicated approach the prayer.\"" [Ḍaʿīf (Weak) — Abū Dāwūd narrated it (3670)]"""
"1828","(1828) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Yaḥyā narrated from Sufyān from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him: that a man from the Anṣār invited him and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, and they gave them to drink before wine was made unlawful. So ʿAlī led them in Maghrib and recited {Say: O disbelievers} [al-Kāfirūn: 1], but he mixed it up in his recitation. Then the verse was revealed: {Do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying} [al-Nisāʾ: 43]. [Ṣaḥīḥ (Authentic) — Abū Dāwūd narrated it (3671)]"
"1829","(1829) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāl al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated to him from his father from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Whoever misses a prayer due to intoxication even once"," it is as though the world and all that is in it were taken from him. And whoever misses a prayer due to intoxication four times"," it becomes a right upon Allah to give him to drink from ṭīnat al-khabāl.\"" It was asked: \""And what is ṭīnat al-khabāl"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""The pus of the people of Jahannam.\"" [Ḥasan (Good) — Aḥmad narrated it (2/178)]"""
"1830","(1830) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Maḥmawīyah al-ʿAskarī in al-Ahwāz narrated to us — Abū al-Faḍl Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād al-Qalānisī in al-Ramlah narrated to us — Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us — al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us — Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Three — their prayer is not accepted nor does any good deed ascend for them: the fugitive slave until he returns to his masters and places his hand in theirs; the woman whose husband is angry with her; and the intoxicated until he regains sobriety.\"" Zuhayr was alone in narrating it in this manner. [Ḍaʿīf (Weak) — Ibn Ḥibbān narrated it (5355)]"""
"1831","(1831) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān the trustworthy transmitter informed us in Baghdad, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām informed us, Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad informed us — he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Nāfiʿ, the freedman of Ibn ʿUmar, informed me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that he used to say: \When the Muslims arrived in Madīnah"," they would gather and estimate the times of the prayers"," and no one would call them. One day they spoke about this matter. Some of them said: 'Let us adopt a nāqūs (church bell) like the bell of the Christians.' Others said: 'Rather"," a horn (qarn) like the horn of the Jews.' ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: 'Why do you not send a man who will call people to prayer?' The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'O Bilāl"," stand up and call to prayer.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ḥajjāj"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 579]"""
"1832","(1832) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Khālid informed us from Abū Qilābah from Anas who said: \They mentioned that they should mark the time of prayer by something by which they would recognise it. They mentioned striking a nāqūs or lighting a fire. Bilāl was then ordered to pronounce the adhān in paired phrases and the iqāmah in single phrases.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it from Muḥammad from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī"," and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 578]"""
"1833","(1833) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Quṭaʿī informed us, Rūḥ ibn ʬAṭāʾ ibn Abī Maymūnah informed us, Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ informed us from Abū Qilābah from Anas who said: \When the time of prayer arrived during the era of the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ)"," a man would run through the streets calling out: 'Prayer! Prayer!' This became difficult for the people"," so they said: 'O Messenger of Allāh"," if only we had a nāqūs!' He said: 'That belongs to the Christians.' They said: 'Then a būq (horn)?' He said: 'That belongs to the Jews.' He then ordered Bilāl to pronounce the adhān in paired phrases and the iqāmah in single phrases.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 369]"""
"1834","(1834) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā al-Khutlī and Ziyād ibn Ayyūb — and the ḥadīth of ʿAbbād is more complete — both said: Hushaym informed us from Abū Bishr — Ziyād said: Abū Bishr informed us — from Abū ʿUmayr ibn Anas from his paternal uncles among the Anṣār who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was concerned about the prayer — how to gather the people for it. It was said to him: 'Set up a flag at the time of prayer"," and when they see it"," they will inform one another.' He did not like that. Then the qunʿ (i.e."," the shabbūr) was mentioned to him — Ziyād said: the shabbūr of the Jews — and he did not like that either"," saying: 'That is a matter of the Jews.' Then the nāqūs was mentioned to him"," and he said: 'That is a matter of the Christians.' ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd then departed"," deeply preoccupied with the concern of the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ)"," and he saw the adhān in his dream. He went to the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) in the morning and informed him"," saying: 'O Messenger of Allāh"," I was between sleep and wakefulness when a man came to me and taught me the adhān.' ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb had seen it before him but concealed it for twenty days. Then he informed the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ)"," who said to him: 'What prevented you from informing us?' He said: 'ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd preceded me"," so I felt shy.' The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'O Bilāl"," stand and see what ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd commands you"," and do it.' So Bilāl called the adhān.\"" Abū Bishr said: \""Abū ʿUmayr informed me that the Anṣār used to maintain that had ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd not been ill at that time"," the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) would have appointed him as the muʾadhdhin.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 498]"""
"1835","(1835) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Yaḥyā Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Samarqandī informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿd al-Zuhrī informed us, my uncle Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, my father informed us from Ibn Isḥāq who said: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī informed me from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbd Rabbih who said: My father ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd informed me, saying: \When the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) ordered that a nāqūs be made to be struck for the people to gather for prayer"," a man carrying a nāqūs in his hand circled around me while I was asleep. I said to him: 'O servant of Allāh"," will you sell the nāqūs?' He said: 'What will you do with it?' I said: 'We will call to prayer with it.' He said: 'Shall I not show you something better than that?' I said: 'Yes"," indeed.' He said: 'Say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illa Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illa Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh"," ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ. Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illa Allāh.' Then he stepped back a short distance and said: 'Then when you stand for the iqāmah"," say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illa Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ. Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh"," qad qāmat al-ṣalāh. Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illa Allāh.' When morning came"," I went to the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) and informed him of what I had seen. He said: 'It is a true dream"," in shāʾ Allāh taʿālā. Stand with Bilāl and teach him what you saw"," and let him call the adhān with it"," for his voice is more resonant than yours.' So I stood with Bilāl and taught it to him"," and he called the adhān with it. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb heard of this while he was in his house. He came out dragging his cloak"," saying: 'By the One Who sent you with the truth"," O Messenger of Allāh"," I have seen the same as he saw.' The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'All praise is due to Allāh.'\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 499]"""
"1836","(1836) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed me, my father informed us, Yaʿqūb narrated it with its chain similarly, except that he mentioned the takbīr at the beginning of the adhān twice. Muḥammad ibn Salamah also narrated it from Ibn Isḥāq. [Ḥasan]"
"1837","(1837) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, and Abū Dāwūd said: \Thus al-Zuhrī narrated it from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd — meaning the story of the dream regarding the pairing of the adhān and the singling of the iqāmah.\"" Ibn Isḥāq said from al-Zuhrī: \""Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar.\"" Maʿmar and Yūnus said from al-Zuhrī: \""Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar\"" — they did not pair it. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," saying: I heard the Imam Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb say: I heard Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muṭarriz say: I heard Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā say: \""There is no narration in the reports of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd regarding the story of the adhān more authentic than this one\"" — meaning the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd — \""because Muḥammad heard from his father"," while Ibn Abī Laylā did not hear from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd.\"" In the Kitāb al-ʿIlal of Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī"," it is stated: \""I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī about this ḥadīth\"" — meaning the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī — and he said: \""It is"," in my view"," a ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1838","(1838) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir, the grandson of Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr the Qāḍī, informed us, my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr informed us, Abū Bakr ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Sadūsī informed us, ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī informed us, al-Masʿūdī informed us, ʿAmr ibn Murrah informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā informed us from Muʿādh ibn Jabal who said: \The prayer went through three states.\"" He mentioned first the state of the qiblah and last the state of one who joins the prayer late. Between these he mentioned the state of the adhān"," saying: \""They used to gather for the prayer"," some of them informing one another"," until they nearly adopted a nāqūs — or were about to adopt one. Then a man called ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allāh"," while I was between sleep and wakefulness"," I saw a figure wearing two green garments. He stood"," faced the qiblah"," and said: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar — until he completed the adhān"," phrase by phrase in pairs. Then at the end of his adhān he said: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illa Allāh. Then he paused briefly"," then stood and said the same as he had said"," except that he added: Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh"," qad qāmat al-ṣalāh.' The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'Teach it to Bilāl.' So the first to call it was Bilāl. Then ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb came and said: 'O Messenger of Allāh"," a figure circled around me just as it circled around ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd"," except that he preceded me to you.'\"" A group narrated its meaning from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Masʿūdī. However"," ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā did not meet Muʿādh"," so it is mursal. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 507]"""
"1839","(1839) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad informed us — he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Nāfiʿ, the freedman of Ibn ʿUmar, informed me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that he used to say: \When the Muslims arrived in Madīnah…\"" — and he narrated the ḥadīth about the origin of the adhān. At the end of it is: \""The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'O Bilāl"," stand up and call to prayer.'\"" Muslim narrated it as above. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1840","(1840) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad, Abū Muḥammad Jaʿfar ibn Hārūn informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Sinān informed us, Salm ibn Sulaymān al-Ḍabbī informed us, Ṣadaqah ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Māzinī informed us, al-Ḥārith ibn ʿUtbah informed us, ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil informed us from his father who said: \It is a right and an established sunnah that a man should not call the adhān unless he is in a state of purity"," and he should not call it unless he is standing.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1841","(1841) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿUmarī narrated from Nāfiʿ, who said: Ibn ʿUmar would sometimes give the adhān for Fajr while mounted on his riding animal, and then give the iqāmah on the ground. [Ḥasan for other than its own chain.]"
"1842","(1842) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Qilābah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī from Abī Ṭuʿmah, that Ibn ʿUmar used to give the adhān while mounted on his riding animal. And a mursal ḥadīth has been narrated regarding it. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"1843","(1843) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: Ismāʿīl narrated from al-Ḥasan, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilāl during a journey, so he gave the adhān while mounted on his riding animal. Then they dismounted and prayed two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs. Then he commanded him, so he gave the iqāmah, and he led them in the Fajr prayer. [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"1844","(1844) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad, who said: I visited Abū Zayd al-Anṣārī, and he gave the adhān and the iqāḥah while sitting. He said: A man came forward and led us in prayer, and he was lame; his foot had been injured in the cause of Allah, the Exalted. And it has been narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ that he said: It is disliked for one to give the adhān while sitting, except due to an excuse. [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"1845","(1845) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Imām Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us: my father narrated from ʿĀmir al-Aḥwal from Makhūl from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥayrīz from Abī Maḥdhūrah, that the Prophet ﷺ taught him this adhān: \Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh.\"" Then he would repeat: \""Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh (twice). Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ (twice). Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh.\"" Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from Muʿādh ibn Hishām. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Muslim"," 379.]"""
"1846","(1846) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated among the last narrators, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Muslim ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥayrīz informed him — and he was an orphan under the care of Abī Maḥdhūrah when he set out for al-Shām — so I said to Abī Maḥdhūrah: \O my uncle"," I am going out to al-Shām"," and I fear that I may be asked about your adhān"," so inform me.\"" Abī Maḥdhūrah said: \""Yes. I went out with a group of people"," and we were at a point along the road to Ḥunayn. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was returning from Ḥunayn"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met us along the road. The muʾadhdhin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the adhān for the prayer in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and we heard the voice of the muʾadhdhin while we were turning aside. We began shouting"," imitating him and mocking him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard"," so he sent to us until we stood before him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Which one of you is the one whose voice I heard raised?' The people all pointed to me"," and they spoke the truth. He sent all of them away and detained me. He said: 'Stand and give the adhān for the prayer.' So I stood"," and there was nothing I disliked more than the Prophet ﷺ or what he was commanding me to do. I stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me the adhān himself. He said: 'Say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh.' Then he said to me: 'Go back and raise your voice.' Then he said: 'Say: Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh"," ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ. Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh.' Then he called me when I had completed the adhān"," and he gave me a small pouch containing some silver. Then he placed his hand on the forelock of Abī Maḥdhūrah"," then passed it over his face"," then between his two breasts"," then over his liver"," until his hand reached the navel of Abī Maḥdhūrah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'May Allah bless you and bless upon you.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," command me to give the adhān in Makkah.' He said: 'I have already commanded you to do so.' Everything that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had of dislike departed"," and all of that turned into love for the Prophet ﷺ. I came to ʿAttāb ibn Asīd"," the governor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and I gave the adhān for the prayer by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" Ibn Jurayj said: \""Those of the family of Abī Maḥdhūrah whom I reached informed me in the same manner as Ibn Muḥayrīz informed me.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""I met Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah"," and he used to give the adhān as Ibn Muḥayrīz narrated"," and I heard him narrate from his father from Ibn Muḥayrīz from Abī Maḥdhūrah from the Prophet ﷺ the meaning of what Ibn Jurayj narrated.\"" And with its meaning"," it was narrated by Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad"," Abū ʿĀṣim"," and Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah from Ibn Jurayj. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 632.]"""
"1847","(1847) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Yaḥyā al-Samarqandī narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me: ʿUthmān ibn al-Sāʾib, their freedman, narrated from his father — the elder, the freedman of Abī Maḥdhūrah — and from Umm ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah, that both of them heard from Abī Maḥdhūrah, who said: \I went out with ten young men with the Prophet ﷺ to Ḥunayn. They gave the adhān"," and we stood giving the adhān"," mocking them. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Bring these young men to me.' He said: 'Give the adhān.' So they gave the adhān"," and I had the loudest voice among them. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Yes"," this is the one whose voice I heard. Go and give the adhān for the people of Makkah"," and say to ʿAttāb ibn Asīd: The Messenger of Allah has commanded me to give the adhān for the people of Makkah.' And he said: 'Say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh (twice). Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh (twice). Then repeat: Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh (twice). Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh (twice). Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh (twice). Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ (twice). Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh. And when you give the iqāmah"," say it twice: Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh"," qad qāmat al-ṣalāh.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than its own chain. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī.]"""
"1848","(1848) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn ʿUbayd narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah from his father from his grandfather, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," teach me the Sunnah of the adhān.\"" He said: He wiped the front of my head and said: \""You say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar — raise your voice with it. Then you say: Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh — lower your voice with it. Then raise your voice with the testimony: Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh"," ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ. If it is the Fajr prayer"," you say: Al-ṣalāḥu khayrun min al-nawm"," al-ṣalāḥu khayrun min al-nawm. Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh.\"" And in some narrations from Abī Maḥdhūrah in this ḥadīth"," there is mention of returning to the words of takbīr after the two testimonies"," but that is not strong"," given its contradiction of the well-known narrations and the practice of the people of the Ḥijāz. [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than its own chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 500.]"""
"1849","(1849) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdād: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd ibn ʿAmmār ibn Saʿd ibn ʿĀʾidh al-Qaraẓī said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmmār, ʿAmmār, and ʿUmar, the two sons of Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar ibn Saʿd, narrated to me from ʿAmmār ibn Saʿd from his father Saʿd al-Qaraẓī, that he heard him say: \This adhān — meaning the adhān of Bilāl — which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to perform"," and his iqāmah"," is: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Then he would repeat: Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh"," ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ. Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh. And the iqāmah is one by one"," and he would say: Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh once.\"" Thus it is in the book"," and others narrate it from al-Ḥumaydī"," mentioning the takbīr at the beginning of the adhān twice"," while al-Ḥumaydī narrates it in the ḥadīth of Abī Maḥdhūrah as four. And we take by it because it is additional. [Ḥasan for other than its own chain. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 3/703.]"""
"1850","(1850) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAwn ibn Abī Juḥayfah from Abī Juḥayfah, who said: \I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a red tent at al-Abṭaḥ. Bilāl came out to us with the leftover water of the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and people were scrambling for it — some obtaining some and some obtaining nothing. Then Bilāl gave the adhān"," and I began following his mouth — here and here.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 503.]"""
"1851","(1851) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAwn ibn Abī Juḥayfah narrated to us from his father, and he mentioned the hadith, and in it he said: \He performed wuḍūʾ"," and Bilāl gave the adhān. I followed his mouth — here and there — turning right and left"," saying: Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," from Wakīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1852","(1852) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā narrated to us; Qays, meaning Ibn al-Rabīʿ, narrated to us from ʿAwn ibn Abī Juḥayfah from his father, who said: \I saw Bilāl come out to the Abṭaḥ and give the adhān. When he reached ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," he turned his neck to the right and to the left"," but he did not turn around completely. Then he went inside and brought out the spear","\"" and he narrated the rest of the hadith.\n\nThus narrated it Qays. But al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāʾah contradicted him and said: \""And he turned around in his adhān.\"" [Munkar. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (520)]"""
"1853","(1853) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us; al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāʾah narrated to us from ʿAwn ibn Abī Juḥayfah from his father, who said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at the Abṭaḥ in a red tent. Then Bilāl came out and placed water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for purification. Then he gave the adhān"," placing his fingers in his ears"," and he turned around in his adhān.\""\n\nIt is possible that al-Ḥajjāj intended by \""turning around\"" (al-istidārah) his turning of the neck at ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," in which case he would be in agreement with the rest of the narrators. (c) Al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāʾah is not a ḥujjah (authoritative proof). May Allah forgive us and him.\n\nʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it from Sufyān al-Thawrī from ʿAwn ibn Abī Juḥayfah"," interpolated within the hadith. However"," Sufyān only narrated this wording in al-Jāmiʿ through the narration of al-ʿAdanī from him"," from an unnamed man"," from ʿAwn.\n\nIt was also narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah from ʿAwn ibn Abī Juḥayfah as a mursal narration"," in which he did not say \""from his father.\"" And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other routes. Ibn Mājah narrated it (711)]"""
"1854","(1854) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us from al-Ḥajjāj from ʿAwn ibn Abī Juḥayfah from his father, who said: \I saw Bilāl giving the adhān"," having placed his fingers in his ears"," and he was turning in his adhān to the right and to the left.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it (197)]"""
"1855","(1855) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; ʿAbdān narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd ibn ʿAmmār ibn Saʿd narrated to me; my father narrated to me from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilāl to place his fingers in his ears, and his iqāmah was given singly: \Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh\"" once only. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other routes. Ibn Mājah narrated it (710)]"""
"1856","(1856) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rustah narrated to us; and Ibn Abī ʀāṣim informed us; both said: Ibn Kāsib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad, and ʿUmar, and ʿAmmār, the two sons of Ḥafṣ, from their fathers, from their grandfathers, from Bilāl, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \When you give the adhān"," place your fingers in your ears"," for it raises your voice.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Kabīr (1072)]"""
"1857","(1857) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, he said: it was read to Ibn Wahb: Ibn Lahīʿah informed you from Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Anṣārī from ʿĪsā ibn Ḥārithah from Ibn al-Musayyab that he said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilāl to give the adhān"," so he placed his fingers in his ears"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was looking at him and did not disapprove of that. From that day the Sunnah was established.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn Sīrīn that Bilāl placed his fingers in his ears during some of his adhān or during his iqāmah. [Very weak]"""
"1858","(1858) Abū Bakr al-Ḥārithī al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Ibn Abī ʀāṣim narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us from Muʿāwiyah ibn Yaḥyā from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ said: \No one should give the adhān except one who is in a state of wuḍūʾ.\"" Thus narrated it Muʿāwiyah ibn Yaḥyā al-Ṣadafī. (c) And he is weak.\n\nThe authentic narration is that of Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī and others from al-Zuhrī"," who said: Abū Hurayrah said: \""No one should call to prayer except one who is in a state of wuḍūʾ.\"" [Munkar. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it (200)]"""
"1859","(1859) Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh, informed us; ʿAbdān narrated to us; Hilāl ibn Bishr narrated to us; ʿUmayr ibn ʿImrān al-ʿAllāf narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn ʿUtbah narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil from his father, who said: \It is a right and an established Sunnah that no one should give the adhān except while in a state of purity"," and no one should give the adhān except while standing.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil's narration from his father is mursal. (q) This is the statement of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ. Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī said: \""They saw no harm in a man giving the aladhān without wuḍūʾ.\"" Al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī and Qatādah held the same view. The discussion on this matter relates to the recommendation of purification during dhikr"," and this has already been addressed in the Book of Purification. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1860","(1860) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, among the last of those who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Mālik informed us.\n\n(ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhṭawayh informed us; al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; Mālik informed us from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ṣaʿṣaʿah al-Anṣārī, then al-Māzinī, from his father, that he informed him that Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī said: \I see that you love sheep and the desert. So when you are among your sheep or in your desert and you give the adhān for the prayer"," raise your voice with the call"," for nothing hears the range of the muʾadhdhin's voice — no jinn"," no human"," and nothing at all — except that it will testify for him on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Abū Saʿīd said: \""I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Abī Uways.\n\nIn the hadith of al-Shāfiʿī"," from Mālik"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṣaʿṣaʿah"," from his father"," that Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī said to him: \""And when you give the adhān for the prayer"," raise your voice"," for nothing hears the range of your voice.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (3122)]"""
"1861","(1861) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from Mūsā ibn Abī ʿUthmān. Shuʿbah said: \And he used to give the adhān from the tallest minaret in Kūfah.\"" He said: \""Abū Yaḥyā narrated to me while I was performing ṭawāf with him — meaning around the House (the Kaʿbah).\"" He said: \""I heard Abū Hurayrah say: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and I heard it from his mouth"," saying: \""The mu'adhdhin is forgiven to the extent of the reach of his voice"," and every wet and dry thing testifies on his behalf. And the one who attends the prayer is recorded for him twenty-five good deeds"," and whatever is between them (the two prayers) is expiated for him.\""'\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for others. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (515)]"""
"1862","(1862) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us: Abū ʿUbayd ibn Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Abū ʿĀmir al-Khazzāz narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Abī Maḥdhūrah, who said: \When ʿUmar arrived in Makkah"," I gave the adhān. ʿUmar said to me: 'O Abā Maḥdhūrah"," are you not afraid that your upper chest will split open?'\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (2060)]"""
"1863","(1863) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʔUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us: Musaddad informed us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, and ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd, the companion of al-Ziyādiyyāt, from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith, who said: \Ibn ʿAbbās delivered a sermon to us on a day of muddy rain (dhi radgh). When the mu'adhdhin reached 'Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh","' he instructed him to announce: 'Pray in your dwellings (al-ṣalāh fī al-riḥāl).' The people looked at one another"," and he said: 'It is as though you find this objectionable. One who is better than me has done this"," and indeed it is a matter of firm resolve (ʿazmah).'\""\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Rabīʿ from Ḥammād ibn Zayd and ʿĀṣim"," and from two other routes from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (591)]"""
"1864","(1864) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Marwān ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Bazzār in Damascus informed us: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār informed us: ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ḥabīb ibn Abī al-ʿIshrīn informed us: al-Awzāʿī said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī narrated to me that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī narrated to him from Nuʿaym ibn al-Naḥḥām, who said: \I was with my wife under her cloak on a cold morning when the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called out for the Fajr prayer. When I heard it"," I said: 'I wish the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: \""And whoever sits"," there is no harm.\""' When he said: 'Al-ṣalāhayrun min al-nawm (Prayer is better than sleep)","' he said: 'And whoever sits"," there is no harm.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for others]"""
"1865","(1865) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Hishām ibn ʿAlī al-Sīrāfī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Rajāʾ informed us: Muḥammad — meaning Ibn Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif — narrated from Jāmiʿ ibn Shaddād, from Mūsā ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Anṣārī, from Sulaymān ibn Ṣurd, who was a Companion (ṣāḥabī): \He used to give the adhān in the military camp and would instruct his servant with some task while he was in the midst of his adhān.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1866","(1866) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī informed us: al-Muḥāribī narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ: \Ibn ʿUmar gave the adhān one night at Ḍaḥnān on a cold night"," then he said: 'Pray in your dwellings (Ṣallū fī riḥālikum).' Then he informed them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to instruct the caller to call out the prayer"," and then to call out thereafter: 'Pray in your dwellings on a cold night or a rainy night.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (635)]"""
"1867","(1867) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb — and the ḥadīth is from Muḥammad — informed us: Musaddad informed us: Yaḥyā narrated from ʿUbaydullāh, who said: \Nāfiʿ narrated to me that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar gave the adhān one night at ʿIshāʾ at Ḍaḥnān on a cold night"," and said immediately after that: 'Verily"," pray in your dwellings (Alā ṣallū fī al-riḥāl).' And he informed us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to instruct a mu'adhdhin to give the adhān and then to call out thereafter: 'Pray in your dwellings on a cold night or a rainy night during travel.'\""\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from ʿUbaydullāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1868","(1868) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz in Baghdad informed us: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī in Makkah informed us: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrat informed us: Ibn Abī Uways informed us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm, from Nuʿaym ibn al-Naḥḥām of Banī ʿAdī ibn Kaʿb, who said: \The Fajr adhān was called out on a cold day while he was under his wife's cloak. He said: 'I wish the caller would also announce: \""And whoever sits"," there is no harm.\""' So the caller of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called out at the end of his adhān: 'And whoever sits"," there is no harm.' And this was during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\nal-Awzāʿī followed him up"," narrating from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"," except that he said: \""When he said: 'Al-ṣalāhayrun min al-nawm (Prayer is better than sleep)","' he said: 'And whoever sits"," there is no harm.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for others]"""
"1869","(1869) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us: Ibn Abī Maryam informed us: al-Firyābī narrated — ʿAlī said: \And Jāmiʿ ibn Sawādah narrated to me: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to me\"" — they both said: \""Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād"," from Ziyād ibn Nuʿaym"," from Ziyād ibn al-Ḥārith al-Ṣudāʾī"," who said: 'I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and gave the adhān for Fajr. Then Bilāl came to give the iqāmah"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""O Bilāl"," the brother of udāʾ has given the adhān"," and whoever gives the adhān"," he is the one to give the iqāmah.\""'\""\nThere is a witness for it from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar"," but its chain contains weakness. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"1870","(1870) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Jamīl informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us: Khalaf ibn Hishām al-Muqrīʾ Abū Muḥammad al-Bazzār informed us: Saʿīd ibn Rāshid al-Māzinī informed us: ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ narrated from Ibn ʿUmar: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a journey when the time for prayer arrived. The people dismounted and searched for Bilāl but could not find him. A man stood up and gave the adhān. Then Bilāl came"," and the people said: 'A man has already given the adhān.' The people remained for a while. Then Bilāl wanted to give the iqāmah"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: 'Hold on"," O Bilāl! Indeed"," the one who gives the iqāmah is the one who gave the adhān.'\""\nSaʿīd ibn Rāshid is the sole narrator of it"," and he is weak. [Munkar]"""
"1871","(1871) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to me: al-Shaybānī narrated from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ, who said: I saw Abū Maḥdhūrah come, and a person had already given the adhān before him, so he gave the adhān and then gave the iqāmah.\n\nThis is a sound (ṣaḥīḥ) chain of narration, serving as a corroborating witness for what has preceded. [Sound. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah (2242)]"
"1872","(1872) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Wāqifī narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Anṣārī from his uncle ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd, that he saw the adhān in a dream. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: \And Bilāl gave the adhān.\"" He said: \""Then my uncle came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I also saw the vision"," and Bilāl is giving the adhān.'\"" He said: \""Then you stand (and give the iqāmah).\"" So my uncle gave the iqāmah.\n\nThus Abū Dāwūd narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr.\n\nAnd Maʿn narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Wāqifī from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: There is room for scrutiny regarding it. [Weak. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī (3/11)]"""
"1873","(1873) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqrī informed us in Baghdad: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Najjād narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated from Abī al-ʿUmayth from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd from his father from his grandfather, who said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of how I had seen the adhān. He said: \Teach it to Bilāl"," for his voice is more resonant than yours.\"" When Bilāl gave the adhān"," ʿAbdullāh felt regretful"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him"," and he gave the iqāmah. Thus narrated Abū al-ʿUmayth.\n\nAnd it was narrated from Zayd ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh from his father from his grandfather likewise. And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Faqīh used to weaken this hadith by what has been previously mentioned. [Weak]"""
"1874","(1874) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Hushaym informed us from Abī Bishr from Abī ʿUmayr ibn Anas, who said: My paternal uncles from the Anṣār, who were Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me. They said: The Prophet ﷺ was concerned… and he mentioned the hadith, and in it he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd was ill on that day, and the Anṣār used to assert that had he not been ill, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have appointed him as the mu'adhdhin.\n\nThe Sheikh said: Even if the hadith of ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd were authentic and the hadith of al-Ṣudāʾī were authentic, the ruling would be in accordance with the hadith of al-Ṣudāʾī, because it came after the hadith of ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd. And with Allah is the success. [Weak]"
"1875","(1875) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Zurārah narrated to us: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father, who said: We came to Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh and I said: \Inform me about the Ḥajj of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\nHe mentioned the hadith and said in it: Then Bilāl gave the adhān"," then he gave the iqāmah"," and he prayed Ẓuhr. Then he gave the iqāmah and prayed ʿAṣr"," and he did not pray anything between them. Then he mounted. He said: When he came to al-Muzdalifah — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — he prayed Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ with one adhān and two iqāmahs.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl"," incorporated within the long hadith concerning the Ḥajj of the Prophet ﷺ. It is said that this portion of the hadith is mursal. [Sound]"""
"1876","(1876) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muslimah narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us. He said: And Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, he said: And Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us — the meaning is one and the same — from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ prayed Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr at ʿArafah with a single adhān and two iqāmahs, and he did not offer any supererogatory prayer between them. And he prayed Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ at Jamʿ (al-Muzdalifah) with a single adhān and two iqāmahs, and he did not offer any supererogatory prayer between them.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: This hadith was given its full chain by Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl in the long hadith, and Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī agreed with Ḥātim on its chain from Jaʿfar from his father from Jābir, except that he said: \He prayed Maghrib and al-ʿAtamah with an adhān and an iqāmah.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: Aḥmad — meaning Ibn Ḥanbal — told me: \""Ḥātim made an error in this long hadith.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: And Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated it from Jaʿfar just as Ḥātim narrated it. [Sound for other reasons. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1906)]"""
"1877","(1877) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Aḥmad ibn Bishr ibn Saʿd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father from Jābir, that the Prophet ﷺ prayed Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ with one adhān and two iqāmahs.\n\nAnd it has been narrated regarding Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ at Jamʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet ﷺ, and there is disagreement concerning it. [Sound]"
"1878","(1878) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Egypt: Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ at al-Muzdalifah, and he did not call for either of them except with an iqāmah, and he did not offer any supererogatory prayer between them, nor after either of them.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb. [Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1589)]"
"1879","(1879) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb from al-Zuhrī with the same meaning, and he said: \With an iqāmah"," an iqāmah — he combined them.\"" Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: Wakīʿ said: \""He prayed each prayer with an iqāmah.\"" [Sound. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1927)]"""
"1880","(1880) And Abū ʿAlī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Shabābah narrated to us. Abū Dāwūd said: And Makhlad ibn Khālid narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us — with the same meaning — from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb with the chain of Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal from Ḥammād, and with the same meaning, and he said: \With a single iqāmah for each prayer"," and he did not give the adhān for the first"," and he did not offer any supererogatory prayer after either of them.\""\n\nMakhlad said: \""He did not give the adhān for either of them.\"" Thus is the narration of Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh from his father"," and it is the most authentic of the narrations from Ibn ʿUmar. And Saʿīd ibn Jubayr narrated it from Ibn ʿUmar likewise. [Sound. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1928)]"""
"1881","(1881) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us, from Abū Isḥāq, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: We returned with Ibn ʿUmar, and he led us in Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ with a single iqāmah — three rakʿahs and two rakʿahs — then he said: \Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer in this place.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr"," from Ismāʿīl; and he also recorded it from the ḥadīth of al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah and Salamah ibn Kuhayl"," from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," with the same meaning.\n\nAnd al-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Isḥāq as well. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim recorded it"," 1288.]"""
"1882","(1882) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ṣaydalānī informed us from his original copy, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mālik al-Azdī, who said: I prayed Maghrib with Ibn ʿUmar at Jamʿ — three rakʿahs — and ʿIshāʾ — two rakʿahs — with a single iqāmah. Mālik ibn Khāld said to him: \What is this prayer"," O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?\"" He said: \""I prayed them both with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this place with a single iqāmah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd recorded it"," 1929.]"""
"1883","(1883) And Sharīk al-Qāḍī narrated it from Abū Isḥāq, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mālik, who both said: We prayed with Ibn ʿUmar at al-Muzdalifah — Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ — with a single iqāmah.\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Anbārī narrated to us: Isḥāq, meaning ibn Yūsuf, narrated to us, from Sharīk, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd Isrāʾīl narrated it from Abū Isḥāq, but he differed from others in its matn. [Ṣaḥīḥ by virtue of other narrations.]"
"1884","(1884) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ informed us: Isrāʾīl narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mālik, who said: I prayed behind Ibn ʿUmar two prayers at Jamʿ, with a single adhān and a single iqāmah altogether. Khālid ibn Mālik said to him: \What is this prayer"," O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?\"" He said: \""I prayed them both with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this place.\""\n\nThe narration of al-Thawrī and Sharīk is more authentic"," as it agrees with the narration of Saʿīd ibn Jubayr. The narration of Saʿīd may possibly agree with the narration of Sālim in that he intended a single iqāmah for each prayer — and Allah knows best.\n\nAnd something similar to the narration of Isrāʾīl has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar through another chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ by virtue of other narrations.]"""
"1885","(1885) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us: Ashʿath ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from his father, who said: I came with Ibn ʿUmar from ʿArafāt to al-Muzdalifah, and he did not cease from takbīr and tahlīl until we reached al-Muzdalifah. Then he gave the adhān and the iqāmah — or he ordered a man, and he gave the adhān and the iqāmah — then he led us in Maghrib, three rakʿahs. Then he turned to us and said: \The prayer","\"" and he led us in ʿIshāʾ"," two rakʿahs. Then he called for his supper.\n\nHe said: And ʿIlāj ibn ʿAmr informed me with a similar ḥadīth from his father"," from Ibn ʿUmar. And it was said to Ibn ʿUmar about that"," and he said: \""I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ thus.\""\n\nAnd it is narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd that they both prayed each of the two prayers at the time of ʿIshāʾ"," separated"," each with an adhān and an iqāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd recorded it"," 1933.]"""
"1886","(1886) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us: Abū al-ʿUmays narrated to us, from al-Ḥakam, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, that one of them accompanied ʿUmar and the other accompanied ʿAbd Allāh — may Allah be pleased with them both — and they both narrated from them that they did not pray Maghrib until they alighted at Jamʿ. Then they prayed Maghrib with an adhān and an iqāmah, then they had supper, then they prayed with an adhān and an iqāmah. This is a ṣaḥīḥ isnād. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"1887","(1887) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Zurʿah ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Dimashqī narrated to us: Aḥmad, meaning ibn Khālid al-Wahbī, narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, who said: I went out with Ibn Masʿūd to Makkah. He mentioned the ḥadīth and said: Then we arrived at Jamʿ, and he led us in the two prayers, each prayer separately, with an adhān and an iqāmah, and supper was between them.\n\nAl-Bukhārī recorded it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ, from Isrāʾīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī recorded it, 1599.]"
"1888","(1888) And Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated it from Abū Isḥāq, and he said in the ḥadīth: He ordered a man, and he gave the adhān and the iqāmah. Then he prayed Maghrib, and after it he prayed two rakʿahs. Then he called for his supper. Then he ordered — Zuhayr said: I think he hesitated — and he gave the adhān and the iqāmah. Then he prayed the last ʿIshāʾ, two rakʿahs.\n\nMuḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿArabah al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Bajalī narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abū Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd say: ʿAbd Allāh performed Ḥajj. He mentioned the ḥadīth and mentioned in it what we have previously cited.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn Khālid, from Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī recorded it, 159.]"
"1889","(1889) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī — may Allah have mercy on him — informed us by dictation: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb al-Zamharānī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to me: My father narrated to me: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us, from Jābir al-Juʿfī, from ʿAdī ibn Thābit, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Anṣārī, from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī, that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Jamʿ the prayer of Maghrib — three rakʿahs — and the prayer of ʿIshāʾ — two rakʿahs — and he prayed them both together with a single adhān and a single iqāmah. Thus Jābir al-Juʿfī narrated it. (And Jābir is not used as a ḥujjah.) [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"1890","(1890) And al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmārah narrated it from ʿAdī ibn Thābit, from ʿAbd Allāh, from Abū Ayyūb, that he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Muzdalifah the prayer of Maghrib and the prayer of ʿIshāʾ with a single iqāmah, and he did not mention the adhān.\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me: My father narrated to me: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmārah, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd al-Ḥasan is not used as a ḥujjah. [Very Ḍaʿīf.]"
"1891","(1891) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Bashr ibn ʿUmar al-Zahrānī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, from his father, who said:\n\n\We were detained on the Day of the Trench (al-Khandaq) from performing the prayer until it was well after Maghrib"," deep into the night"," until we were relieved. And that is the statement of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {And Allah sufficed the believers in fighting"," and Allah is All-Powerful"," All-Mighty} [al-Aḥzāb: 25].\""\n\n\""Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded Bilāl"," so he called the iqāmah"," and he (the Prophet ﷺ) prayed Ẓuhr"," performing its prayer in the best manner just as he used to pray it. Then he commanded him"," so he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed ʿAṣr likewise. Then he commanded him"," so he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed Maghrib likewise. Then he commanded him"," so he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed ʿIshāʾ likewise. And this was before Allah"," the Most High"," revealed regarding the prayer of fear: {On foot or mounted} [al-Baqarah: 239].\""\n\nAnd thus al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in al-Jadīd from Ibn Abī Fudayk from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb. And Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb with the same meaning"," and he said in the hadith: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded Bilāl"," so he called the iqāmah for each prayer with a separate iqāmah.\""\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in al-Qadīm from more than one narrator from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"," without naming any of them"," and he said in the hadith: \""He commanded Bilāl"," so he gave the adhān and called the iqāmah"," and he prayed Ẓuhr. Then he commanded him"," so he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed ʿAṣr. Then he commanded him"," so he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed Maghrib. Then he commanded him"," so he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed ʿIshāʾ.\""\n\nAnd thus Abū ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Masʿūd narrated from his father in this story"," in one of the two narrations from him"," except that Abū ʿUbaydah did not meet his father"," and it is a good mursal narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"," 661.]"""
"1892","(1892) Abū Muḥammad Junāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Junāḥ al-Qāḍī in al-Kūfah informed us: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah, narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr, from Abī ʿUbaydah, who said: ʿAbdullāh (ibn Masʿūd) said:\n\n\The polytheists distracted the Prophet (ﷺ) from four prayers on the Day of the Trench"," until such portion of the night had passed as Allah willed. Then he commanded Bilāl"," so he gave the adhān and called the iqāmah"," and he prayed Ẓuhr. Then he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed ʿAṣr. Then he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed Maghrib. Then he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed ʿIshāʾ.\""\n\nThus narrated a group from Hushaym ibn Bashīr from Abū al-Zubayr.\n\nAnd Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated it from Abū al-Zubayr"," and there was disagreement regarding the adhān from him; some preserved it from him and some did not. And al-Awzāʿī narrated it from Abū al-Zubayr and said: \""Some of them followed one another with an iqāmah for each prayer.\"" [Ḥasan for other than its chain. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 179.]"""
"1893","(1893) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbdillāh informed me: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned from the expedition of Khaybar… and he mentioned the hadith, and in it is: \Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wuḍūʾ and commanded Bilāl"," so he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed Fajr with them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah. And there is no mention of the adhān in it"," and no one mentioned the adhān along with the connection (waṣl) except Abān al-ʿAṭṭār from Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 680.]"""
"1894","(1894) Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Abān al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made camp with us upon his return from Khaybar and said: 'Who will guard the prayer for us?' Bilāl said: 'I will.' So they slept until the sun rose. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'O Bilāl"," have you slept?' He said: 'The same One who took your breaths has taken my soul.' Then he commanded Bilāl"," so he gave the adhān and called the iqāmah. And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Move from the place where overtook you heedlessness.' And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever forgets a prayer"," let him pray it when he remembers it"," for Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: {Establish the prayer for My remembrance} [Ṭā Hā: 14].'\""\n\nAnd Mālik narrated it in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ from al-Zuhrī from Ibn al-Musayyab as a mursal narration"," and he mentioned the adhān in it. And the adhān in this story is authentically established"," as it was narrated by other than Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1895","(1895) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated from Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father, who said:\n\n\We were travelling one night with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and some of the people said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," would you not make camp with us?' He said: 'I fear that you will sleep and miss the prayer.' Bilāl said: 'I will wake you.' So the people dismounted and lay down"," and Bilāl leaned his back against his mount"," and sleep overcame him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) awoke when the edge of the sun had risen. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'O Bilāl"," where is what you said?' Bilāl said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," never was such a sleep cast upon me as this.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed"," Allah takes your souls when He wills and returns them to you when He wills.' Then he said: 'O Bilāl"," stand and announce the prayer to the people.' So he performed wuḍūʾ"," and when the sun had risen and turned white"," he stood and prayed.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿImrān ibn Maysarah from Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 570.]"""
"1896","(1896) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to me: Thābit al-Bunānī narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabāḥ, from Abī Qatādah, and he mentioned the hadith in full regarding their sleeping past the prayer until the sun rose, and in it is: \Then Bilāl called the prayer"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed two rakʿahs"," then he prayed the morning prayer"," doing as he used to do every day.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Shaybān ibn Farrūkh from Sulaymān"," and he said in the hadith: \""Then Bilāl gave the adhān for the prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"1897","(1897) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬāʾ informed us: ʿAwf ibn Abī Jamīlah narrated from Abū Rajāʾ al-ʿUṭāridī, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said:\n\n\We were on a journey with the Prophet (ﷺ)…\"" and he mentioned the hadith regarding their sleeping past the prayer. He said: \""When he awoke"," we complained to him about what had befallen us. He said: 'No harm' — or 'no injury' — ʿAwf was uncertain. Then he said: 'Move on.' So the Prophet (ﷺ) mounted and travelled a short distance"," then he stopped and called for water for ablution"," and he called the prayer"," and he prayed with the people.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl from ʿAwf. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 337.]"""
"1898","(1898) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬāʾ informed us: Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd narrated from al-Ḥasan, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, that the Prophet (ﷺ) was on a journey and slept past the prayer until the sun rose. He said: \Then he commanded Bilāl"," so he gave the adhān"," and he prayed two rakʿahs. Then he waited until the sun had fully risen. Then he commanded him"," so he called the iqāmah"," and he prayed with them.\""\n\nAnd thus narrated Hishām from al-Ḥasan. [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than its chain.]"""
"1899","(1899) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī narrated from Zāʾidah, from Simāk, from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Ibn Masʿūd, who said:\n\n\We travelled one night with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)…\"" and he mentioned the hadith regarding their sleeping past the prayer until the sun rose"," and in it is: \""Then he commanded Bilāl"," so he gave the adhān"," then he called the iqāmah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than its chain. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 1/450.]"""
"1900","(1900) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Ḥaywah informed us: ʿAyyāsh ibn ʬabbās informed us that Kulaib ibn Ṣubayḥ narrated to him that al-Zibriqān narrated to him from his paternal uncle, ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī, who said:\n\n\We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on one of his journeys"," and he slept and did not pray Fajr until the sun had risen. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and none of his Companions awoke until the heat of the sun distressed them. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded them to move from that place. Then he commanded Bilāl"," so he gave the adhān. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed the two rakʿahs of Fajr"," and he commanded his Companions"," so they prayed the two rakʿahs of Fajr. Then he commanded Bilāl"," so he called the iqāmah"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed.\""\n\nAnd we have narrations in this regard from Ibn ʿAbbās"," Dhī Mikhbar al-Ḥabashī"," and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," raised to the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 444.]"""
"1901","(1901) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, meaning Ibn 'Abd al-Hakam, informed us: Anas ibn Iyyad informed us from Hisham ibn 'Urwah from his father, that Zayd ibn al-Salt went out with 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, toward al-Jurf. He looked and found that he had experienced a nocturnal emission (ihtilam). He said: \By Allah"," I do not think I have had a nocturnal emission without realizing it"," and I performed prayer (Salah) without performing the ritual bath (ghusl).\"" He said: He then performed the ritual bath"," washed what he saw on his garment"," and sprinkled water on what he did not see. He then gave the call to adhan"," pronounced the iqamah"," and performed the prayer after the sun had risen"," sitting firmly in his place. [Weak — 'Abd al-Razzaq recorded it (3644)]"""
"1902","(1902) Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Malini al-Sufi informed us: Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz informed us: al-Baghawi informed us: Abu Khaythamah informed us: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan informed us from Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to launch a raid (ghazw) when the dawn broke. He would listen for the call to prayer (adhan); if he heard the adhan, he would hold back, and if not, he would launch the raid. He said: One day he heard a man saying, \Allah is the Greatest"," Allah is the Greatest.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""He is upon the primordial nature (al-fitrah).\"" Then the man said: \""I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""You have departed from the Hellfire.\"" He said: They looked"," and lo"," he was a goatherd of sheep. Muslim recorded it in his Sahih from Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb. [Sahih — Muslim recorded it (382)]"""
"1903","(1903) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi informed us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Musa ibn Isma'il informed us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us: Thabit informed us from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to launch a raid at the time of the dawn prayer (Salah al-Fajr). He would listen; if he heard a call to prayer (adhan), he would hold back, and if not, he would launch the raid. One day he listened and heard a man saying, \Allah is the Greatest"," Allah is the Greatest.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""Upon the primordial nature"," upon the primordial nature (al-fitrah"," al-fitrah).\"" Then the man said: \""I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah.\"" He said: \""You have departed from the Hellfire.\"" Muslim recorded it in his Sahih from Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb. [Sahih]"""
"1904","(1904) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us: Sa'id informed us from Qatadah from Abu al-Ahwaz from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, on one of his journeys, we suddenly heard a caller proclaiming, \Allah is the Greatest"," Allah is the Greatest.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""He is upon the primordial nature (al-fitrah).\"" He said: \""I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""He has departed from the Hellfire.\"" He said: We rushed toward him"," and lo"," he was a herdsman whose prayer time had overtaken him"," so he called out with it. [Sahih — Ahmad recorded it (1/406)]"""
"1905","(1905) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: Harun ibn Ma'ruf informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us from 'Amr ibn al-Harith that Abu 'Ushshanah al-Ma'afi related to him from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: \Your Lord marvels at a shepherd of sheep upon the summit of a mountain crag"," who gives the call to prayer (adhan) and performs the prayer (Salah). Allah"," the Almighty and Exalted"," says: 'Look at this servant of Mine — he gives the call to prayer and pronounces the iqamah for the prayer; he fears Me. I have forgiven My servant and admitted him into My Paradise.'\"" [Sahih — Abu Dawud recorded it (1203)]"""
"1906","(1906) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Abu Bakr Yahya ibn Ja'far Abi Talib in Baghdad in the year 268 AH. And Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan al-'Adl informed us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi from Salman, who said: No man is in a desolate land (ard fi) and performs the ablution (wudu') — or performs dry ablution (tayammum) with pure earth — then calls out for the prayer (adhan) and pronounces the iqamah and performs the prayer, except that hosts of the hosts of Allah, whose flanks cannot be seen, — or he said: whose extremities cannot be seen — al-Taymi expressed doubt. [Sahih — Ibn Abi Shaybah recorded it (1766)]"
"1907","(1907) And Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Sulayman informed us from Abu 'Uthman from Salman, who said: No man is in a desolate land and performs the ablution (wudu') if he finds water, and if not, performs dry ablution (tayammum), then calls out for the prayer (adhan) and pronounces the iqamah, except that he is led in prayer by hosts of the hosts of Allah, the Almighty and Exalted, whose extremities cannot be seen — or he said: whose extremity cannot be seen. This is the correct version, as a mawquf narration. It has also been narrated as a marfu' narration, but its being raised (raf') is not correct. [Sahih]"
"1908","(1908) Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Bayruti in Beirut informed us: Ishaq, meaning Ibn Suwayd al-Ramli, informed us: al-Walid, meaning ibn al-Nadr, informed us: al-Qasim, meaning ibn Ghusn, informed us from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi from Salman al-Farisi, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \No man is in a desolate land and gives the call to prayer (adhan) at the time of the prayer"," and pronounces the iqamah for the prayer and performs it"," except that rows of angels whose flanks cannot be seen form behind him — they bow with his bowing"," prostrate with his prostration"," and say 'Amen' to his supplication.\"" [Munkar]"""
"1909","(1909) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Saffar al-Isfahani informed us: Ahmad ibn Yunus al-Dabbi informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi informed us: al-Walid ibn Jumay' informed us from Laylah bint Malik and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid al-Ansari from Umm Waraqah al-Ansariyyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to say: \Let us go to the female martyr so that we may visit her.\"" And he ordered that the adhan and iqamah be given for her"," and that the people of her household lead them in the obligatory prayers. [Weak — Abu Dawud recorded it (591)]"""
"1910","(1910) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isfahani informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr informed us: Abu Mu'awiyah from al-A'mash from Ibrahim from al-Aswad and 'Alqamah, who said: We came to 'Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Mas'ud, in his house. He said: \Did these people perform the prayer behind you?\"" We said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Stand up and pray.\"" He did not command us to give the adhan or the iqamah. Then he completed his prayer with them. Muslim recorded it in his Sahih from Abu Kuraib from Abu Mu'awiyah. [Sahih — Muslim recorded it (534)]"""
"1911","(1911) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿruf al-Mihrajānī informed us; he said: Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us; he said: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad al-Kātib narrated to us; he said: Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; he said: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlqamah, who said:\n\nʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd led me and al-Aswad in prayer without an adhān or an iqāmah. And he would sometimes say: \The adhān and iqāmah of the community suffices us.\""\n\n[Ḥasan for other than its own chain. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it as 1961.]"""
"1912","(1912) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; he said: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; he said: Sulaymān, meaning Ibn Ḥarb, narrated to us; he said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Yazīd al-Faqīr, who said:\n\nIbn ʿUmar said: \If you are in a village in which the adhān is called and the iqāmah is made"," that suffices you.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1913","(1913) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us; he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; he said: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; he said: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; he said: Sufyān said: I heard ʿAmr narrating from ʿIkrimah ibn Khālid, that he heard him narrating from ʿAbdullāh ibn Wāqid, that:\n\nIbn ʿUmar would not perform the iqāmah for prayer in a land in which the prayer had already been established, and he would not pray the two rakʿahs of Fajr while travelling, and he would not omit them while resident.\n\nIt was said to Sufyān: \Indeed Ḥammād ibn Zayd says in this hadith"," or part of it"," from Yazīd al-Faqīr.\"" Sufyān said: \""I never heard ʿAmr mention Yazīd al-Faqīr at all. He only told us that he heard ʿIkrimah"," meaning Ibn Khālid"," narrating from ʿAbdullāh ibn Wāqid.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it as 1965.]"""
"1914","(1914) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; he said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; he said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; he said: Ibn Wahb informed me; he said: Mālik ibn Anas and Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, from his father, that:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined the Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ prayers at Muzdalifah.\n\nIbn Abī Dhiʾb said in the hadith: \He did not call out for each of them separately except with an iqāmah"," and he did not pray any supererogatory prayer between them"," nor after either of them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," from Mālik.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it as 1589.]"""
"1915","(1915) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; he said: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī, narrated to us; he said: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; he said: Abū ʿĀmir Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us; he said: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us; he said: Abū ʿAmr, meaning al-Awzāʿī, said: Abū al-Zubayr al-Makkī informed me, from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from Abī ʿUbaydah, from his father ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said:\n\nWe were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, facing the enemy on the day of the Khandaq, and they kept the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, and ʿIshāʾ prayers until half the night had passed. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and began with the Ẓuhr, so he prayed it, then the ʿAṣr, then the Maghrib, then the ʿIshāʾ, following one after the other with a single iqāmah for each.\n\n[Ḥasan for other than its own chain. Al-Nasāʾī narrated it as 662.]"
"1916","(1916) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; he said: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; he said: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; he said: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd, from Abū Hurayrah, and from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the prayer is established"," then walk"," and upon you should be tranquillity and dignity. Whatever you catch"," pray"," and whatever you miss"," complete it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from al-Zuhrī.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""Whoever catches the end of the prayer has missed being present for the adhān and iqāmah. He does not call the adhān for himself"," nor does he make the iqāmah. And I do not know of anyone who holds the view that if a person comes to the mosque and the imām has already finished the prayer"," he may pray without an adhān or an iqāmah.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it as 866.]"""
"1917","(1917) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; he said: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; he said: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; he said: ʿUmar ibn Qays narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, who said:\n\nIbn ʿUmar used to say: \Whoever prays in a mosque in which the prayer has already been established"," their iqāmah suffices him.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""Al-Ḥasan"," al-Shaʿbī"," and al-Nakhaʿī also held this view.\""\n\n[Very weak.]"""
"1918","(1918) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād; he said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; he said: ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī ʿĪsā al-Turqufī narrated to us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; he said: Sufyān narrated to us, from Yūnus, from Abī ʿUthmān, who said:\n\nAnas ibn Mālik came to us after we had already prayed the Fajr. So he called the adhān and made the iqāmah, then he led his companions in the Fajr prayer.\n\nAnd it has also been narrated from Salamah ibn al-Akwāʿ regarding the adhān and iqāmah, and also from Ibn al-Musayyab and al-Zuhrī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1919","(1919) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; he said: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; he said: al-Shāfiʿī informed us; he said: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad informed me; he said: ʿUmarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to me, from Khubayb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿĀṣim, who said:\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ heard a man calling the adhān for the Maghrib, so the Prophet ﷺ said the same as the man had said. Then the Prophet ﷺ arrived, and the man had said: \The prayer has been established.\"" So the Prophet ﷺ said: \""Come down and pray the Maghrib with the iqāmah of that black slave.\""\n\nThis is a mursal hadith.\n\n[Baseless. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it as 124.]"""
"1920","(1920) Abū Zakariyyā al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; he said: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; he said: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: \ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar informed you"," from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," that he said:\n\n'There is no adhān and no iqāmah upon women.'\""\n\n[Weak. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it as 5022.]"""
"1921","(1921) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdiyy informed us; Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsá narrated to us; Yaḥyá ibn Ḥamzah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from al-Qāsim, from Asmāʾ, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no Adhān upon women"," nor Iqāmah"," nor Jumuʿah"," nor the Ghusl of Jumuʿah"," and no woman shall lead them; rather she shall stand in their midst.\"" Al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aylī narrated it thus"," and he is weak (ḍaʿīf). We have narrated regarding the Adhān and Iqāmah from Anas ibn Mālik"," both as a Mawqūf and a Marfūʿ narration"," and its raising (rafʿ) is weak. This was the view of al-Ḥasan"," Ibn al-Musayyib"," Ibn Sīrīn"," and al-Nakhaʿī. [Mawḍūʿ (Fabricated)]"""
"1922","(1922) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated from Layth, from ʿAṭāʾ, from ʿĀʾishah, that she used to give the Adhān, pronounce the Iqāmah, lead the women in prayer, and stand in their midst. [Ḥasan for other than itself. Al-Ḥākim narrated it (1/320)]"
"1923","(1923) Abū Bakr al-Ḥārithī al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Ibn Ṣāʿid informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Barqī informed us; ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah narrated: I asked Ibn Thawbān, \Is there an Iqāmah upon women?\"" He narrated to me that his father narrated to him"," saying: I asked Makhūl"," and he said: \""If they give the Adhān and then pronounce the Iqāmah"," that is more excellent; and if they do not go beyond the Iqāmah"," it will suffice them.\"" Ibn Thawbān said: And if they do not pronounce the Iqāmah"," then indeed al-Zuhrī narrated from ʿUrwah"," from ʿĀʾishah"," who said: \""We used to pray without an Iqāmah.\"" And if this is sound along with the first narration"," they do not contradict each other"," for it is possible that she did this on one occasion and omitted it on another"," since both matters are permissible. And Allah knows best. It is also narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that it was said to him: \""Does a woman pronounce the Iqāmah?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" [Weak (Ḍaʿīf)]"""
"1924","(1924) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ṣaydalānī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Yūnus al-Ḍabbī informed us in Aṣbahān; Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: Nāfiʿ, the freed slave of Ibn ʿUmar, informed me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that he used to say: \The Muslims"," when they arrived in Madīnah"," would gather and estimate the time for prayer"," and no one would call it. One day they spoke about it"," and some of them said: 'Adopt a bell like the bell of the Christians.' And some of them said: 'Rather"," a horn like the horn of the Jews.' ʿUmar said: 'Why do you not send a man to call to prayer?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'O Bilāl"," stand and call to prayer.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs]"""
"1925","(1925) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us by dictation, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sharqī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyá al-Dhuhlī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Mālik, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you hear the call"," say what the muʾadhdhin says.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá"," both from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (586)]"""
"1926","(1926) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us by dictation; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsá al-Hilālī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Jahḍam narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from ʿUmarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Khubayb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, from his father, from his grandfather ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the muʾadhdhin says"," 'Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar","' one of you should say"," 'Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar.' Then when he says"," 'Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh","' he should say"," 'Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh.' Then when he says"," 'Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh","' he should say"," 'Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh.' Then when he says"," ʿḤayya ʿalā al-Ṣalāh","' he should say"," 'Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā bi-Allāh.' Then when he says"," ʿḤayya ʿalā al-Falāḥ","' he should say"," 'Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā bi-Allāh.' Then when he says"," 'Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar","' he should say"," 'Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar.' Then when he says"," 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh","' and he says"," 'Lā ilāha illā Allāh' from his heart"," he will enter Paradise.\"" Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr"," from Muḥammad ibn Jahḍam. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (385)]"""
"1927","(1927) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim al-Dārabardī in Marw informed us; Abū al-Muwajjih informed us; ʿAbdān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn ʿUthmān ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf narrated: I heard Abā Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf say: I heard Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān, while he was sitting on the pulpit, and the muʾadhdhin gave the call and said, \Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar.\"" Muʿāwiyah said"," \""Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar.\"" He said"," \""Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh.\"" Muʿāwiyah said the same. He said"," \""Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh.\"" Muʿāwiyah said"," \""And I (bear witness).\"" When the Adhān was completed"," he said: \""O people"," I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say from this gathering when the muʾadhdhin gave the call"," the same as you heard from my words.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (872)]"""
"1928","(1928) Abū ʿAbd Allāh and Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsá both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Yaḥyá ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us; Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh al-Dustawāʾī narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Manīʿī informed us; Abū Khaythamah narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Yaḥyá ibn Abī Kathīr; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us; ʿĪsá ibn Ṭalḥah narrated: We entered upon Muʿāwiyah, and the caller called to prayer and said, \Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar.\"" Muʿāwiyah said"," \""Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar.\"" He said"," \""Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh.\"" Muʿāwiyah said"," \""And I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah.\"" He said"," \""Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh.\"" Muʿāwiyah said"," \""And I bear witness that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah.\"" Yaḥyá said: A companion of ours narrated to us that when he said"," ʿḤayya ʿalā al-Ṣalāh","' he said"," 'Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā bi-Allāh.' Then he said: \""Thus we heard your Prophet (ﷺ).\"" The wording is that of the Ḥadīth of Muʿādh ibn Hishām"," and ʿAbd al-Wahhāb"," or those who narrated from him"," did not include this detail from Yaḥyá ibn Abī Kathīr. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muʿādh ibn Faḍālah"," from Hishām"," in an abridged form"," without this addition from Yaḥyá. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1929","(1929) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Mahdī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Mushhir narrated from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he heard the muʾadhdhin reciting the Tashahhud, would say: \And I"," and I.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (526)]"""
"1930","(1930) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl and Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz in Baghdād both informed us, saying: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī in Makkah informed us; Abū Yaḥyá ibn Abī Masarrat narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated to us; Kaʿb ibn ʿAlqamah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you hear the muʾadhdhin giving the Adhān"," say what he says"," and send blessings upon me"," for indeed there is no one who sends blessings upon me but that Allah sends ten blessings upon him. And ask Allah for me the Wasīlah"," for indeed the Wasīlah is a station in Paradise that is not befitting except for one servant of Allah"," and I hope that I will be that one. And whoever asks it for me"," my intercession will become permissible for him on the Day of Resurrection.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (384)]"""
"1931","(1931) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz informed us, Abū Muḥammad informed us, Abū Yaḥyā informed us, al-Muqriʾ informed us, Ḥaywah informed us, Kaʿb ibn ʿAlqamah informed us that he heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Jubayr say that he heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr say that he heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: \When you hear the muʾadhdhin…\"" Then al-Muqriʾ narrated to us something similar to his ḥadīth from Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1932","(1932) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Muḥmmad ibn Salamah al-Murādī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us from Ḥaywah and Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb and others, from Kaʿb ibn ʿAlqamah, and he mentioned it with its chain of narration and its meaning, and he said: \And I hope that I am he. So whoever asks for al-Wasīlah for me"," al-Shafāʿah (intercession) will become permissible for him.\"" Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Salamah al-Murādī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1933","(1933) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Fāmī informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAyyāsh informed us, Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah informed us from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever says upon hearing the call (adhān): 'O Allah"," I ask You by the right of this perfect call (al-daʿwah al-tāmmah) and the established prayer (al-ṣalāh al-qāʾimah)"," grant Muḥammad al-Wasīlah and al-Faḍīlah"," and raise him to al-Maqām al-Maḥmūd which You have promised him. Indeed"," You do not break Your promise' — my intercession will become permissible for him.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAyyāsh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it (589)]"""
"1934","(1934) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Qutaybah informed us, al-Layth informed us from Ḥukaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qays, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, from Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: \Whoever says when he hears the muʾadhdhin: 'And I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah alone"," without partner"," and that Muḥammad is His servant and His Messenger. I am pleased with Allah as Lord"," with Muḥammad as Messenger"," and with Islam as religion' — he will be forgiven.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (386)]"""
"1935","(1935) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd al-ʿAdanī informed us, al-Qāsim ibn Maʿn al-Masʿūdī informed us from Abī Kathīr, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) taught me to say at the adhān of al-Maghrib: \O Allah"," indeed this is the approach of Your night and the departure of Your day"," and the voices of Your callers"," so forgive me.\"" Thus it is in my book"," and someone else said: from al-Qāsim ibn Maʿn"," who said: al-Masʿūdī narrated to us. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq narrated it from Abī Kathīr and added in it: \""And the presence of Your prayer.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (530)]"""
"1936","(1936) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Ibn al-Sarḥ and Muḥammad ibn Salamah both said: Ibn Wahb informed us from Ḥuyayy, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥublī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, that a man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," indeed the muʾadhdhins surpass us.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""Say as they say"," and when you have finished"," ask and you will be given.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (524)]"""
"1937","(1937) Abū ʿAlī informed us, Abū Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us, Sufyān informed us from Zayd al-ʿAmmī, from Abī Iyās, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Duʿāʾ is not rejected between the adhān and the iqāmah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than it. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (521)]"""
"1938","(1938) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī, Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ṣaydalānī informed us, all saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us, Mūsā ibn Yaʿqūb al-Zamʿī informed us, Abū Ḥāzim ibn Dīnār informed me that Sahl ibn Saʿd informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Two things are not rejected — or are seldom rejected: duʿāʾ at the time of the call (nidāʾ)"," and at the time of al-baʾs when some of them fight against others.\"" al-Zamʿī raised it (as a marfūʿ ḥadīth)"," and Mālik ibn Anas"," the Imām"," stopped it (as a mawqūf ḥadīth). [Munkar. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (2540)]"""
"1939","(1939) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed him, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik informed us from Abī Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, who said: Two moments during which the gates of the heavens are opened, and very rarely is the supplication of a supplicant rejected at them: the presence of the call (adhān) to prayer, and the row (ṣaff) in the cause of Allah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Adab al-Mufrad (661)]"
"1940","(1940) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAtakī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Thābit informed us, a man from the people of al-Shām informed me from Shahr ibn Ḥawshab, from Abī Ummāmah or from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him): Indeed, Bilāl began the iqāmah, and when he said \Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh","\"" the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \""May Allah establish it and perpetuate it.\"" And he said regarding the rest of the iqāmah something similar to the ḥadīth of ʿUmar regarding the adhān. The Shaykh said: And this"," if authentic"," is a witness for what al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy on him) recommended of his statement: \""O Allah"," establish it and perpetuate it"," and make us among the righteous of its people in deed.\"" And some of this wording is in it. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (528)]"""
"1941","(1941) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata' informed us: Shu'bah reported from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu 'Iyyas al-Aswari, who said: Whenever Ibn 'Umar heard the adhan, he would say: \O Allah"," Lord of this responded-to call"," the call of true faith and the word of piety"," cause me to die upon it"," and grant me life upon it"," and make me among its righteous people in deed on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\n[Hasan. Al-Tabarani recorded it in al-Du'a' (468).]"""
"1942","(1942) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us: Hajib ibn Ahmad al-Tusi narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us: Waki' reported from Sufyan from Khalid al-Hadha' from Abu Qilabah from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, who said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ along with a cousin of mine. He said: \When you two travel"," give the adhan and pronounce the iqamah"," and let the older of you lead you in prayer.\""\n\n[Sahih. Al-Bukhari recorded it (604).]"""
"1943","(1943) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya and al-Mani'i said: Ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us: al-Firyabi narrated to us: Sufyan mentioned it with its chain and its meaning, except that he did not mention his (Malik's) statement \a cousin of mine.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi.\n\nAnd among what has passed in the hadith of Abu Juwayfi regarding Bilal's adhan in al-Abtah"," and the hadith of Abu Qatadah and others regarding Bilal's adhan upon their return from Khaybar"," and what we shall mention in the chapter on cooling the noon prayer"," there is evidence that the adhan and the iqamah are among the established practices (sunan) of prayer during travel. [Sahih.]"""
"1944","(1944) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Malik ibn Anas informed you from Nafi', that Ibn 'Umar used not to add anything beyond the iqamah in the prayer during travel, except in the dawn prayer (al-subh), for he would give the adhan and pronounce the iqamah therein, and he would say: \The adhan is only for the imam around whom the people gather.\""\n\n[Sahih. Recorded by Malik.]"""
"1945","(1945) Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan in Baghdad informed us: Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas narrated to us: al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri narrated to us: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyyah, Abu Khaythamah, narrated from his brother al-Ruhayl from Abu al-Zubayr, who said: I asked Ibn 'Umar: \Shall I give the adhan during travel?\"" He said: \""For whom do you give the adhan? For insects and vermin?\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: What Ibn 'Umar held is a matter that may be interpreted"," were it not for the hadith of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri regarding the adhan in the wilderness"," and the hadith of Anas ibn Malik and others regarding the adhan of the shepherd. In all of that there is evidence that the adhan is among the established practices (sunan) of prayer even if one is alone. The hadith of Ibn 'Umar is used as evidence that omitting the adhan during travel is less severe than omitting it during residence.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Asim ibn Damrah from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib that he said regarding the traveler: \""If he wishes"," he may give the adhan and pronounce the iqamah; and if he wishes"," he may only pronounce the iqamah.\"" And some people have erroneously elevated the hadith of Ibn 'Umar to a marfu' narration"," and that is a gross error. [Da'if.]"""
"1946","(1946) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us: Abu Hamid ibn Bilal al-Bazzar narrated to us: Abu al-Azhar narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata' al-Khaffaf narrated to us: Khalid narrated from Abu Qilabah from Anas, who said: Bilal was commanded to pronounce the adhan in pairs (shaf') and the iqamah in odd numbers (watr). [Hasan.]"
"1947","(1947) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ja'far ibn Muhammad said: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadha' narrated from Abu Qilabah from Anas, who said: Bilal was commanded to pronounce the adhan in pairs and the iqamah in odd numbers. I mentioned it to Ayyub, and he said: \Except the iqamah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdillah from Ibn Ulayyah"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari recorded it (578).]"""
"1948","(1948) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Saffar narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Simak ibn Atiyyah from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Anas, who said: Bilal was commanded to pronounce the adhan in pairs and the iqamah in odd numbers, except the iqamah. Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Sulayman ibn Harb. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari recorded it (1580).]"
"1949","(1949) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Abu al-Qasim ibn bint Mani' narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us: Khalid al-Hadha' narrated from Abu Qilabah from Anas, who said: Bilal was commanded to pronounce the adhan in pairs and the iqamah in odd numbers. Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Khalaf ibn Hisham. [Sahih. Muslim recorded it (378).]"
"1950","(1950) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us. And Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Adib al-Bastami narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed me: Ibn Khuzaymah — with some doubt regarding him — narrated to us: Bishr ibn Hilal narrated to us: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadha' narrated from Abu Qilabah from Anas, who said: They mentioned the fire and the bell, and they mentioned the Jews and the Christians. So Bilal was commanded to pronounce the adhan in pairs and the iqamah in odd numbers. The wording is that of the hadith of Abu 'Amr. Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Imran ibn Mayssarah from 'Abd al-Warith. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari recorded it (578).]"
"1951","Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Musaddad and Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj both said: ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas, who said: \Bilāl was commanded to repeat the words of the Adhān in pairs (i.e."," twice each) and to state the Iqāmah in odd numbers (i.e."," once each).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qawārīrī from ʿAbd al-Wārith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 378]"""
"1952","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Wahayb narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \When the people grew numerous"," they mentioned that they should signal the time of prayer by something they would recognize. They mentioned lighting a fire or striking a bell. So Bilāl was commanded to state the Adhān in pairs (i.e."," twice each) and to state the Iqāmah in odd numbers (i.e."," once each).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim from Bahz ibn Asad from Wahayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 378]"""
"1953","Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, Bundār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, meaning al-Thaqafī, narrated to us, Khālid narrated from Abū Qilābah, from Anas, who said: \When the people grew numerous"," they mentioned that they should signal the time of prayer by something they would recognize. They mentioned lighting a fire or striking a bell. So Bilāl was commanded to state the Adhān in pairs (i.e."," twice each) and to state the Iqāmah in odd numbers (i.e."," once each).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad"," and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm"," both from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 578]"""
"1954","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Naṣr ibn ʿUmar informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated to us, Ayyūb narrated from Abū Qilābah, from Anas, who said: \Bilāl was commanded to state the Adhān in pairs (i.e."," twice each) and to state the Iqāmah in odd numbers (i.e."," once each).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh al-Qawārīrī from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb.\n\nLikewise"," al-Shāfiʿī narrated it from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb"," and Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn and Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated it from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb with its chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded Bilāl. And in the context of those who narrated the story of the ḥadīth"," there is evidence that the one who commanded it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1955","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī narrated from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded Bilāl to state the Adhān in pairs (i.e., twice each) and to state the Iqāmah in odd numbers (i.e., once each). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī, 624]"
"1956","And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ and Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb both said: Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn al-Mubārak al-Mustamlī narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded Bilāl to state the Adhān in pairs (i.e."," twice each) and to state the Iqāmah in odd numbers (i.e."," once each).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1957","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Hārūn ibn Sulaymān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Abān ibn Yazīd, from Qatādah: that Anas ibn Mālik's Adhān was in pairs (twice each) and his Iqāmah was once each. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"1958","Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmrawah al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Ibn Abī Khaythamah narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak narrated. And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak both said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Simāk ibn ʿAṭiyyah, from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas, who said: \Bilāl was commanded to state the Adhān in pairs (i.e."," twice each) and to state the Iqāmah in odd numbers (i.e."," once each)"," except for the Iqāmah (phrase).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1959","Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzār narrated to us, Abū al-Azhar narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas, who said: \Bilāl was commanded to state the Adhān in pairs (i.e."," twice each) and to state the Iqāmah in odd numbers (i.e."," once each)"," except his saying: 'Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh' (The prayer has been established)"," which he said twice.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/239]"""
"1960","Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr among others said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Hārūn ibn Sulaymān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Jaʿfar, from Abū al-Muthannā, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: \During the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," the Adhān was in pairs (twice each) and the Iqāmah was once each"," except that when the muʾadhdhin said 'Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh' (The prayer has been established)"," he said it twice.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 510]"""
"1961","(1961) Abū al-Muthannā reported: I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: \During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," the adhān was pronounced in pairs (i.e."," each phrase repeated twice)"," and the iqāmah was pronounced singly (i.e."," each phrase once)"," except that when he said 'Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh","' he repeated it twice. So when any of us heard the iqāmah"," he would perform wuḍū' and then come out.\""\n\nGundar and ʿUthmān ibn Jabalah narrated it from Shuʿbah from Abū Jaʿfar al-Madanī from Muslim ibn al-Muthannā. And Abū ʀāmir narrated it from Shuʿbah from Abū Jaʿfar"," the mu'adhdhin of the Masjid al-ʿUryān"," who said: I heard Abū al-Muthannā"," the mu'adhdhin of the Masjid al-Akbar. [Ḥasan]"""
"1962","(1962) Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah reported: \I found my father and my grandfather pronouncing this adhān which I pronounce"," and performing this iqāmah"," and they would say: 'Indeed the Prophet ﷺ taught it to Abū Maḥdhūrah.'\"" He mentioned the adhān and then said: \""And the iqāmah is singular (each phrase once): Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāḥ"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"1963","(1963) Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah reported: \I heard my father and my grandfather narrating from Abī Maḥdhūrah that he used to give the adhān for the Prophet ﷺ"," and he would pronounce the iqāmah singly"," except that he would say: 'Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh.'\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"1964","(1964) Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib narrated regarding the call (adhān): \The first person to whom it was shown in a sleep was a man from the Anṣār"," from Banī al-Ḥārith ibn al-Khazraj"," whose name was ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd said: \""While I was asleep"," a man appeared to me walking"," holding a nāqūs (bell) in his hand. I said: 'O servant of Allah"," will you sell this nāqūs?' He said: 'What do you want with it?' I said: 'I want to use it to call people to prayer.' He said: 'Shall I not tell you something better than that?' Say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh. Then he said: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh.\""\n\nIbn al-Musayyib said: \""ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd woke up"," gathered his garments"," and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to inform him of what he had seen.\"" Ibn al-Musayyib said: \""And ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb was shown something similar"," and he came to inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of what he had seen. The first of the two to report the vision to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī. He found that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had already commanded the adhān"," so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilāl"," who gave the first adhān and then the iqāmah.\""\n\nThus narrated by Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī from al-Zuhrī. And Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yāsār narrated it as follows. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1965","(1965) ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbd Rabbih said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided to strike the nāqūs (bell) to gather the people for prayer — and he disliked it due to its resemblance to the practice of the Christians — a figure came to me during the night while I was asleep. He was wearing two green garments and carrying a nāqūs in his hand. I said to him: 'O servant of Allah"," will you sell the nāqūs?' He said: 'What will you do with it?' I said: 'I will call people to prayer with it.' He said: 'Shall I not direct you to something better than that?' I said: 'Yes"," indeed.' He said: 'Say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh.' Then he stepped back a short distance and said: 'Then when you stand for prayer (iqāmah)"," say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh.'\""\n\n\""When I woke up"," I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of what I had seen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This is a true vision"," if Allah the Most High wills.' Then he commanded the adhān"," and Bilāl"," the freedman of Abū Bakr"," used to give the adhān with it.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yāsār has another chain of narration for it with similar content. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Aḥmad 4/42]"""
"1966","(1966) ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that the nāqūs be made so that people could be struck with it to gather for prayer…\"" He mentioned the hadīth regarding his vision"," and in the account of the adhān it is similar to the hadīth of Ibn al-Musayyib. And regarding the iqāmah he said: \""Then when you stand for prayer"," say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh.\""\n\nThe hadīth returns to the rest of the words of the iqāmah being singular (each phrase once)"," and the repetition of his saying: \""Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh.\""\n\nAbū Bakr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah said: I heard Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā say: \""There is no report in the narrations of ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd regarding the story of the adhān that is more authentic than this"," because Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd heard it from his father"," while ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā did not hear it from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"1967","(1967) ʿAmmār ibn Saʿd narrated from his father Saʿd al-Qaraẓ that he heard him say: \Indeed this adhān is the adhān of Bilāl"," which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded"," and his iqāmah is: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh. Then he would repeat: Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh. And the iqāmah is one by one (each phrase once)"," and he would say: 'Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh' only once.\"" He then mentioned the rest of the hadīth at length.\n\nAl-Ḥumaydī said: Abū Ismāʿīl Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah narrated: I heard my grandfather ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah narrating from his father Abī Maḥdhūrah that the Prophet ﷺ taught him this adhān. He mentioned the takbīr at the beginning four times"," then he mentioned the adhān with tarjīʿ (repetition of the shahādah phrases).\n\nAl-Ḥumaydī said: And Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah narrated: \""I found my grandfather"," my father"," and my family performing the iqāmah"," and they would say…\"" He mentioned the iqāmah as singular (each phrase once) and said: \""Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh.\""\n\nAl-Ḥumaydī said: \""The position regarding both of them together is the position of the people of Makkah.\""\n\nAl-Ḥumaydī said: \""Abū Maḥdhūrah testified that the Prophet ﷺ taught him at the beginning of the adhān: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar (once)"," and Saʿd testified regarding Bilāl with a single occurrence"," so he agreed with Abū Maḥdhūrah in it. And Abū Maḥdhūrah is an additional witness over the other. We arrive at: 'Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh' being said twice"," because Anas ibn Mālik said: 'Bilāl was commanded to make the adhān in pairs (even) and the iqāmah in singles (odd)"," except the iqāmah (phrase).' So Anas is a witness that Bilāl was commanded to repeat the word of iqāmah (i.e."," 'Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh' twice). For this reason"," we hold to the repetition of 'Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh","' and because of the consensus of the people of Madīnah upon their repetition of it.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: \""This discourse which al-Ḥumaydī mentioned"," he took it from his teacher Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah the Most High have mercy on him"," who mentioned it in the book al-Qadīm"," in the narration of al-Zaʿfarānī from him"," in abridged form.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"1968","(1968) Abū Maḥdhūrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him the adhān as nineteen phrases and the iqāmah as seventeen phrases. The adhān is: Allāhu Akbar, Allāhu Akbar, Allāhu Akbar, Allāhu Akbar, Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh, Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh, Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh, Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh, Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh twice, Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ twice, Allāhu Akbar, Allāhu Akbar, Lā ilāha illallāh. And the iqāmah is in pairs (each phrase twice).\n\nʿAffān narrated it from Hammām and explained the iqāmah as \mathnā mathnā\"" (in pairs)"," and added at its end: \""Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh.\"" And Saʿīd ibn ʀāmir narrated it from Hammām as well. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 502]"""
"1969","(1969) Abū Maḥdhūrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ commanded approximately twenty men to give the adhān, and he was most pleased with the voice of Abū Maḥdhūrah. He said: \Say: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh. And the iqāmah is like that.\""\n\nThus narrated"," and they are unanimously agreed that the iqāmah is not like the adhān in the number of phrases when the adhān includes tarjīʿ. This indicates that what is meant by it is the category (jins) of phrases"," and that its explanation was given by some of the narrators.\n\nHishām ibn Abī ʿAbdullāh al-Dustawāʾī narrated this hadīth from ʀāmir al-Aḥwal without mentioning the iqāmah in it. And that portion is what Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj extracted in the Ṣaḥīḥ"," as we have previously mentioned. Perhaps he omitted the narration of Hammām ibn Yaḥyā due to doubt regarding the chain of the iqāmah mentioned in it. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan]"""
"1970",""1970","

When the Messenger of Allah - peace be upon him - returned from Hunayn, I set out with a group of people from Makkah to look for them. I heard them calling the Adhan for prayer, so we stood up to call the Adhan, and we were mocking them. Then the Prophet - peace be upon him - stood up and said, ""I have heard a man with a good voice among these people.""

He then sent a man to us, and I was the last one to be sent. When I called the Adhan, the Prophet - peace be upon him - sat me down in front of him, and he placed his hand on my shoulder and blessed me three times, saying, ""Go and call the Adhan at the House of Allah.""

I said, ""How, O Messenger of Allah?"" He taught me the Adhan as they are calling it now, saying, ""Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, there is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, there is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the prayer is better than sleep, the prayer is better than sleep, the prayer is better than sleep, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah.""

He then taught me the Iqamah twice, saying, ""Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah, there is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the prayer is better than sleep, the prayer is better than sleep, the prayer is better than sleep, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah."""," I set out as the tenth of ten men from Makkah seeking them"," and I heard them giving the adhān for the prayer. So we stood up and gave the adhān"," mocking them. The Prophet ﷺ stood up and said: 'I have indeed heard in these people the adhān of a man with a beautiful voice.' He sent for us"," and we gave the adhān one by one"," and I was the last of them. When I gave the adhān"," he said: 'Come here.' He sat me down before him"," wiped over my forehead"," and invoked blessings upon me three times. Then he said: 'Go and give the adhān at the Sacred House (al-Bayt al-Ḥarām).' I said: 'How"," O Messenger of Allah?' So he taught me the adhān as they give it now: Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Aṣ-ṣalātu khayrun min al-nawm"," aṣ-ṣalātu khayrun min al-nawm"," in the first (adhān) of the morning (ṣubḥ)"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh.\""\n\nHe said: \""And he taught me the iqāmah twice twice (each phrase twice): Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūlullāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalaṣ-ṣalāh"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Qad qāmatiṣ-ṣalāh"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Lā ilāha illallāh.\""\n\nIbn Jurayj said: \""ʿUthmān informed me all of it from Umm ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah"," that she heard it from Abī Maḥdhūrah.\"" Thus narrated by Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi]"""
"1971","(1971) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Abū Ḥumayd al-Miṣṣīṣī narrated to us; Ḥajjāj said: Ibn Jurayj said: ʿUthmān ibn al-Sāʾib informed me; my father and Umm ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah informed me, from Abī Maḥdhūrah, who said: When the Prophet ﷺ set out for Ḥunayn, he mentioned the hadith and said regarding the takbīr at the beginning of the adhān — four times. And he said: \He taught me the iqāmah twice:\n\n'Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ. Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh"," qad qāmat al-ṣalāh. Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh.'\""\n\nThus"," he mentioned the iqāmah as single (mufarradah)"," as you see"," and his statement \""twice\"" refers to the word of the iqāmah (i.e."," \""Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh\"" said twice). The narration of ʿAbd al-Razzāq from Ibn Jurayj also indicates the same. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1972","(1972) Abū Bakr ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; ʿUthmān ibn al-Sāʾib, their client, narrated to me, from his father — the shaykh, client of Abī Maḥdhūrah — and from Umm ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah, that they both heard that from Abī Maḥdhūrah. Then he mentioned the hadith similar to the hadith of Ḥajjāj, and said at its end: \And when you give the iqāmh"," say it twice: 'Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh"," qad qāmat al-ṣalāh — did you hear?'\"" And he added: \""Abū Maḥdhūrah used to neither cut his forelock nor part it"," because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had passed his hand over it.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah said: The tarjīʿ (repetition with a lower voice) in the adhān along with the tathniyah (doubling) of the iqāmh is of the category of permissible difference (al-khilāf al-mubāḥ). Thus"," it is permissible for the muʾadhdhin to give the adhān with tarjīʿ and to double the iqāmah"," and it is also permissible to double the adhān and to make the iqāmah single"," since both matters have been authentically reported from the Prophet ﷺ. As for the doubling of both the adhān and the iqāmah"," there is no established command from the Prophet ﷺ regarding both of them together.\n\nThe Shaykh said: There is a consideration regarding the tathniyah (doubling) of the words of the iqāmah other than the takbīr and the two words of iqāmah (i.e."," \""Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh\""). In the differing narrations"," there is what suggests that the command of doubling returned to the two words of iqāmah. And in the persistence of Abū Maḥdhūrah and his children upon the tarjīʿ of the adhān and the singling of the iqāmah"," there is what necessitates the weakness of the narration of whoever narrated the doubling of both"," or it implies that the matter settled upon what he and his children and Saʿd al-Qaraẓ and his children remained upon in the Ḥaram of Allah"," the Most High"," and the Ḥaram of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," until the change occurred during the days of the Egyptians. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1973","(1973) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; al-Shāfiʿī said: I came across Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah giving the adhān as Ibn Muḥayrīz narrated it — meaning with tarjīʿ. And I heard him narrate from his father, from Ibn Muḥayrīz, from Abī Maḥdhūrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, the meaning of what Ibn Jurayj narrated.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And I heard him give the iqāmah, saying: \Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ. Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh"," qad qāmat al-ṣalāh. Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And I think I heard him narrate the iqāmah as a report (khabar) just as he narrated the adhān.\n\nIn the narration of al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī from al-Shāfiʿī regarding the question of the manner of the adhān and iqāmah"," al-Shāfiʿī said: The narration in which it is stated that the adhān was given five times in the day and night in the two mosques in the presence of the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār"," and that the muʾadhdhins of Makkah were the family of Abī Maḥdhūrah — and Abū Maḥdhūrah had given the adhān for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he taught him the adhān — then his children in Makkah"," and the family of Saʿd al-Qaraẓ gave the adhān since the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madīnah"," and the time of Abū Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him — all of them narrated the adhān and the iqāmah and the tathwīb at Fajr as we have stated. If it is permissible that this was an error on the part of their group while the people were present with them"," and someone came from the far end of the earth to teach us"," then it would be permissible for him to ask us about ʿArafah and Minā and then contradict us. And if he contradicted us in the mawāqīt"," it would be more permissible for him to contradict us in this matter which is openly practiced. [Ṣaḥīgh.]"""
"1974","(1974) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Yaḥyā Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Qurashī narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim said: I asked Mālik ibn Anas about the Sunnah regarding the adhān. He said: \What do you say about the adhān"," and from whom did you take the adhān?\"" Al-Walīd said: I said: \""Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," Ibn Jābir"," and others besides them informed me that Bilāl did not give the adhān for anyone after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and intended to go out for jihād. Abū Bakr wanted to prevent him and detain him"," so he said: 'If you freed me for the sake of Allah"," then do not detain me from jihād"," and if you freed me for yourself"," then I will stay.' So he let him go. He was in al-Shām until ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb came to them at al-Jābiyah. The Muslims asked ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb to ask Bilāl to give the adhān for them"," so he asked him"," and he gave the adhān for them one day — or they said"," one prayer. They said: 'No day was seen in which there were more people weeping than that day"," when they heard his voice"," remembering the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They said: 'We consider — or we say — that the adhān of the people of al-Shām is from his adhān on that day.'\""\n\nMālik said: \""I do not know what adhān of a day or prayer of a day — rather"," Saʿd al-Qaraẓ gave the adhān one day in this mosque during the time of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb while the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were present in large numbers"," and none of them objected to it. So Saʿd and his sons continued giving the adhān with his adhān until this day. And if there were a governor who heard from me"," I would think that he would gather this ummah upon their adhān.\""\n\nIt was said to Mālik: \""How was their adhān?\"" He said: \""He would say: 'Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh.' Then he would repeat"," saying: 'Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh"," ashhadu anna Muḥammadan Rasūl Allāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh"," ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh. Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ. Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh.'\"" He said: \""And the iqāmah was said once (once each).\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh said: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr said: \""I see that the fuqahāʾ of the people of ḥadīth have agreed upon the singling of the iqāmah"," and they have differed regarding the adhān. Some of them chose the adhān of Abī Maḥdhūrah — among them Mālik ibn Anas"," al-Shāfiʿī"," and their companions. And a group among them chose the adhān of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd.\"" The Shaykh said: \""Among them was al-Awzāʿī"," who chose the doubling of the adhān and the singling of the iqāmah. And to the singling of the iqāmah went Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr"," al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī"," Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn"," al-Zuhrī"," Makḥūl"," and ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," along with other eminent shaykhs among the Tābiʿīn"," may Allah be pleased with them.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh.]"""
"1975","(1975) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said: \The Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I saw in a dream a man standing on top of a wall. He gave the adhān doubled (mathnā)"," and he gave the iqāmah doubled (mathnā)"," and he sat briefly"," and he had upon him two green cloaks.'\""\n\nThus narrated a group from ʿAmr ibn Murrah. And it was also narrated from him"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"," from Muʿādh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it 5/232.]"""
"1976","(1976) Abū Ṣāliḥ, the son of the daughter of Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, informed us; my grandfather narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Sadūsī narrated to us; ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; al-Masʿūdī narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Murrah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Muʿādh ibn Jabal, who said: \The prayer was changed through three states.\"" Then he mentioned the hadith regarding the dream of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd"," and mentioned the adhān twice twice"," then said at the end of his adhān: \""Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh.\"" Then he paused briefly"," then stood and said the same as what he had said"," except that he added: \""Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh"," qad qāmat al-ṣalāh.\""\n\nAnd thus narrated Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh from al-Aʿmash"," from ʿAmr ibn Murrah"," from Ibn Abī Laylā"," from Muʿādh. And it was narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"1977","(1977) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Ḥuṣayn ibn Numayr narrated to us; Ibn Abī Laylā narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ, his hadith regarding his dream. (T) And thus narrated Sharīk and ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām from Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd. And it was narrated by Ḥuṣayn ibn Numayr from Ḥuṣayn, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted the people regarding the adhān.\"" Then he mentioned the hadith and said in it: \""He gave the adhān doubled doubled"," then he sat briefly"," then he gave the iqāmah doubled doubled.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1978","(1978) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Ḥuṣayn ibn Numayr narrated to us; Ḥuṣayn narrated it.\n\nAnd thus narrated a group — Ibn Fuḍayl and others — from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā.\n\nAnd the hadith, along with the difference in its chain of narration, is mursal (disconnected). Because ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā did not meet Muʿādh, nor ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd, and he did not name the one who narrated to him from either one of them or from one of the two.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah said: \ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā did not hear from Muʿādh ibn Jabal"," nor from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbd Rabbihi"," the companion of the adhān. Therefore"," it is not permissible to use as evidence a report that is not firmly established against firmly established reports.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And there have been narrated in this topic reports from other directions"," all of which are weak"," and I have explained their weakness in the book of al-Khilāfiyyāt.\n\nThe most excellent chain of narration reported regarding the doubling of the iqāmah is the hadith of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā. And if it is authentic"," then every adhān that has been narrated as doubled came after the dream of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd"," so it would be more deserving than what was narrated regarding his dream with respect to the iqāmah. The Madīnans narrate the iqāmah as single"," and the Kūfans narrate it as doubled doubled. The chain of the Madīnans is connected (mawṣūl)"," and the chain of the Kūfans is disconnected (mursal). Along with the connected chain of the Madīnans"," there is the mursal narration of Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," and he is the most accurate of the Tābiʿīn in irsāl. Then there is what we have narrated of the command to make it single after that"," and the practice of the people of the two Ḥarams. And in Allah is the success.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1979","(1979) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Muthannā informed us; Musaddad narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn ʿUbayd, Abū Qudāmah, narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," teach me the Sunnah of the adhān.'\"" Then he mentioned the hadith and said in it: \""'Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ.' And if it is the Ṣubḥ prayer"," say: 'Al-ṣalātu khayrun min al-nawm"," al-ṣalātu khayrun min al-nawm.' 'Allāhu Akbar"," Allāhu Akbar. Lā ilāha illā Allāh.'\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1980","(1980) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim and ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Ibn Jurayj; ʿUthmān ibn al-Sāʾib informed me; my father and Umm ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Maḥdhūrah informed me, from Abī Maḥdhūrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it, and in it: \Al-ṣalātu khayrun min al-nawm"," al-ṣalātu khayrun min al-nawm\"" in the first (call) of the Ṣubḥ. [Ṣaḥīgh for other than it.]"""
"1981","(1981) It has been narrated to us from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Ja'far, from Abu Salman, from Abu Mahdhurah, who said: I heard him say, \I used to give the adhan for the Prophet ﷺ"," and I would say in the first adhan of Fajr"," after 'Hayya 'ala al-falah"," hayya 'ala al-falah': 'As-salatu khayrun min an-nawm"," as-salatu khayrun min an-nawm. Allahu Akbar"," Allahu Akbar. La ilaha illa Allah.'\""\n\nAbu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Ali ibn Hamshadh narrated to us; Yazid ibn al-Haytham narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated to us; al-Ashja'i narrated from Sufyan"," and he mentioned it. And Abu Salman's name is Hammam al-Mu'adhdhin. [Sahih (authentic) according to other than him. Al-Nasa'i reported it (647).]"""
"1982","(1982) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn 'Umar informed us; Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Hafs ibn 'Umar ibn Sa'd al-Mu'adhdhin, that Sa'd used to give the adhan for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Hafs said: \My family informed me that Bilal came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to give him the adhan for the Fajr prayer"," and they said: 'He is asleep.' So Bilal called out in his loudest voice: 'As-salatu khayrun min an-nawm (Prayer is better than sleep).' And so it was established in the Fajr prayer.\"" [Sahih (authentic) according to other than him.]"""
"1983","(1983) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; Abu Muhammad al-Muzani informed us; 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman informed us; Shu'ayb informed me, from al-Zuhri, who said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me, and he mentioned the story of 'Abdullah ibn Zayd and his vision, up to the point where he said: \Then Bilal added in the adhan: 'As-salatu khayrun min an-nawm.' That was because Bilal came after having given the first adhan of the Fajr prayer to notify the Prophet ﷺ of the prayer"," and it was said to him: 'The Prophet ﷺ is asleep.' So Bilal called out in his loudest voice: 'As-salatu khayrun min an-nawm.' And so it was established in the adhan for the Fajr prayer.\"" [Sahih (authentic) according to other than him. Ibn Majah reported it (716).]"""
"1984","(1984) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us; Abu Usamah narrated to us; Ibn 'Awn narrated from Muhammad, from Anas, who said: \It is from the Sunnah that when the mu'adhdhin says in the Fajr adhan: 'Hayya 'ala al-falah","' he should say: 'As-salatu khayrun min an-nawm"," as-salatu khayrun min an-nawm. Allahu Akbar"," Allahu Akbar. La ilaha illa Allah.'\""\n\nA group narrated it from Abu Usamah"," and it is a sahih (authentic) chain of narration. [Sahih (authentic). Al-Daraqutni reported it (1/243).]"""
"1985","(1985) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'd al-Hafiz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanjhi narrated to us; Hisham ibn 'Amir ibn Nusayr al-Sulami, then al-Zafari, Abu al-Walid al-Dimashqi, narrated to us; 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Habib ibn Abi al-'Ishrin narrated to us; al-Awza'i narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari informed me that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to him from Nu'aym ibn al-Nahham, who said: \I was with my wife under her cloak on a cold morning"," when the announcer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out for the Subh (morning) prayer. When I heard it"," I said: 'If only he had said: \""And whoever sits"," there is no harm.\""' He said: Then when he said: 'As-salatu khayrun min an-nawm","' he said: 'And whoever sits"," there is no harm.'\"" [Sahih (authentic) according to other than him.]"""
"1986","(1986) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabrani narrated to us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \In the first adhan"," after al-falah"," was: 'As-salatu khayrun min an-nawm"," as-salatu khayrun min an-nawm.'\""\n\n'Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-'Adani narrated it from al-Thawri with his chain"," from Ibn 'Umar"," that he used to say: \""'Hayya 'ala al-falah"," hayya 'ala al-falah"," as-salatu khayrun min an-nawm' — in the first adhan"," twice"," meaning in the morning (Subh).\"" [Hasan (good). Al-Tahawi reported it (1/37).]"""
"1987","(1987) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Hasani narrated to us; Waki' narrated from al-'Umari, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from 'Umar. And Waki' narrated from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from 'Umar, that he said to his mu'adhdhin: \When you reach 'Hayya 'ala al-falah' in the Fajr"," then say: 'As-salatu khayrun min an-nawm"," as-salatu khayrun min an-nawm.'\"" [Hasan (good). Al-Daraqutni reported it (1/343).]"""
"1988","(1988) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us; Shu'bah narrated from al-Hakam ibn 'Utbah, from 'Abd Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: \Bilal was commanded to give the tathwib (calling 'as-salatu khayrun min an-nawm') in the Subh prayer and not to give it in any other.\"" [Da'if (weak). 'Abd al-Razzaq reported it (1823).]"""
"1989","(1989) 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran informed us; Abu Ja'far al-Razzaz narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ja'far informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Asim narrated to us; 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me not to give the tathwib except in the Fajr.\""\n\nAnd this is also mursal (disconnected). For 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla did not meet Bilal. Al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated it from Talhah ibn Musarrif and Zubayd"," from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah"," that Bilal used not to give the tathwib except in the Fajr"," and he would say in his adhan: \""Hayya 'ala al-falah"," as-salatu khayrun min an-nawm.\"" [Da'if (weak). Ibn Majah reported it (715).]"""
"1990","(1990) Abu al-Hasan ibn Bishran informed us in Baghdad; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us; Ma'mar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated from al-Hajjaj.\n\nAnd Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; Abu Yahya narrated from Mujahid, who said: \I was with Ibn 'Umar"," and a man gave the tathwib in the Zuhr or the 'Asr"," so he said: 'Leave us"," for this is an innovation (bid'ah).'\"" [Da'if (weak). Abu Dawud reported it (538).]"""
"1991","(1991) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us: Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Nāfiʿ, who said: Ibn ʿUmar used to pronounce the takbīr three times in the call to prayer (adhān) and the shahāda three times. And sometimes, when he said \Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ\"" (Come to success)"," he would follow it with: \""ḿayya ʿalā khayr al-ʿamal\"" (Come to the best of deeds).\n\nAnd ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated it from Nāfiʿ"," who said: Ibn ʿUmar would sometimes add in his adhān: \""Ḥayya ʿalā khayr al-ʿamal.\"" And al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it from Nāfiʿ similarly. [Ṣaḥīgh in other than this chain. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (2239)]"""
"1992","(1992) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Dāwūd narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Nāfiʿ, who said: Ibn ʿUmar would not give the adhān during his journey. He would say: \Ḥayya ʿalā al-ṣalāh"," ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ\"" (Come to prayer"," come to success). And sometimes he would say: \""Ḥayya ʿalā khayr al-ʿamal\"" (Come to the best of deeds).\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated it from Ibn ʿUmar that he used to say that in his adhān. And Nusayr ibn Dhūʿlūq narrated it similarly from Ibn ʿUmar"," and he mentioned it in the context of travel. And it was narrated from Abī Umāmah as well. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"1993","(1993) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Dāwūd narrated to us: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father: that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn used to say in his adhān, when he said \Ḥayya ʿalā al-falāḥ\"": \""Ḥayya ʿalā khayr al-ʿamal\"" (Come to the best of deeds)"," and he would say: \""This is the first adhān.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah (2239)]"""
"1994","(1994) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī, narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rustah narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Ḥumayd ibn Kāsib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd al-Muʾadhdhin narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmmār, ʿAmmār, and ʿUmar, the two sons of Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar ibn Saʿd, from their fathers, from their grandfathers, from Bilāl: that he used to call out at dawn (fajr) and say: \Ḥayya ʿalā khayr al-ʿamal\"" (Come to the best of deeds). So the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to replace it with: \""Al-ṣalātu khayrun min al-nawm\"" (Prayer is better than sleep)"," and he abandoned \""Ḥayya ʿalā khayr al-ʿamal.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: This wording is not established from the Prophet ﷺ regarding what he taught Bilāl and Abū Mahdhūrah"," and we disapprove of adding it. And in Allah lies success. [Very weak. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr (1071)]"""
"1995","(1995) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr from a woman of Banī al-Najjār, who said: My house was among the tallest houses around the mosque. Bilāl would give the fajr adhān upon it. He would come at the time of suḥūr and sit on the house, watching for the dawn. When he saw it, he would stretch and then say: \O Allah"," I praise You and seek Your help against Quraysh that they establish Your religion.\"" Then he would give the adhān. She said: By Allah"," I did not know that he ever left these words out for a single night. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (519)]"""
"1996","(1996) Khālid ibn ʿAmr narrated, saying: Sufyān narrated from al-Jurayrī from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaqīq from Abū Barzah al-Aslamī, who said: It is from the Sunnah that the adhān be given from the minaret and the iqāmah in the mosque. Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us of it: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us: Ibn Abī Ḥātim narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Aṭrāblusī narrated to us: Khālid ibn ʿAmr narrated it.\n\nThis is a munkar hadith; no one narrated it other than Khālid ibn ʿAmr, and he is weak, munkar al-ḥadīth. [Very weak. Narrated by Tammām in his Fawāʾid (1570)]"
"1997","(1997) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Ayyūb ibn Salmūyah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Sulamī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us: Ḥaywah narrated from Nāfiʿ ibn Sulaymān al-Makkī from Muḥammad ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ from his father from ʿĀʾishah: that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The imām is a guarantor (ḍāmin)"," and the muʾadhdhin is a trusted custodian (muʾtaman). May Allah guide the imāms and pardon the muʾadhdhins.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (517)]"""
"1998","(1998) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Abī Khalaf al-Isfarāʾinī informed us with it: the faqīh Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zaydān al-Bajalī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿĪsā, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, narrated to us. And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣibghī narrated to us: Abū Bakr Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Khaṭmī al-Anṣārī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥimānī narrated to us: Ḥusayn ibn ʿĪsā al-Ḥanafī narrated to us: al-Ḥakam ibn Abān narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let your best among you give the adhān for you"," and let the one most proficient in recitation lead you in prayer.\"" [Munkar. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (590)]"""
"1999","(1999) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Muqriʾ, Ibn al-Ḥammāmī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us in Baghdad: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated to me: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Mahdhūrah narrated to me — and he is Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Mahdhūrah — from his father, from his grandfather, from Abī Mahdhūrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The custodians (umanāʾ) of the Muslims over their prayers and their suḥūr are the muʾadhdhins.\"" [Weak. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr (6743)]"""
"2000","(2000) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated from Yūnus from al-Ḥasan: that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The muʾadhdhins are the custodians (umanāʾ) of the Muslims over their prayers.\"" He mentioned other things along with it. This mursal narration serves as a witness for what preceded it. [Weak]"""
"2001","(2001) And Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās related to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr related to us, he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ informed you from Bakr ibn ʿAmr from Ṣafwān ibn Sulaym: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Banū Khaṭmaʾ of the Anṣār: \O Banū Khaṭmaʾ"," make your muʾadhdhin the best among yourselves.\""\n\nAnd this is also a mursal (hadith). [Weak]"""
"2002","(2002) And Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim related to us: We came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and he said: \Who are your muʾadhdhins?\"" We said: \""Our slaves and our freedmen.\"" He gestured with his hand in this manner — meaning he was turning them over"," i.e."," our slaves and our freedmen. He said: \""This is a great shortcoming on your part. Were I able to give the adhān in addition to my role as caliph"," I would give it.\"""""
"2003","(2003) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār related to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī related to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah related to us — Mālik related to us. And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us — Abū Khalīfah related to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah related to us — from Mālik — from Ibn Shihāb — from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh — from his father: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," Bilāl gives the call at night"," so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call.\"" Ibn Shihāb said: And Ibn Umm Maktūm was a blind man who would not give the call until it was said to him"," \""You have reached morning"," you have reached morning.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī. [Authentic]"""
"2004","(2004) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr related to us — Abū Dāwūd related to us — Muḥammad ibn Salamah related to us — Ibn Wahb related to us — from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh and Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah — from his father — from ʿĀʾishah: that Ibn Umm Maktūm was a muʾadhdhin for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was blind.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Salamah al-Murādī. [Authentic. Muslim narrated it, no. 381]"
"2005","(2005) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb related to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī related to us — Saʿ ibn ʿĀmir related to us — Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah related to us — Mālik ibn Dīnār related to us — from Abī ʿArūbah: that Ibn al-Zubayr used to dislike that the muʾadhdhin be blind.\n\nAnd the narration from Ibn Masʿūd regarding that is understood to refer to a blind muʾadhdhin who is alone, without a sighted person to inform him of the time. [Weak. Ibn Shaybah narrated it, no. 2254]"
"2006","(2006) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah related to us — Abū Dāwūd related to us — Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭūsī related to us — Yaʿqūb related to us — from his father — from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī related to me — from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbd Rabbih, who said: My father ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd related to me, and he mentioned his dream to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ﷺ said: \It is indeed a true dream"," if Allah the Most High wills. Rise with Bilāl and teach him what you saw"," and let him give the call with it"," for he has a more resonant voice than you.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated in the hadith of Abī Maḥdhūrah to that effect"," where in one of the two narrations he ﷺ said: \""Which of you is the one whose voice I heard raised?\"" And in the other narration: \""I have indeed heard among these people the adhān of a man with a beautiful voice.\"" And this is the narration of ʿUthmān ibn al-Sāʾib. [Good]"""
"2007","(2007) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Warrāq informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān related to us — Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd related to us — from Mālik ibn Anas — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ṣaʿṣaʿah al-Anṣārī — from his father: that he informed him that Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī said: \I see that you love sheep and the desert. So"," when you are among your sheep and in your desert and you give the call to prayer"," raise your voice with the call"," for no jinn"," no human"," and nothing else hears the voice of the muʾadhdhin except that it will bear witness for him on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Abū Saʿīd said: \""I heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: The encouragement to raise the voice indicates the practice of tartīl (measured recitation) in the adhān. [Authentic]"""
"2008","(2008) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Mālik al-Mālikī informed us — Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-ʿUmarī related to us — Muʿallā ibn Mahdī informed us — ʿAbd al-Munʿim al-Baṣrī related to us — Yaḥyā ibn Muslim related to us — from al-Ḥasan and Aṭāʾ — from Jābir: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Bilāl: \O Bilāl"," when you give the adhān"," do so slowly and deliberately"," and when you give the iqāmah"," do so briskly. And place between your adhān and your iqāmah an interval sufficient for the eater to finish his meal"," the drinker to finish his drink"," and the one who has entered to relieve himself to finish his need. And do not stand (for prayer) until you see me.\"" Thus did a group narrate it from ʿAbd al-Munʿim ibn Nuʿaym"," Abū Saʿīd.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: He is a narrator of rejected hadith (munkar al-ḥadīth)"," and Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn declared Yaḥyā ibn Muslim al-Bakkāʾ al-Kūfī weak.\n\nAnd it has been narrated through another chain from al-Ḥasan and Aṭāʾ from Abī Hurayrah"," but it is not well-known. [Very weak. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it"," no. 195]"""
"2009","(2009) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed him — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān related to us — Ḥamdān ibn al-Haytham ibn Khālid al-Baghdādī related to us — Ṣubayḥ ibn ʿUmar al-Sīrāfī related to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh related to us — from al-Ḥasan and Aṭāʾ, both of them — from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Bilāl, and he mentioned the like of it up to his words \to finish his need.\"" The first chain of narration is more well-known than this. [Very weak]"""
"2010","(2010) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawiyah al-ʿAskarī related to us — Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Sūsī related to us — al-Qaʿnabī related to us — Maḥrūm ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-ʿAṭṭār related to us — from his father — from Abī al-Zubayr, muʾadhdhin of al-Bayt al-Muqaddas, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said to me: \When you give the adhān"," do so slowly and deliberately"," and when you give the iqāmah"," do so briskly.\"" [Weak. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it"," no. 225]"""
"2011","(2011) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, saying: Abū ʿUbayd informed me — al-Anṣārī, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh, narrated to me from Maḥrūm al-ʿAṭṭār, from his father, from Abū al-Zubayr, the mu'adhdhin of Bayt al-Maqdis, that ʿUmar said to him: \That is"," except that he said: 'When you give the Iqāmah"," then hasten through it.'\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: al-Aṣmaʿī said: \""Al-ḥadhm means al-ḥadr — that is"," rapidity in the Iqāmah and cutting short of prolongation.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿUmar that he used to recite the Adhān with measured deliberation (tartīl) and would hasten through the Iqāmah.\n\n[Weak]\n\n(2012) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Ibn Abī Uways informed me; Mālik narrated to me from Sumayy"," from Abū Ṣāliḥ"," from Abū Hurayrah"," who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""If the people knew what is in the call (al-nidāʾ) and the first row"," and then found no way to draw lots for it except by drawing lots"," they would draw lots for it. And if they knew what is in the midday prayer (al-taḥjīr)"," they would race to it. And if they knew what is in the ʿIshāʾ and the Ṣubḥ prayers"," they would come to them even if they had to crawl.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: \""And it is mentioned that a group of people disputed over the Adhān"," so Saʿd drew lots among them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 590]"""
"2012","(2012) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Ibn Abī Uways informed me; Mālik narrated to me from Sumayy, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If the people knew what is in the call (al-nidāʾ) and the first row"," and then found no way to draw lots for it except by drawing lots"," they would draw lots for it. And if they knew what is in the midday prayer (al-taḥjīr)"," they would race to it. And if they knew what is in the ʿIshāʾ and the Ṣubḥ prayers"," they would come to them even if they had to crawl.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: \""And it is mentioned that a group of people disputed over the Adhān"," so Saʿd drew lots among them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 590]"""
"2013","(2013) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us; Abū ʿUbayd informed us; Hushaym informed us; Ibn Shubrumah informed us, saying: \The people contended with one another over the Adhān at al-Qādisiyyah"," so they brought their dispute to Saʿd"," and he drew lots among them.\"" [Weak]"""
"2014","(2014) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Ḥasan ibn Sufyān said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr informed us; my father narrated to me from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had two mu'adhdhins: Bilāl and Ibn Umm Maktūm"," the blind man. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed"," Bilāl gives the Adhān at night"," so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the Adhān.' And there was no interval between the two of them except that one would descend and the other would ascend.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2015","(2015) And with this chain of narration, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from al-Qāsim, from ʿĀʾishah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), a similar narration.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr, and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from ʿUbayd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"2016","(2016) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us from Isrāʾīl, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) had three mu'adhdhins: Bilāl"," Abū Maḥdhūrah"," and Ibn Umm Maktūm.\""\n\nAbū Bakr said: \""And both reports are sound — meaning this one and the one that preceded it. So whoever said he had two mu'adhdhins"," he meant the two who used to give the Adhān in Madīnah"," and whoever said three"," he meant Abū Maḥdhūrah"," who used to give the Adhān in Makkah.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And the fact that he limited himself to one mu'adhdhin in Makkah is an indication of the permissibility of limiting oneself to a single mu'adhdhin.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 408]"""
"2017","(2017) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Firyābī informed us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and Yazīd ibn Mawhab said: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us from ʿUqayl, from al-Zuhrī, from al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd, who informed him: \The third Adhān on the day of Jumuʿah was only commanded by ʿUthmān when the people of Madīnah increased in number. And the Adhān on the day of Jumuʿah was when the Imām would sit upon the minbar.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr from al-Layth.\n\nAnd it is said that the third Adhān was established along with the Iqāmah. And the report pertains to the Adhān"," not to the mu'adhdhin. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 873]"""
"2018","(2018) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us; ʿAffān informed us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us; al-Jurayrī informed me from Abū al-ʿAlāʾ, from Muṭarrif, from ʿUthmān ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ, who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," make me the imām of my people.' He said: 'You are their imām"," so follow the weakest among them"," and appoint a mu'adhdhin who does not take a wage for his Adhān.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 531]"""
"2019","(2019) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad al-Basṭāmī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; ʿImrān ibn Mūsā informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Mayssarah al-Qawārīrī informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yazīd, Abū Maʿshar al-Barrāʾ, informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn ʿAbbās: \A group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a tribe of the Arab tribes among whom there was a person stung by a scorpion (ladīgh) or severely wounded (salīm). They said: 'Is there among you a practitioner of incantation (rāqīn)? For in the water there is a person who has been stung or is severely wounded.' So a man from among them went and performed incantation for him in exchange for a flock of sheep"," and he was cured. When he came to his companions"," they disapproved of that and said: 'You have taken a wage for the Book of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic.' When they came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," they informed him of that. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The most deserving thing for which you may take a wage is the Book of Allah.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Saydān ibn Muḍārib from Abū Maʿshar.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us in the ḥadīth of Abū Maḥdhūrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) called him when he had completed the Adhān and gave him a pouch containing some silver. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 2156]"""
"2020","(2020) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad narrated to me from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The imāms are guarantors (ḍumanāʾ) and the mu'adhdhins are trustees (umanaʾ). May Allah guide the imāms and forgive the mu'adhdhins.\""\n\nImām Aḥmad said: \""And this ḥadīth was not heard by Suhayl from his father; rather"," he heard it from al-Aʿmash.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 531]"""
"2021","(2021) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to me; Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ informed me, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The imām is a guarantor"," and the mu'adhdhin is a trusted one. May Allah guide the imāms and forgive the mu'adhdins.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2022","(2022) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd al-Ghaffār and Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd both said: al-Aʿmash narrated to us. And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Abū al-Muwajjih Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Muwajjih informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us; Abū Ḥamzah al-Sukkari said: I heard al-Aʿmash narrating from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The imām is a guarantor"," and the mu'adhdhin is a trusted one. O Allah"," guide the imāms and forgive the mu'adhdins.\""\n\nAbū Ḥamzah added in his narration that a man said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you have left us"," and we used to compete in giving the adhān after you for a long time.\"" He said: \""After you"," there will come a time whose lowest ones will be their mu'adhdins.\""\n\nAl-Aʿmash did not hear this hadith with certainty from Abū Ṣāliḥ; rather"," he heard it from a man from Abū Ṣāliḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it (207)]"""
"2023","(2023) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; Ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated, from a man, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The imām is a guarantor"," and the mu'adhdhin is a trusted one. O Allah"," guide the imāms and forgive the mu'adhdins.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2024","(2024) Abū ʿAlī informed us; Abū Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated to us; al-Aʿmash said: I was informed from Abū Ṣāliḥ — and I do not think except that I heard it from him — from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said the like of it.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Muḥammad ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah. And it has reached me from al-Bukhārī that he said: The hadith of Abū Ṣāliḥ from ʿĀʾishah is more authentic. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Aḥmad narrated it (2/282)]"
"2025","(2025) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī in Naysābūr and Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz in Baghdād both informed us, saying: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī in Makkah informed us; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrat narrated to us; al-Muqriʾ Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us; Ḥaywah narrated to us; Nāfiʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to me that Muḥammad ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ narrated to him from his father, that he heard ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The imām is a guarantor"," and the mu'adhdhin is a trusted one. May Allah guide the imām and pardon the mu'adhdin.\""\n\nAnd it has been said: from al-Aʿmash"," from Mujāhid"," from Ibn ʿUmar. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Ṭaḥāwī narrated it (3/53)]"""
"2026","(2026) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us orally; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Farrāʾ, and Qaṭn ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to me, from al-Aʿmash, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he said: \The mu'adhdhin is forgiven to the extent of the reach of his voice"," and every moist and dry thing testifies for him.\"" He said: And I heard him say that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""The imām is a guarantor"," and the mu'adhdhin is a trusted one. O Allah"," guide the imāms and forgive the mu'adhdins.\"" Thus did Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrate it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Sirāj narrated it in his Musnad (1/23)]"""
"2027","(2027) And ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq narrated it from al-Aʿmash, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The mu'adhdhin is forgiven to the extent of the reach of his voice"," and every moist and dry thing that hears his voice testifies for him.\""\n\nThis much is narrated as marfūʿ (elevated)"," without the other hadith. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū al-Jawwāb narrated to us; ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq narrated it.\n\nAnd ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd al-Ghaffār narrated it as well. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (515)]"""
"2028","(2028) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd al-Ghaffār narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated, from Mujāhid, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The mu'adhdhin is forgiven to the extent of the reach of his voice"," and every moist and dry thing that hears it testifies for him.\""\n\nAnd Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated it as well. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"2029","(2029) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb al-Faqīh narrated to us; al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The mu'adhdhin is forgiven to the extent of the reach of his voice"," and every moist and dry thing that hears it testifies for him.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated this hadith from Mūsā ibn Abī ʿUthmān"," from Abū Yaḥyā"," from Abū Hurayrah"," as marfūʿ. And we have narrated the first hadith from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," as mursal. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2030","(2030) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl informed us; Abū Shuʿayb al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAdī informed us; Yūnus narrated, from al-Ḥasan, that it was mentioned from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \The imām is a guarantor"," and the mu'adhdhin is a trusted one. May Allah guide the imāms and forgive the mu'adhdins\"" — or he said: \""May Allah forgive the imāms and guide the mu'adhdins.\"" Ibn Abī ʿAdī was uncertain. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"2031","(2031) And with this isnad, Muhammad ibn Abī ʿAdīyy narrated to us — from Yūnus — from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The muezzins are the trustees (amīnūn) of the Muslims over their prayers and their needs (ḥawā'ij).\""\n\nAnd this has been narrated from Yūnus from al-ḥasan from Jābir"," but it is not preserved (maḥfūẓ). And regarding this"," [a narration] has been reported from Abī Umāmah. [Weak (ḍaʿīf)]"""
"2032","(2032) Abū Naṣr ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us — ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl al-Khuzāʿī informed us — Abū Shuʿayb informed us — ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us — Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us — Abū Ghālib said: I heard Abā Umāmah saying: \The muezzins are the trustees (amīnūn) of the Muslims"," and the imams are the guarantors (ḍumanā').\"" He said: \""And the adhān is more beloved to me than the imāmah.\"" (Ḥasan)"""
"2033","(2033) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Yaʿlā al-Muhallabī informed us — they both said: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar narrated — from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the call to prayer (al-ṣalāh) is given"," the Shayṭān turns his back"," passing wind"," so that he cannot hear the adhān. When the adhān is completed"," he returns. When the iqāmah is called"," he turns away again. When the iqāmah is completed"," he returns and insinuates between a person and his own self"," saying to him: 'Remember such and remember such' — things he had not been remembering before — until the man remains unaware of how he prayed.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and al-Bukhārī extracted it from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah.\n\nWhat is meant by al-tathwīb here is the iqāmah. And that which indicates this is what… [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ). Al-Bukhārī extracted it (no. 583)]"""
"2034","(2034) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Jarīr narrated — from al-Aʿmash — from Abī Ṣāliḥ — from Abī Hurayrah — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When the Shayṭān hears the call to prayer"," he passes wind — so that he cannot hear its voice. When it falls silent"," he returns and whispers. When he hears the iqāmah"," he departs until he cannot hear its voice. When it falls silent"," he returns and whispers.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah.\n\n(T) And in the narration of Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ from his father: \""He turns away and has an urge to urinate (ḥuṣāṣ).\"" [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"2035","(2035) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us — Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated — from al-Aʿmash — from Abī Sufyān — from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the muezzin gives the adhān"," the Shayṭān flees until he reaches al-Rawḥā'.\"" And it is thirty miles from al-Madīnah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Abī Muʿāwiyah. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"2036","(2036) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us — Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us — Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyá narrated to me — ʿĪsā ibn Ṭalḥah said:\n\nI heard Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \Indeed"," the muezzins will have the longest necks among mankind on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from two Ṭalḥah ibn Yaḥyá. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ). Muslim extracted it (no. 387)]"""
"2037","(2037) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar, Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī, said: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Dāwūd said: I heard my father saying — the meaning of the statement of the Prophet ﷺ: \The muezzins will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection\"" — it does not mean that their necks will grow long. Rather"," it is that mankind will be thirsty on the Day of Resurrection"," and when a person is thirsty"," his neck contracts"," whereas the muezzins will not be thirsty"," so their necks will remain upright. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"2038","(2038) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us — Khayr ibn ʿArafah narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyá al-Ādamī in Baghdād narrated to us — Abū Ismāʿīl Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sulamī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Miṣrī narrated to me — Yaḥyá ibn Ayyūb narrated — from Ibn Jurayj — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever gives the adhān for twelve years"," Paradise becomes obligatory for him"," and for each adhān he gives"," sixty good deeds are recorded for him"," and for each iqāmah"," thirty good deeds.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh said: \""This is an authentic ḥadīth"," and it has a corroborating witness (shāhid) from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Lahīʿah.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And it has been narrated by Yaḥyá ibn al-Mutawakkil from Ibn Jurayj from one who narrated to him from Nāfiʿ.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: \""And this is more likely (ashbah).\""\n\nAs for the ḥadīth of Ibn Lahīʿah: Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us of it — Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānī' narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Mihrān narrated to us — Abū al-Ṭāhir and Abū al-Rabīʿ both said: Ibn Wahb informed us — Ibn Lahīʿah informed me — from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar"," that the Prophet ﷺ said: \""Whoever gives the adhān for twelve years"," Paradise becomes obligatory for him"," and for each adhān"," sixty good deeds are recorded for him"," and for each iqāmah"," thirty good deeds.\"" [Denounced (munkar). Al-Ḥākim extracted it (1/322)]"""
"2039","(2039) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us orally — Abū al-Faḍl al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Qūhyār informed us — Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Sulamī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Muḥammad ibn Yazīd narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Rustum narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated — from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr — from Abī Salamah — from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever gives the adhān for five prayers and leads them in prayer (ammahum) with faith (īmān) and expectation of reward (iḥtisāb)"," his past sins will be forgiven.\""\n\n\""I do not know this except from the ḥadīth of Ibrāhīm ibn Rustum from Ḥammād.\"" As for the ḥadīth which… [Weak (ḍaʿīf). Al-Iṣbahānī extracted it in al-Targhīb wa al-Tarhīb (1/40)]"""
"2040","(2040) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us — Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdīyy al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Hārūn al-Hāshimī informed us — al-Qāsim ibn Naṣr al-Mukharramī informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAmr al-Bajalī informed us — Jaʿfar ibn Ziyād narrated — from Muḥammad ibn Sūqah — from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir — from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that the imam should also be the muezzin. This is a ḥadīth whose isnad is entirely weak (ḍaʿīf).\n\nIsmāʿīl ibn ʿAmr ibn Najīḥ, Abū Isḥāq al-Kūfī, narrated aḥādīth for which he was not corroborated (lā yutābaʿu ʿalayhā), and Jaʿfar ibn Ziyād is weak (ḍaʿīf). [Denounced (munkar). Ibn al-Ghaṭrīf extracted it in his Juz' (no. 39)]"
"2041","Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated that 'Umar said: \If I had been able to give the adhan alongside the Khalifah"," I would certainly have given it.\"" [Sahih]"""
"2042","Umm Farwah, who was among those who gave bay'ah to the Prophet ﷺ and was among the first Muhajirat, narrated that she heard the Prophet ﷺ being asked about the best of deeds, and he said: \Salah at its earliest time.\"" Abu Dawud narrated it in the Sunan. [Sahih li ghayrihi. Narrated by Abu Dawud"," 426]"""
"2043","'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud narrated: \I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Which deed is most excellent?' He said: 'Salah at its earliest time.' I said: 'Then which?' He said: 'Jihad in the cause of Allah.' I said: 'Then which?' He said: 'Kindness to parents.'\"" Muhammad ibn Bashar Bundar narrated it from 'Umar from him; Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in Mukhtasar al-Mukhtasar; and 'Ali ibn Hafs al-Mada'ini narrated it from Shu'bah from al-Walid ibn al-'Ayzar. It was also narrated from Ghundar from Shu'bah from 'Ubayd al-Muktab from Abu 'Amr from a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ with the same meaning. [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 327]"""
"2044","Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated: \We asked Jabir ibn 'Abdullah about the times of the Prophet's ﷺ prayers"," and he said: \""He used to pray Dhuhr at midday"," and pray 'Asr while the sun was still bright"," and pray Maghrib when the sun had set"," and pray 'Isha' — when the people gathered quickly"," he would pray it early"," and when they were few"," he would delay it — and pray Fajr in the darkness (ghalas).\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Muslim ibn Ibrahim"," and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Shu'bah. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 535]"""
"2045","'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated: \I heard Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud al-Ansari narrating from his father"," who said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying Dhuhr when the sun had passed its zenith"," and sometimes he would delay it when the heat became intense. I saw him praying 'Asr while the sun was still high and white"," before any yellowness entered it"," so that a man would leave the prayer and reach Dhu al-Hulayfah before the sun set. He prayed Maghrib when the sun had set"," and prayed 'Isha' when the horizon darkened"," and sometimes he would delay it until the people gathered. He prayed Fajr in the darkness (ghalas). Then he prayed it another time and brightened with it (is fara biha). After that"," his prayer was always in the darkness until he passed away"," and he did not return to praying it in brightness.'\"" [Sahih]"""
"2046","'A'ishah narrated: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never prayed any prayer at its later time until Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," took him.\"" Mu'alla ibn 'Abd al-Rahman similarly narrated it from al-Layth. And Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated it from al-Layth as well. [Sahih li ghayrihi. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi"," 104]"""
"2047","'A'ishah narrated: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never prayed any prayer at its later time"," except twice"," until Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," took him.\"" This is a mursal narration"," for Ishaq ibn 'Umar did not meet 'A'ishah. [Sahih li ghayrihi]"""
"2048","(a) Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The earliest time is the pleasure of Allah"," and the latest time is the pardon of Allah.\"" (b) A similar narration is reported from Ibn 'Umar. (c) Abu Ahmad said: \""There is discussion regarding this chain. The correct position is what we have stated"," as narrated by Ibn Sa'id and Ibn Asbat"," that this chain with this isnad is invalid — whether it is said to be 'Abdullah or 'Ubaydullah.\"" (d) The Sheikh said: \""This hadith is known through Ya'qub ibn al-Walid al-Madani. Ya'qub is munkar al-hadith; Yahya ibn Ma'in declared him weak"," and Ahmad ibn Hanbal declared him a liar"," as did all the other hafiz"," and they attributed fabrication to him. We seek refuge in Allah from misguidance. It has also been narrated through other chains"," all of which are weak.\"" [Batil. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi"," 172]"""
"2049","Abu Mahdhurah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The earliest time is the pleasure of Allah"," the middle time is the mercy of Allah"," and the latest time is the pardon of Allah.\"" Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya"," who is al-'Ijli al-Darir"," Abu Ishaq"," narrated it — he used to narrate fabrications from trustworthy narrators"," as reported to us by Abu Sa'id al-Malini from Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz. Ibrahim ibn Abi Mahdhurah is Ibrahim ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Mahdhurah"," who is well-known. This hadith with the first wording has also been narrated in a marfu' manner from Ibn 'Abbas"," Jarir ibn 'Abdullah"," and Anas ibn Malik"," but it is not established. Its origin lies in the statement of Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Baqir. [Munkar]"""
"2050","Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated from his father: \The earliest time is the pleasure of Allah"," and the latest time is the pardon of Allah.\"" This is how Abu Uways narrated it from Ja'far. It has also been narrated from Musa ibn Ja'far from his father from his grandfather from 'Ali from the Prophet ﷺ. [Da'if]"""
"2051","(2051) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us — Shuʿbah, on the authority of Abū al-Minhāl, on the authority of Abū Barzah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform the Ẓuhr prayer when the sun had passed its meridian, and he would perform the ʿAṣr prayer at such a time that one of us would go to the farthest part of al-Madīnah and return while the sun was still bright and alive. And I forgot the Maghrib. And he would not mind delaying the ʿIshāʾ prayer until the third part of the night — then he said, until the half of the night — and he would dislike sleeping before it and talking after it. And he would perform the Ṣubḥ prayer at such a time that any one of us would recognize his companion whom he would recognize, and he would recite therein from sixty to one hundred verses."
"2052","(2052) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Yaḥyā, on the authority of Shuʿbah, on the authority of Simāk ibn Ḥarb, on the authority of Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform the Ẓuhr prayer when the sun descended — meaning, when it passed its meridian."
"2053","(2053) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us — al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us — Sufyān, on the authority of Ḥakīm ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibrāhīm, on the authority of al-Aswad, on the authority of ʿĀʾishah, who said: I have not seen anyone more hastening with the Ẓuhr prayer than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, not excepting Abū Bakr or ʿUmar."
"2054","(2054) Isḥāq al-Azrāq narrated it from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm — Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir informed us — Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Adhramī narrated to us — Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azrāq narrated to us, mentioning something similar, without his statement: \not excepting Abū Bakr or ʿUmar.\"" And that is an error"," and the correct narration is the one narrated by the group"," as stated by Ibn Ḥanbal and others. And Isḥāq narrated it once correctly."""
"2055","(2055) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us — Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us — ʿAlī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us — al-Zuhrī, on the authority of Saʿīd, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the heat becomes intense"," delay the prayer"," for the intensity of heat is from the blazing of Jahannam.\"" And the Fire complained to its Lord"," the Almighty and Majestic"," saying: \""O Lord"," some parts of me are consuming others.\"" So He permitted it two breaths: one breath in winter and one breath in summer. Thus"," the most intense heat you experience is from its heat"," and the most intense cold you experience is from its bitter cold."""
"2056","(2056) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Sufyān, on the authority of al-Zuhrī, mentioned something similar, except that he said: \The most intense heat you experience is from its heat"," and the most intense cold you experience is from its bitter cold.\"""""
"2057","(2057) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Khālid ibn Mawhab and Qutaybah informed us — that al-Layth narrated to them, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the heat becomes intense"," delay the prayer.\"" Ibn Mawhab said: \""Delay the prayer"," for the intensity of heat is from the blazing of Jahannam.\"""""
"2058","(2058) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us — Mālik, on the authority of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd, the freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyān, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When there is heat"," delay the prayer"," for the intensity of heat is from the blazing of Jahannam.\"" And he mentioned that the Fire complained to its Lord"," the Almighty and Majestic"," so He permitted it two breaths every year: one breath in winter and one breath in summer."""
"2059","(2059) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-ʿAlawī and Abū Muḥammad Junāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Junāḥ al-Qāḍī in al-Kūfah said — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAbsī narrated to us — Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated to us — from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Saʿīd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Perform the Ẓuhr prayer when it is cool"," for the intensity of heat is from the blazing of Jahannam.\"""""
"2060","(2060) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated to me — Abū al-Ḥasan said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb saying: I heard Abū Dharr saying: We were with the Prophet ﷺ, and the muʾadhdhin intended to give the adhān for Ẓuhr, so he said: \Wait (abrid).\"" Then he intended to give the adhān again"," so he said: \""Wait\"" — twice or three times"," until we saw the shadows of the hillocks. Then he said: \""Indeed"," the intensity of heat is from the blazing of Jahannam. So when the heat becomes intense"," delay the prayer.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: He is the Muhājir"," Abū al-Ḥasan."""
"2061","(2061) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, al-Asfāṭīy informed us, Abū al-Walīd informed us — he mentioned it with his chain of narration, that he heard Abū Dharr saying: He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and the mu'adhdhin called the adhān, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \Delay (the prayer).\"" And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth. And Ghundar likewise narrated it from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 514]"""
"2062","(2062) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib and al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād both said: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā informed us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from Muhājir Abī al-Ḥasan, that he heard Zayd ibn Wahb narrating from Abū Dharr, who said: The mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the adhāh for Ẓuhr, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \Delay! Delay!\"" — or he said: \""Wait! Wait!\"" — and he said: \""Indeed"," the intensity of heat is from the exhaling of Jahannam. When the heat becomes severe"," delay the prayer.\"" Abū Dharr said: \""Until we saw the shadows of the mounds.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā.\n\nAnd in this is the indication that the command to delay came after the adhān"," and that the adhān was given at the beginning of the time. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded in the one before it.]"""
"2063","(2063) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us verbally, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Jābir, meaning Ibn Samurah.\n\nḤammād said: And Sayyār ibn Salāmah narrated it to me from Abū Barzah al-Aslamī. One of them said: \Bilāl used to give the adhān when the sun declined.\"" And the other said: \""Bilāl used to give the adhān when the sun began to set.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī"," 769]"""
"2064","(2064) Abū Bakr narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Yūnus informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Sharīk narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: \Bilāl would not hasten the adhān"," and he would sometimes delay the iqāmah a little.\"" And his statement has already passed: \""Bilāl used to give the adhān when the sun began to set.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2065","(2065) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus informed us, Zuhayr informed us — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī informed us, Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr informed us, Abū Khaythamah informed us, Abū Isḥāq narrated from Saʿīd ibn Wahb from Khabbāb, who said: \We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of Ramaḍān"," but he did not grant our complaint.\"" I said to Abū Isḥāq: \""About Ẓuhr?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" I said: \""About hastening it?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 619]"""
"2066","(2066) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzāz informed us in Baghdād from the original of his hearing, Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī informed us in Makkah, Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrrah informed us, Khallād ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated from Abī Isḥāq, who said: Saʿīd ibn Wahb narrated to me, who said: Khabbāb ibn al-Aratt narrated to me, who said: \We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the heat of Ramaḍān"," and he did not grant our complaint. And he said: 'When the sun has set (i.e."," passed the meridian)"," then pray.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 5/110]"""
"2067","(2067) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal and Musaddad both said: ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbbād informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Ḥārith al-Anṣārī from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \I used to pray Ẓuhr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and I would take a handful of pebbles so that they would cool in my palm"," and I would place them for my forehead to prostrate upon them due to the intensity of the heat.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 399]"""
"2068","(2068) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Khazzāz informed us, Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn informed us, Isḥāq al-Azraq informed us — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us, Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated from Sharīk from Bayān ibn Bishr from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, who said: \We used to pray Ẓuhr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the midday heat"," and he said to us: 'Delay the prayer"," for indeed the intensity of heat is from the exhaling of Jahannam.'\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said — as it reached me from him: \""I asked Muḥammad"," meaning al-Bukhārī"," about this ḥadīth"," and he considered it preserved (maḥfūẓ)"," and he said: 'Other than Sharīk narrated it from Bayān from Qays from al-Mughīrah"," who said: We used to pray Ẓuhr during the midday heat"," and it was said to us: Delay the prayer"," for indeed the intensity of heat is from the exhaling of Jahannam.'\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿĪsā narrated it from ʿUmar ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Mujālid from his father from Bayān"," as al-Bukhārī stated."""
"2069","(2069) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Shaybān al-Baghdādī informed us, Muʿādh ibn Najdah informed us, Khallād ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Nāfiʿ, meaning al-Jumaḥī, narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb arrived in Makkah and heard the voice of Abū Maḥdhūrah, so he said: \Woe to him! How loud his voice is! Does he not fear that his throat will split?\"" He said: \""Then he came to him while he was giving the adhān for the prayer"," and he said: 'Woe to you! How loud your voice is! Do you not fear that your throat will split?' He said: 'I only raised my voice because of your arrival"," O Commander of the Faithful.' He said: 'You are in a hot land"," so delay for the people (until the heat lessens)"," then delay two or three times"," then give the adhān"," then come down and bow two rakʿahs"," then call your iqāmah.'\"" [Ḥasan for other than it. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 1854]"""
"2070","(2070) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Naṣr al-Dārabardī informed us in Marw, Abū al-Muwajjih informed us, ʿAbdān informed us, ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Khālid ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me, Ghālib al-Qaṭṭān narrated from Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the midday heat"," we would prostrate upon our garments as a protection against the heat.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Ghālib with different wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 517]"""
"2071","(2071) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us in Isfarāyin, that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Mūsā Abī al-ʿAlāʾ, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the Ẓuhr prayer during the winter days"," and we did not know whether more of the day had passed or what remained was greater.\""\n\nAnd in this narration"," if it is authentic"," there is an indication of the distinction between winter and summer in the timing of his (peace and blessings be upon him) prayer. The report of Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī is to be understood as referring to his delaying the prayer in extreme heat"," but he did not delay it to the extent of reaching its final time. Thus"," they would still feel the heat of the sands and the valley floor despite the delay. And Allah knows best. [Authenticated by others. Reported by Aḥmad 3/135]"""
"2072","(2072) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us, that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, that al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from what he read to Mālik. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā informed us, that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: \I read to Mālik"," from Ibn Shihāb"," from Anas ibn Mālik"," who said: 'We would perform the ʿAṣr prayer"," then a person would go to Qubāʾ and reach them while the sun was still high.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by al-Bukhārī 522]"""
"2073","(2073) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, that Qutaybah narrated to us, that al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Anas ibn Mālik, who informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the ʿAṣr prayer while the sun was white, high, and still alive (i.e., its heat was still felt), and a person would go to al-ʿAwālī while the sun was still high and alive.\\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ. And ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated it from al-Layth"," from Yūnus"," from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by al-Bukhārī 525]"""
"2074","(2074) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Naẓīf al-Miṣrī informed us in Makkah, that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Kharūf, Abū Kāmil al-Madanī, dictated to us in Egypt, that Aḥmad ibn Bukayr al-Ḥamrāwī narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ, the scribe of al-Layth, narrated to us, that al-Layth ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Yūnus, who informed me, and Ibn Shihāb informed me, that Anas ibn Mālik informed me: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the ʿAṣr prayer while the sun was high and alive (i.e."," its whiteness and brightness remained). A person would go to al-ʿAwālī while the sun was still high. And the distance of al-ʿAwālī from al-Madīnah is four miles or three.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: al-Layth added from Yūnus: \""And the distance of al-ʿAwālī is four miles or three.\"" [Ḥasan for others. Reported by al-Ṭabarānī in Musnad al-Shāmiyyīn 67]"""
"2075","(2075) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, that Abū al-Yamān informed us, that Shuʿayb narrated to us from al-Zuhrī, who said: \Anas ibn Mālik informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the ʿAṣr prayer while the sun was high and alive. A person would go to al-ʿAwālī and reach it while the sun was still high. And the distance of al-ʿAwālī from al-Madīnah is four miles.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and he said: \""Some of al-ʿAwālī are at a distance of four miles or thereabouts from al-Madīnah.\"" And this is from the statement of al-Zuhrī"," which Maʿmar mentioned from him as his own statement. [Reported by al-Bukhārī 525]"""
"2076","(2076) Abū Ṣāliḥ, the son of the daughter of Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, informed us of its authenticity, that my grandfather informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, that Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, who informed me, that Anas ibn Mālik informed me: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the ʿAṣr prayer"," and a person would go to al-ʿAwālī while the sun was still high.\""\n\nAl-Zuhrī said: \""And al-ʿAwālī are at a distance of two miles or three"," and I think he said: 'and four.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 405]"""
"2077","(2077) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir narrated to us, that my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr informed us, that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, that Jarīr narrated to us from Manṣūr, who said: \We discussed the matter of the sun being 'alive' (ḥayyah) before Khaythamah"," and the sun was white and bright. He said: 'Its being alive means that its heat is still felt.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Abū Dāwūd 406]"""
"2078","(2078) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, that ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk al-Bazzār narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, that al-Layth narrated to us from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Usāmah ibn Zayd, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah, who said: \Bashīr ibn Abī Masʿūd al-Anṣārī informed me"," from his father Abū Masʿūd"," who said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performing the Ẓuhr prayer when the sun had passed its meridian"," and he would sometimes delay it in extreme heat. And he would perform the ʒAṣr prayer while the sun was still high. A person"," upon finishing the prayer"," would travel to Dhū al-Ḥulayfah"," which is six miles from al-Madīnah"," before the setting of the sun.'\"" And he mentioned the rest of the hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2079","(2079) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, that Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us, that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Khuzāʿī informed us, that Abū al-Yamān al-Ḥakam ibn Nāfiʿ al-Ḥimṣī informed us in the year twenty-one and two hundred, that Abū Bishr Shuʿayb ibn Dīnār, Abū Ḥamzah al-Qurashī, narrated to me from Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī, who said: \I heard ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz during his caliphate"," and ʿUmar used to delay the prayer at that time. ʿUrwah said to him: 'Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah delayed the ʿAṣr prayer one day while he was the governor of al-Kūfah. Thereupon Abū Masʿd ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmr al-Anṣārī"," who was the grandfather of Zayd ibn al-Ḥasan on his mother's side and was among those who witnessed Badr"," came to him and said: \""What is this"," O Mughīrah? By Allah"," you certainly know that Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came down and prayed"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed"," then he prayed and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed—five prayers in all—then he said: 'Thus I was commanded.'\"" ʿUmar became alarmed when ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated this to him and said: \""Be careful what you narrate"," O ʿUrwah! Did Jibrīl indeed establish the times of prayer for them?\"" ʿUrwah replied: \""Thus would Bashīr ibn Abī Masʿūd narrate from his father.\""\n\nʿUrwah further said: \""And ʿĀʾishah informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the ʿAṣr prayer while the sun was still in her chamber"," before it appeared (i.e."," before the shadow appeared).\"" And ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz continued from that day to learn the timing of prayer by that sign until he departed this world. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2080","(2080) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah ibn Qaʿnab narrated to us, that Mālik narrated to us from Ibn Shihāb: \ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz delayed the prayer one day"," so ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr came to him and informed him that al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah had delayed the prayer one day while he was in al-Kūfah"," and Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī came to him and said: 'What is this"," O Mughīrah? Did you not know that Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came down and prayed"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed?'\"" And he mentioned the hadith in similar terms.\n\nʿUrwah said: \""And ʿĀʾishah"," the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the ʿAṣr prayer while the sun was in her chamber"," before it appeared (i.e."," before the shadow emerged).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān and from al-Qaʿnabī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik.\n\nYūnus and al-Layth said from al-Zuhrī: \""While the sun was in her chamber—the shadow had not yet appeared from her chamber.\""\n\nIbn ʿUyaynah said from al-Zuhrī: \""While the sun was rising in my chamber—the shadow had not yet appeared.\""\n\nHishām ibn ʿUrwah said from his father"," from ʿĀʾishah: \""While the sun had not yet emerged from her chamber.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: And Abū Usāmah said from Hishām: \""From the innermost part of her chamber.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2081","(2081) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Ibn Nājiyah narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated from Hishām from his father from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray ʿAṣr while the sun was still in the interior of my chamber.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 520]"""
"2082","(2082) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us, my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated it and said: \The sun was white"," shining in the interior of my chamber"," still high.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said after the ḥadīth of Mālik: \""This is among the clearest narrations reported regarding the beginning of the time"," because the chambers of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) were situated in a low-lying area of Madīnah and were not spacious"," and that is closer to the sun not having risen above them at the beginning of the time of ʿAṣr.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 520]"""
"2083","(2083) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Sawwād al-Sarḥī narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb that Mūsā ibn Saʿd al-Anṣārī narrated to him from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUbayd Allāh from Anas ibn Mālik that he said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed ʿAṣr with us. When he had finished"," a man from Banī Salamah came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we wish to slaughter a camel of ours"," and we would love for you to be present.' He said: 'Very well.' So he departed and we went with him. We found that the camel had not yet been slaughtered. It was then slaughtered"," then cut into pieces"," then some of it was cooked"," and we ate from it before the sun had set.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn Sawwād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 624]"""
"2084","(2084) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us, Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us, al-Awzāʿī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sūsī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to me, al-Awzāʿī narrated to me, Abū al-Najāshī narrated to me, Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj narrated to me, who said: \We would pray ʿAṣr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," then a camel would be slaughtered and divided into ten portions"," then it would be cooked"," and we would eat well-cooked meat before the sun had set.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf from al-Awzāʿī"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Mihrān al-Rāzī from al-Walīd ibn Muslim from al-Awzāʿī.\n\nThis authentic narration from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj indicates the error of what was narrated by ʦAbd al-Wāḥid or ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Nāfiʿ or Nufayʿ al-Kilābī from Ibn Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj from his father"," that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to command them to delay the ʿAṣr prayer. There is disagreement regarding his name and his father's name"," and there is disagreement regarding the name of Ibn Rāfiʿ; it is said his name was ʿAbd Allāh and it is also said ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: \""He is not to be followed in this","\"" and he cited as evidence against his error the ḥadīth of Abū al-Najāshī from Rāfiʿ. Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī said"," as Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us from him: \""This is a weak narration in its chain"," and the authentic narration from Rāfiʿ and others contradicts this.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 2353]"""
"2085","(2085) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah narrated from Mālik. He said: And Abū al-Ḥasan narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, he said: \I read to Mālik from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Anas ibn Mālik"," who said: 'We would pray ʿAṣr"," then a person would go out to Banī ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf and find them praying ʿAṣr.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. In the ḥadīth of al-Qaʿnabī it reads: \""then a person would go out.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī]"""
"2086","(2086) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī informed us in Baghdād, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated to us, Fulayḥ narrated from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that Anas ibn Mālik informed him: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray ʿAṣr at such a time that a camel could be slaughtered and we could distribute its portions before sunset"," and at such a time that a man could go to Banī Ḥārithah ibn al-Ḥārith and return before sunset.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in light of other narrations. Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā"," 4330]"""
"2087","(2087) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Bukhārī narrated to us, Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim and Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal both narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn ʿUthmān ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf narrated, saying:\n\n\I heard Abū Umāmah say: 'We prayed Ẓuhr with ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," then we went out until we came to Anas ibn Mālik. We found him praying ʿAṣr. I said: \""Uncle"," what is this prayer that you are praying?\"" He said: \""ʿAṣr"," and this is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that we used to pray with him.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil from ʿAbd Allāh"," and Muslim narrated it from Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 524]"""
"2088","(2088) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Bishr al-Marthadī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated: \He entered upon Anas ibn Mālik in his house in Baṣrah when he had finished Ẓuhr — he said: 'His house was adjacent to the mosque' — so when we entered upon him"," he said: 'Have you prayed ʿAṣr?' We said: 'We have only just finished Ẓuhr.' He said: 'Then pray ʿAṣr.' So we stood and prayed. When we had finished"," he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""That is the prayer of the hypocrite — he sits watching the sun until"," when it is between the two horns of Satan"," he stands and pecks it four times"," mentioning Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," in it only very little.\""'\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū al-Rabīʿ.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 622]"""
"2089","(2089) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that he said: \We entered upon Anas ibn Mālik after Ẓuhr"," and he stood to pray ʿAṣr. When he had finished his prayer"," we mentioned hastening the prayer"," or he mentioned it himself"," and he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""That is the prayer of the hypocrites"," that is the prayer of the hypocrites"," that is the prayer of the hypocrites. One of them sits until"," when the sun turns yellow and is between the two horns of Satan or upon the two horns of Satan"," he stands and pecks four times"," mentioning Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," in it only very little.\""'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 413]"""
"2090","(2090) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq informed us in Baghdād, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ayyūb al-Bazzāz narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us, Muslim narrated. And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us, Abū Qilābah narrated to us, Abū al-Malīḥ narrated: \We were with Buraydah on a military expedition on a day of overcast skies. He said: 'Pray ʿAṣr early"," for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Whoever abandons the ʿAṣr prayer"," his deeds are rendered void.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm. Al-Awzāʿī contradicted him in both its chain and its text. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 569]"""
"2091","(2091) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us in Naysābūr, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUmar ibn Burhān al-Ghazzāl and Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān and others in Baghdad — they said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah informed us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī narrated from al-Awzāʿī; from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr; from Abū Qilābah; from Abū al-Muhājir; from Buraydah al-Aslamī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was on one of his military expeditions and said: \Perform the prayer early on a cloudy day"," for whoever misses the ʿAṣr prayer"," his deeds are rendered void.\""\n\n[Shādh. Narrated by Aḥmad 5/361]"""
"2092","(2092) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah narrated from Mālik. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: I read to Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \He who misses the ʿAṣr prayer is as though his family and his wealth were plundered.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 527]"""
"2093","(2093) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb informed us; Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī; from Sālim; from his father, reaching the Prophet (ﷺ), regarding the one who misses the ʿAṣr prayer: \It is as though his family and his wealth were plundered.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 527]"""
"2094","(2094) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs said: I heard ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī say: I heard ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī say regarding the ḥadīth of Sufyān from al-Zuhrī from Sālim from his father from the Prophet (ﷺ): \Whoever misses the ʿAṣr prayer"," it is as though his family and his wealth were plundered.\""\n\nʿAlī said: I said to Sufyān: \""Indeed Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrates it with a chain going back to Nawfal ibn Muʿāwiyah"," who heard the Prophet (ﷺ).\"" He said: \""I heard it from him"," and my heart retained it"," and I memorized it just as you are here narrating from Sālim from his father.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr al-Nāqid from Sufyān"," and he also narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī likewise. Similarly"," Maʿmar and Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated it from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 527]"""
"2095","(2095) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Abī Fudayk informed me; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Ibn Shihāb; from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām; from Nawfal ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Dīlī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever a prayer eludes"," it is as though his family and his wealth were plundered.\""\n\nIbn Shihāb said: I said: \""O Abū Bakr"," do you know which prayer it is?\"" Ibn Shihāb said: \""It has reached me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever misses the ʿAṣr prayer"," it is as though his family and his wealth were plundered.'\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"," and he said at its end: al-Zuhrī said: \""I mentioned that to Sālim"," and he said: 'My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Whoever abandons the ʿAṣr prayer…'\""\n\nṢāliḥ ibn Kaysān narrated it from Ibn Shihāb from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muṭīʿ ibn al-Aswad from Nawfal ibn Muʿāwiyah"," similar to the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding the tribulations"," except that Abū Bakr added in it: \""And among the prayers is a prayer — whoever misses it"," it is as though his family and his wealth were plundered.\"" It is recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs"," and the ḥadīth is preserved from both of them. ʿIrbāk ibn Mālik narrated it from both of them together — from Nawfal ibn Muʿāwiyah and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar — either as a balāgh or from direct hearing. [Narrated by Aḥmad 5/429]"""
"2096","(2096) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah said: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najīd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Ibn Bukayr informed us; Mālik narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī: \Perform the ʿAṣr prayer while the sun is white and clear"," to the extent that a rider may travel three farsakhs"," and perform the ʿIshāʾ prayer between you and the third of the night. If you delay it"," then up to the half of the night"," and do not be among the heedless.\""\n\nHe said: And Mālik narrated to us from Nāfiʿ"," the freedman of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to his governors: \""The most important of your affairs to me is the prayer. Whoever preserves it or guards over it has preserved his religion"," and whoever neglects it is even more neglectful of everything else.\"" Then he wrote: \""Perform the Ẓuhr prayer when the shadow is one cubit until the shadow of everything is equal to it; and the ʿAṣr prayer while the sun is white and clear"," to the extent that a rider may travel two or three farsakhs; and the Maghrib prayer when the sun sets; and the ʿIshāʾ prayer when the twilight disappears"," up to the third of the night. Whoever sleeps"," may his eye not sleep — whoever sleeps"," may his eye not sleep — whoever sleeps"," may his eye not sleep. And the Fajr prayer while the stars are visible and intermingled. Whoever sleeps"," may his eye not sleep.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Mālik 8]"""
"2097","(2097) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Ziyād ibn Lāḥiq, who said: Tāmiʿah bint Salamah narrated to me that she came to ʿĀʾishah with some women from the people of Kūfah and said: \O Mother of the Believers"," we ask you about the timings of the prayers.\"" She said: \""Sit down.\"" So we sat. When the time they call \""half of the day\"" arrived"," she stood and led us in prayer"," standing in the middle of us. When we finished"," I said to her: \""O Mother of the Believers"," we call this 'half of the day' in our land.\"" She said: \""This is the prayer of the family of Muḥammad (ﷺ).\"" Then we sat"," and when the time they call \""between the two prayers\"" arrived"," she led us in the ʿAṣr prayer. We said to her: \""O Mother of the Believers"," we call this 'between the two prayers' in our land.\"" She said: \""This is the prayer of the family of Muḥammad (ﷺ). Indeed"," the family of Muḥammad do not pray when the sun turns yellow.\"" Then we sat"," and had it been other than ʿĀʾishah"," we would have thought she had prayed the Maghrib before its time came. But I knew that ʿĀʾishah would not pray except at the time when it became due"," and she recited aloud in the Maghrib prayer. Some women from the people of Shām sought permission to enter upon her"," and she said: \""Do not give them permission — they are the companions of the bathhouses.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2098","(2098) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim informed us; Wakīʿ informed us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah; from Ḥakīm ibn ʿAbbād ibn Ḥunayf; from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim; from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Jibrīl (peace be upon him) led me in prayer at the House twice.\"" He then mentioned the entire ḥadīth"," stating that each prayer has two times"," and regarding the Maghrib on both days he said: \""He led me in the Maghrib prayer when the fasting person breaks his fast.\"" [Ḥasan in meaning; its takhrij was given previously in ḥadīth 1702]"""
"2099","(2099) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb the Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ḥāmid ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqrīʾ informed us; Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd narrated. And Abū Saʿd al-Zāhid informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us. And Abū Ṣāliḥ, the son of the daughter of Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, informed us; my grandfather informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī informed us; Ḥātim, meaning Ibn Ismāʿīl, narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd; from Salamah ibn al-Akwʿ, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray the Maghrib when the sun set and disappeared behind the veil.\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Abū Ṣāliḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm, and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ; its takhrij was given in ḥadīth 1727]"
"2100","(2100) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf informed us; Abū al-Mughīrah informed us; al-Awzāʿī narrated.\n\nAnd Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed me; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Shuʿayb ibn Isḥāq al-Dimashqī informed us; al-Awzāʿī informed me; Abū al-Najāshī informed me; Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj narrated to me, who said: We used to pray the Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and one of us would depart and still be able to see where his arrows had fallen.\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Abū Ṣāliḥ. Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Walīd ibn Muslim from al-Awzāʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ; its takhrij was given previously in ḥadīth 1725]"
"2101","(2101) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Khusrawajirdī in Khusrawjird informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated to us; Thābit narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \We would pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," then we would shoot arrows"," and one of us could see the place where his arrow landed.\""\n\nGharīb with this isnād. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2102","(2102) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Sarī narrated to us; Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq narrated from al-Walīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Sumayrah, who said: Abū Ṭarīf narrated to me that he was present with the Prophet ﷺ when he was besieging the people of al-Ṭāʾif. He said: \He would pray with us Ṣalāt al-Baṣr"," such that if a person shot his arrows"," he could see where his arrows landed.\""\n\nAbū Jaʿfar al-Ḥulwānī expressed doubt regarding some of its wordings"," and the ḥadīth is preserved from Yaḥyā and others from Bishr with this wording.\n\nṢalāt al-Baṣr refers to Ṣalāt al-Maghrib. It was called Ṣalāt al-Baṣr because it is performed before the darkness of night.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ for other than itself. Aḥmad narrated it"," 3/416]"""
"2103","(2103) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; al-Kudaymī narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn ʿAqīl al-Hilālī narrated to us; Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq narrated from al-Walīd ibn Abī Sumayrah from Abū Ṭarīf al-Hudhalī, who said: \We besieged the fortress of al-Ṭāʾif with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he would pray Maghrib with us"," and one of us could see where his arrows landed.\""\n\nṢaḥīḥ for other than itself. Aḥmad [3/416]"""
"2104","(2104) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Madīnī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to me; al-Aʿmash narrated from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr from Abū ʿAṭiyyah al-Wādiʿī, who said: \I entered upon ʿĀʾishah"," the Mother of the Believers"," along with Masrūq. Masrūq said to her: 'Two men from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ—neither of them falling short in the pursuit of good—one of them hastens Maghrib and hastens ifṭār"," and the other delays Maghrib and delays ifṭār.' She said: 'Which of them is the one who hastens Maghrib and hastens ifṭār?' He said: 'Ibn Masʿūd.' She said: 'Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ use to do.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb from Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 1099]"""
"2105","(2105) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from Burayd from Abū Burdah, who said: \I came from al-Jabbānah and passed through Juʿfiyy"," saying: 'Now the sun has set.' I passed by Suwayd ibn Ghafalah near their mosque and said: 'Have you prayed?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'I see that you have hastened.' He said: 'ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb used to pray it at this time.'\""\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"2106","(2106) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Yūnus, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, and Mālik ibn Anas informed me from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf informed me that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān would pray Ṣalāt al-Maghrib when they would look at the blackness of night, before breaking their fast, and then they would break their fast after the prayer.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it, 636]"
"2107","(2107) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; al-Asfaṭī informed us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Abī Isḥāq from al-Aswad, who said: \ʿAbd Allāh would pray Maghrib when the sun set"," and he would say: 'By the One besides whom there is no deity"," this is the time of this prayer.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 2/395]"""
"2108","(2108) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdad narrated to us by dictiction in the Mosque of al-Manṣūr; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Najjād narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to me; Hārūn—that is, Ibn Maʿrūf—narrated to me. ʿAbd Allāh said: \I heard it myself from Hārūn.\"" He said: Ibn Wahb informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Aswad al-Qurashī narrated to me that Yazīd ibn Khuṣayfah narrated to him from al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'My Ummah will remain upon the fiṭrah so long as they pray Maghrib before the stars appear.'\""\n\n[Ḥasan for other than itself. Aḥmad narrated it"," 3/449]"""
"2109","(2109) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā al-Farrāʾ narrated to us; ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from ʿUmar ibn Ibrāhīm from Maʿmar from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan from al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays from al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'My Ummah will remain upon the fiṭrah so long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars become intermingled.'\n\nWe have narrated previously the ḥadīth of Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī, and it has also been narrated from the ḥadīth of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and Anas ibn Mālik. Some of those who delay Maghrib have used as evidence…\n\n[Ḥasan for other than itself. Abū Dāwūd narrated it, 418]"
"2110","(2110) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīb ibn Milḥān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to me; Khayr ibn Nuʿaym al-Ḥaḍramī informed me from Ibn Hubayrah al-Sabāʾī from Abī Tamīm al-Jayshānī from Abū Baṣrah al-Ghifārī, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed ʿAṣr with us at al-Mukhammiṣ"," and he said: 'This prayer was presented to those who came before you"," and they neglected it. Whoever upholds it shall be given his reward twice"," and there is no prayer after it until the witness rises.'\""\n\nIbn Bukayr said: \""I asked al-Layth about 'the witness' and he said: 'It is the star.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth.\n\nIt is not permissible to abandon the well-known authentic aḥādīth on account of this. The purpose of this ḥadīth is not to define the time of Maghrib; rather"," the intent is the negation of voluntary prayers after ʿAṣr.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," 292]"""
"2111","(2111) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us that Abu al-Muthanna narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Abu 'Awanah narrated from Abu Bishr, from Bashir ibn Thabit, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: \I am the most knowledgeable of people regarding the time of prayer — the prayer of al-'Isha'. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform it at the setting of the moon on the third night.\""\n\nAnd all that has been narrated regarding the general hastening of prayers has already been mentioned. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi"," 165.]"""
"2112","(2112) And 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn Bishran informed us that Abu Ja'far 'Amr al-Razzaz narrated to us that Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydillah ibn al-Munadi narrated to us that Ruh ibn 'Abadah narrated. And Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Isma'il al-Tabarani narrated to us therein that 'Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Sa'igh narrated to us that Ruh narrated to us that Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us that 'Ali ibn Zayd narrated from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed al-'Isha' for nine nights until one-third of the night had passed. Then Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," if you were to hasten this prayer"," it would be more suitable for our night prayer.'\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Ibn al-Munadi"," it reads: \""it would be more suitable for our standing in prayer at night.\"" Then he hastened it after that. This was narrated uniquely by 'Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an"," and he is not strong (in hadith). [Da'if. Narrated by Ahmad"," 5/42.]"""
"2113","(2113) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us that Abu Dawud narrated to us that Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us that Shu'bah narrated from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, who said: \We asked Jabir about the prayer times of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he said: 'He used to pray al-Zuhr at midday"," and al-'Asr while the sun was still bright"," and al-Maghrib when the sun had set"," and al-'Isha' — when the people were many he would hasten it"," and when they were few he would delay it"," and al-Subh in the pre-dawn darkness.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Muslim ibn Ibrahim"," and Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it through another chain from Shu'bah. [Its grading has preceded in hadith 2044.]"""
"2114","(2114) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu 'Amr ibn Isma'il narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Abi Hafs narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Rafi' narrated to us that 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us that Ibn Jurayj said: \I said to 'Ata': 'Which time do you prefer for me to pray al-'Isha' — which the people call al-'Atamah — whether as an imam or alone?' He said: 'I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: \""The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) delayed al-'Isha' one night until the people fell asleep and then woke up"," and fell asleep again and woke up. Then 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and said: 'The prayer!' 'Ata' said: Ibn 'Abbas said: 'Then the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) came out — and I can almost see him now — with water dripping from his head"," his hand placed on the side of his head"," and he said: 'Were it not that I would burden my Ummah"," I would command them to pray it at this time.'\""'\""\n\nHe said: \""I asked 'Ata' to confirm how the Prophet (ﷺ) had placed his hand on his head"," as Ibn 'Abbas had informed him. So 'Ata' spread his fingers somewhat apart"," then placed the tips of his fingers on the crown of the head"," then drew them together"," moving them thus over the head until his thumb touched the edge of the ear nearest the face"," then along the temple and the side of the jaw — neither shortening nor doing more than that.\""\n\nI said to 'Ata': \""How long did the Prophet (ﷺ) delay it that night?\"" He said: \""I do not know.\"" 'Ata' said: \""I prefer that you pray it — whether as an imam or alone — delayed"," as the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed it that night. But if that is difficult for you alone or for the people in congregation"," and you are their imam"," then pray it at a moderate time — neither hastened nor delayed.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi'"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from Mahmud from 'Abd al-Razzaq. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 454.]"""
"2115","(2115) Abu Muhammad 'Abdillah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkari informed us in Baghdad that Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us that Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us that 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us that Ibn Jurayj informed us that Nafi' narrated to us that 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar informed us that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) was occupied from prayer one night, and he did not come out until we fell asleep, then woke up, then fell asleep again, then woke up. Then he came out to us and said: \There is no one among the people of the earth awaiting this prayer other than you.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Mahmud"," and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi'"," both from 'Abd al-Razzaq. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 454.]"""
"2116","(2116) And Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir al-'Anbari informed us that my grandfather Yahya ibn Mansur narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us that Jarir narrated from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from al-Hakam ibn 'Utbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \We waited one night for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for al-'Isha' al-Akhirah. He came out to us when one-third of the night had passed or after that. When he came out"," he said: 'You are awaiting a prayer that no people of any religion other than you are awaiting. Were it not that it would be burdensome upon my Ummah"," I would have prayed it with them at this hour.' Then he commanded the mu'adhdhin"," who gave the iqamah"," and then he prayed.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 639.]"""
"2117","(2117) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sadiq ibn Abi al-Fawaris both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us that Hajjaj said: Ibn Jurayj said. And Abu Muhammad 'Abdillah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkari informed us in Baghdad that Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us that Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us that 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us that Ibn Jurayj informed us that Mughirah ibn Hakim narrated from Umm Kulthum ibn Abi Bakr, who informed him from 'A'ishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed al-'Isha' one night until most of the night had passed and the people of the mosque had fallen asleep. Then he came out to them and prayed with them"," and said: 'Indeed"," this is its time"," were it not that I would burden my Ummah.'\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of 'Abd al-Razzaq. In the hadith of Hajjaj from 'A'ishah"," Mother of the Believers"," she said"," and he did not mention \""al-'Isha'.\"" The rest is the same in meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Harun ibn 'Abdillah from Hajjaj"," and from Muhammad ibn Rafi' and others from 'Abd al-Razzaq. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 638.]"""
"2118","(2118) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us that Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq informed us that Abu al-Muthanna narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Yahya narrated to us that 'Awf narrated to us that Abu al-Minhal narrated to us, saying: \I went with my father to Abu Barzah al-Aslami"," and my father said to him: 'Tell us how the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray the obligatory prayers.' He said: 'He used to pray al-Hajir — which you call the first prayer — when the sun declined"," and he would pray al-'Asr"," then one of us would return to his family at the farthest end of Madinah while the sun was still bright. I have forgotten what he said about al-Maghrib.' He said: 'And he used to prefer to delay al-'Isha'. And he used to dislike sleeping before it and conversation after it. And he would finish the prayer of al-Ghadah when one of us could recognize the one sitting next to him"," and he would recite from sixty to a hundred verses.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Abu al-Minhal. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 516.]"""
"2119","(2119) Abu al-Hasan 'Ala' ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sa'id al-Mihrajani informed us therein that Abu Sahl Bishr ibn Ahmad ibn Bishr narrated to us that Ibrahim ibn 'Ali al-Dhuhli narrated to us that Yahya ibn Yahya informed us that Abu al-Ahwas narrated from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) used to delay the prayer of al-'Isha' al-Akhirah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya and others. [Hasan. Narrated by Muslim"," 643.]"""
"2120","(21120) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us that 'Ali ibn 'Asim informed us that Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed the prayer of al-'Isha' al-Akhirah until close to half the night. Then he came out and prayed with them"," and said: 'You will remain in prayer as long as you wait for it"," were it not for the frailty of the elderly and the weakness of the weak.' And I think he said: 'and the one in need — I would have delayed this prayer until half the night.'\""\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated by Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal"," Ibn Abi 'Adi"," al-Warith"," and others from Dawud. And Abu Mu'awiyah narrated it from Dawud"," but he said \""from Jabir\"" instead of \""from Abu Sa'id.\"" [Sahih. Its grading has preceded in hadith 1758.]"""
"2121","(2121) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān informed us: Ḥarīz ibn ʿUthmān al-Raḥabī informed us, from Rāshid ibn Saʿd, from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḥumayd al-Sakūnī, the companion of Muʿādh ibn Jabal, from Muʿādh, who said:\n\n\We waited one night for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for the ʿAtamah prayer (i.e."," ʿIshāʾ)"," and he delayed it until the one who speculated thought that he had already prayed or that he would not come out. Then he came out after that"," and someone said to him: 'O Prophet of Allah"," we thought you had already prayed"," O Prophet of Allah"," or that you would not come out.' He (ﷺ) said to us: 'Delay this prayer (i.e."," pray ʿIshāʾ late)"," for you have been given preference over all other nations through it"," and no nation before you ever prayed it.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 5/237]"""
"2122","(2122) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Yazīd: He heard Ibn ʿAbbās expressing his preference for delaying the ʿIshāʾ prayer, and he would recite: {And in the hours of the night} [Ḥūd 114].\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Tafsīr al-Ṭabarī 7/124]"
"2123","(2123) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Sufyān narrated from ʿAwf al-Aʿrābī, from Abū al-Minhāl, from Abū Barzah, from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said:\n\n\I dislike sleeping before it and conversing after it\"" — meaning the ʿIshāʾ prayer.\n\n[Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it as mentioned previously. Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 516]"""
"2124","(2124) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us: Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṭāʾifī narrated to me, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never slept before it (ʿIshāʾ) and never engaged in conversation after it.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 702]"""
"2125","(2125) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Muʿāwiyah, who is Ibn Ṣāliḥ, narrated from Abū Ḥamzah, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), who said:\n\n\I never saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sleeping before ʿIshāʾ or engaging in idle talk after it. He would either be in remembrance (of Allah)"," thereby gaining reward"," or he would be sleeping"," thereby being at peace.\""\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā 4878]"""
"2126","(2126) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Ibn Fuḍayl narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) disapproved of conversing after the ʿAtamah prayer (i.e."," ʿIshāʾ).\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 6678]"""
"2127","(2127) Abū Muḥammad Junāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Junāḥ al-Muḥāribī informed us in Kūfah: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghurzah informed us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr, from Khaythamah, from one who heard Ibn Masʿūd say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\There is no conversation after the prayer except for one who has just prayed or a traveler.\""\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/379]"""
"2128","(2128) Junāḥ informed us: Ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr, from Khaythamah, from a man of the Juʿfī tribe, who heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\There is no conversation after the prayer except for one who has just prayed or a traveler.\""\n\nḤammād ibn Shuʿayb narrated it from Manṣūr"," from Khaythamah"," from al-Aswad"," from ʿAbdullāh"," but he erred in it. And it is also said: from ʿAlqamah"," from ʿAbdullāh"," and that is also an error.\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. See the preceding narration]"""
"2129","(2129) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, who said:\n\n\A man came to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was at ʿArafah and said: 'O Commander of the Faithful"," I have come from Kūfah"," and I left behind a man there who dictates the muṣḥaf from memory.'\""\n\nHe said: \""ʿUmar became angry and swelled with rage until he nearly filled the space between the two branches of the saddle. Then he said: 'Woe to you! Who is he?' He said: 'ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd.' Then ʿUmar's anger subsided and he calmed down until he returned to his previous state. Then he said: 'Woe to you! By Allah"," I do not know anyone among the Muslims who has more right to that than him. I will tell you about that. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to remain in conversation about the affairs of the Muslims at the house of Abū Bakr"," and he remained in conversation with him one night"," and I was with him. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out"," and we went out walking with him. Suddenly"," there was a man standing praying in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood listening to his recitation. When we were about to recognize the man"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever would like to recite the Qurʾān fresh as it was revealed"," let him recite it according to the recibration of Ibn Umm ʿAbd (i.e."," ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd).' Then the man sat down supplicating"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began saying to him: 'Ask"," and it will be given to you.'\""\n\nHe said: \""Then ʿUmar said: 'I said: I will go to him in the morning and give him the glad tidings.' So I went to him in the morning to give him the glad tidings"," but I found that Abū Bakr had preceded me to him and had already given him the glad tidings. By Allah"," I have never raced Abū Bakr to any good except that he beat me to it.\""\n\nA group narrated it from al-Aʿmash"," and in this narration is evidence that the report of the post-prayer conversation (al-samar) is from ʿUmar"," not from ʿAbdullāh"," in the narration of ʿAlqamah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/25]"""
"2130","(2130) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, who said:\n\n\A man came to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: 'I have come to you from a man who dictates the muṣḥaf from memory.' He mentioned part of the hadith"," then ʿUmar said: 'I will tell you about ʿAbdullāh. We spent a night in the house of Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) concerning some need of the Prophet (ﷺ).'\"" Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith with the same meaning.\n\nAt the end of it"," Muḥammad al-ʿAṭṭār said to al-Aʿmash: \""Did not Khaythamah say that the name of the man was Qays ibn Marwān?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He meant the man who had come to ʿUmar.\n\nThis hadith was not heard by ʿAlqamah ibn Qays directly from ʿUmar; rather"," he narrated it from al-Qarthaʿ"," from Qays"," from ʿUmar.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/25]"""
"2131","(2131) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us that ʿAffān informed us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh informed us that Ibrāhīm informed us that ʿAlqamah informed us that al-Qurthaʿ informed us that Qays — or Ibn Qays — a man from Juʿfī, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by while I was with him, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd was reciting. Then he mentioned the story with its meaning, except that he did not mention the account of the evening conversation. [Ḥasan]"
"2132","(2132) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Hishām informed us that Qatādah informed us that al-Ḥasan informed us that ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and he spoke at length with us. Then we returned to our families. When we awoke in the morning, we went early to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The prophets were shown to me with their nations and their followers from among their nations.\"" Then he mentioned the hadith in its entirety. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it (15/420).]"""
"2133","(2133) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that informed me Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī, who said: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us that Abū al-Yamān informed us that Shuʿayb informed us that al-Zuhrī informed me that Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Ḥathmah informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the ʿIshāʾ prayer in the final part of his life. When he gave the salām, he stood and said: \Have you considered your night? Upon the completion of one hundred years from this night"," no one who is upon the surface of the earth today will remain.\""\n\nʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: The people were confused by the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," leading them to speak about these hadiths concerning one hundred years. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ only said: \""No one who is upon the surface of the earth today will remain.\"" By this he meant that it would bring that century to an end.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (116).]"""
"2134","(2134) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us that al-Layth informed us that ʿUqayl informed us that Ibn Shihāb said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, informed him that she had informed him that women from among the believing women used to attend the Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, wrapped in their outer garments. Then they would return to their homes after completing the prayer, and no one would recognize them due to the darkness.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (365).]"
"2135","(2135) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us — and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, both saying: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Sufyān informed us that al-Zuhrī informed us that ʿUrwah informed us that ʿĀʾishah said: Women from among the believing women used to pray the Ṣubḥ prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, wrapped in their outer garments. Then they would return to their families, and no one would recognize them.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others, from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (365).]"
"2136","(2136) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāh al-Muzakkī and others informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik informed us — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah informed us that Mālik informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us that ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us that ʿĀʾishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray the Ṣubḥ prayer, and the women would depart wrapped in their outer garments, unrecognizable due to the darkness.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf, and Muslim narrated it from Naṣr ibn ʿAlī from Maʿn, both from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding narration.]"
"2137","(2137) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us — dictating — that Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Naysābūrī informed us that Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Waḥāẓī informed us that Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim informed us that al-Qāsim informed us that ʿĀʾishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray the Ṣubḥ prayer, and the women of the believers would depart wrapped in their outer garments, unrecognizable due to the darkness.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Mūsā from Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr from Fulayḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Same meaning as previously.]"
"2138","(2138) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us that Ḥabbān informed us that Ibn al-Mubārak informed us that ʿAwf informed us that Sayyār ibn Salāmah said: I and my father entered upon Abū Barzah al-Aslamī, and my father said to him: \Inform us about how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray the obligatory prayers.\"" Then he mentioned the hadith"," saying: \""And he would conclude the morning prayer when a man would recognize the one sitting beside him"," and he would recite sixty to one hundred verses.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Abū al-Minhāl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (522).]"""
"2139","(2139) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqriʾ in Baghdad informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad informed us that Wahb ibn Jarīr and ʿAbd al-Ṣamad informed us, both saying: Shuʿbah informed us that Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥasan said: Al-Ḥajjāj used to delay the prayers. So I asked Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, and he said: \The Prophet ﷺ would pray the Ẓuhr when the sun had passed its meridian"," and the ʿAṣr while the sun was still bright"," and the Maghrib when the sun had set"," and the ʿIshāʾ — if he saw that the people were few"," he would delay it"," and if he saw that they were many"," he would hasten it — and the Ṣubḥ in the darkness.\""\n\nExtracted in the two Ṣaḥīḥ collections from the hadith of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its extraction preceded in hadith 2044.]"""
"2140","(2140) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that al-Layth informed us that Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb informed us that Usāmah ibn Zayd informed us that Ibn Shihāb informed us that ʿUrwah informed me that Bashīr ibn Abī Masʿūd informed me, from Abū Masʿūd, from the Prophet ﷺ. Then he mentioned the hadith and said in it: \Then he prayed the Ṣubḥ in the darkness"," then one day he prayed it when it was quite bright (asfara)"," and he never returned to praying it bright until Allah"," the Almighty and Exalted"," took him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Its extraction preceded in hadith 1701.]"""
"2141","(2141) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bazzār in Ṭabarānā informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭūsī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us: Rūḥ narrated — and Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Dūrī informed me: Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAṭāʾ al-Muqriʾ al-Jallāb narrated to us: Rūḥ narrated to us: Saʿīd, meaning Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, narrated from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and Zayd ibn Thābit took the pre-dawn meal (suḥūr). When they finished their suḥūr, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up for the prayer and prayed. I said to Anas: \How much time was there between their finishing the suḥūr and their entering the prayer?\"" He said: \""The amount of time in which a man recites fifty verses.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ"," from Rūḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 550.]"""
"2142","(2142) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā narrated to us: al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Hammām narrated from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, that Zayd ibn Thābit narrated to him: \I took the pre-dawn meal with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" He said: \""Then I went out to the prayer.\"" Anas said: \""So I said to Zayd: 'How much time was there between that?'\"" He said: \""The amount of fifty or sixty verses.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn ʿĀṣim"," from Hammām"," except that he said"," on the authority of Zayd: \""They took the pre-dawn meal with the Prophet (ﷺ)"," then they stood up for the prayer.\""\n\nAnd Muslim narrated it from ʿAmr al-Nāqid"," from Yazīd ibn Hārūn"," from Hammām"," with the same meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""
"2143","(2143) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to me: my brother Abū Bakr narrated from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, from Abū Ḥāzim, that he heard Sahl ibn Saʿd say: \I used to take the pre-dawn meal with my family"," then I would hasten quickly so as to catch the Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 552.]"""
"2144","(2144) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed me: my father informed me. He said: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: Nuhīk ibn Yarīm narrated to me: Mughīth ibn Sumayy narrated to me, saying: \I prayed the Fajr prayer with Ibn al-Zubayr. He prayed it in the darkness of dawn (ghalas)"," and he used to make it bright (yusfir) with it. When he gave the salām"," I said to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar — who was beside me — 'What is this prayer?' He said: 'This is our prayer with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," Abū Bakr"," and ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with them both. Then when ʿUmar was killed"," ʿUthmān made it bright (asfara) with it.'\""\n\nAnd in the Kitāb al-ʿIlal of Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī"," he said: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: \""The hadith of al-Awzāʿī from Nuhīk ibn Yarīm regarding praying Fajr in darkness (al-taghlīs) is a ḥasan hadith.\"" [Ḥasan. Abū Yaʿlā narrated it"," no. 5747.]"""
"2145","(2145) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Muslim ibn Jundub, from al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAmr al-Hudhalī, that ʿUmar wrote to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī: \I am writing to you regarding the prayer"," and it is the most deserving of what the Muslims uphold of their religion. You have seen the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and how he used to pray. You have preserved of that what you have preserved and forgotten of that what you have forgotten. He prayed Ẓuhr at midday (hājirah)"," and he prayed ʿAṣr while the sun was still alive (bright)"," and he prayed Maghrib when the fasting person breaks his fast"," and he prayed ʿIshāʾ so long as the people's sleeping was not feared"," and he prayed Fajr in the darkness of dawn (ghalas)"," and he lengthened the recitation in it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in meaning through other chains. Its grading has been discussed many times; see no. 2096.]"""
"2146","(2146) And Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Khaṭīb al-Isfarāʾinī informed us: Abū Baḥr al-Barbarī narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated from Manṣūr ibn Ḥayyān al-Asadī. He said: I heard ʿAmr ibn Maymūn al-Awdī say: \I prayed the Fajr prayer with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb at such a time that if my son were at a distance of three cubits from me"," I would not recognize him unless he spoke.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it"," no. 3236.]"""
"2147","(2147) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated. He said: al-Shāfiʿī said: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Shabīb ibn Gharaqadah, from Ḥibbān ibn al-Ḥārith, who said: \I came to ʿAlī while he was at a camp at the monastery of Abū Mūsā"," and I found him eating. He said: 'Come near and eat.' I said: 'I intend to fast.' He said: 'And I intend it.' So I drew near and ate. When he finished"," he said: 'O son of al-Nabbāḥ"," establish the prayer!'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it"," no. 7609.]"""
"2148","(2148) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us: Abū Muḥammad Dalaj ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Ḥafṣ, the maternal uncle of al-Nufaylī, narrated. He said: We recited to Maʿqil ibn ʿUbaydillāh, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Abī ʿUbaydah, from Ibn Masʿūd, who said: \He used to lead us in the Fajr prayer when the dawn rises"," and the Maghrib prayer when the sun sets"," then he would say: 'This is our prayer with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).'\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Farāfiṣah ibn ʿUmayr that he said: \""I did not learn Sūrat Yūsuf except from ʿUthmān's recitation of it in the Fajr prayer"," due to how frequently he used to repeat it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"2149","(2149) Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd and Rabīʿah that al-Farāfiṣah ibn ʿUmayr said — then he mentioned it. (Q) And that indicates that he used to enter into it while it was still dark (mughallisān)."
"2150","(2150) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Sālim, meaning Ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, from Thawbān, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Be steadfast"," though you will not enumerate [all good deeds]. And know that the best of your deeds is the prayer"," and none maintains wuḍūʾ except a believer.\""\n\nAbū Kabshah al-Salūlī followed it up from Thawbān"," and al-Layth narrated it from Mujāhid"," from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr"," from the Prophet (ﷺ). And it has been narrated from Abī Ummāmah"," raising it (to the Prophet).\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""The prayer offered at the beginning of its time is among the highest of the deeds of the children of Ādam.\"" He then mentioned the previously cited hadith from the Prophet (ﷺ) when he was asked: \""Which deed is best?\"" He said: \""The prayer at the beginning of its time.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in meaning through other chains. Ibn Mājah narrated it"," no. 277.]"""
"2151","(2151) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah from Maḥmūd ibn Labīd from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Perform the Fajr prayer in brightness (isfār)"," for it carries the greatest reward.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than him. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it (154).]"""
"2152","(2152) Abū Usāmah Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim al-Muqrʾ al-Harawī informed us in Makkah: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Naqqāsh informed us: Abū Yaʿlā al-Mawṣilī informed us: ʿAmr al-Nāqid informed us: Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī informed us: Sufyān informed us from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Fajr (dawn) is two dawns: a dawn in which food becomes forbidden and prayer becomes permissible"," and a dawn in which food becomes permissible and prayer becomes forbidden.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than him. Its takhrīj has preceded in hadith 1767.]"""
"2153","(2153) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd informed us from Qatādah from Anas ibn Mālik: that Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with him) led them in the Subh (Fajr) prayer during the night (before its time), so he repeated the prayer with them, then he prayed with them again and repeated the prayer with them three times. (T) And something similar has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīgh]"
"2154","(2154) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqrʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us: Shuʿbah informed us from ʿAmr, meaning Ibn Abī Ḥakīm, from al-Zibriqān from ʿUrwah from Zayd ibn Thābit: that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray al-Hajīr or al-Hājira (the midday heat), and it was the heaviest of prayers upon his Companions. Then the verse was revealed: \Guard strictly your prayers"," and the middle prayer"," and stand before Allah in devout obedience\"" [al-Baqarah: 238]. He said: \""Because there are two prayers before it and two prayers after it.\"" And Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar Ghundar and ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith similarly narrated it from Shuʿbah"," and they both said in the hadith: \""al-Ẓuhr (the noon prayer) at al-Hājira.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (411).]"""
"2155","(2155) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us from al-Zibriqān from Zuhrah, who said: We were sitting with Zayd ibn Thābit when they sent to Usāmah ibn Zayd and asked him about the middle prayer. He said: \It is al-Ẓuhr (the noon prayer). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray it at al-Hajīr (the intense midday heat).\"" And someone other than him narrated it from Abū Dāwūd and added therein: \""He said"," meaning Zayd: 'It is al-Ẓuhr.' So they sent to Usāmah.\"" And someone other than him narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb from al-Zibriqān ibn ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī from Zayd ibn Thābit and Usāmah"," similarly. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Nasāʾī narrated it in al-Kubrā (361).]"""
"2156","(2156) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Baṣrī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd informed us: Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ informed us: Abū ʿAqīl Zuhrah ibn Maʿbad informed us that Ibn al-Musayyab narrated to him: that he was sitting with ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr and Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭalḥah when Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab said: \I heard Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī say: 'The middle prayer is the Ẓuhr prayer.'\"" He said: \""Then Ibn ʿUmar passed by us"," so ʿUrwah said: 'Send to Ibn ʿUmar and ask him.' So we sent a boy to him and he asked him. Then the messenger came back and said: 'It is the Ẓuhr prayer.' So we doubted the boy's statement"," so we all stood up and went to Ibn ʿUmar and asked him"," and he said: 'It is the Ẓuhr prayer.'\"" [Ṣaḥīgh. Ibn Jarīr narrated it in his Tafsīr (2/569).]"""
"2157","(2157) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us: ʿAffān informed us: Hammām informed us from Qatādah from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Ibn ʿUmar from Zayd ibn Thābit that he said: \The middle prayer is the Ẓuhr prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh for other than him. Ibn Jarīr narrated it in his Tafsīr (2/569).]"""
"2158","(2158) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Mukram ibn Aḥmad al-Qāḍī informed us in Baghdad: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zibriqān informed us: Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī informed us: Fuḍayl ibn Marzūq informed us: Shaqīq ibn ʿUqbah al-ʿAbdī informed us: al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib informed us, who said: \We recited: 'Guard strictly your prayers and the prayer of al-ʿAṣr (the afternoon prayer)' during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for as long as Allah willed us to recite it. Then Allah abrogated it and revealed: 'Guard strictly your prayers and the middle prayer' [al-Baqarah: 238].\"" A man said to him: \""Is it then the ʿAṣr prayer?\"" He said: \""I have already told you how it was revealed and how Allah abrogated it. And Allah knows best.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from Yaḥyā ibn Ādam from al-Fuḍayl"," except that he said: \""A man said: 'Is it then the ʿAṣr prayer?' So al-Barāʾ said: 'Have I not told you how it was revealed and how Allah"," the Most High"," abrogated it?'\"" Muslim said: \""And al-Ashjaʿī narrated it"," meaning similarly.\"" [Ṣaḥīgh. Muslim narrated it (630).]"""
"2159","(2159) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī both said: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth informed us. (H) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdad: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth informed us: al-Ashjaʿī informed us from Sufyān from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Shaqīq ibn ʿUqbah from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: \We recited it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for a time: 'Guard strictly your prayers and the prayer of al-ʿAṣr.' Then we recited it afterwards: 'Guard strictly your prayers and the middle prayer.' I do not know whether it is that one or not.\"""""
"2160","(2160) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī al-Wazīr informed us: Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us: al-Anṣārī informed us: Hishām ibn Ḥassān informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn informed us: ʿUbaydah al-Salmānī informed us: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, who said: \We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of al-Khandaq (the Trench) and he said: 'May Allah fill their houses and their graves with fire"," just as they distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun had set"," and it was the ʿAṣr prayer.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ thus from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī. [Ṣaḥīgh. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (2773).]"""
"2161","(2161) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah — Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Ṣanʿānī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Sharḥbīl ibn Juʿshum narrated to us — Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abī al-Ḍuḥā from Shutayr ibn Shakl al-ʿAbsī, who said: I heard ʿAlī say: \On the day of al-Aḥzāb"," we prayed ʿAṣr between Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ.\"" Then the Prophet ﷺ said: \""They distracted us from the middle prayer — the prayer of ʿAṣr. May Allah fill their graves and their bellies with fire.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Abī Muʿāwiyah from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrih. Aḥmad 1/146]"""
"2162","(2162) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Ḍabbī narrated to us — Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Kathīr, narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us — ʿĀṣim narrated from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, who said: A man was told, \Ask ʿAlī about the middle prayer.\""\n\nSo he asked him"," and ʿAlī said: \""We used to think it was the prayer of Fajr"," until I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of al-Aḥzāb: 'They distracted us from the middle prayer — ʿAṣr — until the sun had set. May Allah fill their graves and their bellies with fire.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned in the preceding narration"," and it is a ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth from another chain.]"""
"2163","(2163) Abū Muḥammad Junāḥ ibn Nudhayr al-Muḥāribī informed us in al-Kūfah — Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us — al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn and ʿAwn ibn Salām both said: Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah narrated to us — Zubayd al-Yāmī narrated from Murrah from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of al-Khandaq: \They distracted us from the middle prayer — the prayer of ʿAṣr. May Allah fill their bellies and their graves with fire.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAwn ibn Salām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it 628.]"""
"2164","(2164) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād — Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us — ʿAffān narrated to us — Hammām narrated to us — Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan from Samurah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The middle prayer is the prayer of ʿAṣr.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrih. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it 2983.]"""
"2165","(2165) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us — Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh narrated to us. And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh, meaning Ibn al-Munādī, narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us — Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abī Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The middle prayer is the prayer of ʿAṣr.\""\n\nIt was thus narrated with this isnād. Others contradicted him and narrated it from al-Taymī as a mawqūf narration from Abī Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrih. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it 1338.]"""
"2166","(2166) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us — al-Anṣārī narrated to me — Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated it as a mawqūf narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"2167","(2167) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me — my father narrated to me — Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from al-Taymī, and he narrated it as a mawqūf narration.\n\nʿAbdullāh said: My father said: \This is not Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Sammān nor Bādhām; this is a Baṣran whose name"," I think"," is Mīzān.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""This is the view of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in the more authentic of the two narrations from him"," and the view of Ubayy ibn Kaʿb"," Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī"," Abī Hurayrah"," ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," one of the two narrations from Ibn ʿUmar"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," and ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with them all. It was narrated from Qabīṣah ibn Dhuʾayb"," who was from the Tābiʿūn"," that the middle prayer is the prayer of Maghrib.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Mālik narrated it balāghan.]"""
"2168","(2168) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik informed us that it reached him that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās used to say: \The middle prayer is the prayer of al-Ṣubḥ (Fajr).\""\n\nMālik said: \""And that is my opinion.\"" [Ḍaʿīf jiddan. Mālik narrated it balāghan 316.]"""
"2169","(2169) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us — ʿAffān narrated from Hammām from Qatādah from Abī al-Khalīl from Jābir ibn Zayd from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The middle prayer is the prayer of Fajr.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrih. Ibn Jarīr narrated it in his Tafsīr 2/578.]"""
"2170","(2170) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn al-Faḍl ibn al-Samḥ narrated to us — Sahl ibn Tamām narrated to us — Abū al-Ashhab and Salm ibn Zarīr narrated from Abī Rajāʾ al-ʿUṭāridī, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās led us in the prayer of al-Ṣubḥ (Fajr) while he was the governor over al-Baṣrah. He recited the qunūt before the rukūʿ and raised his hands such that had a man been standing before him, he would have seen the whiteness of his armpits. When he completed the prayer, he turned his face toward us and said: \This is the prayer that Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," mentioned in His Book: {Guard strictly the prayers"," and the middle prayer"," and stand before Allah in devout obedience} [al-Baqarah: 238].\""\n\nAnd ʿAwf similarly narrated it from Abī Rajāʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrih. This is a ḥasan isnād.]"""
"2171","(2171) Abū ʿAbdillāh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, from ʿAwf, from Abī Rajāʾ, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās led us in the Fajr prayer and recited the qunūt before the rukūʿ. When he finished, he said: \This is the middle prayer (al-ṣalāt al-wusṭā) concerning which Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: {And stand before Allah in devout obedience} [al-Baqarah: 238].\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh for others. This isnād is ḍaʿīf.]"""
"2172","(2172) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us: Dāwūd al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us: Ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated to us, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The middle prayer (al-ṣalāt al-wusṭā) is the Fajr prayer.\""\n\nAnd it has also been narrated from Anas ibn Mālik"," and he used the same evidence that Ibn ʿAbbās used. This is the view of ʿAṭāʾ"," Ṭāwūs"," Mujāḥid"," and ʿIkrimah. Whoever held this view cited as evidence that which…\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh for others. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it (8616).]"""
"2173","(2173) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from al-Qaʿqaʿ ibn Ḥakīm, from Abū Yūnus, the freed slave of ʿĀʾishah, that he said: \ʿĀʾishah"," raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhā"," instructed me to write a muṣḥaf for her. Then she said: 'When you reach this āyah"," inform me: {Guard strictly the prayers"," and the middle prayer} [al-Baqarah: 238].' When I reached it"," I informed her"," and she dictated to me: {Guard strictly the prayers"," and the middle prayer"," and the ʿAṣr prayer"," and stand before Allah in devout obedience.} ʿĀʾishah said: 'I heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. (Q) And in it is evidence that the middle prayer is other than the ʿAṣr prayer.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (629).]"""
"2174","(2174) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from ʿAmr ibn Rāfiʿ, who said: \I was writing a muṣḥaf for Ḥafṣah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," and she said: 'When you reach this āyah"," inform me: {Guard strictly the prayers"," and the middle prayer} [al-Baqarah: 238].' When I reached it"," I informed her"," and she dictated to me: {Guard strictly the prayers"," and the middle prayer"," and the ʿAṣr prayer"," and stand before Allah in devout obedience}.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Mālik narrated it (314).]"""
"2175","(2175) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, who said: \Ḥafṣah ordered that a muṣḥaf be written for her"," and she said to the one who was writing: 'When you come to the mention of the prayer"," leave its place until I inform you of what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite.' So he did that"," and she wrote: {Guard strictly the prayers"," and the middle prayer"," and the ʿAṣr prayer.} Nāfiʿ said: 'I saw the wāw suspended (i.e."," written separately).'\""\n\nThis is a musnad narration"," except that there is an irsāl from the side of Nāfiʿ. Then he corroborated it with what he reported from his observation. And the ḥadīth of Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAmr the scribe is mawṣūl"," and even if it is mawqūf"," it is a witness for the authenticity of the narration of ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār narrated it from Abū Jaʿfar — who is Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī — and Nāfiʿ"," the freed slave of Ibn ʿUmar"," both from ʿUmar ibn Rāfiʿ"," the freed slave of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu"," who said: \""I used to write the maṣāḥif during the time of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar asked me to write a muṣḥaf for her"," and she said to me: 'O my son"," when you reach this āyah — {Guard strictly the prayers"," and the middle prayer} [al-Baqarah: 238] — do not write it until you come to me"," so that I may dictate to you as I memorized it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' When I reached it"," I brought the parchment and the inkpot until I came to her"," and she said: 'Write: {Guard strictly the prayers"," and the middle prayer} — it is the ʿAṣr prayer — {and stand before Allah in devout obedience.}'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh for others. Ibn Jarīr narrated it (2/569).]"""
"2176","(2176) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Abū Zurʿah al-Dimashqī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Khālid narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated it. But he contradicted the narration of Zayd ibn Aslam and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar in both the isnād and the matn entirely, in that he said: from ʿUmar ibn Rāfiʿ, when in fact it is ʿAmr ibn Rāfiʿ, and ʿUmar did not correctly say it — al-Bukhārī said so. And in that he said: \It is the ʿAṣr prayer","\"" when in fact it is \""and the ʿAṣr prayer.\""\n\nThe isnād of the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah has also been contradicted in its matn"," and the ṣaḥīḥ is what we have mentioned. And it has been narrated in agreement with it. And it has been narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that he recited: {Guard strictly the prayers"," and the middle prayer"," and the ʿAṣr prayer.}\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us"," saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us"," from Shuʿbah"," from Abī Isḥāq"," from Hubayrah ibn Yarīm"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," to that effect.\n\nAnd the Book came"," then the Sunnah"," specifying the Fajr prayer with an increase in virtue.\n\n[Ḥasan for others.]"""
"2177","(2177) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān narrated to us: Shuʿayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, who narrated to me: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me that Abū Hurayrah said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the Fajr prayer.'\"" Then Abū Hurayrah said: \""Recite"," if you wish: {And the Qurʾān of Fajr — indeed"," the Qurʾān of Fajr is ever witnessed} [al-Isrāʾ: 78].\""\n\nIt is narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of Abū al-Yamān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī narrated it (4440).]"""
"2178","(2178) Abū Muḥammad Junāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Junāḥ al-Qāḍī in Kūfah narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿUthmān ibn Ḥakīm, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī ʿAmrah, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever prays al-ʿIshāʾ in congregation"," it is as if he stood in prayer for half the night. And whoever prays al-Fajr in congregation"," it is as if he stood in prayer for the entire night.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from two routes from al-Thawrī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (656).]"""
"2179","(2179) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan, from Jundub ibn Sufyān al-ʿAlaqī, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever prays al-Ṣubḥ (Fajr)"," he is under the protection (dhimmah) of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic. So beware"," O son of Ādam! Let not Allah demand from you anything of His protection.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from Yazīd ibn Hārūn.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (657).]"""
"2180","(2180) Abū al-Qāsim Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿUrwah in Baghdād narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Abū al-Sarī Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan al-Nasāʾī narrated to us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated to us: Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sīrīn, who said: \I heard Jundub ibn ʿAbdillāh say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever prays the Ṣubḥ (Fajr) prayer"," he is under the protection (dhimmah) of Allah. So let not Allah demand from you anything of His protection. For whoever He demands something of it and He finds him unable to fulfill it"," He will cast him on his face into the Fire of Jahannam.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Naṣr ibn ʿAlī"," from Bishr.\n\nAnd the Book came"," then the Sunnah"," with an increase in the virtue of both al-Fajr and al-ʿAṣr together.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. It preceded in the one before it from the ḥadīth of Jundub ibn ʿAbdillāh.]"""
"2181","(2181) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated from Ismāʿīl; Qays narrated to me, saying: Jarīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh said to me: We were in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ when he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said: \Verily"," you will see your Lord just as you see this moon; you will not experience any difficulty or confusion in seeing Him. Therefore"," if you are able to avoid being overcome by anything before the prayer before the sunrise and before the sunset"," then do so.\"" Then he recited: {So glorify the praises of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before the sunset.}\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 529.]"""
"2182","(2182) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy upon him, informed us; Abū al-Qāsim ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Bālawayh al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The angels take turns among you — angels by night and angels by day. They gather together at the Fajr prayer and the ʿAṣr prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend to Him"," and He asks them"," though He knows best about them: 'How did you leave My servants?' They reply: 'We left them while they were praying"," and we came to them while they were praying.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 3051.]"""
"2183","(2183) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī informed us; Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah; Abū al-Zinād informed me from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that he heard him say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — and he mentioned it with the same meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, and al-Bukhārī also narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah.\n\n[Reference as above.]"
"2184","(2184) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jārūd ibn Dīnār al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us; Hammām narrated to us; Abū Jumarah narrated from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qays, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever prays the two cool prayers (al-Bardayn) will enter Paradise.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 548.]"""
"2185","(2185) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us, dictating in the year thirty-three; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-ʿAwfī and Hudhaybah ibn Khālid both narrated to us, saying: Hammām narrated to us; Abū Jumarah narrated from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qays, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever prays the two cool prayers will enter Paradise.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it from Hudhaybah ibn Khālid"," except that they did not trace Abū Bakr's lineage through Hudhaybah"," but rather traced it through someone else. He is Abū Bakr ibn Abī Mūsā al-Ashʿarī"," and the name of Abī Mūsā is ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qays.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Referred to in the preceding ḥadīth.]"""
"2186","(2186) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Faqīh al-Ṭabarānī therein informed us; Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ṣawwāf in Baghdād narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan, meaning Abū Shuʿayb al-Ḥarrānī, narrated to us; ʿAffān narrated to us; Hammām narrated from Abū Jumarah, from Abū Bakr, from his father, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever prays the two cool prayers will enter Paradise.\""\n\nAbū Shuʿayb said: Some of the grammarians said: \""A morning prayer and an evening prayer.\"" He said: And this Abū Bakr is said to be Abū Bakr ibn ʿUmarah ibn Ruwaybah.\n\nThe Shaykh said: The one from whom Abū Jumarah narrated is Abū Bakr ibn Abī Mūsā. And Abū Bakr ibn ʿUmarah also narrated it with the same meaning. And it is in what…\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Referred to in the preceding ḥadīth.]"""
"2187","(2187) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Hāshimī in Baghdād narrated to us; Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from Abū Bakr ibn ʿUmarah. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — and the wording is his — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; Shaybān narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from Ibn ʿUmarah ibn Ruwaybah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \No one who prays before the rising of the sun and before its setting will enter the Fire.\"" A man from the people of Baṣrah was present and said: \""Did you hear this from the Prophet ﷺ?\"" He said: \""Yes"," I bear witness to it upon him.\"" The man said: \""And I bear witness that I heard the Prophet ﷺ say it in the same place where you heard it from him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr"," and he also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Khālid.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 634.]"""
"2188","(2188) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us; Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind informed us.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me; ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us; Khālid narrated from Dāwūd, meaning Ibn Abī Hind, from Abū Ḥarb, meaning Ibn Abī al-Aswad, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Faḍālah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me, and among what he taught me was: \Guard the five prayers.\"" I said: \""These are times in which I have preoccupations"," so command me with a comprehensive matter which"," if I do it"," will suffice me.\"" He said: \""Guard the two ʿAṣr prayers.\"" This was not a word from our language"," so I said: \""What are the two ʿAṣr prayers?\"" He said: \""A prayer before the rising of the sun and a prayer before its setting.\""\n\nThe wording is that of al-Qaṭṭān. The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: It is as though he intended — and Allah knows best: Guard them at the beginning of their times. Then he offered the excuse of preoccupations that would lead to delaying them from the beginning of their times"," so he commanded him to guard these two prayers by hastening them at the beginning of their two times. And success is from Allah.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 428.]"""
"2189","(2189) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Qāsim al-Sarraj, among others, said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: While the people were at Qubāʾ performing the Ṣubḥ prayer, a person came to them and said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been sent down to him tonight a Qur'ānic revelation"," and he has been commanded to face the Kaʿbah"," so face it.\"" Their faces had been towards al-Shām"," so they turned towards the Kaʿbah.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah from Mālik.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 395"," 4218.]"""
"2190","(2190) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Ibn Rajāʾ informed us; Isrāʾīl narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʀĀzib, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madīnah and prayed towards Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen or seventeen months. The Prophet ﷺ had loved to be directed towards the Kaʿbah, so Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {We have certainly seen the turning of your face toward the heaven, so We will surely turn you to a qiblah with which you will be pleased. So turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Ḥarām} [al-Baqarah: 144]. A man who had been praying with the Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of the Anṣār who were praying in prostration towards Bayt al-Maqdis, and he said: \I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been directed towards the Kaʿbah.\"" So they turned towards the Kaʿbah. The foolish among the people — they were the Jews — said: {What turned them from their qiblah which they had been upon?} [al-Baqarah: 142]. Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: {Say: To Allah belong the east and the west; He guides whom He wills to a straight path} [al-Baqarah: 142].\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ"," and Muslim narrated it through two other chains from Abū Isḥāq.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 390.]"""
"2191","(2191) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed facing Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months or seventeen months, and he wished that his qiblah would be towards the House (the Kaʿbah). He prayed ʿAṣr, and a group of people prayed with him. A man from among those who had prayed with him passed by the people of a mosque while they were in rukūʿ, and he said, \I bear witness by Allah that I have prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) facing Makkah.\"" So they turned"," as they were"," towards the House (the Kaʿbah).\n\n[Saḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 41]"""
"2192","(2192) And with his chain of narration from al-Barāʾ, who said: It was said concerning those who had died before the change of the qiblah to the Kaʿbah, and those who had been killed, that we did not know what to say about them. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And Allah would never cause your faith to be lost; indeed, Allah is, to the people, Kind and Merciful} [al-Baqarah: 143]. Both narrations were reported by al-Bukhārī from Abū Nuʿaym.\n\n[Saḥīḥ. And it has been mentioned in the one before it]"
"2193","(2193) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Sulaymān, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray towards Bayt al-Maqdis while the Kaʿlah was in front of him, and after he had turned towards al-Madīnah for sixteen months, then Allah, the Most High, directed him to the Kaʿbah.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad, 1/352]"
"2194","(2194) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, who said: I heard Saʿd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed after arriving in al-Madīnah for sixteen months towards Bayt al-Maqdis, then he was turned after that towards al-Masjid al-Ḥarām two months before Badr.\n\nThus narrated al-ʿUṭāridī from Ibn Fuḍayl.\n\nAnd Mālik, al-Thawrī, and Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, mursal, without mentioning Saʿd.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Mawḍūʿ]"
"2195","(2195) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed me; Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿUmayrah ibn Ziyād al-Kindī, from ʿAlī (may Allah, the Most High, be pleased with him), regarding {So turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Ḥarām} [al-Baqarah: 144], he said: \Sharṭrah\"" means qiblah (facing it).\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 2/295]"""
"2196","(2196) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Ādam informed us; Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujājid, regarding His words {sharṭrah} [al-Baqarah: 144], meaning: towards it (nahwahu).\n\n[Saḥīḥ. al-Durr al-Manthūr, 1/355]"
"2197","(2197) And likewise ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah narrated it from Ibn ʿAbbās. Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated it to us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us; ʿUthmān al-Dārimī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, to that effect.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Jarīr in al-Tafsīr, 2/22]"
"2198","(2198) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Dūrī narrated to us; Aḥmad, that is Ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī, narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us; Manṣūr ibn Saʿd narrated from Maymūn ibn Siyāḥ, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever prays our prayer"," faces our qiblah"," and eats our slaughtered animal"," then that one is a Muslim"," under the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger. So do not betray Allah in His covenant.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAbbās from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\n\n[Saḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 391]"""
"2199","(2199) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh al-ʿAdl informed us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk informed us that Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to them; Ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. When they testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah"," and they pray our prayer"," face our qiblah"," and eat our slaughtered animal"," their blood and their wealth are forbidden to us except by right"," and their reckoning is upon Allah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād.\n\n[Saḥīḥ mawqūf. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 392] marfūʿan."""
"2200","(2200) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Aḥmad ibn Kāmil al-Mustamlī informed us; Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: I read to Mālik, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray upon his mount wherever it turned with him.\n\nʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār said: Ibn ʿUmar used to do that. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Shāfiʿī, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray upon his mount during travel wherever it turned with him. He did not mention what comes after it.\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another chain from Ibn Dīnār.\n\n[Saḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 1096]"
"2201","(2201) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: Ibn ʿUmar used to pray upon his mount, gesturing with his head in whichever direction it faced, as a voluntary prayer. He then said: \The Prophet ﷺ used to do the same","\"" and then he recited this verse: {And to Allah belong the east and the west"," so wherever you turn"," there is the Face of Allah. Indeed"," Allah is All-Encompassing"," All-Knowing} [al-Baqarah: 115]. Then he said: \""This verse was revealed concerning this.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 2958.]"""
"2202","(2202) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us that Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawārīrī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān, who narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Jubayr narrated to us from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray upon his mount while travelling from Makkah to Madinah"," in whatever direction his face was turned.\"" He said: \""And concerning this"," the verse was revealed: {So wherever you turn"," there is the Face of Allah} [al-Baqarah: 115].\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh al-Qawārīrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 700.]"""
"2203","(2203) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Qurqūb al-Tammār in Hamadhān informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us that Ādam narrated to us that Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Surāqah narrated to us from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Anmār praying upon his mount"," facing towards the east"," as a voluntary prayer.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 3909.]"""
"2204","(2204) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Saʿdān narrated to us that Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us that al-Ashʿath narrated to us from al-Ḥasan, that he used to see no harm in praying a voluntary prayer while driving the camels, in whichever direction they faced. And if he came upon a verse of prostration, he would recite it and prostrate. [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"2205","(2205) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated to us that my father narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray his voluntary prayer in whatever direction his she-camel faced. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its grading has been previously mentioned, 2202.]"
"2206","(2206) Abū Jaʿfar Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī informed us that Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī informed us that Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: I read to Mālik from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā al-Māzinī, from Abū al-Ḥubāb Saʿīd ibn Yasār, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying upon a donkey"," facing towards Khaybar.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2207","(2207) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Tamtām narrated to us that ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us that Hammām narrated to us. (Ḥ) And ʿAlī informed us that Aḥmad narrated to us that Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us that Ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us that Hammām narrated to us from Anas ibn Sīrīn, who said: \We met Anas ibn Mālik"," may Allah be pleased with him"," when he came from Shām"," and I met him at ʿAyn al-Tamr. I saw him praying upon a donkey"," and his face was on this side—meaning to the left of the qiblah. So I said to him: 'I see you praying other than towards the qiblah.' He said: 'Were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing it"," I would not have done it.'\"" In the ḥadīth of ʿAffān"," it states: \""His face was on that side","\"" and Hammām gestured towards the left of the qiblah. And at the end of it"," he said: \""I did not do it","\"" meaning the voluntary prayer. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd from Ḥabbān from Hammām"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim from ʿAffān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 1049.]"""
"2208","(2208) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayd narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us that Ribʿī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Jārūd ibn Abī Sabrah al-Hudhalī narrated to me that ʿAmr ibn Abī al-Ḥajjāj narrated to me that al-Jārūd ibn Abī Sabrah narrated to me that Anas ibn Mālik narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he travelled and intended to perform a voluntary prayer, would turn his she-camel towards the qiblah and say the takbīr, then he would pray in whatever direction the she-camel faced. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī, 2228.]"
"2209","(2209) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us that Abū al-Yamān narrated to us from Shuʿayb, from al-Zuhrī, who said: Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform his voluntary prayers on the back of his mount, paying no attention to which direction his face was turned, and he would gesture with his head. And ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to do the same. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad, 2/132/6155.]"
"2210","(2210) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us that Ḥajjāj said: Ibn Jurayj informed me that Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī saying: \I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying the supererogatory prayers upon his mount from every direction"," but he would lower the two prostrations of the rakʿah and gesture with his head.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 3/366"," 380.]"""
"2211","(2211) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us, from Sufyān, who narrated to me: Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) sent me on an errand. When I returned"," he was praying upon his mount facing towards the east"," and his prostration was lower than his bowing. I greeted him with salām"," but he did not respond to me. When he finished"," he said: 'Indeed"," I was praying.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah (2/236)]"""
"2212","(2212) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated to me.\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated, saying: I read to Mālik, from Abū Bakr ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, from Saʿīd ibn Yasār, who said: \I was with Ibn ʿUmar on the road to Makkah. When I feared the approach of dawn"," I dismounted and performed the witr prayer. Ibn ʿUmar said: 'Is there not in the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) a good example for you?' I said: 'Indeed"," yes.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform the witr upon the camel.'\""\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (999)]"""
"2213","(2213) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in Baghdād, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ubbī al-Qāḍī and Tamīm ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb narrated to us, saying: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar used to pray upon his mount whichever direction it faced"," and he would perform the witr upon it"," and he would inform that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to do that.\""\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2214","(2214) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī narrated to us, saying: Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Akhnas, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: \That the Prophet (ﷺ) used to perform the witr upon his mount.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad (6/347)]"""
"2215","(2215) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us, saying: Abū Salamah narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAwn, from Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim, who said: \I said to Nāfiʿ: 'Did Ibn ʿUmar used to perform the witr upon the mount?' He said: 'Does the witr have a virtue over other voluntary prayers? Yes"," by Allah"," he used to perform the witr upon it.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn ʿAdī in al-Kāmil (2/192)]"""
"2216","(2216) It was narrated by other than Muḥammad ibn Ghālib from Abū Salamah in this manner, and he added at the end: Abū Salamah said: \And Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated it to me.\"" Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us"," saying: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us"," saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī Maʿshar narrated to us"," saying: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmār ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us"," saying: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl"," meaning Abū Salamah"," narrated it with its addition. Ṣaḥīḥ; see the one before it."""
"2217","(2217) Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Sufyān al-Thawrī informed me, from Thawr ibn Abī Fākhitah, from his father: \That ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to perform the witr upon his mount.\"" Others added from al-Thawrī: \""He would gesture with a gesture (īmāʾan).\""\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated it"," saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us"," saying: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us"," saying: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us"," from Sufyān"," and he mentioned it with its addition. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its chain is ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2218","(2218) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from his father ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform voluntary prayers upon the mount in whatever direction it faced"," and he would perform the witr upon it"," but he would not perform the obligatory prayer upon it.\""\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah"," from Ibn Wahb"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Layth"," from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1047)]"""
"2219","(2219) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us, saying: ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Samarqandī narrated to us, saying: Muʿādh ibn Faḍālah narrated to us, saying: Hishām narrated to us.\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir ibn al-Bayāḍ narrated to us in Baghdād, saying: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ayyūb al-Bazzāz narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Hishām narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā, meaning Ibn Abī Kathīr, narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both): \That the Prophet (ﷺ) used to pray upon his mount facing towards the east. When he intended to perform the obligatory prayer"," he would dismount"," face the qiblah"," and pray.\""\nThe wording is that of Muslim's ḥadīth. In the narration of Muʿādh"," he said: \""Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me","\"" and he said \""towards the east\"" (nahwa al-mashriq).\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm and Muʿādh ibn Faḍālah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī similarly (391)]"""
"2220","(2220) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated to us, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah, from his father, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing voluntary prayers while upon his mount"," gesturing with his head in whatever direction it faced. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not do that in the obligatory prayer.\""\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yūnus"," from Ibn Shihāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1098)]"""
"2221","(2221) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us, Duḥaym al-Dimashqī narrated to us, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muʿāwiyah ibn Sallām narrated to me from his brother Zayd, from his grandfather Abū Sallām, from Abū Kabshah al-Salūlī, from Sahl ibn al-Ḥanẓaliyyah, who said: We travelled with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in an army. He mentioned the hadith and said therein: \Who will guard us tonight?\"" Anas ibn Abī Marthad al-Ghanawī said: \""I will"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: \""Go to this mountain pass until you are at its highest point"," and do not come down except for prayer or to relieve yourself.\"""""
"2222","(2222) Al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Maḥmūd ibn Khālid narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb narrated to us from al-Nuʿmān ibn al-Mundhir, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ, that he asked ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): \Has permission been granted for women to pray upon riding animals?\"" She said: \""Permission has not been granted for them"," neither in times of hardship nor in times of ease.\""\n\nMuḥammad said: This pertains to the obligatory prayer."""
"2223","(2223) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh al-Mihrajānī narrated to us there, Abū Sahl — Bishr ibn Aḥmad — narrated to us, Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad al-Kātib narrated to us, Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubārak and al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us from al-Awzāʿī, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), that he used to make his sick dismount during travel so that they would perform the obligatory prayer on the ground — except that Ibn al-Mubārak did not mention Nāfiʿ in his hadith."
"2224","(2224) As for the hadith that Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of — Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá informed us, ʿUmar ibn al-Rammāḥ informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Salamah al-Hamadhānī informed us there, Abū Sahl — Bishr ibn Aḥmad ibn Bishr al-Isfarāʾinī — narrated to us there, Abū Sulaymān Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAqīl al-Bayhaqī narrated to us, Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá informed us, Ibn al-Rammāḥ informed us, from Kathīr ibn Ziyād, from ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaʿlá, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to a narrow pass, he and his Companions, with the sky — Yaḥyá said: and I think he said \or the rain\"" — above them and the mud below them"," and the time for prayer arrived. He commanded the mu'adhdhin"," who gave the iqāmah"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came forward upon his mount and led them in prayer"," gesturing"," making the sujūd lower than the rukūʿ"," or his sujūd lower than his rukūʿ.\n\nIn the narration of Abū ʿAbd Allāh"," Yaḥyá said: I think he said: \""and the enemy was above them"," and the rain below.\""\n\nThere is weakness in its chain of narration"," and the reliability of some of its narrators has not been established such as would necessitate acceptance of their report. It is possible that this was in a situation of extreme fear."""
"2225","(2225) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik ibn Anas informed us, from his paternal uncle Abū Suhayl ibn Mālik, from his father, that he heard Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbayd Allāh say: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and he was asking about Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Five prayers during the day and night.\"" He said: \""Is there anything else upon me?\"" He said: \""No"," unless you perform voluntary prayers.\""\n\nThis is narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Mālik."""
"2226","(2226) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us, from Yaḥyá ibn Saʿīd ibn Qays al-Anṣārī, from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyá ibn Ḥabbān, from Ibn Muḥayriẓ, that a man from Banī Kinānah called al-Mukhdajī heard a man in Shām called Abū Muḥammad saying: \Indeed"," the witr prayer is obligatory.\"" Al-Mukhdajī said: \""So I went to ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit and intercepted him as he was heading to the mosque"," and I informed him of what Abū Muḥammad had said. ʿUbadah said: 'Abū Muḥammad has lied. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: \""Five prayers which Allah has enjoined upon the servants. Whoever comes with them"," not neglecting any of them out of disdain for their right"," shall have a covenant with Allah that He will admit him into Paradise. And whoever does not come with them shall have no covenant with Allah; if He wills"," He will punish him"," and if He wills"," He will admit him into Paradise.\""'\"""""
"2227","(2227) Yaḥyá ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyá informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Sulmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Faqīh informed us, saying: It was recited to Yaḥyá ibn Jaʿfar while I was listening, and Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī informed us, Sufyān informed us, from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The witr is not an obligation"," but it is a Sunnah established by the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\""\n\nThis is the position of ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit and Ibn ʿAbbās"," and all of this"," along with the other narrations on the subject"," belongs in the chapter on voluntary prayers."""
"2228","(116) Chapter: Permission to Face Other Than the Qiblah in the Obligatory Prayer During Close Combat and Intense Fighting"
"2229","(2228) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik ibn Anas informed us, from Nāfiʿ, that when ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar was asked about the prayer of fear, he would say: \The imam advances with one group","\"" and then he narrated the hadith.\n\nAnd Ibn ʿUmar said in the hadith: \""If the fear is more severe than that"," they pray on foot and mounted"," facing the qiblah and not facing it.\""\n\nThis is established through the chain of Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah"," from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from the Prophet (peace be upon him). Its proper place is in the Book of the Prayer of Fear."""
"2230","(2229) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyá ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us.\n\nIbn Jurayj informed us, saying: I said to ʿAṭāʾ, \Did you hear Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them) say: 'You have been commanded only with the ṭawāf"," and you have not been commanded to enter it'?\"" He said: \""He was not forbidden from entering it"," but I heard him say: Usāmah ibn Zayd informed me that when the Prophet (peace be upon him) entered the House"," he supplicated in all its corners and did not pray in it until he came out. When he came out"," he performed two rakʿahs facing the Kaʿbah and then said: 'This is the qiblah.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Naṣr"," from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," without the story of entering from ʿAṭāʾ and without the mention of Usāmah. The correct version is what we have narrated. Muslim narrated it through another chain from Ibn Jurayj in its entirety"," and he mentioned Usāmah."""
"2231","(2230) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mujabbir narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \What is between the east and the west is a qiblah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 1/323]"""
"2232","(2231) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāʾīnī narrated to us that Abū Yūsuf Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us that Shuʿayb ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \What is between the east and the west is a qiblah.\""\n\nThe first narration is uniquely narrated (tafarrada) by Ibn Mujabbir"," and the second is uniquely narrated by Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-Khallāl. The well-known narration is that of the group — Ḥammād ibn Salamah"," Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah"," Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān"," and others — from ʿUbayd Allāh from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from ʿUmar"," as a statement of ʿUmar himself. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous takhrij]"""
"2233","(2232) The faqīh Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr al-Ṭūsī informed us that Abū Bishr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāḍirī narrated to us that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh informed us that Nāfiʿ informed him from Ibn ʿUmar from ʿUmar who said: \What is between the east and the west is a qiblah.\""\n\nAnd others besides the two of them narrated it from Nāfiʿ. It has also been narrated from Abū Hurayyah in a marfūʿ (elevated) chain. It has also been narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Abū Qilābah from the Prophet (ﷺ) in a mursal (interrupted) chain. It has also been narrated from ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās as their own statement.\n\nAnd what is meant by it — and Allah knows best — is the people of al-Madīnah and whoever has his qiblah in the direction of the people of al-Madīnah: what is between the east and the west encompasses their qiblah generally"," after which one seeks its precise direction. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it"," 461]"""
"2234","(2233) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us that Nāfiʿ ibn Abī Nuʿaym narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: \What is between the east and the west is a qiblah"," when you face the direction of the House (al-Bayt).\"" [Ḥasan. Ṭabaqāt Ibn Khayyāṭ"," 1/381]"""
"2235","(2234) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us by dictation. Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed me that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAnbasah Abū Muḥammad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū Muḥammad Jaʿfar ibn ʿAnbasah ibn ʿAmr ibn Yaʿqūb al-Yashkurī in Nakhīlah narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Makkī, from the progeny of ʿAbd al-Dār, narrated to us that Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʬāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The House (al-Bayt) is a qiblah for the people of the Mosque (al-Masjid)"," and the Mosque is a qiblah for the people of the Ḥaram"," and the Ḥaram is a qiblah for the people of the earth in its east and its west"," from my Ummah.\""\n\nIt is uniquely narrated by ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Makkī"," and he is weak (ḍaʿīf) and cannot be used as a proof (lā yuḥtaju bihi).\n\nIt has also been narrated through another weak chain from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥubshī"," likewise in a marfūʿ form"," and one cannot use such a narration as a proof. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2236","(2235) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Bishr al-Marthadī narrated to us that Dāwūd ibn ʿAmr narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Wāsiṭī narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sālim from ʬāʾ from Jābir who said: \We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey or in a military expedition when clouds overtook us. We exercised our best judgment (taḥarraynā) but differed regarding the qiblah. So each of us prayed on his own"," and one of us drew a line before him so that we might know our positions. When we looked at it in the morning"," we found that we had prayed facing other than the qiblah. We mentioned that to the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he said: 'Your prayer has sufficed you (ajzaʾat ṣalātukum).'\""\n\nIt is uniquely narrated by Muḥammad ibn Sālim and Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-ʿArzamī from ʬāʾ"," and both of them are weak (ḍaʿifān).\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr al-Ḥārithī al-Faqīh both informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ said: It was recited to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz while I was listening: \""Dāwūd ibn ʿAmr narrated to you","\"" and he mentioned it with the same narration as that of al-Marthadī.\n\nThen ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ said: \""Thus he said — from Muḥammad ibn Sālim — while others said: from Muḥammad ibn Yazīd from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-ʿArzamī from ʬāʾ"," and both of them are weak.\""\n\nAbū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ṭayyib al-Ḥusayn ibn Mūsā al-Raqqī in Anṭākiyyah narrated to us that Mūsā"," meaning Ibn Marwān al-Raqqī"," narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Wāsiṭī narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," and he mentioned it with the same meaning. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 1/324]"""
"2237","(2236) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Khālid narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī narrated to us that Isrāʾīl narrated from Abū Ḥuṣayn from Yaḥyā ibn Waththāb from Masrūq from ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, that he said: \Do not make your religion blindly follow (tuqallidū) men. If you refuse"," then follow the dead"," not the living.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Lālaʾkāī narrated it in Sharh al-Iʿtiqād"," 1/93]"""
"2238","(2237) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān informed us that Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us that Yūnus narrated from al-Zuhrī from Ibn Abī Namlah from his father who said: \I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) when a Jewish man came to him and said: 'O Muḥammad"," does this janāzah (corpse) speak?' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Allah knows best.' The Jew said: 'I bear witness that it speaks.' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Whatever the People of the Book narrate to you"," do not confirm them and do not deny them. Rather say: We believe in Allah"," His Books"," and His Messengers. If it is true"," you will not have denied them"," and if it is false"," you will not have confirmed them.'\""\n\nIbn Abī Namlah is Namlah ibn Abī Namlah al-Anṣārī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (without the qaṣr)"," 3644]"""
"2239","(2238) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us by dictation. Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah informed us that al-Haytham ibn Sahl al-Tustarī narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us that Mujālid ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿĀmir al-Shaʿbī from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not ask the People of the Book about anything"," for they will never guide you"," since they themselves have gone astray.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Aḥmad narrated it"," 3/338]"""
"2240","(2239) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Ibn Qaʿnab and Ibn Bukayr narrated from Mālik from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: \While the people were at Qubāʾ performing the morning prayer (ṣalāt al-ṣubḥ)"," someone came to them and said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sent down Qurʾān last night"," and he has been commanded to face the Kaʿbah"," so face it.' Their faces had been towards al-Shām"," so they turned towards the Kaʿbah.\""\n\nBoth of them (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its takhrij has been given previously under no. 2189]"""
"2241","(2240) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us — Ḥammād narrated from Thābit and Ḥumayd from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that:\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ and his Companions were praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis. When this verse was revealed: *\So turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque. And wherever you are"," turn your faces toward it\""* [al-Baqarah: 144]"," a man from Banū Salamah passed by them while they were in rukūʿ performing the Fajr prayer toward Bayt al-Maqdis. He called out to them: \""Behold! The qiblah has been changed to the Kaʿbah!\"" — he said it twice. He (Anas) said: So they turned while still in rukūʿ toward the Kaʿbah.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Salamah from Thābit from Anas. [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated by Muslim"," no. 527]"""
"2242","(2241) Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad informed us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us — Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us — al-Ashʿath ibn Saʿīd Abū al-Rabīʿ and ʿUmar ibn Qays both informed us — ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbaydullāh narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah from his father, who said:\n\nDarkness overtook us while we were on a journey, and the qiblah became uncertain for us. So each man among us prayed according to his own estimation. When the darkness lifted, lo — some of us had prayed toward other than the qiblah, and some of us had prayed toward the qiblah. We mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: *\Your prayer has been fulfilled.\""* And the verse was revealed: *\""So wherever you turn"," there is the Face of Allah\""* [al-Baqarah: 115].\n\n[Ḍaʿīf — narrated by al-Ṭayālisī in his Musnad"," no. 1145]"""
"2243","(2242) And Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us — it was read to Ibn Wahb: al-Ḥārith ibn Nabḥān informed you from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said:\n\nWe prayed one night while it was cloudy, and the qiblah became hidden from us, so we placed a marker. When we finished, we looked and found that we had prayed toward other than the qiblah. We mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: *\You have done well"," and He did not command us to repeat it.\""*\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sālim from ʿAṭāʾ"," and from ʿAbd al-Malik al-ʿArzamī from ʿAṭāʾ. As for the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Sālim from ʿAṭāʾ"," it has already passed. As for the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Malik"," it is among the wijādāt of Aḥmad ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnbarī from his father. [Munkar]"""
"2244","(2243) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ruṣāfī in Baghdad informed us — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-ʿAskarī informed me — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnbarī informed me, saying: I found in the book of my father — ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān al-ʿArzamī narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a detachment in which I was present. Darkness overtook us, and we could not determine the qiblah. A group among them said: \The qiblah is here"," toward the north.\"" So they prayed and drew a line. And some of us said: \""The qiblah is here"," toward the south","\"" and they drew a line. When morning came and the sun rose"," those lines were found to be toward other than the qiblah. We returned from our journey and came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about that. He remained silent"," and Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," revealed: *\""To Allah belong the east and the west. So wherever you turn"," there is the Face of Allah\""* [al-Baqarah: 115] — meaning"," wherever you are.\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated by al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Shabīb al-Maʿmarī and Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Bāghandī from Aḥmad ibn ʿUbaydullāh. We do not know for this ḥadīth a strong"," sound isnād. That is because ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar al-ʿUmarī"," Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-ʿArzamī"," and Muḥammad ibn Sālim al-Kūfī — all of them are weak (ḍuʿafāʾ). The route to ʿAbd al-Malik al-ʿArzamī is not clear due to the wijādah in it and other matters. In his ḥadīth there is also the mention of the revelation of the verse regarding that.\n\nAnd what is authentic from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān al-ʿArzamī is from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with them"," that the verse was revealed specifically regarding the voluntary (nafl) prayer — where your mount faces. And that has already been mentioned. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2245","(2244) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Abū al-Muthannā informed us — Yaḥyā narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān — Saʿīd ibn Jubayr narrated from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray on his mount while traveling from Makkah to Madinah, wherever his face was directed. And regarding this the verse was revealed: *\So wherever you turn"," there is the Face of Allah\""* [al-Baqarah: 115].\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qawārīrī from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," that it was revealed regarding the obligatory (farḍ) prayer"," then it was abrogated"," and that is concerning this matter."""
"2246","(2245) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū Bakr Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh in al-Rayy informed us — Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq informed us — Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said:\n\nThe first thing that was abrogated from the Qurʾān, as far as we have been informed — and Allah knows best — was the matter of the qiblah. Allah, the Blessed and Most High, said: *\To Allah belong the east and the west. So wherever you turn"," there is the Face of Allah\""* [al-Baqarah: 115]. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced it and prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis"," leaving the Bayt al-ʿAtīq. Then He said: *\""The foolish among the people will say: 'What has turned them from the qiblah which they used to face?'\""* [al-Baqarah: 142] — meaning Bayt al-Maqdis. So He abrogated it and turned him toward the Bayt al-ʿAtīq. He said: *\""So from wherever you go out"," turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque. And wherever you are"," turn your faces toward it\""* [al-Baqarah: 150].\n\nAnd in the words of al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," there is an explanation of what is in this narration from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," which is that it entered into the expanded scope of his words. When he migrated to Madinah"," he faced Bayt al-Maqdis"," turning away from the Sacred House"," while he wished that Allah would decree for him to face the Sacred House. So Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," revealed this verse until He revealed: *\""We see your face turning in the heaven\""* [al-Baqarah: 144].\n\nThe Sheikh said: And it was narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that it was revealed regarding their statement: *\""What has turned them from the qiblah which they used to face?\""* [al-Baqarah: 142].\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh in other than this chain — narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 2/294]"""
"2247","(2246) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās said:\n\nIndeed, the first thing abrogated in the Qurʾān was the qiblah. That is because when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ migrated to Madinah, and most of its inhabitants were Jews, Allah commanded him to face Bayt al-Maqdis. The Jews rejoiced, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced it for some thirteen months. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved the qibrāh of Ibrāhīm, peace be upon him, and he would supplicate to Allah and look toward the heaven. So Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, revealed: *\We see your face turning in the heaven. We will surely turn you toward a qiblah that will please you. So turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque\""* [al-Baqarah: 144] — up to His words: *\""So turn your faces toward it\""* [al-Baqarah: 144] — meaning"," toward it. The Jews were troubled by that and said: *\""What has turned them from the qiblah which they used to face?\""* [al-Baqarah: 142]. So Allah"," the Most High"," revealed: *\""Say: To Allah belong the east and the west. So wherever you turn"," there is the Face of Allah\""* [al-Baqarah: 115]. *\""And We did not make the qiblah which you used to face except so that We might know who follows the Messenger from who turns on his heels\""* [al-Baqarah: 143].\n\nIbn ʿAbbās said: So as to distinguish the people of certainty from the people of doubt and suspicion. Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," said: *\""And indeed it is difficult except for those whom Allah has guided\""* [al-Baqarah: 143] — meaning"," its turning is difficult upon the people of doubt — *\""except upon those who are humble\""* [al-Baqarah: 45] — meaning"," those who believe in what Allah"," the Most High"," has revealed.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said regarding His words: *\""There is the Face of Allah\""* [al-Baqarah: 115] — meaning"," and Allah knows best — there is the direction to which Allah has directed you. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2248","(2247) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us — Abū Usāmah narrated from al-Naḍr, meaning Ibn ʿArabī, from Mujāhid regarding the words of Allah, the Most High: *\So wherever you turn"," there is the Face of Allah\""* [al-Baqarah: 115]. He said: The qiblah of Allah — so wherever you are"," in east or west"," do not turn except toward it. [Ḥasan]"""
"2249","(2248) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Rafāʿī informed us — Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashīr informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways informed us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from the jurists of Madinah, that they used to say:\n\nWhoever prays without purification or toward other than the qiblah must repeat the prayer, whether within the time or outside of it — unless his error in the qiblah is a slight deviation or a minor thing.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī that he said regarding the one who prays toward other than the qiblah: He does not repeat. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"2250","(2249) Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Yūnus informed us — Layth narrated from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ was feeling unwell, so we prayed behind him while he was sitting. He turned toward us and saw us standing, so he gestured to us — and then mentioned the ḥadīth in full. [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated by Muslim; also narrated by Aḥmad, 3/334]"
"2251","(2250) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Ja'far Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid ibn Ibrahim al-Hafiz in Hamadan informed us; Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn informed us; Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' informed us; Mu'awiyah ibn Salam informed me; Zaid ibn Salam informed me that he heard Abu Salamah say: Abu Kabshah al-Saluli informed me that Sahl ibn al-Hanzalih narrated to him, saying: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out for Hunayn, he said: \Is there a man who will guard us tonight?\"" Anas ibn Abi Murthad al-Ghanawi said: \""I will"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Go ahead.\"" When morning came"," the Prophet (ﷺ) came out to pray and said: \""Have you sensed anything of your horseman?\"" They said: \""No.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) began to pray while glancing toward the mountain pass. When he completed the prayer"," he said: \""Your horseman has come.\"" When he arrived"," the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Perhaps you dismounted.\"" He said: \""No"," except for praying or attending to a need.\"" Then he said: \""I surveyed both mountain passes and found Hawazin with their families"," their sheep"," and their camels"," heading toward Hunayn.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""The Muslims' spoils of war tomorrow"," insha'Allah.\"" And he mentioned the hadith. [Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawud 2501]"""
"2252","(2251) Abu 'Amr al-Adib al-Razjahi narrated to us; Abu Ahmad al-Husayn ibn 'Ali al-Tamimi informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi narrated to us; Mahmud ibn Ghaylan al-Marwazi narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abu Muhammad Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Abhari al-Sufi in Hamadan informed us; Jibril ibn Muhammad ibn Isma'il in Hamadan narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Hayyuwayh narrated to us; Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind narrated from Thawr ibn Yazid from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to glance in his prayer to the right and to the left, but he would not turn his neck behind his back. Thus did al-Fadl ibn Musa narrate it, but others contradicted him and narrated it with a broken chain. [Da'if. Narrated by Ahmad 1/275]"
"2253","(2252) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us; Hajib ibn Ahmad narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind narrated from a man among the companions of 'Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to glance in his prayer without turning his neck with it. [Da'if. See the one before it]"
"2254","(2253) And that is from what Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us; they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Malas al-Numayri narrated to us; Harmalah ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Juhani narrated to me; my uncle 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah narrated from his father from his grandfather from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \Command the boy to pray when he is seven years old"," and strike him for it when he is ten.\""\n\nIbrahim ibn Sa'd followed him in narrating from 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi'. [Sahih. Narrated by Abu Dawud 494]"""
"2255","(2254) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakka, and Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Sarraj informed us; they said: Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani informed us; Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah al-Sa'di narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun informed us; Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi informed us that he heard 'Alqamah ibn Waqqas say: I heard 'Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Actions are but by intention"," and each person shall have only what he intended. So whoever migrated for Allah and His Messenger"," his migration is for Allah and His Messenger. And whoever migrated for worldly gain or to marry a woman"," his migration is for that which he migrated.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ibn Numayr from Yazid ibn Harun"," and al-Bukhari narrated it through other routes from Yahya ibn Sa'id. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 1]"""
"2256","(2255) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; he said: I heard Abu 'Amr al-Isfahani, i.e. Ibn Manda, say: I heard Sufyan ibn Harun ibn Sufyan al-Qadi say: I heard Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi say: I heard al-Buwayti say: I heard al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) say: The hadith \Actions are but by intentions\"" encompasses one-third of knowledge. [Sahih]"""
"2257","(2256) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya informed us; Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated from Mansur from Ibrahim from 'Alqamah from 'Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed a prayer and added to it or omitted from it. When he finished the prayer, they said: \O Messenger of Allah"," has something new occurred in the prayer?\"" He said: \""What is that?\"" So they mentioned what he had done. He folded his legs"," faced the qiblah"," and prostrated two prostrations. Then he turned to us with his face and said: \""Had something new occurred in the prayer"," I would have informed you. I am but a human being; I forget just as you forget. So if I forget"," remind me. And whoever among you forgets something in his prayer"," let him consider what he believes to be correct"," complete upon that"," and then prostrate two prostrations of forgetfulness.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"," and al-Bukhari narrated it through another route from Mansur. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 392]"""
"2258","(2257) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf informed us by dictation; Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Basri in Makkah narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbaḥ al-Za'faranī narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us; al-A'mash narrated from Ibrahim from 'Alqamah from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forgot in his prayer and so he performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Kurayb and others from Abu Mu'awiyah. [Sahih. Preceded before it and is part of it]"
"2259","(2258) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Saydalani and Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; they said: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us; 'Ubaidullah, i.e. Ibn 'Umar, narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting in a corner of the mosque. He prayed and then came and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \And upon you be peace. Go back and pray"," for you have not prayed.\"" So he went back and prayed"," then came and greeted him. He said: \""And upon you be peace. Go back and pray"," for you have not prayed.\"" On the third time or the one after it"," he said: \""Teach me"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""When you stand for prayer"," perform the ablution thoroughly"," then face the qiblah and say the takbir"," then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qur'an"," then bow until you are at ease in bowing"," then rise until you stand upright"," then prostrate until you are at ease in prostrating"," then raise your head until you are at ease sitting"," then do that throughout all your prayer.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Mansur"," and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr"," both from 'Abdullah ibn Numayr. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 5897]"""
"2260","(2260) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us; Budayl narrated from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to commence the prayer with the takbir and the recitation with {Al-hamdu lillahi Rabb al-'alamin}. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim]"
"2261","(2261) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭabarānī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, from al-Thawrī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl, from Ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah, from ʿAlī, who raised it to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The key to prayer is purification"," its consecration (iḥrām) is the takbīr"," and its release (iḥlāl) is the taslīm.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," raḥimahullāh"," said in the Qadīm: And similarly it has been narrated from Ibn Masʿud. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 61.]"""
"2262","(2262) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \The key to prayer is the takbīr"," and its completion is the taslīm.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr with a similar wording"," 9/257.]"""
"2263","(2263) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥanẓalī informed us, Abū Qilābah al-Raqāshī narrated to us, Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Bakr, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the imām says 'Allāhu Akbar","' say 'Allāhu Akbar","' and when the imām says 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","' say 'Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 1/335.]"""
"2264","(2264) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us, Ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Abū ʀĀṣim narrated to us — and he mentioned it with its like in a long ḥadīth.\n\nAbū al-Qāsim said: None narrated it from Sufyān except Abū ʀĀṣim.\n\nThe Shaykh, raḥimahullāh, said: And that has also been narrated from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl, from Saʿīd, and Allāh knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding ḥadīth.]"
"2265","(2265) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf ibn Aḥmad al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Shall I not direct you to something by which Allah will expiate sins and increase good deeds?\"" They said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Performing wuḍūʾ thoroughly at times of difficulty"," frequenting these mosques on foot"," and waiting for one prayer after another. There is not a man among you who goes out from his house in a state of purity and prays with the Muslims the prayer in congregation"," then sits in this mosque waiting for the next prayer"," but that the angels say: 'O Allah"," forgive him; O Allah"," have mercy on him.' So when you stand for prayer"," straighten your rows and set them firm"," and close the gaps"," for I see you behind my back. When your imām says 'Allāhu Akbar","' say 'Allāhu Akbar","' and when he bows"," bow"," and when he says 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","' say 'Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd.' The best of the men's rows is the first"," and the worst is the last"," and the best of the women's rows is the last"," and the worst is the first. O women"," when the men prostrate"," lower your gazes so that you do not see the private parts of the men from the tightness of their lower garments.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 3/3.]"""
"2266","(2266) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original, Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us, and he mentioned the ḥadīth with its like, except that in his book it contains the wording \wa yuṣallī maʿa al-Muslimīn\"" — and the rest is the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. See the preceding ḥadīth.]"""
"2267","(2267) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, Tamīm ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Harawī narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us.\n\nAbū al-Naḍr said: And al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Thawr narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us, from Abū ʿUthmān, from Abī al-Zubayr, from ʿAwn ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Ibn ʿUmar, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying, he heard a man saying: \Allāhu Akbar kabīran"," wa al-ḥamdu lillāhi kathīran"," wa subḥāna Allāhi bukratan wa aṣīlan.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Who is the speaker of such-and-such words?\"" A man said: \""I am"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""I was amazed at it; the gates of heaven were opened for it.\"" Ibn ʿUmar"," raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā"," said: \""I have not abandoned them since I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"," from Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm."""
"2268","(2268) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, ʿAffān narrated to us. He said: And ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh informed us, Abū Muslim informed us, that Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to them, and they both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thābit, from Anas, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu, that the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \Send with us a man who will teach us the Sunnah and Islam.\"" So he took Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ"," raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu"," by the hand and said: \""This is the trustworthy one (amīn) of this Ummah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from ʿAmr al-Nāqid"," from ʿAffān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 2419.]"""
"2269","(2269) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Ismāʿīl narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — and the wording is his — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Zurārah narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith, who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we were a group of young men of similar age, and we stayed with him for twenty nights. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was compassionate and tender-hearted. He thought that we had become homesick for our families, and he asked us about those we had left behind in our families, and we informed him. He said: \Return to your families"," establish prayer among them"," and teach them and instruct them. When the time for prayer comes"," let one of you give the adhān"," and let the eldest of you lead you in prayer.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"," from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 602.]"""
"2270","(2270) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Zayd ibn Salām, from his grandfather, who said: Muʿāwiyah wrote to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shibl: \Inform the people of what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" So he gathered them and said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Learn the Qurʾān"," and when you have learned it"," do not go to excess regarding it"," nor be neglectful of it"," nor earn your livelihood by it"," nor seek abundance through it.'\"" And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 3/444.]"""
"2271","(2271) It was narrated to us by the Shaykh al-Imam Abu al-Tayyib: Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman. He informed us: Abu 'Amr: Isma'il ibn Nujayd narrated to us. Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Bajali narrated to us. Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us. Aban ibn Yazid narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Salam, from Abu Salama, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl al-Ansari that the Prophet (ﷺ) said — and he mentioned it in a similar manner. [Sahih. See the previous chain of narration.]"
"2272","(2272) And it was narrated to us by Abu al-Husayn: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad. He informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Darastuyah narrated to us. Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us. Al-Hajjaj, Muslim ibn Ibrahim, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, and Abu 'Amr Adam narrated — they said: Shu'bah narrated to us. He said: 'Alqamah ibn Marthad informed me. He said: I heard Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah narrate from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami from 'Uthman, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Indeed"," the best of you are those who learn the Qur'an and teach it.\""\n\nHe (Abu 'Abd al-Rahman) said: And Abu 'Abd al-Rahman used to recite (and teach) during the caliphate of 'Uthman until the era of al-Hajjaj came. He said: \""That (teaching of the Qur'an) is what brought me to this position of mine.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Hajjaj ibn Minhal. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 4739.]"""
"2273","(2273) It was narrated to us by Abu al-Hasan: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawi. He informed us: Abu al-Fadl: 'Abdus ibn al-Husayn al-Simsar narrated to us. Yusuf ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Mahan al-Dinawari narrated to us. Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us. 'Amir ibn Abi 'Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us. Ayyub ibn Musa narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A father does not give his child any gift better than good manners (adab).\""\n\nAyyub ibn Musa is the son of 'Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-'Asha. And a group narrated it from 'Amir. [Da'if. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi"," 1952.]"""
"2274","(2274) It was narrated to us by Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan. He informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Mahmuyah al-'Askari narrated to us. Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi narrated to us. Adam narrated to us. Shu'bah narrated from 'Asim al-Ahwal from Abu 'Uthman, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah, the Most High, be pleased with him), who said: \Learn Arabic (the Arabic language).\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah"," 29922.]"""
"2275","(2275) It was narrated to us by Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr. He informed us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us. Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us. Abu Usamah narrated from 'Ubayd Allah from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah, the Most High, be pleased with both of them), who said: \When Ibn 'Umar heard any of his children making grammatical errors (lahan)"," he would strike him.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah"," 29919.]"""
"2276","(2276) It was narrated to us by Abu al-Qasim: Talhah ibn 'Ali ibn al-Saqar, and Abu 'Abd Allah: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Tahir al-Daqqaq in Baghdad — they both said: Ahmad ibn 'Uthman ibn Yahya al-Adami informed us. 'Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Dawri narrated to us. Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us. Fulayh narrated from Sa'id ibn al-Harith, who said: Abu Hurayrah fell ill or was absent, so Abu Sa'id al-Khudri led the prayer. He pronounced the takbir aloud when he commenced (the prayer), and when he bowed, and after he said \Sami' Allahu liman hamidah","\"" and when he raised his head from prostration"," and when he prostrated"," and when he raised (his head)"," and when he stood up from the two rak'ahs — until he completed his prayer in that manner. When he finished"," it was said to him: \""The people have objected to your prayer.\"" So he went out until he stood by the minbar and said: \""O people"," by Allah"," I do not care whether your prayer differed or did not differ. Indeed"," I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) praying in this manner.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Salih from Fulayh ibn Sulayman.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to lead the people in prayer and raise his voice with the takbir. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 791.]"""
"2277","(2277) It was narrated to us by Abu Tahir al-Faqih. He informed us: Abu Bakr: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us. Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us. 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us. Ma'mar narrated from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abu Hurayrah (may Allah, the Most High, be pleased with him) narrated to us, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Imam is only appointed to be followed"," so do not differ from him. When he says the takbir"," say the takbir. When he bows"," bow. When he says 'Sami' Allahu liman hamidah","' say 'Allahumma Rabbana wa lak al-hamd.' When he prostrates"," prostrate. And if he prays sitting"," then all of you pray sitting.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad"," and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi' — both of them from 'Abd al-Razzaq. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 689.]"""
"2278","(2278) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz. Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far informed me. 'Abd Allah Muhammad informed us. Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us. Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan narrated to us. Zuhayr narrated to us. Simak narrated from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah, the Most High, be pleased with him), who said: \Bilal used to give the adhan when the sun had set — meaning when it had declined — and he would not give the iqamah until the Prophet (ﷺ) came out. When he came out"," he would give the iqamah upon seeing him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Salamah ibn Shabib. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 606.]"""
"2279","(2279) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz. Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us. Muhammad ibn Ghalib informed us. Abu 'Umran al-Hawdi, 'Amr ibn Marzuq, and Muslim ibn Ibrahim informed us — they said: Shu'bah informed us from Mansur. He said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf narrate from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The mu'adhdhin has greater authority over the adhan"," and the imam has greater authority over the iqamah.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Sharik from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah"," as a marfu' (elevated) narration"," but it is not preserved (as such). [Sahih. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq"," 1836.]"""
"2280","(2280) It was narrated to us by Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz. Abu Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Darimi narrated to me. Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us. Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us. Khalid narrated from al-Jurayri from Ibn Buraydah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Between every two adhans there is a prayer\"" — he said it three times — \""for whoever wishes.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Shahin"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from al-Jurayri. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 598.]"""
"2281","(2281) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed me; Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Jaʿfar, narrated to us; Shuʿbah said: I heard ʿAmr ibn ʿĀmir al-Anṣārī narrating from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the mu'adhdhin gave the adhān, some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would rise and hasten to the pillars, praying until the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out, and they would continue thus, praying the two rakʿahs before Maghrib. And there was nothing [no interval] between the adhān and the iqāmah.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār.\n\nAnd ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated it from Shuʿbah, and he said: \And there was a short interval between the adhān and the iqāmah","\"" meaning thereby in the Maghrib prayer.\n\n[Sound. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 599.]\n\n---"""
"2282","(2282) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Warrāq, whose nickname was Ḥamdān, narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mubārak narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Munʿim, the son-in-law of ʿAmr ibn Fāʾid, narrated to me; Yaḥyā ibn Muslim narrated to me from al-Ḥasan and ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Bilāl: \O Bilāl"," make an interval between your adhān and your iqāmah sufficient for the eater to finish his meal"," the drinker to finish his drink"," and the one relieving himself to attend to his need. And do not stand [for prayer] until you see me.\""\n\nThere is a question regarding its chain of narration. [Very weak. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it"," no. 195.]\n\n---"""
"2283","(2283) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Bazzāz in Baghdād informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī in Makkah informed us; Abū Yaḥyā ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Zakariyyā ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Masarra narrated to us; my father narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Majīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj; Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah informed me from Sālim Abī al-Naḍr that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to come out to the mosque after the call [adhān]. When he saw that the people of the mosque were few, he would sit until he saw a congregation among them, then he would pray. And when he came out and saw a congregation, he would establish the prayer.\n\nHe [the narrator] said: And Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah also narrated to me from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr from Masʿūd ibn al-Ḥakam al-Zuraqī from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, a similar hadith. And Abū ʿĀṣim also narrated it from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n[Weak. Al-Fākihī narrated it in his Fawāʾid, no. 114.]\n\n---"
"2284","(2284) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Sahl and Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib said: Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us from al-Awzāʿī from al-Zuhrī from Abī Salamah from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The prayer would be established for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and the people would take their places before the Prophet (ﷺ) took his place.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā from al-Walīd ibn Muslim. [Sound. Muslim narrated it, no. 605.]\n\n---"
"2285","(2285) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Sadūsī narrated to us; ʿAwn ibn Kahmas narrated to us from his father Kahmas, who said: We stood up for prayer in Minā while the imam had not yet come out. Some of us sat down, and a shaykh from the people of Kūfah said to me: \What is making you sit?\"" I said: \""Ibn Buraydah.\"" He said: \""This is al-sumūd [standing for a long time].\"" The shaykh said to me: \""ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Awsajah narrated to me from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib"," who said: We would stand in rows for prayer for a long time before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would say the takbīr.\"" He [al-Barāʾ] also said: \""Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who are close to the first row"," and there is no step more beloved to Allah—exalted be His praise—than a step one takes to join a row.\""\n\nWhat has been narrated from Ibn Buraydah in this hadith has also been narrated from ʿAlī. It was narrated from Abū Khālib al-Wālibī that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," may Allah be pleased with him"," came out to us while we were standing"," and he said: \""Why do I see you standing in bewilderment [sāmids]?\"" meaning standing.\n\nIbrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī was asked: \""Do you wait for the imam standing or sitting?\"" He said: \""Rather"," sitting.\"" And it is more likely that they used to stand for prayer before the Prophet (ﷺ) came out and would take their places before he took his place. Then he commanded them not to stand until they saw that he had come out"," as a concession to lighten the burden upon them. [Weak. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 543.]\n\n---"""
"2286","(2286) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah from his father that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When the prayer is established [iqāmah]"," do not stand until you see me.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm. [Sound. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 611.]\n\n---"""
"2287","(2287) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus and ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: Maʿmar narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah from his father from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \When the prayer is established"," do not stand until you see me"," that I have come out.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm.\n\nAnd likewise al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated it from Shaybān from Yaḥyā: \""until you see me"," that I have come out.\"" And al-Ḥajjāj al-Ṣawwāf said the same from Yaḥyā in the narration of Muḥammad ibn Bashshār from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from him. And Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from Maʿmar"," and Abū Nuʿaym from Shaybān"," and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿīd from Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān from al-Ḥajjāj"," without his saying: \""that I have come out.\"" As for what some of the jurists narrate in this hadith—\""until you see me standing in the row\""—it has not reached us.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that when it was said"," \""The prayer has been established [qad qāmat al-ṣalāh]","\"" he would leap up and stand.\n\nAnd from al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," may Allah be pleased with both of them"," that he used to do that. And this is the view of ʿAṭāʾ and al-Ḥasan.\n\n[Sound. Previously mentioned.]\n\n---"""
"2288","(2288) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadhābādhī and Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz said: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), after the prayer had been established [iqāmah] and before he said the takbīr, turned his face toward his Companions and said: \Straighten your rows and stand close together"," for I see you from behind my back.\"" He [Anas] said: \""I would see a man pressing his shoulder against his brother's shoulder when he stood for prayer.\"" [Sound. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 687.]\n\n---"""
"2289","(2289) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr narrated to us; Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; Zāʾidah narrated to us; Ḥumayd narrated to us; Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turned his face toward us and said: \Straighten your rows and stand close together"," for I see you from behind my back.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Abī Rajāʾ from Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr. [Sound. Previously mentioned.]\n\n---"""
"2290","(2290) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. And Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Isfarāʾinī informed us; Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Khaythamah narrated to us from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, who said: I heard al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to straighten our rows as though he were straightening arrows with them, until he saw that we had understood from him. Then one day he came out and stood, and he was about to say the takbīr, when he saw a man whose chest was protruding from the row. He said: \O servants of Allah"," straighten your rows"," or Allah will cause your faces to diverge.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Sound. Muslim narrated it"," no. 436.]"""
"2291","(2291) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, meaning Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith; Ḥātim narrated to us, meaning Ibn Abī Ṣaghīrah, from Simāk, who said: I heard al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would straighten our rows when we stood for the prayer, and when they were aligned, he would say the takbīr."
"2292","(2292) Abū Aḥmad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl — informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to command the straightening of the rows. When the one appointed for this came to him and informed him that the rows had been straightened, he would say the takbīr."
"2293","(2293) Abū Aḥmad al-ʿAdl informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from his paternal uncle Abū Suhayl ibn Mālik, from his father, who said: I was with ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) when the prayer was established, and I was speaking to him about granting me a stipend. I continued speaking to him while he was levelling the pebbles with his sandals, until some men whom he had appointed to straighten the rows came to him and informed him that the rows had been straightened. He then said to me: Stand straight in the row. Then he said the takbīr."
"2294","(2294) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Qutaybah narrated to us; Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Muṣʿab ibn Thābit ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr, from Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn al-Sāʾib, the keeper of the maqṣūrah, who said: I prayed one day beside Anas ibn Mālik, and he said: Do you know why this piece of wood was placed here? I said: No, by Allah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to place his hand upon it and say: \Be straight"," straighten your rows.\"""""
"2295","(2295) Abū ʿAlī informed us; Abū Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Ḥumayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to us; Muṣʿab ibn Thābit narrated from Muḥammad ibn Muslim, from Anas, with this hadith, saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood for the prayer, he would take it in his right hand, then turn and say: \Be straight"," straighten your rows.\"" Then he would take it in his left hand and say: \""Be straight"," straighten your rows.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah"," the Most High"," have mercy on him) said: The rest of the Sunan concerning the straightening of the rows and its manner are recorded in the chapters of Imāmah"," by the will of Allah"," the Most High."""
"2296","(2296) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Shaybān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The prayer was established while the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was engaged in private conversation with a man at the side of the mosque, and he did not stand for the prayer until the people dozed off.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Maʿmar, from ʿAbd al-Wārith, and Muslim narrated it from Shaybān ibn Farrūkh."
